const e={introduction:`You, fortunate Rat, are truly lucky. In China, Rats are highly valued, and not merely for culinary purposes. You possess a strong desire for power and instinctively know how to pursue your ambitions. Once your small, tenacious Rat claws firmly grasp an esteemed position, you cling to it with unwavering determination. Leadership suits you well.
People hold you in high regard; you project an image of composure. You are sociable and enjoy having fun. However, your inner self is often restless and anxious. You feel a need to discuss your problems thoroughly, as expressing your worries helps you clear your mind of them.
Some individuals accuse you of being overly talkative, but it is more accurate to say you communicate extensively. You are not inclined to idleness; you are quick-witted and complete tasks swiftly, leaving ample time to involve yourself in the affairs of others. When navigating delicate situations, you instinctively know how to maintain a clean reputation. Yet, you are not inherently straightforward; you would always prefer to navigate a winding path to achieve fame and fortune rather than follow a direct and narrow one.
You tend to be particular and exhibit paradoxical traits. You are an unusual combination of extravagance and frugality, saving everything from worn-out rubber bands to frayed shirt collars, just in case. Then, you might spend lavishly on an exorbitantly priced trinket that you consider vital to your well-being. You skillfully persuade others to comply with your desires. For you charming Rat individuals, winning friends and seducing lovers comes effortlessly. Nevertheless, I do not perceive you as promiscuous; you are inclined towards marriage and require a family. Why not venture out and secure a vibrant Dragon, a conscientious Ox, or a more cunning-than-thou Monkey as a partner? It would be wise to avoid Cats and Horses. Your youth is a joyous period, energetic Rat, but midlife may bring setbacks due to errors in judgment concerning love or business matters. If you decide to seek advice from friends, your later years should prove comfortable and untroubled. My counsel? Cease worrying. You will never face destitution, whether for love or money. Resourceful go-getters like you rarely do.`,elements:{Wood:`This element provides a soothing influence that calms the inherent zigzag nervousness of the Rat's character. Unlike other Rats, this one understands how to relax and accept situations as they unfold. Its temperament is more composed than that of other Rats but, as if to conceal its natural aloofness, the sociable Wood Rat displays a more agreeable charm and extroverted nature.
Most Rats are concerned about their public image and care immensely about how others perceive them, but the Wood Rat appears to possess a more stable sense of its standing in society. This added security enables it to exhibit a carefree, open demeanor and imbues its personality with a touch of cheerfulness and a devil-may-care attitude that associates and members of the opposite sex find captivating. It is jovial and even a bit light-hearted when serious matters are impending.
This element grants the Rat a particular aptitude for recognizing both the beauty and value of art objects. When combined with its strong business acumen, the Wood Rat may achieve significant success in antiques or become a respected art dealer. Alternatively, it might become an author of important literary works, a painter of considerable renown, or a world-class musician. It draws inspiration from its surroundings and is sensitive to every subtle detail of aesthetic input it encounters.
Always aware of its need to belong to a social group, the Wood Rat openly displays its unwavering principles. It constantly declares what it will and will not tolerate in its own life and in the lives of those it cherishes. It worries ceaselessly about its children and their descendants. It would likely commit a crime to safeguard them and prevent them from acquiring a poor reputation.
These Rats possess substantial egos. They require approval, applause, and encouragement almost more than they need sustenance. A part of their open-door policy and apparent willingness to be flexible and understanding stems from their desire to be accepted by those to whom they extend their hospitality and with whom they agree to cohabit. If left to fend for itself without moral support for its projects or shared ideals, this Rat will offer nothing but complaints and tales of misfortune. These Rats dislike being alone and feel justified in blaming anyone who fails to provide what they need.
This individual typically succeeds in their undertakings. They understand their limitations and intelligently aim only as high as they know they can reach. They experience social frustration, however. People outwardly like the Wood Rat, are willing to chat and spend time with them, visit their elegant home for dinner, and offer compliments. Nevertheless, this Rat often feels overlooked. They have few genuine friends. Although they provide every opportunity, people do not confide in them easily. Do others fear their sharp, critical tongue? Or is it their lack of compassion? Either way, they feel excluded. Perhaps they should curb their unfortunate habit of seeking bargains when choosing friends. Wood Rats, take note: love those you befriend for their hearts, not for what you believe you can gain from their connections. Always seek qualities of soul in those you love, and you will be rewarded with the unconditional friendship and steadfast loyalty that you so deeply desire.`,Fire:`These high-strung talkers, these quick-paced Rats, are composed of raw energy, infused with a substantial dose of nerves, and covered by a significant case of restlessness. No lazy individuals need apply. These Rats will relentlessly overcome game-players, insincere friends, snobs, and deceivers. They demand truth, beauty, and justice—or else!
The Fire Rat embodies the ultimate expression of all Rats. In appearance, it is a concentrated version of its industrious Rat counterparts. It resembles them in every aspect: outwardly calm, inwardly anxious, protective, generous, acquisitive, charming, articulate, persuasive, and resilient. However, the Fire Rat is more completely absorbed in being itself than in being the person who pleases and cares for others. This trait, which some might consider extreme selfishness, distinguishes it from the Rat who settles down, raises a family, and remains tied to a mundane lifestyle for the family's benefit. Fire Rats aspire to build something magnificent that they can unequivocally claim as their own. They make passionate lovers and are daring pursuers of a romantic life. They consume passion voraciously and continuously savor the remnants of love.
These Rats are also exceptionally brilliant intellectuals. Not only do they win all the prestigious academic awards, but they are also endowed with remarkably swift perception. They can translate a fleeting thought into action before competitors have even registered its presence. Evidently, this rapidly thinking mind effortlessly outwits and outmaneuvers its adversaries.
Since all success comes early and relatively easily to them, the Fire Rat is impatient with rejection, heartbreak, and obstacles. When faced with a significant hurdle or major disappointment, they may find it difficult to concentrate and will impulsively move to where opportunities seem more favorable and where more people will appreciate them. They fear loneliness more profoundly than death. They are impulsive and constantly seeking new experiences to divert and stimulate them. Whether as a remedy for frustration or in response to a sudden whim, the Fire Rat dives in headfirst, consumes its way through the new situation, relationship, or job, eventually realizing that it has spread itself too thinly. The Fire Rat may have accumulated three ex-wives, as many families, four lovers, several careers, and a dozen hobbies. By then, it is too late; they are ensnared in their own trap.
The Fire Rat can only learn through direct experience. Yet, experience can also be its adversary. No one who becomes involved with the Fire Rat remains unaffected by its captivating charm. Fragments of its influence are scattered everywhere. By dispersing its energies, it can end up losing its grasp on what it desires before even recognizing what it was longing for. Accepting failure or rejection is out of the question for Fire Rats. Instead, they may succumb to nervous breakdowns, severe depressions, and debilitating drug abuse problems.
Physically, this Rat thrives on its resilience; it is composed of sheer determination, stoicism, and courage. It pushes itself harder in every new undertaking, striving to prove it can accomplish more and advance further. It leaps out of bed at 6 a.m. to tackle the day and collapses into bed at 3 a.m., exhausted, yet willing and ready to rise again three hours later and confront the next day with the same intensity. Unless compelled to slow down, taught to approach life with more philosophical detachment, and consistently praised and encouraged, the workaholic Fire Rat will relentlessly push itself until it collapses.
Typically, the Fire Rat desires to earn and retain substantial wealth. If, due to scattering its energies, it finds itself unable to do so, it will relentlessly criticize itself, blaming its own weaknesses and deeply regretting its past flawed approach to life. Somehow, from the moment it identifies the defect in its previous strategy, it can begin to perceive a clear path to achieving a comfortable, sane livelihood. As if by a miracle, it ceases to develop stomach ulcers, alters its methods, adopts an entirely new direction, and, despite being a deeply sentimental and honorable soul, dances joyfully on the metaphorical graves of its former tormentors. It may take this Rat some time to realize its full potential, but when (and if) it finally decides to do so—be prepared!`,Earth:`This is the practical, no-nonsense Rat who achieves success cleverly and rapidly. It appears to have known its objective from the day it was born, diligently worked to secure the position it has always desired, and by the age of forty, finds itself there, comfortably established and contentedly humming a cheerful tune.
Something about the Earth Rat immediately conveys that it can competently handle any challenge life presents. It is strong-willed and demanding, always prioritizing its own needs first, yet unafraid to make concessions and negotiate when it cannot prevail. It is more stable than other Rats, more inclined to maintain peace. Its willpower is immense; it can overcome resistant detractors or overwhelming workloads and emerge refreshed and ready for more.
Unlike most other Rats, the Earth Rat maintains its composure in the face of emotional turmoil. Its philosophical perspective helps it to see through panic, preventing it from being consumed by the intensity of the moment, as other Rats so frequently are. Earth Rats are steady, persistent workers. They rise at a reasonable hour, adhere to a disciplined routine, and approach both work and leisure with a measured, sensible intelligence. The typical acquisitiveness of most Rats is absent; they are solidly dependable and remarkably soft-spoken. While they may hold unshakeable opinions and are persuasive speakers, Earth Rats do not feel obligated to impose their ideals on others.
Earth Rats are amiable individuals. They enjoy eating and need to be surrounded by others. Hosting parties or small social gatherings is a significant talent for them; they instinctively know how to pair compatible guests at a dining table. Despite their sociability, you will not often find Earth Rats attending elegant catered events in expensive restaurants; they feel more at ease during cozy family receptions where their superior position as host is never questioned, and they can express themselves freely without fear of criticism.
Take an Earth Rat out of its hospitable home environment, and you will discover that in daily life or business, it is rather smug and self-satisfied. Since it has always strived diligently to reach its current position, it has a notable tendency to judge others as less industrious or eager to succeed, labeling them as idlers and good-for-nothings without just cause.
Earth Rats often test our patience with their continuous pontificating and self-righteous speeches. However, they are not always as virtuous as they wish to appear. When called upon to protect its family or show care for a loved one, the Earth Rat is unsurpassed. It can be faithful and strives to maintain its own and its family's reputation as pure. Yet, it is a committed romantic and craves passion as much as any other Rat. Its common remedy for setbacks often takes the form of a brief extramarital affair or a secret liaison. Is it fickle? Not truly—just pleasure-seeking and desperate to feel itself captivated by love.
Earth Rats may carry prejudices to extremes. They can also be spiteful and will complain about the shortcomings of people they perceive as less competent or successful than themselves. They dislike not being loved and whine when they feel excluded or lonely. Nevertheless, of all the Rats, the Earth Rat is the most wholesome.
Some assert that due to its judgmental tone and arrogant air of superiority, the Earth Rat is cruel and unfeeling. Nothing could be further from the truth. This Earthy Rat is entirely compassionate. It may appear formidable, but observe how it behaves when it comes to kissing babies and openly displaying affection to its loved ones. Earth Rats enjoy creating a cozy home and invariably keep many domestic animals. Their comfortable houses are always filled with plants and pianos. Their children are warmly socialized and appear well-fed and happy.`,Metal:`The Metal Rat endeavors to acquire wealth and recognition through influential connections and by skillfully applying its talents to shrewd networking. It is not as intellectually inclined as other Rats, but its street-smart instincts are more fully developed. This Rat is a master persuader, who will stop at nothing to achieve the desired outcome. When engaging in an eloquent charm offensive, the cunning Metal Rat tirelessly entices, coaxes, and flatters its target until its objective is within reach and it feels confident it has made its point.
This Rat takes achievement and "getting there" almost excessively seriously. It is not in a hurry and never acts impulsively before meticulously examining its landing spot a hundred times. It considers matters thoroughly, scrutinizing each detail as it proceeds. It is also a contemplative individual and a problem-solver.
Although it may process information slowly, the Metal Rat registers hostility and resentments, and detects pain and rage on its inner radar screen with remarkable speed. Any profession where intuition and extrasensory perception are valuable will be a perfect outlet for this sensitive soul's unique abilities. It might choose psychiatry, education, astrology, the police force, detective work, research, or social work.
However, such keen perceptiveness as it possesses may sometimes backfire. It observes others' flaws so clearly that it quickly becomes judgmental. These exceptionally sharp evaluations can diminish some of the joy in its life, stripping away illusion and youthful idealism. Some Metal Rats become pessimistic, possessive, and materialistic, even paranoid about how others treat them. Being so acutely aware of others' mistakes makes it edgy, and it is prone to bouts of brooding and pure pessimism. After a while, it becomes known for its irritability and loses the ability to laugh at itself. If it does not take steps in early adulthood to cultivate objectivity and refine its social skills, by middle age, this Rat may evolve into a jaded cynic for whom social acceptance is difficult to attain.
Meticulous by nature, the Metal Rat despises anything careless or halfhearted. It considers itself businesslike and strives to behave soberly when interacting with its peers. It is economical and criticizes those it perceives as wasteful or extravagant. It dislikes lukewarm sentiment and condemns halfway measures, which it regards as both lazy and shoddy. The Metal Rat cannot tolerate individuals who lack enthusiasm—especially if they lack it for him and his favored projects.
Curiously, however, this sometimes ill-tempered person is overtly pleasure-seeking. It enjoys food and consumes it abundantly. It takes love and marriage seriously, pursuing sexual pleasure with zeal, dexterity, and skill. It typically has little interest in carousing but will occasionally become slightly intoxicated at its own parties, where it feels secure from the scrutinizing gaze of outsiders it considers so threatening to its impeccable reputation.`,Water:`The assertive Rat personality is agreeably softened by the influence of the Yin element, Water. For this Rat, ambition and the pursuit of success are inherent traits. Its primary interest is to lead a fortunate life and navigate its challenges gracefully without emerging scarred and impaired.
The Water Rat exhibits more feminine qualities than many of its fellow Rats. It prefers elegant clothing and luxurious accessories such as gold earrings, diamond clips, or rings—items not typically associated with more robust Rats. The Water Rat possesses a talent for offering advice, for which people seek its counsel.
Water Rats, particularly women, have a fondness for sweets. While they are unwilling to compromise other significant aspects of their health, they tend to overindulge in sugar, and a predisposition to obesity in middle age is common among them. The recommended solution would be to reduce sugar intake, consume green vegetables, and substitute meat with fish and grain dishes. Sugar not only contributes to the Water Rat's weight gain but also negatively impacts the healthy function of its pancreas and its delicate nervous system.
The Water Rat possesses keen intuition and intellect; it comprehends underlying meanings and also knows how to resolve human problems almost before they arise. It is adept at asserting authority, quietly yet effectively outmaneuvering its adversaries, and defeating enemies at their own game. Though not truly dangerous or cruel, it can unsettle the most courageous individuals by demonstrating its extraordinary ability to perceive through obscurity. Its dreams are vivid visions and often foretell future events. Heeding their messages may spare its close associates much distress.
This type of Rat is content to live a comfortable, middle-class life. It is ambitious, yet it desires to live in comfort, even luxury, and appears less compelled to work as diligently as others. Awards, employment, significant positions, and even fame and fortune come its way with little effort.
Water Rats are not naturally altruistic. Developing in the refined atmosphere of its plush home and immediate surroundings, this Rat sometimes forgets that there are poorer, less fortunate individuals than itself. Instead of enhancing its sophisticated central heating system, it ought, perhaps, to consider the lives of those who are in need of a blanket, a cup of coffee, or even a comforting gesture to persevere. Its political views often lean towards conservatism.
This Rat is constantly acquiring new knowledge, eagerly enrolling in courses on previously unexplored subjects, and immersing itself in cultural events designed to impart obscure information to its already impressive personal repository. Its mind is particularly fertile and capable of transforming abstract concepts into art. Many Water Rats write proficiently, produce excellent paintings and music, and earn a substantial living doing so. They often prosper more due to their charm and appeal than any strenuous effort. Water Rats are not lazy—just a little self-satisfied because success comes their way due to their inherent superiority.
This Water Rat can be a genuine challenge to its companions. Uncharacteristically for a Rat, it tends towards lethargy, is occasionally untidy, and sometimes avoids responsibilities, claiming they are better suited for less important individuals. Sudden outbursts of self-pity and self-aggrandizement both annoy and perplex those with whom it lives. Due to a fundamental disdain for the system, it is easily corrupted and somewhat materialistic in its outlook.
However, it is patriotic and loyal to family and friends, towards whom it is sincere and affectionate. It is capable of facing adversity with composure and bravery. Its sense of justice is well-developed, and it is willing to fight for what is right—provided it does not have to venture far from its leather chair and paneled office.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"A marriage between two Rats is certain to enrich their lives. Both partners fear loneliness, and each clings to the relationship unit with tiny, tough teeth and claws. The Rat understands how to act as a friend as well as a lover, supporting a mate in business ventures and helping them through difficult periods. One Rat will shower the other with presents and attentive care. The Rat appreciates acts of kindness, comprehends the needs of its Rat mate, and provides complete support. A few challenging moments may arise. Both individuals are prone to outrageous flirting. He might be eyeing a beautiful dinner guest while she subtly touches the foot of the same guest's husband under the dining table. This can lead to bitter accusations, disagreements, breaches of trust, and days of silent tension. Early in their relationship, this couple should make a commitment to discuss everything as it happens. They ought to openly address jealousies and suspicions so these issues can be properly analyzed and discarded before week-long silences begin. They should also limit their social life. Too much innocent flirtation with casual acquaintances at cocktail parties may ultimately weaken their bond. Typically, their sexual intimacy is fantastic. Both partners require extensive time together in bed. They also agree on adventurous sexual experiences. Rat bedroom activities are incredibly intricate—yet harmless.",Ox:"Union between these two signs guarantees matrimonial stability. The Ox provides the energetic Rat with the grounding it lacks, and the Rat subtly influences the Ox's conventionality and resistance to change, enlivening what could otherwise be a dull, plodding existence. This combination fits well, with each partner complementing the other's sharper characteristics. The Ox's steadfastness offers the Rat the kind of security it requires. The devoted Ox will willingly assume the role of provider, which allows the Rat to act as the family protector. The sociable Rat enjoys hosting parties and attending social functions. This arrangement is ideal for the quiet Ox, who, without the Rat's exuberant nature, would simply remain at home contemplating. Each partner is content to fulfill their respective role. Alluring and meticulous, a Rat serves as a perfect assistant for an Ox in business, going to great lengths to encourage the Ox’s career. Of course, the Ox demands complete fidelity. Despite an occasional nagging desire to stray, the Rat will largely remain faithful. What about passion? Neither the Rat nor the Ox is excessively concerned with the whimsical idea of extravagant lovemaking practices. Their sex life will be lusty, though routine.",Tiger:"Upon their initial meeting, these two immediately charm each other. The Rat finds the Tiger captivating and would love to show it off, while the confident Tiger is amused by the Rat's lively conversation and vibrant sense of humor. However, friction is likely to develop in the long term. After the initial spark of love, these two will begin to find faults with each other. The boisterous, adventurous Tiger will constantly seek excitement—venturing on safari to Kenya, then moving on to San Francisco to experience the next earthquake. The more domestic Rat will eventually grow to despise the sight of suitcases. The Tiger pursues instability, drawn by danger and the prospect of having a new job every year. Everything presents a challenge to this aggressive creature. The Rat will not always find the Tiger's inconsistencies appealing and will be plagued by worry. The Rat's mental stability largely depends on material security, and with the Tiger constantly changing jobs, the Rat will fret over finances. For their relationship to endure, both must remember the initial reasons that drew them together. They have much to discuss and agree on many subjects. If the Rat can recall how the Tiger captivatingly entered his or her life, and the Tiger can continue to appreciate the Rat's powers of seduction, there is hope for an exciting, long-lasting marriage.",Rabbit:"This game of Cat and Mouse is one I would advise against playing. Although both the Cat and the Rat share some similar traits, they are not very compatible. Both have strong needs for a home. One might imagine them browsing an IKEA catalog together or jointly selecting wallpaper for their new kitchen. But unfortunately, the Rat and Cat disagree on almost everything. In times of conflict, they will constantly evade each other, with neither prepared to make concessions or take steps towards reconciliation. The Cat will be hissing, and the Rat will be sulking. This irritable relationship becomes more particular and petty with each passing day. However discordant a note they strike, once united, it will be difficult for this pair to separate. They both cling to security. Divorce would lead both of them into the unknown. As they find familiarity reassuring, they would probably prefer to be mildly content together than without a partner. Sexually, they tend to be aroused by sadomasochistic games, pulling each other's hair in the midst of a passionate embrace. Over time, such practices will lead to a sexually destructive relationship. A prolonged commitment is not advisable.",Dragon:"This is an absolutely delightful marriage; the Chinese consider it one of their most favorably arranged unions. The restless Rat will be invigorated by the dynamism of the flamboyant Dragon, and the Dragon will thrive on the Rat's generous admiration. These two will complement each other beautifully, guaranteeing bliss. With the strong-willed Dragon present, the Rat will willingly relinquish complete control; anxieties will gradually subside, bringing peace and comfort. The Dragon is so emotionally expressive that the burden of worry will be lifted from the poor little Rat's shoulders. Larger and bolder, the Dragon will bear the weight of the loving Rat's turmoil. The Rat will not feel competitive about the Dragon's position of strength in this couple, content to remain in the background of a fervent friend/mate. The Dragon and Rat team will feel like royalty. In the Rat's perception, the Dragon makes no mistakes. This is ideal for the fortunate Dragon, who loves to be the center of attention. The dazzling Dragon is so brilliant and exciting that even the Rat's typically robust appetite for sex may be overwhelmed and suddenly diminish. Despite its inherent wisdom, the proud Dragon might fail to recognize the issue (the Dragon's ego can sometimes overshadow its intellect) and place blame on the Rat. A calm, rational discussion will clear the air, and in no time, the Dragon's engaging conversation will reignite the Rat's temporarily diminished sensuality.",Snake:"Although this alliance can often lead to an interesting friendship, I would not recommend it as a romantic relationship. Rat and Snake may be sexually attracted to each other, but ideally, their connection should remain purely social. On a daily basis, life for a Rat/Snake couple will be filled with upheaval, disagreement, and disappointment. After the initial physical attraction, the Snake will withdraw and keep aspects of its life securely private. The Serpent's inclination for flirtation will be even stronger if the Snake is attached to a clingy Rat. The Rat will grow uneasy and fearful about security. The Snake's investments may not prove profitable, and the restless Rat will have to take charge of the family's finances. Tempers will flare, especially the Rat's, who struggles under the burden of trying to maintain the crumbling foundation. The Snake? It will storm out of the house to the nearest Dior boutique to add to an already extensive wardrobe of fine lingerie. The only moments of tranquility in this union will be spent intimately, passionately entwined for hours. The Rat will appreciate the sexual attention the elusive Snake provides and, ever generous, will be forgiving. Be cautious, gentle Rat, of your enchanting Snake. If you are not careful, even you can become a victim. Snakes will draw you in with promises, love you intensely, then metaphorically consume you whole for breakfast.",Horse:"In China, even the local grocer recoils at the mention of this unlikely pairing. The Horse is far too self-centered for the Rat's kind, giving, and dependent nature. Although initially drawn by their differences, they should not marry. Beyond a shared love of money and all it can provide, no common ground exists between these two. The Rat is likely to be mistreated by the arrogant Horse. The Horse is moody, causing the Rat to feel unstable, and so individualistic that it will not even consider the Rat's feelings, which will unnerve the already anxious rodent. Ultimately, the Horse will not feel sufficiently challenged by a Rat partner. To express its disappointment, the Horse may criticize and attack the Rat who, because marriage is so fundamental to its security, will continue trying to please the nagging Horse. This only exacerbates the situation. Now the Horse despises the Rat for its 'weakness.' The Horse's impatience can lead to a search for pleasure elsewhere and subsequent merciless infidelity. In short, all the negative aspects of the Horse's personality will be brought out by the Rat's vulnerabilities. The usually strong Rat will be starved for security. A family and children could temporarily restore the Rat to its whimsical self. But when the children grow up and leave home, the Rat parent will become depressed and lonely. Yet, no matter its unhappiness, the Rat, fearing disruption, will be unable to leave the punishing Horse and will only grow bitter and vengeful. This is definitely a marital no-no.",Goat:"This is a tricky one. The Goat enjoys the loving Rat's company but finds its nervousness unappealing. The Goat's peaceful nature attracts the affectionate Rat, but the Goat's lack of interest in the mundane tasks of everyday life will cause the Rat to fret and worry. The Goat's whimsical, carefree nature will strike the industrious Rat as sheer laziness. The Goat will spend too much money on unnecessary items. The Rat will experience anxiety about debt, fiscal responsibility, and pervasive insecurity. This household exists in a constant state of cold war. The Rat worries quietly, and the Goat lacks the necessary initiative to ease its troubled mate. All their conflicts will be fought with subtle tactics and hostile stares. The Rat will long for a partner with more drive. The gracious Goat, not courageous enough to confront the Rat, will resist lethargically—but not emphatically enough to satisfy the Rat's need for challenge. Their mutual feelings of inadequacy will be alleviated during sexual intimacy. The Goat is exceptionally sensual and can exert an almost magical power over the Rat. Thrilled by such intense sexual excitement, the Rat (for once) will gladly surrender control. The Goat may gain confidence from the Rat's submissiveness and see an opportunity to discuss some of their differences. If the physical union is strong, this couple may eventually resolve their disagreements in the bedroom.",Monkey:"If all other options fail, these two could embark on a career as a comedy duo. Humor, games, parties, and friends! What immense enjoyment you will experience! How fortunate you are to have been brought together! Shared, your lives will be an unending roller-coaster ride. The entertaining Monkey, constantly making faces from the top of the jungle gym, keeps the Rat in perpetual laughter. Amidst bursts of laughter, the Rat suggests funnier, more ingenious antics, inspiring the witty Monkey with even more hilarious movements. It is a matrimonial delight. The sometimes-reserved Rat will become an incessant chatterbox alongside a mellow Monkey. However, the Monkey never grows weary of the clever Rat. For the Monkey, it is like having a walking radio show. Both being so personable, they will always be dining out or hosting gatherings at home. They have a multitude of friends and spend little time alone. As neither is afraid of hard work, money comes easily to them. The Monkey sometimes uses its typically diverse interests to justify a desire for sexual promiscuity. Should the Monkey betray the ever-devoted Rat, the relationship will become strained. However, ultimate discord is rare. Mostly, this joyful couple lives in an amusement park of happiness.",Rooster:"The Rat and the Rooster incessantly peck away at each other. They are equally jealous and possessive, as well as anxious about their combined future. One would expect this alliance to devote long hours to mutual accounts, carefully monitoring each debit. Nervous and impatient to pin down every detail, they’ve surely planned ahead, booking their flights to London and their trips to Morocco months in advance. Not so! Each considers that the other should be the adult in the relationship. Indeed, each wants freedom from burdensome responsibility. Rooster and Rat are forever arguing over money. Each deems the other too extravagant on the wrong items. The showy Rooster desires a shimmering new Jaguar. The Rat wants a crumbling stone house in the countryside. They will never agree. A lively Rat with an active social calendar makes a possessive Rooster turn green with envy. A socially active Rat paired with a conservative Rooster feels stifled. The rebellious Rat accepts prestigious invitations and leaves the jilted Rooster at home alone. Crushed by the Rat's frequent absences, the Rooster grows insecure and seeks new ways to confine the Rat. Using sex as a weapon, each deprives the other when they quarrel. Although fundamentally capable of enjoying each other, their mundane conflicts surface in the bedroom. This allows for only intermittent pleasure on the occasional peaceful Tuesday. The union is unstable, at best.",Dog:"This is a potentially happy marriage. Provided the relationship is conducted fairly, the Rat and Dog can be more than satisfied in each other's company. However, be prepared for long, intense discussions to resolve political, social, and financial differences of opinion. The materialistic Rat may find it difficult to reason with a generous Dog. The Dog gives money away, sometimes forgetting to save enough for the rent. Dogs cannot resist the opportunity to rescue those in need. The Dog's stability depends on being perceived as the philanthropic good person. The Rat does not agree. It is the hoarder, consumed by anxiety about savings, unable to comprehend its puppy-faced mate's desperate need to give everything away. Disagreements are plentiful. But as each half of this couple feels deeply passionate about the other, true harmony is possible. The Dog's love is unconditional, offering a gentle sanctuary for the Rat's restless soul. The happiness you find together, both in and out of bed, will be enhanced by the arrival of numerous children and pets whom you will nurture and raise together as a team.",Pig:"Indeed, these two make wonderful partners. In China, the Pig symbolizes prosperity, which alone prevents a restless Rat from grinding its teeth. The practical Pig soothes the anxious Rat and is fortunate with money. Money alone brings a constant smile to the face of the contented Rat. But the Pig's gentle nature also counts for a great deal. They share a common love for food, taking holidays in France and Italy to savor the delights of old-world cuisine. The restless Rat, now secure in the peaceful Pig's presence, finally lets go, abandoning worry beads and tranquilizers for a glamorous indulgence in luxury. Despite this affluent couple's inclination for spending freely, they are both potential hoarders. Having robust savings to rely on will make the cheerful Rat even more cheerful. Overly kind and sensitive, the Pig is not always as shrewd as the Rat in business dealings. The cautious Rat's advice is welcomed here. This sociable and delightful couple is on every host's A-list. Genuine love characterizes this union. You can expect many children to abound. This pair delights in lovemaking. The sensual Pig not only stimulates the lusty Rat's erogenous zones, but emotional and financial security allow the Rat to fully surrender in bed—where it truly matters!"},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"This period threatens to be a time of financial restraint for you Rats. Commercial activity tends to slow down in Snake years. You will not face bankruptcy, but your income may decrease sufficiently to cause you some restless nights. It would be wise to set aside some cash in a secure location. There is political instability and global unrest now, so prepare to hunker down and perhaps even take on new and different responsibilities. Your romantic life might cool somewhat during the months of June and July. This period of coolness is only temporary, so do not lose heart. Someone in your immediate circle will want to fabricate a damaging rumor, and your private life may very well be its subject. Certain individuals consider gossip harmless, but the fabricated story in question carries more weight than a mere fib; it has the potential to create scandal. Keep your awareness sharp during the initial months of the year to fend off any deception you sense is approaching. Additionally, be prepared to compromise where you might otherwise have refused to yield. Flexibility proves beneficial in Snake years."},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"Rats and Horses typically argue—over everything from how money is spent to how to cultivate geraniums. Despite the Horse's peculiar attraction to you, as soon as you two begin a relationship, the conflict starts! Arguments can be constructive, but in the case of the Horse and Rat, continuous disagreements consume much of your valuable time and lead neither of you to a positive outcome. Therefore, rather than living this year in constant turmoil, try to remain out of the public eye. Do not attempt to gain more power. (For now, remove political office from your aspirations. Forget about asking for a raise or bidding for that promotion.) If you are too conspicuous and/or acquisitive in a Horse year, you might face both financial and emotional ruin. The Horse dislikes being told what to do, and you enjoy being in charge. As you can see, this year portends disruptive chaos—unless, of course, you wisely choose to avoid the spotlight. Since you will not be parading or appearing in public very much, why not plan to undergo the cosmetic surgery you have been postponing during this Horse year? The following year promises to bring you back into public view, so you might as well do everything you can now to enhance your appearance, refresh your wardrobe, and transform that outdated hairstyle into a more contemporary look."},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Yin Fire",prediction:"In the Goat year, you will find yourself navigating calmer waters. You have experienced a couple of challenging seasons recently, which may have inhibited your style and dulled your creativity. However, this year promises to alleviate all the stress associated with economic slowdown for Rats. Money will cease to be the most critical concern. By June, you will feel more inclined to socialize and showcase your sparkling social skills, attending parties and public events where your innate charm is greatly appreciated. Of course, as soon as you put yourself out there, someone attractive and lovable may become attached to you and be reluctant to let go. This new romantic interest could threaten an already stable marriage or long-term relationship. Be careful not to jeopardize the steady home life that you so desperately need. Be polite, but firm. Resist the intense desire for a quick, passionate summer romance. The Goat year favors your fortunes and offers you renewed peace of mind. Do not squander it. Towards the end of the year, seek financial advice from someone with more experience than you in the area you intend to invest in. Whether it is real estate or diamond mines, if you are new to it, heed the counsel of an older, wiser—and wealthier—associate."},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Yang Earth",prediction:"Here comes enjoyment! You and the Monkey consistently get along well. Monkeys are fond of surprises and excitement. They respond favorably to activity and appreciate action for its own sake. Monkeys are social creatures. However, unlike you Rats, Monkeys do not genuinely concern themselves with power. They are willing to take a supportive role, preferring to operate discreetly, solving problems and serving as the 'brains' behind an operation. Therefore, in Monkey years, you are free to assume leadership again. Pursue that board position. Run for public office. Endeavor to become the president of the world. Ask for authority, and you will most likely receive your wish. One quick word of caution: be prepared to flatter a family member who is decidedly not on your side. The individual in question may be only a distant cousin or a nephew by marriage, but they possess a jealous nature and will do everything in their power to hinder your progress. Since they are susceptible to admiration and praise, go ahead and lavish it upon them."},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Yin Earth",prediction:"Do not anticipate becoming wealthy this year. The Rooster is known for economizing during difficult times. Make the most of what you have; that is the Rooster's message for Rats. Avoid overspending. Catch yourself before you indulge in what appear, on the surface, to be 'bargains.' A bargain is only beneficial to the extent that it reduces your budget. And you will definitely need to budget in the Rooster year—or face consequences! The good news is that early in the year, you will be very close to falling in love. I cannot guarantee that this person will be the one with whom you will spend the remainder of your life. It may indeed be merely a 'teaching affair,' through which you learn to accept that certain independent aspects of a loved one's character will never align with your need to protect and 'possess' that person's complete attention. Do not let my advice impede your progress here. The love you invest in this relationship will be well spent, as the lessons you learn will be crucial and valuable for a long time to come."},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Yang Metal",prediction:"Financial worries will dissipate for Rats this year. You can now breathe more easily and even indulge in one or two lavish parties or luxurious vacations. However, do use your time wisely for a new endeavor. It may not be a business venture or directly related to increasing your own income. Instead, I foresee you becoming involved in some form of charitable pursuit, which might cost you a few thousand of your local currency's largest denominations. Proceed slowly. Do not immediately seize the first opportunity to assist starving populations or support underprivileged girls in a particular region you fancy visiting. Ensure that the charity in which you invest your good intentions and resources will utilize your money wisely and that those who need it most will benefit. Conduct thorough research before you donate. Sparks may fly in your romantic life in 2030. You tend to be inflexible on matters crucial to your mate's emotional well-being. Take everything he or she tells you more seriously than you have in the past. Be willing to discuss alternatives to the lifestyle you have previously been able to impose. Perhaps it is your lover's turn to make the decisions for a while."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Yin Metal",prediction:"This is a fortunate year for Rats. The Pig approves of you and encourages all your money-making and wealth-accumulating plans. However, you will need to be more cautious about health issues. You likely have some chronic condition—a persistent backache, palpitations, or intermittent nausea—that you have successfully ignored for quite some time now. This will be the year to resolve those symptoms. Seek a medical professional or accredited health practitioner before summer arrives. You will most likely be required to follow some new regimen: diet and exercise? A change of climate during allergy season? A new medication? Whatever it is, you must take it very seriously to prevent the condition from worsening and causing more severe problems later on. Your romantic situation will have improved—provided you were able to adopt a more flexible perspective regarding your significant other's needs."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Yang Water",prediction:"Relax, my little Rat friend. The Dragon and you are long-standing allies. You respect the flamboyant Dragon’s need for attention and never threaten to overshadow its brilliance. Your intelligent handling of Dragons is, in fact, legendary. You understand how to let it shine while quietly building your own empire in the background. The mood of the Dragon year is celebratory. These magnificent creatures enjoy hosting large gatherings for thousands at numerous festivals and events of all kinds. Any excuse for a grand commemoration is welcomed. It is the Dragon’s way—the more ceremonial the event, the more it enjoys watching people have fun. You do not mind playing the charming guest among the Dragon’s countless friends, all the while planning your own networking strategies. Play hard this year and make the most of opportunities while the Dragon’s brilliant sun is shining on your life. Enjoy this hectic but fortunate year; it is guaranteed to be one of your most memorable and best."},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Yin Water",prediction:"This period threatens to be a time of financial restraint for you Rats. Commercial activity tends to slow down in Snake years. You will not face bankruptcy, but your income may decrease sufficiently to cause you some restless nights. It would be wise to set aside some cash in a secure location. There is political instability and global unrest now, so prepare to hunker down and perhaps even take on new and different responsibilities. Your romantic life might cool somewhat during the months of June and July. This period of coolness is only temporary, so do not lose heart. Someone in your immediate circle will want to fabricate a damaging rumor, and your private life may very well be its subject. Certain individuals consider gossip harmless, but the fabricated story in question carries more weight than a mere fib; it has the potential to create scandal. Keep your awareness sharp during the initial months of the year to fend off any deception you sense is approaching. Additionally, be prepared to compromise where you might otherwise have refused to yield. Flexibility proves beneficial in Snake years."},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Yang Wood",prediction:"Rats and Horses typically argue—over everything from how money is spent to how to cultivate geraniums. Despite the Horse's peculiar attraction to you, as soon as you two begin a relationship, the conflict starts! Arguments can be constructive, but in the case of the Horse and Rat, continuous disagreements consume much of your valuable time and lead neither of you to a positive outcome. Therefore, rather than living this year in constant turmoil, try to remain out of the public eye. Do not attempt to gain more power. (For now, remove political office from your aspirations. Forget about asking for a raise or bidding for that promotion.) If you are too conspicuous and/or acquisitive in a Horse year, you might face both financial and emotional ruin. The Horse dislikes being told what to do, and you enjoy being in charge. As you can see, this year portends disruptive chaos—unless, of course, you wisely choose to avoid the spotlight. Since you will not be parading or appearing in public very much, why not plan to undergo the cosmetic surgery you have been postponing during this Horse year? The following year promises to bring you back into public view, so you might as well do everything you can now to enhance your appearance, refresh your wardrobe, and transform that outdated hairstyle into a more contemporary look."},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"In the Goat year, you will find yourself navigating calmer waters. You have experienced a couple of challenging seasons recently, which may have inhibited your style and dulled your creativity. However, this year promises to alleviate all the stress associated with economic slowdown for Rats. Money will cease to be the most critical concern. By June, you will feel more inclined to socialize and showcase your sparkling social skills, attending parties and public events where your innate charm is greatly appreciated. Of course, as soon as you put yourself out there, someone attractive and lovable may become attached to you and be reluctant to let go. This new romantic interest could threaten an already stable marriage or long-term relationship. Be careful not to jeopardize the steady home life that you so desperately need. Be polite, but firm. Resist the intense desire for a quick, passionate summer romance. The Goat year favors your fortunes and offers you renewed peace of mind. Do not squander it. Towards the end of the year, seek financial advice from someone with more experience than you in the area you intend to invest in. Whether it is real estate or diamond mines, if you are new to it, heed the counsel of an older, wiser—and wealthier—associate."},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"This is a fortunate year for Rats. The Pig approves of you and encourages all your money-making and wealth-accumulating plans. However, you will need to be more cautious about health issues. You likely have some chronic condition—a persistent backache, palpitations, or intermittent nausea—that you have successfully ignored for quite some time now. This will be the year to resolve those symptoms. Seek a medical professional or accredited health practitioner before summer arrives. You will most likely be required to follow some new regimen: diet and exercise? A change of climate during allergy season? A new medication? Whatever it is, you must take it very seriously to prevent the condition from worsening and causing more severe problems later on. Your romantic situation will have improved—provided you were able to adopt a more flexible perspective regarding your significant other's needs."}}},t={introduction:`Hail, Diligent Ox, a veritable Gibraltar. You are an indomitable fortress. This zodiac sign might have been named Bulldozer instead of Ox. You are an inherently temperate individual who deeply values rigor, hard work, strength of character, and, most importantly, tangible outcomes! You are capable of persisting at a task for longer and applying yourself more intensely than anyone else. You spare no effort. You detest being defeated, so you simply never surrender. Some may describe you as slow; others might complain that you are clumsy. In reality, you proceed at your own comfortable pace and refuse to be rushed or pressured by impulsive, fleeting individuals. You believe in simplicity and accomplishment. Lightheartedness in business matters exasperates you.
You are capable of profound, enduring love, yet romantic gestures leave you unaffected. You prefer practical action over sentimental displays like beds of roses and vials of exotic perfumes. You approach life with great seriousness, but life does not always reciprocate that favor. You typically do not speak much, but you possess a remarkable talent for storytelling. If you are truly aiming for results, utilize that distinctive flair. Engage in conversation with the conservative Rooster you have been wanting to invite to dinner. Share some pink sparkling wine with a talkative Rat, or send dozens of white roses to a luxury-loving Snake. They are all well-equipped to respond positively to your unique method of persuasion. The initial two phases of your life will be characterized by strenuous effort. During the second adult stage, a misunderstanding between you and a neighbor or colleague may lead to a profound, long-lasting disagreement. Do not lose hope. Your old age will be both lengthy and healthy, with peace of mind becoming your top priority after the age of fifty.
My advice? Yes. Lighten up. And cease judging others by your own elevated standards. You will only experience disappointment. Nobody (except you, my dear Ox) is flawless.`,elements:{Wood:`The Wood Ox is the most exceptionally hardworking among all Oxen. If you find that the Wood Ox is not engaged in working, studying, composing, or striving to lift a massive weight, you might reasonably assume he is no longer alive. However, even in death, the Wood Ox is not the kind of individual to quietly fade away, leaving behind pleasant memories of a romantic, lyrical spirit. When this person departs, all the water seems to drain from the swimming pool, leaving a colossal, resounding impression of their significant, creative, and impactful presence.
The Wood Ox is not universally regarded as a pleasant individual. On the contrary! He is what my mother used to describe as "a real piece of work," a relentless combatant against all forces he does not already command. In an effort to dominate, direct, achieve superiority, and emerge as the controlling factor in every undertaking, this fearless, cunning, brilliant, and persistent person allows no obstacle to deter him. His guiding principle is "Progress Gratia Progress"—advancement for its own sake—and if it means stepping over a few fallen individuals along the way, well, the Wood Ox simply says, "that's life."
I once knew a Wood Ox whose father traditionally made bricks in the French countryside but earned very little money. At eighteen, when my friend completed her schooling, she began working for her father in the office. She was convinced that her father was mismanaging everything, so she informed him of this. They argued. This Ox packed her belongings and left home. Four years later, her father fell ill. The brick business was in its usual precarious state. The Ox was called home to assist. While her father was unwell, the Ox went to the factory. She contacted a bank or two, secured capital, purchased cement-block manufacturing equipment, installed it, reassigned the old brick salesmen to sell the blocks to builders, and began accumulating a fortune in profits. When a few former customers inquired about old-style bricks, the Ox informed them that her father's company no longer produced bricks and that all the best builders had transitioned to cement blocks. When her father, who was not yet sixty-five, recovered, he returned to work. But the Ox had moved into his office, relocating him to a freshly painted anteroom. "Papa," the Ox informed him, "you can relax. Sit back. You only need to assist me now." She had effectively retired her father from his own business! And she boasts about it. It is the first in the Ox's collection of "See How Wonderful I Am" narratives.
The Ox's father passed away—I suspect from a broken heart, but the Ox does not interpret it that way. "My father lacked resilience. He used to take time off to work in his garden. Sometimes, he would even go fishing. I had to rescue his business. Just to demonstrate how truly weak he was after I semi-retired him, he fell into a deep depression. He died before the next Christmas." I find this story shocking. But for the Wood-born Ox, whose constitution is as robust as its resolve, it is either its way or no way. There are no clever solutions other than its own. No one else works as diligently as it does, so no one deserves as much. It takes everything, claims it as its own, and then lends it back to its rightful owners.
Wood Oxen are formidable individuals. However, despite their expertise in the art of dominance, they can be remarkably generous. The Wood Ox cherishes nature, children, and family, and reveres those who know how to cultivate nature in return for its abundant gifts. Whether they are farmers, doctors, artists, or householders, Wood Oxen will always assist those they believe are doing a 'good job,' exerting all their strength and achieving success.
One intriguing benefit of befriending Wood Oxen is that they are often incredibly witty, perceiving life satirically and communicating their ironic perspective. Although they may engage in much romantic small talk in bed and are utterly inept at candle-lit dinners, Wood Oxen possess sublime eloquence. When they utilize this gift to enhance their presence or to expand their business, no one communicates more effectively. Wood Oxen always know how to select the perfect phrase to convey the pain, the humor, or the sensation they experienced. If you are fortunate enough to persuade one of these taciturn individuals to tell you a story, you are in for a delightful experience.
Wood Oxen are frequently unaware that many people dislike them. They disregard the feelings of those they do not favor. You will never hear one of these resolute individuals express regret about divorcing their spouse, quitting their boss, or moving far away from their aging mother. Wood Oxen simply believe they should proceed. If they do not cultivate many heartfelt friendships and must endure numerous adversaries, it does not concern them. If friendship requires them to concede even an inch of progress, they will abandon the friend for the sake of advancement.
Although teamwork is hardly its forte, the Wood Ox enjoys being married and raising a family. However, at best, being the wife or husband, child, or even sibling of this character is challenging. A Wood Ox can only be managed by someone weaker than itself. Do not challenge what it says with a retort or a taunt. Never disagree with it. Do not respond when it orders you to bring coffee, make love, or walk the dog. Only your passive inertia can provoke even a slight reaction in this excessively self-important person's impenetrable ego. It possesses so much willpower that it is baffled by a lack of resolve in others. To irritate this individual, act as though you agree with everything it does and says. Play obedient-pet games, complete with whimpering if necessary—but continue doing exactly as you please. Provided that, in this outwardly subservient manner, you keep your intentions hidden, the Wood Ox is guaranteed to become your devoted servant.`,Fire:`The most agreeable way to begin a description of the intricate Fire Ox is to caution you that Fire influences the Ox in precisely the same manner it affects dynamite, jet planes, and helium-filled airships. Where there is already an abundance of latent power, the Fire element leads to excess and, at times, even to catastrophe. Unlike other Oxen, the Fire Ox is impatient. Like them, it desires to advance and reach destinations, but it struggles more with adopting a long-term perspective. Oxen do not often risk making fools of themselves. Most are natural planners. They prefer to observe developments from a safe distance before entering the fray. However, the Fire Ox's long-term view is inverted; it acts impulsively before considering the consequences.
Like most Oxen, this one assumes it is inherently superior. Do not give it a second thought. The Fire Ox is inherently better and more deserving of success, money, and whatever else it perceives, desires, and acquires. To the appealing Oxen's blend of self-assurance and strength of will, this creature adds an endearing new characteristic: moral self-righteousness. Fire Oxen fear nothing—not even ridicule—and will forge ahead, brandishing slogans as if bound to their moral exhortations, proselytizing speeches, and "enlightened" schemes until death separates them. This can be terribly tedious. It can even be self-destructive. But Fire Oxen will persist, waving their fiery ideals, displaying their moral indignation openly, and often losing the respect they are due from their peers. The inverse of this apparent disadvantage is that the Fire Ox is often a genius, remarkably successful, and frequently accurate in selecting its objectives. Warren Beatty, Robert Redford, Jack Nicholson, Bill Cosby, and Dustin Hoffman have all been exceedingly outspoken in public, pushed the limits of their talents in many unconventional areas of show business, and have all emerged with an excellent reputation.
The Ox's inherent strength, when combined with Fire's dynamism and vigor, can indeed create an exceptionally effective human being. Furthermore, work is never an issue; this person possesses extraordinary powers of endurance. Because it is fortunate enough to believe so fervently that it is always correct, it can appear inconsiderate and overbearing. Its justification? It is idealistic and a true champion for its cause. Any self-respecting Fire Ox will defend its beliefs against all odds. This irritating trait often leads the Fire Ox to triumph.
It is frequently bolder than it is intelligent, more willful than it is attuned to what is truly happening. For this Ox, the battle is the most satisfying part of the conflict. It also desires some applause, but it is not truly seeking one grand achievement or a lifelong victory that would allow it to settle down and raise a family. The Fire Ox is often engaged in conflict and is more than willing to defend its ideals indefinitely.
Sadly, this stubborn individual is more often respected than loved. It lacks subtlety and does not always know the best way to relate to others. It is also ruthless. It may glorify everything associated with tradition until it no longer serves its purpose. Then it may well glorify something new and label it traditional.
I suppose the best way to interact with this unyielding, appealingly active person is to begin by being strong-minded—at least a Tiger, or a Dragon, a philosophical Snake, or an utterly indifferent Rooster. To impress it, demonstrate your strength upfront. Occasionally, startle your Fire Ox by showing it a different perspective. This will not cure its shortsightedness, but it might sufficiently jolt its ego to give it a hint about how far off the mark it truly is. Otherwise, to capture its attention, try tickling the soles of its feet. It is certain to pretend to dislike that. But ultimately, only pure silliness and sweet, innocent (yet powerful) love can subdue the explosive Fire Oxen and encourage it to stop taking itself so excessively seriously.
The Fire Ox can be a family-oriented person. If it chooses to have children, it is deeply responsible and committed to the well-being of its spouse and offspring. It will also govern their domain and refuses to tolerate any back talk or criticism. It can be kind and makes a generous parent. It may not be very receptive to children who complain or share their troubles—emotions are not its strong suit. But if anyone were to attack a member of its family—even its good-for-nothing brother-in-law who cannot find a decent job and drinks too much—the Fire Ox will rise up and protect its own.`,Earth:`The Earth Ox is the intrusive Ox. It is excessively curious, meddlesome, and interfering. It believes it knows best, and often it does. Generally, Oxen consider themselves somewhat superior to other people. Earth Oxen not only think they are better; they are convinced they were born to guide others, to instruct those less fortunate on how to live, and to command them. What we have here is a highly nature-oriented, grounded, power-obsessed megalomaniac whose ability to detect flaws in life's various situations is practically unerring.
You will rarely encounter a more self-assured person. This Ox is not only self-reliant—it is convinced that you are not. Ask the Earth Ox a foolish question, and you will receive a profound sigh of impatience in return. "How can you be so obtuse?" it might groan. "I already informed you that the mouse controls the arrow on the screen. Are you too unintelligent to learn how to operate a computer?" Do not let this condescending attitude deter you. Ox groans signify very little. All that tut-tutting and complaining is merely a defensive mechanism, a method of humiliation designed to keep you off balance so that you do not notice it has gained too much weight or dyed its hair green. I am not attempting to excuse this Ox's tyrannical teaching methods, but its behavior is often so offensively pushy that it requires considerable patience and much tolerance.
Earth Oxen firmly believe that the true objective in life is to achieve perfection in every area. They do not flinch at the prospect of intense hard work. They are perpetually organized and cannot tolerate excessive spontaneity. The Earth Ox is not the life and soul of the party. It leads. It is never truly an integral part of the group.
But it is brave. And it is bold. Audacity is its defining characteristic. Consider it—Earth and Ox combined equal a bulldozer. This individual will relentlessly advance, like a caterpillar-tractor, over any number of obstacles to enter any board meeting, cabinet meeting, or bedroom it feels it should be permitted to enter without knocking. As long as it needs something and desires it, it considers it its own.
Now, such a seize-and-take approach may seem horrifyingly ruthless to you, but the Earth Ox behaves as it does because (believe it or not) it is insecure! Yes. Insecurity is the root cause of all bullying on earth, and Earth Ox bullies are no exception. This person secretly suffers from a fear of being unloved, rejected, and abandoned. It is never certain of its best friend or even its best romantic partner. It is well aware that it is clumsy and lacks skill in appreciating subtleties. So... to protect its own tender feelings, it employs aggressive tactics to preempt any potential aggression from others.
We must forgive it. It genuinely does not know any better. Even the most successful Earth Ox is somewhat awkward, an unsophisticated individual in refined attire, who wishes it had never become so prominent as to be compelled to socialize with all these splendid people who only make it feel more like a country bumpkin. What the Earth Ox intended to do when it decided to take over the world was to lead the populace. But it did not anticipate that they would ask it to learn to drink champagne, engage in small talk, or dance the Tango.
Consider this. If you awakened one day and faced the responsibility of guiding the world, it might be less than easy to maintain your composure. Since the Earth Ox was born with this certainty of leadership and is fundamentally a sincere person, when it undertakes the immense task of shepherding the world, it desires everything to proceed smoothly. After all, the outcome of all human endeavor rests with it. If things go well, it feels it is performing its job correctly, and then it can afford to be in a good mood. If the operations become stalled (which they invariably do), this poor, overly responsible creature believes it is entirely its fault.
Does it become depressed and sulk? Will it explode and overturn tables and chairs? Or might it resort to alcohol or drugs? No. The domineering Earth Ox who observes that its subjects have flagrantly disregarded its rules abandons the leader role and opts for dictator. It is convinced that because it defines the boundaries, it need not hesitate to overstep them—constantly.
One way to help this excessively bold person feel more comfortable in their own skin would be to show them how to curb their ego-driven exploits. But to do this, you would have to persuade them to accept advice, and they despise advice. They know everything, so why waste time heeding other people's chatter? The one sure path to its heart is through its stomach. This person enjoys eating. Drown it in rich, country-style soups. Lure her away from her chores with a plateful of lobster delicacies. Then play a thirty-minute CD recording of applause—the Earth Ox's preferred lullaby.
To the Earth Ox, sex is a physical act. Romance may be charming, but it is not their method of communication. The Earth Ox engages in sex; it does not "make love." Do not expect an Earth Ox lover to confess intricate fantasies or devise elaborate scenarios to awaken your diminished desire in the bedroom. When you go on picnics with Earth Oxen, leave your poetry books at home. A good hearty meal, a glass of wine, and a little physical intimacy will suffice for them.
Finally, although the Earth Ox is a meticulous rule-maker and a disciplined self-starter, it is often literary or artistic in some specialized field. It always finishes what it begins and can be relied upon for promptness and trusted for its fundamental honesty. However, its blindness to its own fallibility may lead it to commit some dreadful errors, and as profound guilt and denial follow, it may lose confidence and become impossibly defensive. If by the age of forty, it does not become more flexible, the Earth Ox can expect to live out a bitter old age, rigid and unyielding, forever lacking a sense of humor about its own flaws.`,Metal:`The Metal Ox is the most socially skilled Ox. It possesses charisma; there is a magical quality about Metal Oxen. An aura or halo surrounds their spirit, and it radiates. People are automatically drawn to the Metal Ox's warm public demeanor. The charm that emanates from it is natural, unpretentious—and captivating. In true Ox fashion, it harbors great personal ambition, desires to achieve success in its chosen fields, and sees no reason why it should not become the best in its profession. Consider a few of the 1901 Ox individuals, for example: Walt Disney was talented, but there were many animators in Hollywood at that time. If he had not possessed the crisp, resolute drive and determination of a Metal Ox, he probably would not have created the colossal industry that bears his name today. Or Andre Malraux—a giant of intellect. Had he been born a Dog or a Pig, he might have been content to write poetry and teach at university. Instead, he became a global traveler, art critic, cultural minister of France, public figure, and a creator of strict laws regarding the preservation of France's artistic heritage. Or take Eddie Murphy, born in 1961: He was already working on TV as a teenager, writing his own hilarious scripts and performing them in nightclubs. By the age of twenty-two, he was a star. Now he is a wealthy and famous man who can select which roles he desires in movies.
This person is not your typical stay-at-home, pipe-and-slippers, beer-and-peanuts individual. Metal Oxen do not usually languish, waiting for Godot or the Tooth Fairy to assure them they are loved. If you are the partner of a Metal Ox, remember that you are expected to be not only faithful, loyal, and true, but also dutiful, cheerful, and energetic. We already know that the Metal Ox strives hard to reach the pinnacle, but because not every day brings sufficient triumph, it will become frustrated and often return home in a foul mood. During these times, it is unreachable, lost in a haze of gloom, sulking.
As far as the Metal Ox is concerned, it is your duty (or at least its family's responsibility) either to help it emerge from this state or to remove yourself from the situation. You can argue, and it will argue back. You can shout, and it will do likewise. You can even reason, and it will engage you in a debate. But your Metal Ox will not accept criticism gracefully. It cannot tolerate reassessment of its methods or approach by anyone other than itself. It refuses to consider another's point of view. Even if it admires it, it cannot accept being wrong. Its pride obstructs its rational thought.
The Metal Ox's refusal of external interference reveals another unfortunate aspect of this charming person's stubborn character. Metal Oxen tend to distrust the judgment of those closest to them in favor of that of a complete stranger—a hazardous attitude, as strangers may attempt to deceive it.
This Ox is also stubbornly patriotic. It firmly believes that might makes right and becomes more conservative with age. It is neurotically nostalgic: in the past, it believes, the world functioned smoothly. It yearns for things to be right again, for people to be straightforward, for rain to fall only at night. A Disneyland-like world of obedient children and pleasant music, without the presence of villains, is the Metal Ox's ideal dream-world.
Since life does not often unfold in that manner, the Metal Ox is frequently in a state of semi-despair, complaining and grumbling, and assuming that everything, from today's lazy youth to hippies or hooligans or the breakdown of dress codes in banking institutions, is to blame. It finds fault with everyone except its own family. Never criticize its work, its person, or its family. Only it is permitted to dissect them—at home, behind closed doors. For public display, Mr. and Mrs. Metal Ox and all the little Metal Oxen must appear to be exemplary citizens.
The artistic side of the Metal Ox is its greatest redeeming quality. Its true contributions come through its creative endeavors, which are always imaginative and well-intentioned. If the Metal Ox's at-home personality were as sweet and fun-loving as its skillful, lyrical creations, it would not be perceived as such a gloomy individual by its family and close friends.
The Metal Ox is an exceptionally serious individual whose amiable public persona belies the stern, grumpy one who blusters on the front porch. It is as challenging to live with as it is critical of almost everything and everyone it is close to. Its sense of humor may be sharp on life's grand stage, but its ability to laugh at itself is nonexistent. It is intuitive and will listen to your problems and offer advice, but if you do not follow its suggestions, it will take offense. The Metal Ox is dependable and extraordinarily hardworking. It is an excellent provider and will always ensure its loved ones have a roof over their heads. If you possess abundant, easy-going patience, consider a relationship with a Metal Ox. If you struggle to accept criticism, steer clear of it and find yourself a gentler companion.`,Water:`Water (believe it or not) imbues the Ox with an additional measure of profoundness. This individual is a thoughtful, planning, plotting, and steady worker who consistently adopts a long-term perspective. A robust rice-paddy water buffalo, symbolizing fertility and patience, service and strength, offers a true depiction of this kind, yet stern and unwavering soul.
If it can help it, no Water Ox ever resorts to begging for a living. It is clever and hardworking, and will eventually dominate and thrive in every professional undertaking. It is strong and persistent, accomplishing tasks in a deliberate manner that suits its measured temperament. Water Oxen make little noise and demand little attention. They always advance, slowly. They begin a task and labor at it with regularity and certainty. They do not require modern methods or technological marvels to achieve success. Water Oxen are born knowing how to triumph.
No one should obstruct a Water Ox. Because they are patient, they are slow to react. Instead of confronting their adversaries directly, they simmer for a long while, quietly going about their business, saying nothing, and waiting to observe how situations unfold. Then, just as they are about to reach their boiling point, they accelerate and strike! They put an end to their rage by annihilating the enemy.
Water Oxen are not content with short-term solutions. For them, if something is worth doing, it merits being thoroughly considered, reflected upon, and deliberated until all aspects have been examined under a microscope—no hasty risk-taking here. They have all the time in the world to ponder while awaiting some impulsive individual to make a tactical error.
The Water Ox is most content in the countryside. Deep down, it is a farmer (usually a prosperous one), and it is also a leader. It will champion the causes of less fortunate farmers or conduct the Rotary Club orchestra. The Water Ox is not lazy, but as its pace is unhurried, it can be perceived as lethargic. From an outsider's perspective, the Water Ox never appears very busy. It does not rush about trying to accomplish sixty things at once, nor does it passively allow life to control it. It learned this at birth: steady perseverance wins the race.
Outwardly, the Water Ox is never frantic or pressured, yet it often achieves significantly more than those who rush ahead and overlook hundreds of daily activities. The Water Ox enjoys routine, reveres punctuality, and takes pleasure in doing things as they "should" be done. It desires to wake up and retire to bed at the same hour every day. It feels secure knowing that lunch is at noon and dinner at eight.
The Water Ox is profoundly family-oriented. It cannot live without its relatives surrounding it. It is possessive and jealous of their affections and always wishes them to conform as it does. The Water Ox is the type of parent who has five children and assigns each a profession at birth: Charlie will be a lawyer, Arielle a doctor, and so on. No arguments, no substitutions.
The unwavering resolve of the Water Ox should be bottled and marketed to indecisive individuals. Add to that a clear understanding of reality. It comprehends the pitfalls of human interaction so well that, if it desired, it could be president of the universe. But this rustic individual wants no part in politics. It feels awkward at sophisticated parties and is inhibited in small talk. It is happiest when comfortably settled in its solid stone house, in its cozy living room, surrounded by old friends and family. Traditional feasts elevate its appreciation for ritual. It loves to cook and eat the food it grows, preserves, and prepares with loving care. It is a country person with the financial success of a bank president.
The Water Ox is a loving, sensitive soul and will gladly listen to and empathize with other people's troubles. It will take time to contemplate a complex situation and will provide a thoughtful response. Neither egotistical nor self-centered, it does, however, prefer things to be managed its way. It is generous to those it loves, always giving them the benefit of the doubt and a helping hand when they are in difficulty.
It is, however, rare for a Water Ox to retract an opinion. It is stubborn and uncompromising, firmly believing that it possesses the sole truth. It never openly questions its own methods or asks, "Am I doing the right thing?" But it is secretly sentimental and can be swayed through its emotions. The Water Ox finds affection irresistible. Finally, Water bestows a substantial dose of vengefulness upon this unsophisticated individual. Anyone who betrays or wrongs a Water Ox will regret the day they did. The Water Ox could teach an elephant lessons in remembering every detail of pain ever inflicted upon it. Water Oxen wait, think, ruminate, conspire, plot, and can even kill. Stay clear of their resentment.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"Union between these two signs guarantees matrimonial stability. The Ox provides the energetic Rat with the grounding it lacks, and the Rat subtly influences the Ox's conventionality and resistance to change, enlivening what could otherwise be a dull, plodding existence. This combination fits well, with each partner complementing the other's sharper characteristics. The Ox's steadfastness offers the Rat the kind of security it requires. The devoted Ox will willingly assume the role of provider, which allows the Rat to act as the family protector. The sociable Rat enjoys hosting parties and attending social functions. This arrangement is ideal for the quiet Ox, who, without the Rat's exuberant nature, would simply remain at home contemplating. Each partner is content to fulfill their respective role. Alluring and meticulous, a Rat serves as a perfect assistant for an Ox in business, going to great lengths to encourage the Ox’s career. Of course, the Ox demands complete fidelity. Despite an occasional nagging desire to stray, the Rat will largely remain faithful. What about passion? Neither the Rat nor the Ox is excessively concerned with the whimsical idea of extravagant lovemaking practices. Their sex life will be lusty, though routine.",Ox:"The combined strength of a double-Ox marriage could cultivate forty acres before breakfast. Being dutiful and methodical, they mutually protect and provide for each other. Their household will be blessed with a rare harmony, so perfectly balanced that any external influence might disrupt its equilibrium. Anticipate a certain healthy predictability. In their organized kitchen, this couple meticulously plans to uphold their shared need for order. Despite their fundamental agreement, this strong-willed pair sometimes struggles with sharing authority. Oxen prefer to dominate, and each expects the other to obey. Depending on their Western signs, planetary influences, and other factors, they can likely resolve their differences amicably. Ox couples are mutually stubborn and will not be inclined to disclose minor disagreements—not even to each other. Rather than expressing dissatisfaction, Oxen will deny their differences, maintain an appearance of marital bliss, and suffer silently, diligently persevering, accepting the heavy burdens they perceive they must bear. Stasis becomes them. Their wholesome lovemaking brings consistent sexual fulfillment to this marriage. Passionate exuberance and emotional outbursts are unfamiliar to the Ox. Their sex life will be healthy, but it probably will not awaken the children. With both partners diligently working, an Ox-filled home will not lack financial security. Ample money will be earned but rarely spent foolishly. The Ox permits no frivolous expenditures.",Tiger:"This pairing is disastrous. No matter how you analyze it, this combination is destined for a tumultuous journey. Both possess an unyielding will, supported by the capacity to exert it. Equally self-possessed and determined, the stubborn Ox and the temperamental Tiger are better known as adversaries than as collaborators. Frankly, this quarrelsome duo is best suited for entanglement within a boxing ring. Often, the Tiger disrupts the Ox's tranquil day by instigating trouble. The stoical Ox desires only to remain close to home and continue its steady work. It must exercise considerable patience with the boisterous Tiger, and the Ox finds that exhausting. The rebellious Tiger roars off to a trade union demonstration, complaining bitterly about the mundane, dreary Ox, while the Ox intimidates the Tiger, accusing it of everything from incurable restlessness to outright insanity. If a third round of conflict occurs in the bedroom, there is hope for reconciliation. The Tiger's raw sensuality melts the Ox's icy resistance. With the Tiger, the inhibited Ox feels liberated. Twenty-four-hour truces may result. Even so, this union is best suited for friendship or a business partnership, where dual strong wills can achieve genuine progress. The Tiger/Ox emotional match is a constant struggle. It is not romantically promising.",Rabbit:"This is a cozy pairing. Nestled against a rock-solid Ox, the Cat will have plenty to purr about. The Ox provides the anxious Cat with security, allowing the Cat to dedicate time to creative activities without having to worry about finances. In return, the Cat, naturally endowed with refinement, provides its more unrefined counterpart with much-needed sophistication. The Ox's bossiness is easily managed by a Cat, who typically chooses to avoid conflict. Quiet and submissive, the Cat is content to take a secondary role and allow the Bull to assert dominance, feeling secure in the presence of a strong, forceful mate. To show gratitude, the Cat showers the Ox with affection. Of course, the self-sacrificing Ox finds excessive displays of affection difficult to tolerate and may avoid gestures of tenderness or mock them. This attitude could prove frustrating for the affectionate Cat, who adores cuddling. With luck, in time, its feline companion will melt the Ox's icy resistance and perhaps even teach it a romantic trick or two.",Dragon:"Be prepared for frequent late-night disagreements in an Ox/Dragon combination. Both individuals believe they are more correct than anyone else. The Dragon attempts to impose its will over the opinionated Ox, and the Bull retaliates with its own assertiveness. The Ox has little patience for vanity. The Ox's indifference to the Dragon's fiery appearance is a constant source of disappointment for the Dragon's ego. The glamorous, extravagant Dragon loves to spend money, but with the Ox meticulously counting pennies, it feels constrained and uneasy. The Dragon's tendency to flirt unsettles the faithful Ox, who rarely strays from a good sexual union—it simply does not have the time, being too busy working. With so much conflict, how can this duo reconcile? Their mutual love of home and family could rescue them from complete despair. Both enjoy sexual intimacy, although the Ox's routine techniques may bore the Dragon, whose sentimental nature yearns for fluffy clouds of pink cotton candy to enhance lovemaking. It will not often experience fireworks with the Ox. Furthermore, the methodical Ox expects a regular daily schedule. The Dragon, however, prefers a more unpredictable timetable, such as intense, stormy sexual encounters for a week followed by three weeks of peace and quiet. While an excellent business partnership, this union is not recommended for either marriage or romance—unless the Dragon is free to roam and seek excitement elsewhere.",Snake:"A nimble Snake entwines itself around an Ox's yoke and accompanies it on its journey. The Ox welcomes its agile passenger and steadily progresses through life with contentment. A Snake feels comfortable in the Ox's presence. Yet, the fickle Snake possesses an appetite for new experiences—especially those yet unexplored. Oxen are devoutly monogamous. Deep down, of course, the Snake is devoted to the Ox, whose stability is crucially important for the Snake's survival. If the Ox can learn to curb its suspicious nature and control a jealous temper, this creature can retain an appealing Snake partner better than anyone else. After all, the Ox possesses all the money, power, and patience, and Snakes adore all those qualities. Should the Ox begin to worry over failed ventures or depleted reserves, the Snake must subtly lead it to bed. The Ox is happy to comply with lusty quantity, but to prevent the reptile's attention from wandering, it must develop more imaginative foreplay. This union can be a good one if the Ox can remain courageous and undaunted by a challenging (yet fascinating) Snake mate.",Horse:"This pairing is exhausting! These two get along so poorly that the effort expended in trying is hardly worth the outcome. What a struggle! The conventional Ox desires to tame the wild, independent Horse, whose sole impulse is to gallop far away from an authoritarian Ox partner. Horses prefer to make their own decisions and detest meddlesome suggestions. The stubborn Ox incessantly dictates and advises. If the Ox interferes too strongly with the Horse's single-mindedness, the arrogant Horse will seize every opportunity to humiliate the unsuspecting Ox—in public! The best aspect of this marriage is the work ethic; it is exceptionally high. Both partners will labor and carry burdens without complaint. That is the positive side. But the Horse simply will not conform to the Ox's ways. It drives the Ox to distraction with wildly imaginative ideas, such as painting the house pink, getting married in black pajamas, or taking home a STOP sign from in front of the police station. The Ox fumes and sulks. The Horse merely laughs, convinced it is married to a dullard. Sexually, this strong-willed combination will already be dissatisfied on their honeymoon. The Horse, like a wild bronco unleashed in a corral, utterly overwhelms the Ox's reserve. The slow-paced Ox is still in a state of undress when the Horse is already intensely engaged. No harmony will characterize this union.",Goat:"In the beginning, the delicate Goat appears to be a great catch for a domineering Ox. But one must never judge a Goat by appearances! Although gentle, Goats are not easily controlled. I caution all Oxen against this union. Initially, you will feel a surge of power alongside this dainty mountain creature. But after several shared excursions, your inflated ego will deflate like a tired soufflé. The Goat complains incessantly, and you (slowly but surely) lose interest. The patient Ox tolerates the Goat's lackadaisical attitude for a while, but soon comes to believe that the Goat is not only lazy but also without direction. A hardworking Ox simply cannot comprehend the Goat's inertia. Content to be dependent on others, the Goat simply does not feel the need to work itself to exhaustion. Does not the dedicated Bull provide more than enough for the household? After a while, as the Ox is so docile and responsible, the Goat finds it simply tedious. The Goat enjoys sleeping on different sides of the bed every night for amusement, which exasperates the rigid Ox, who cannot bear the thought of breaking routine. Even in bed, the unadventurous Ox struggles to keep up with all the different Goat positions. This is an awkward couple. Each would be better off without the other.",Monkey:"If the Ox can abandon stubborn conformity and trust its beloved Monkey, the Monkey can significantly enhance the quality of the Ox's life. In return for the Monkey's gift of freedom, the Ox will provide security to its Monkey mate. Much to everyone’s surprise, the Ox, typically angered by any disruption of routine, is captivated by the clever Monkey. The Monkey, in turn, strives harder to entertain and enchant its faithful mate. Both are fundamentally practical and goal-oriented. Moreover, Monkeys can teach Oxen to look beyond themselves, to be genuinely kind to others, and to assist the less fortunate. Charity brings a special thrill to the Ox. It is grateful to the Monkey for opening its eyes to the needs of the impoverished. In the bedroom, expect the imaginative Monkey to invigorate the Ox's predictable technique. With the Monkey's agile guidance, the Ox can anticipate learning far more than a few new moves. It may even learn how to soar!",Rooster:"Should you be fortunate enough to have found each other, remain together. People consistently notice an Ox/Rooster couple. 'Look how content they are!' they remark. Astrologers in China recommend this as one of the most favorable unions ever! Together, your lives will be enriched by a blend of effortless sociability and unwavering security. Individually, the Ox and the Rooster can be equally meticulous, anxious, and perfectionistic. One might expect this pairing to come together and then self-destruct. But, for some reason, they discover peace. This traditional couple lives strictly by the rules. The Ox performs everything correctly, and the Rooster follows suit. They purchase their first home at the appropriate stage of life, have children when expected, and retire to their beautiful country residence when they become wealthy—which often happens very quickly. Both are keen, capable workers. They are not particularly fond of social outings, preferring to remain close to home. Children will be more than welcome here. This stable pair provides great security for a family. Not known for passion or recklessness, their sexual intimacy reflects their practical lifestyle. No embellishments, just basic, normal lovemaking. Two naturally harmonious signs should ensure this happy marriage is long-lived and successful.",Dog:"Do not expect the loyal Dog to howl at the moon out of blind devotion for an Ox mate. They have conflicting objectives. The Dog’s mission—advocating for the homeless in Alaska—is bound to take precedence. And the Ox? It will be championing a major corporation and earning fifty percent of the profits. These two are so divergent in their philosophies that minor disputes create deep rifts in their living room carpet. Despite a gentle, loving nature, a youthful Dog, blessed with clarity, understands that this is a fiercely competitive world, yet believes only in justice and equality. The Dog wants no part of the Ox’s arrogant dominance and responds solely to the call of the afflicted. The Ox believes that charity begins at home and will implore the Dog to disregard the world’s problems. Both are fervent moralizers, but they do not see eye to eye: the Dog argues about starving children in India, attempting to persuade the Ox to contribute to the noble cause; the Ox fights for justice at home, complaining that the money used to establish a shelter for the homeless last month was actually intended to pay for the children’s private school. Sexual intimacy between them can be enjoyable! This is the only area where an Ox's command to 'roll over' holds sway. The Dog is amused by and admires the Ox’s relentlessness and brutally frank style in bed. This is merely an acceptable marriage. No sexual fireworks or undying passion will keep these two very different people together.",Pig:"Indeed, these two get along famously. The good-natured Pig is so adaptable that the Ox will eventually believe it truly is in charge. Let’s imagine that atop a beautiful hill in the mountains of some exquisite location, the Ox and the Pig own a home. This home is so meticulously cared for that it gleams. The Pig enjoys cooking and does not mind tidying up after dinner. Before bedtime, the careful Ox turns off all the lights and puts out the garbage and the cat. Then this affectionate pair settles into bed. It is ideal; they are well-matched. Early in the morning, they awaken to the sound of birds, which sets a harmonious tone for the day. Of course, the birds are fed daily by the disciplined Ox, who keeps this household running on a very strict schedule. But it is the Pig who purchases the birdseed. Pigs love animals, adore country life, and are lavishly generous. Sexual intimacy between these two country folk is lusty and fulfilling. The Ox is a bit conventional and unrefined at first, but the Pig’s rich sensuality soon takes over, and they enjoy creating a beautiful, leisurely lifetime of love."},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"You and the Snake get along like fraternal twins. You do not resemble each other at all, yet you are inseparable companions. Snakes consistently possess an attractive quality and are not afraid of assuming power. The Snake's style never interferes with yours. You proceed steadily, while Snakes move subtly. However, you are both rather deliberate and profound thinkers. Hence, your wavelengths align, and you truly appreciate each other. You each enjoy a quiet, yet steadfast presence. You will be granted all manner of successes this year. Accolades, awards, and honors will come your way because the Snake admires you Ox individuals, and the feeling is mutual. Consume more fiber, take vitamins, and learn to accept the benefits of alternative medicine. If you have children or have the opportunity to borrow or care for some, you will find that you enjoy their company most in this Snake year. You (deliberate Ox that you are) may even find you can have fun at the theme park. An Ox on a roller coaster is not a common sight, but in a Snake year, such a sight is entirely plausible."},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"Due to the general atmosphere of diligent labor that characterizes all Horse years, this year will be fortunate for Oxen. It is no secret: you Oxen love to work and work hard. You possess an exceptional capacity for exertion—both physical and mental. Work energizes you. Why? Because you live for results and are not particularly concerned with how you achieve those results—even if you have to struggle uphill with a thousand-pound boulder on your weary shoulders—reaching the destination is always worth the effort. So when Horse years arrive, you are favored, applauded, and praised for your unparalleled work ethic. When the Japanese enslaved Koreans in a darker period of their history, it was commonly said: 'We worked them like Horses and Oxen.' No one works harder than you two. So in this Horse year, you may be working extremely hard, but the results will be precisely what you sought because the Horse's influence protects and preserves the Ox. It may not prove to be the most joyful year of your life... but then, when you have rich and tangible rewards from your work, who needs fun?"},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Yin Fire",prediction:"Goats will irritate you. There is friction between you and the Goat because the Goat places more emphasis on the lighter side of life, desires to depend on a stronger being or institution, and is frequently not a self-starter. Goats may be geniuses, but they do not possess the kind of assertive presence and persistent spirit that you have. Goats often work in bursts—three or four sleepless nights at the computer followed by a week's rest is perfectly acceptable to them. Their perception of time is different. You, being determined, pre-programmed, and steady at the helm, cannot tolerate this erratic rhythm and alteration of schedules. You desire more stability in your daily life. So, in this Goat year, I suggest you retreat to the countryside. Purchase that château in the south of France, observe your grapes grow, harvest them, and transform them into wine; but do not attempt to compete for awards or honors. Avoid all contests. Enjoy your romantic life now. It can be a top priority because, in this frivolous Goat year, you will not need to spend all your time working. When you are not busy making love, why not plan your next business triumph? Next year, your Monkey friend will arrive. Monkeys allow Oxen to get away with a great deal."},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Yang Earth",prediction:"This year promises abundant activity and an acceleration of pace for you Oxen. I understand you do not enjoy rushing and dislike being told to move faster. But... Monkeys have no time to waste standing around impatiently while you Oxen contemplate and labor through mountains of what Monkeys consider useless details, paperwork, and administrative nonsense. Monkeys identify a problem, address its core, solve it, and move on to the next. So, you will have to abandon your spreadsheets, discard your precious bureaucracy, and learn to quicken your pace. And (because you are determined to advance no matter what) you will indeed accelerate. This hectic rhythm, however, may take a toll on your health. During this Monkey year, be sure to undergo regular checkups and tests for all potential ailments that can affect Oxen (especially digestion-related illnesses). The bottom line? You will thrive in a Monkey year because the Monkey is more astute than all of us and recognizes when it has found a sensible, reliable ally. That, my dear Ox friend, is you. This year will be fruitful, and you will not face sabotage or be denied much of anything. You will, however, need to pick up those heavy feet of yours and get moving."},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Yin Earth",prediction:"Rooster years are consistently beneficial for hardworking individuals, and you Oxen are no exception. However, as the recent Monkey year truly exhausted you and diminished your capacity for tolerating another's pace, you will tend to be reluctant to cooperate this year. Joint projects, group efforts, associations, and partnerships will suffer because you desire a year off from being an ally and companion to someone who is constantly frenetic. You simply wish to be your own person again and move at your own pleasant (slow) pace. For this year, then, I suggest you proceed independently. Continue working at whatever you enjoy and are confident will bring you success. But do not sign any contracts that oblige you to participate in meetings or agree to unpalatable clauses. You are simply not in the right frame of mind for joint ventures. Your romantic life suffered somewhat from the general turmoil of last year. Take some time to express affection and tenderness with your sweetheart or spouse this year. The Rooster enjoys your company and does not truly mind if you sneak away for a few romantic weekends. You always give your all when you return—and you are usually in a much better frame of mind as well. This sign is not called Rooster for nothing. Roosters appreciate the necessity of passion in the lives of their subjects. After all, isn't sexual prowess what Roosters are so famous for?"},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Yang Metal",prediction:"The Dog poses no threat to you Oxen. A Dog can bark, growl, and snarl at a steadfast Ox for as long and as loudly as it wishes, and you will simply stand there, silent and Ox-like, waiting for its tantrum to subside. However, wisdom dictates that in Dog years, the Ox should remain out of the public eye. Why? Because the criticisms and outcries against injustice and demands for fair play in government, for which the Dog is so renowned, do not appeal to you. And if you were to join in, you might draw unwanted attention. You are not the type to carry a placard in the street or shout slogans in front of government buildings to achieve your goals. You are a slow-burning individual who waits, observes, and acts only when certain of a positive outcome. You might be clumsy, but you are not foolish enough to be upfront about how you would change things. You would rather die than spend a night in jail for participating in a riot over healthcare. Instead, you slowly push that rock up the hill, marking all paths with your name, and then you overthrow the entire government by swiftly rolling that massive boulder from the mountaintop onto the offenders' heads. That is what I mean by maintaining a low profile."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Yin Metal",prediction:"Oxen typically thrive during the early part of Pig Years. This year will be no exception. You will undoubtedly find both adventure and abundant enjoyment in the initial months. However, around June, just before summer begins, you will need to monitor your budget more closely than you have been. Quite suddenly, it will seem as though your bank account has developed a leak. Do verify all banking and investment statements, as computers tend to make more errors in Pig years. Being overly generous to those they love, Oxen also frequently fall victim to oversight or miscalculation. The Pig and the Ox are generally complicit in their pursuit of affluence for its own sake. You are equally skilled at accumulating not only money but also precious possessions—art and antiques, or vintage cars and outrageously expensive wines and caviar. So, in a luxury-loving Pig year, you will be tempted to purchase major artworks or cases of rare Bordeaux or Champagne. This may be one clue as to why that bank account is losing funds. Another possibility is the presence of a loved one who is draining you of resources he or she has not earned. Consult with your accountant more frequently, count those pennies, and remain vigilant for deception originating from those closest to you."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Yang Water",prediction:"Rats do not often trouble Oxen. The Rat's hyperactive temperament and the Ox's deliberate pace do not align. Yet, the Rat deeply admires your strength. So, in a Rat year, you Oxen will not be bothered or hindered in your progress. Rats simply do not interfere with Oxen. They respect your tenacity and endurance, and they appreciate the security you provide. All this year, you will be able to work at your own relaxed, steady rhythm, and you can anticipate achieving excellent results. You will earn more money and be offered a promotion to a more influential position. However, I advise you to decline the promotion. A more prestigious position will only add to your workload. It will also require more responsibility and a greater degree of public interaction, which might be detrimental to your well-being. A quiet, diligent, solitary life is what the Ox requires and desires. Public life, with all its fanfare and ceremony, would only make you irritable. Why not just enjoy the peace and quiet of your own home, with all its order and tranquility, and simply take the additional salary that comes with the job offer? The company will be just as pleased, and your liver will thank you for it."},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Yin Water",prediction:"I must caution you against attempting to earn a significant amount of money or securing the prestigious job you desire in an Ox year. Why? It is not merely because the Ox does not wish for your success, but also because your rapid, opportunistic methods exasperate the Ox. As a long-term planner, the Ox becomes disoriented simply observing your quick acceleration and swift movements. Ox individuals possess great talent for leadership; they often become autocratic figures. However, they are not particularly quick on their feet, and they are even slower in their intellectual processing. Their minds operate in an unhurried fashion. Do they linger and adopt a leisurely approach to managing their year or their domain? Absolutely not. But they persevere steadily, and you act impulsively. Therefore, in an Ox year, it is advisable to preemptively temper your intensity so as not to appear threatening or to bewilder the deliberate, task-oriented Ox. You will not need to humble yourself to advance. However, you will need to agree with those in positions of authority. Since you detest being anyone's subordinate, you may experience digestive issues, migraines, and other stress-related ailments as a consequence. Maintain the well-being of your romantic life by making a special effort to perform loving acts of kindness and deference towards your beloved or spouse (or both) in this rather challenging, unaccommodating Ox year. You need all the approval and affection you can gather from those who cherish and admire your spirited demeanor."},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Yang Wood",prediction:"This year is your year. You are in charge. You must, therefore, be vigilant and ensure your subjects do not overthrow you. Do you recall that last year, you were able to spend your time peacefully managing your projects and were not subject to any sudden changes or unexpected events? Well, this year promises to be quite the opposite. The Tiger is an extremely volatile individual who enjoys a thrill a minute. You can handle the chaos, but you will not appreciate having to frequently revise your meticulously planned timetables. Tigers thrive on constant change, and you... well, you do not. I would like to be able to advise you to travel and avoid this hectic atmosphere. Unfortunately, the Tiger and the Ox are traditionally at odds. So, you must remain on guard. If you are not present and vigilant, your enemies will seize the opportunity to usurp your authority. Do not take risks. Do not change jobs or move to a new house. Do not buy a new car. Do not have a baby. Do not invest your money. The only advice I can offer you is: stay where you are, and do not make any significant moves."},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"You can anticipate significant success in the Cat/Rabbit year. In these years, individuals of your temperament are favored by the heavens. You may have experienced some challenging times in the past couple of years, but this year will bring you great joy and a multitude of rewarding experiences. You are a cautious individual who is not prone to making foolish mistakes in your work life or in your romantic entanglements. However, you tend to be overly strict in your judgments and do not easily accept the shortcomings of others. This year, if you can learn to be more tolerant and flexible, you will see a notable improvement in your interactions with others. Family members will show their gratitude with gifts and praise. It is likely that you will be offered a prestigious job that you have desired for a long time. Accept it! Your home life this year will be serene and peaceful. Any ongoing issues will dissipate by themselves. Even your physical health will be excellent. There is no need for you to undergo any plastic surgery or cosmetic procedures. The Cat/Rabbit is not concerned with appearance. Your natural dignity will suffice. So, you can relax. Everything is secure, your future is bright, and no one is attempting to undermine your authority. Enjoy it while you can. Next year promises to be a bit more challenging."},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"You will be highly irritated by the atmosphere of the Dragon year. You enjoy tranquility and do not like to feel that you are being observed or judged. Dragons, on the other hand, are the exact opposite; they require an audience and thrive on being the center of attention. They will never comprehend why a gifted individual such as yourself prefers to work quietly in the background without fanfare or applause. Consequently, there will be friction between you and those in power this year. Since you cannot avoid them, you will have to find a way to navigate their flamboyant events and celebrations without appearing to be the wet blanket that you undoubtedly are. You might consider purchasing an expensive new car or a significant work of art to boost your confidence and allow you to attend those dreaded dinner parties in style. Or you could marry a beautiful, intelligent person to enhance your public image. In short, this year you need to devise strategies to make yourself more socially acceptable and to tolerate the extravagance that you despise. Alternatively, you could adopt some eccentric behavior yourself. Take up tap dancing, try skydiving, or join a rock-and-roll band. Doing so will ensure you are no longer the one judging others for their eccentricities, but the one being judged."}}},o={introduction:`Honorable Tiger, noble and fearless, you are respected for your courage and simultaneously feared for your ferocity and persistent lack of moderation. Like a raging river, you constantly overflow your boundaries. Where are you rushing to with such haste? Can you not take just one tiny glance before you pounce? Try to slow down; practice a little restraint. Stop being so devastatingly attractive; it is exhausting.

Of course, some individuals find you so daring and spirited that they wish to join you and experience the adventure. But you, dear Tiger, are a daring solitary individual. The top is the only place you desire to be. You actively seek danger. The more formidable the adversary, the more dramatic and catastrophic the situation, the broader your Tigerish grin becomes. Your unpredictability, disregard for rules, self-sufficiency, and carefree swagger could ultimately be your downfall.

In matters of the heart, you are excessively demanding. However, you are certainly not dull. You get along best with devoted Dogs, independent Horses, and complicit Dragons also find loving you quite delightful. Monkeys admire you, but remember—Monkeys can be cunning. Whatever you do, do not become involved with a tempestuous Tiger like yourself; you are lucky, but not that fortunate.

You will navigate your youth with ease. But by the age of thirty-five, the excesses of half a lifetime may begin to catch up with you. Bring yourself to order by forty, and by the time you reach fifty, you will feel revitalized, prepared for a productive old age. A piece of advice? Go ahead and accept the position as a five-star general, but select your lieutenants wisely—you will require much loyal counsel.`,elements:{Wood:`Energetic and resilient, the Wood Tiger is a hyper-creative innovator who bounds around like a frenzied dervish, leaping unharmed in and out of monumental vats of scalding hot water. This Tiger lacks the cunning and stealth of more subtle Tigers. It is sociable, direct, and constantly yearns to undertake the most ambitious projects and publicly express its extraordinary views, both of the world and of itself!

There is a positive aspect to the Wood Tiger's impulsive behavior. With so many endeavors in progress simultaneously, it is perpetually busy juggling, planning, and strategizing. It is never bored. The Wood Tiger is delighted when its alarm rings in the morning, as it can almost anticipate the diverse possibilities for expansion and immediate involvement in new deals that each new day offers.

All Tigers enjoy change, but this one is addicted to it. The mere thought of purchasing a loaf of bread from a new shop or taking a different route to the hardware store sends shivers of anticipation down its striped spine. You will never find it philosophizing or languidly daydreaming. The Wood Tiger has an extremely difficult time sitting still. It is also amiable and quite easy to get along with, but it is proud and resents it when others attempt to direct or advise it.

This individual is not an intellectual, but it thinks brilliantly on its feet. It is impatient with lofty idealism and theoretical discussions. It prefers to get straight to the task at hand and complete it—the faster, the better.

It believes it can accomplish everything—and enjoys seeing it done well. Furthermore, it thinks you should not only follow it and believe in it, but to demonstrate your loyalty, you should not hesitate to invest your money in its ventures. The Wood Tiger is a world-beater but often feels frustrated because it cannot find allies as fearless as itself. Its perception of the world is highly personal, sometimes incisive, and often witty. Part of the charm of this magnetic Tiger lies in its never taking itself or anyone else very seriously.

The Wood Tiger's devil-may-care approach does not align with its earnest desire to find a life's work or a true vocation that genuinely suits it. It is constantly torn between settling down and rampaging about, activating its charm and dispensing unsolicited advice to its devoted admirers. The Wood Tiger cannot resist even the slightest hint of an opportunity to shine, to captivate, and to convince others that it is correct.

It is quick to anger and just as swift to calm down. It is a charming, fortunate person who can be taken anywhere at all levels of society without causing embarrassment. It loves all types of people and is tolerant and democratic in its choice of friends and partners, making it a wonderful addition to any social gathering. It always has many clever things to say and a multitude of obscure ideas to contribute to any conversation. The Wood Tiger is generous and will shower its loved ones with comforts. But it is also selfish and, in all human interactions, demands the role of Top Tiger.

What this Tiger requires is a strong, interesting, and stable mate who can hold its attention and compel it to focus diligently. If the home life of the Wood Tiger is sufficiently loving, cozy—and disciplined—it can achieve great things.

The best way to deal with this willful yet lovable, elusive individual is, regrettably, to manipulate it. Telling a Wood Tiger directly what you think of its grandiose delusions or criticizing its ill-conceived plans head-on may result in little more than a black eye or, at best, a wounded ego.

Flatter this daring character, and it will follow you anywhere—at least until something more enticing comes along.`,Fire:`The Fire Tiger is a charismatic, highly dramatic, and sensual leader. Fire imbues the vibrantly impressive Tiger with even more dynamism and vigor. It is as energetic, if not more so, than its Tiger siblings. However, its power often outpaces its good judgment. It is recklessly extravagant with its strengths and overdoes and over-achieves everything it undertakes. The Fire Tiger simply refuses to conserve its own vitality. It pushes, strains, and forces itself through the most challenging obstacles for the sake of its brave ideals, exhausting itself to give form to projects in which it believes almost too fervently.

Sleepless nights are the norm rather than the exception. Erratic dietary habits and excessive sexual escapades are the fuel that powers this powerhouse's constantly revving engine.

From the age of fifty onwards (if it lives that long), the Fire Tiger would be well advised to slow down, take things easy, stabilize its private life, and engage in a consistent program of healthy diet and exercise or yoga. After fifty, it should content itself with delegating authority and managing its vast empires from behind the scenes. It should cultivate hobbies and/or take up meditation. To lead a full and healthy life in its later years, it must narrow its scope of action and find ways to calm its overactive mind. Otherwise, it will be taking a great risk: its nerves may suddenly give out, its heart may suffer an attack, or a stroke may cripple it. I do not even want to contemplate the extreme irritability of a bedridden Fire Tiger.

The Fire Tiger is also a revolutionary. It desires change and is not afraid to initiate it, manage it, and promote it to the public. Consider what Hugh Hefner accomplished in America with the Playboy philosophy. Not only did he establish a magazine, he transformed people's views on many aspects of their sex lives. The same applies to someone like Edouard Leclerc in France. He built a supermarket empire, defied government rules and regulations, undercut and outsold everyone else, and never ceased to be outspoken about it. Then there is Martin Gray, the man who survived the Warsaw Ghetto and wrote a book about it. Afterward, he lost his wife and three children in a forest fire in the South of France and established a foundation to preserve forests. At well over sixty, Martin Gray headed a foundation for global preservation and unity. The Fire Tiger expresses itself freely and openly and is unmoved by disapproving critics who would see it sanctioned for its outrageous ideas. The Fire Tiger is a resilient individual. It devises grand plans effortlessly and can execute them better than almost any other Tiger. Most Fire Tigers either make a world-class impact or perish in the attempt.

Imprudent as this Fire Tiger may be, and as often as it finds itself embroiled in difficulties, it is remarkably resilient. It is almost as if adversity recharges the Fire Tiger's energy. Not only does it desire to be the first and the best, it is always ready to re-enter the arena after being repeatedly defeated. The Fire Tiger possesses immense courage.

The home life of the Fire Tiger will be disrupted by its constant movement. These individuals do not typically marry young. For the sensual, passionate Fire Tiger lover, marriage is an inevitable part of plan B—the period of slowing down. Its sexually liberal youth represents an immature approach to sex, and the element of conquest remains with the Fire Tiger longer than with most. Perhaps in youth, it is too preoccupied with world-altering projects to dedicate sufficient time to long-lasting and profound emotional exchange, or perhaps it is a classic late bloomer. Whatever the reason, do not be surprised if you encounter a sixty-year-old Fire Tiger with a couple of children still in strollers.

The Fire Tiger values honesty and wishes to be regarded as fair and just. However, if provoked, it is capable of deception and even ruthlessness. It does not tolerate foolishness and will swiftly leave any detractors behind without a backward glance. It believes that the ends invariably justify the means. The Fire Tiger knows that its schemes and ideas will improve humanity's condition and never questions its motives or allows self-doubt to hinder its progress.`,Earth:`We twentieth-century Earth Tigers have a grim history of premature death resulting from sudden and tragic events—suicides, accidents, and even murder. In China, the Earth Tiger is known as the thinking person's Tiger. It is believed to be less restless, more determined, and wiser than its counterparts. Earth Tigers make excellent political leaders or top business executives. The desire to lead is strong, as is the desire to occupy a respected position in society. The spirit here is independent, self-reliant, and fiercely individualistic. Despite the calming influence of the Earth element, this Tiger is impulsive and headstrong. It devises scheme after scheme and rushes around, flashing its engaging smile and captivating everyone. However, it generally avoids complete ruin because it seeks advice before acting on its rash impulses. It consults its friends, its lawyer, doctor, and even the neighbors before making significant decisions.

Another distinctive quality about this Tiger is its un-Tiger-like ability to relax and do nothing. Most Tigers find it difficult to sit still, but Earth Tigers can gaze into the distance for hours, contemplating and dreaming of greater moments. They are the most relaxed and temperate of all Tigers.

The Earth Tiger enjoys learning new disciplines and formulating logical plans for the betterment of its own life and the lives of others. Because of this, it is sometimes perceived as meddlesome and overly interfering in the lives of those it cherishes.

Earth Tigers are pillars of strength and champions of justice. They cannot tolerate unfair practices and will fight against social injustice and combat ethical wrongdoing. Like a combination of a terrier and an elephant, the Earth Tiger seizes an idea and holds onto it indefinitely if necessary, because it never forgets. Vengeance will not leave its mind until justice has been served. Nothing brings the Earth Tiger greater satisfaction than demanding and receiving payment for a long-overdue moral debt.

The Earth Tiger is wildly passionate in love. It adores both seducing and being seduced. It is a playful individual who knows how to indulge its mate in imaginative love games. It is relatively faithful and true and prefers not to be informed of its mate's infidelities, as it dislikes being made a fool of. If mistreated, an Earth Tiger can bound away from a negative relationship without even a flicker of regret. It requires total reciprocity in love and rarely allows its heart to rule its head. Unrequited love? It seems like a shameful waste of its precious time.

The health pattern of most Earth Tigers is inconsistent and uneven, but they are fundamentally strong. Although danger befalls them in surprising and terrifying ways, they can survive astonishing ordeals and tend to land safely on all four paws. They assume leadership with ease, enjoy having a good time, and do not give much quarter to self-pity or whining. The Earth Tiger is dutiful and will pay dearly to uphold its beliefs and ideals. But, when wronged, it can also be ruthless and callously cruel. It is purposeful and unyieldingly independent. This last quality can indeed be a flaw, as in its resolute way, the Earth Tiger often ends up stubbornly adhering to its views and feelings without giving space to others, whose fervent desire to love it can never be as grand as its desire to remain aloof.`,Metal:`The Metal Tiger is principled, straightforward, conservative, and energetic, yet it retains its Tiger charm and powerful drive. It is a powerhouse of energy and a performer of grand deeds. But it is somehow more serious than most Tigers. It is not one to leave projects unfinished. It is a bulldozer with the engine of a tank and the scope of at least sixteen aircraft carriers.

The Metal Tiger has a reputation for making the right decisions at the opportune moment and will patiently wait for the precise instant to strike. This behavior can sometimes appear to be procrastination, but its hesitation is a form of strategy. It lies in wait, occasionally raising an eyelid to survey the scene. Then it rises, yawns, stretches its limbs, tenses its muscles, and acts decisively!

On the other hand, if the Metal Tiger has to wait for someone to appear or for something to happen, it becomes frantic. It desires what it wants when it wants it and struggles to understand why others might not wish to adhere to its schedule. It dislikes obeying, yet insists on obedience from others.

This Tiger also possesses a somber inclination. From a young age, it may be fascinated by weapons and intrigued by death and symbols of mortality. It faces a lifelong struggle to suppress this tendency. The Metal Tiger needs to surround itself with optimistic people who keep its mind focused on the positive aspects of life. Otherwise, a predisposition for self-destruction, blind heroism, and a taste for danger can lead it into serious—even fatal—accidents.

The Metal-born Tiger child should be raised in harmonious surroundings, taught to love peace and cherish its fellow human beings. Wise adult choices should lead to harmony and a close-knit family life. Tensions within the family or a tumultuous marriage could disrupt its mental stability. Divorce would be preferable to a stressful marriage.

On the surface, the Metal Tiger appears optimistic, cheerful, and full of humanity. And, on a grand scale, it is. Yet it is not always compassionate in one-to-one situations. You cannot persuade it to sit down and express its thoughts or discuss its feelings. Other people's needs and the complexities of emotional situations seem to escape this Tiger's notice. It can be callous and heartless in love and in family relationships. Yet if its cold-heartedness is remarked upon or criticized, it simply dismisses it with a laugh, pretending it does not exist. There is no remedy for the Metal Tiger's emotional shortcomings. My advice is to adapt to it. Do not take its sharp comments and lack of empathy too seriously, and the Metal Tiger will never seek your sympathy—it sees no use for it.

This Tiger is a creature of legendary magnetism—not classically handsome or even overtly sexy, but more like a charismatic Pied Piper who instinctively knows how to convince its audience and enlist the minds of others in its pursuit of superiority. It is no surprise that de Gaulle was a Metal Tiger. This is a formidable leader who stops at nothing to achieve its objectives. It knows precisely where to strike at the most vulnerable point.

The Metal Tiger desires to improve the world. It will not accept advice or listen to any condemnation of its often unreasonable methods to achieve its goals. For the Metal Tiger, any deception or manipulation is acceptable in the pursuit of victory. And for it, the conflict is always ongoing: right versus wrong, good versus evil, them versus him. It is right, and they are wrong.`,Water:`Water Tigers exhibit smooth, refined manners and appear to lead a charmed life. Great personal success, often achieved early in life, characterizes their existence. This Tiger is a lovable and loving creature, whose strength of will and determination to gain both respect and power are admirable. People honor and esteem the Water Tiger. It is more stable and leads a more balanced life than many of its fellow Tigers. It is often artistically inclined and capable of performing in public. Water Tigers tend to be musical and know how to imitate accents and speech patterns with remarkable accuracy. Possessing a good ear makes them natural linguists. Travel appeals to their preference for effortless adventure; they prefer to journey first class.

Long-term discipline is not always a Tiger's strong suit, but the Water Tiger is capable of sustained diligence in the accomplishment of work projects. It also boasts a socially pleasing personality and enjoys being with groups, telling jokes, and displaying its seductive talents. As this Tiger loves company, it desires to be a family-oriented person. It is reliable and takes responsibility for its relatives and looks after its home.

The Water Tiger is known for its sense of fairness. Unlike some Tigers who cannot tolerate advice or criticism, it is able to view its own shortcomings objectively. Its open-minded approach to difficult issues might lead it to pursue the study of law. It would make an excellent magistrate; its judgments would be unbiased and humane.

Water Tigers are not as intensely vain or ambitious as other Tigers. Scholarly pursuits such as philosophy, languages, and comparative literature are possible, but it is the entertainment professions—especially those concerned with music and communication—which will ensure both the Water Tiger's career stability and bring it joy. Failing success on the stage or screen, it might choose to be a professor, a literary agent, or even a promoter of concerts or other spectacles.

Although they make excellent performers, these Tigers do not crave to be constantly in the spotlight during every waking moment of their lives. They can work contentedly behind the scenes, creating, inventing, and planning. An eager, clear-thinking Water Tiger is a welcome addition to any group effort.

This Tiger is mostly a virtuous creature whose greatest flaw is its rare but terrifying rage. The Tiger cannot tolerate betrayal and will react impulsively when it falls victim to it. The Water Tiger appears calm and unruffled, affecting a smooth, cheerful exterior. It is everyone's friend—until it is wronged. The bitter anger that follows is ruthless and leads to a long-term quest for revenge—a dangerous trait!

Cultivate the friendship of this Tiger. Enjoy its love and bask in its charming company. Accept its proposal to collaborate. But do not try to harm it—or it will turn you into a puree and spread you on its toast for breakfast.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"At first meeting these two charm the pants off each other. The Rat finds the Tiger charming and would love to show him off, while the confident Tiger is amused by the Rat’s vigorous chatter and lively sense of humor. But there is bound to be friction in the long run. After the first spark of love, these two will find fault with each other. The rambunctious, adventurous Tiger will forever be seeking excitement—off on safari to Kenya, then on to San Francisco to catch the next earthquake. The Rat, being more domestic, will come to hate the sight of suitcases. The Tiger stalks instability, tempted by danger and the prospect of having a new job every year. Everything is challenging to this aggressive beast. The Rat will not always find the Tiger’s inconsistencies appealing and will be plagued by worry. Rat’s mental stability depends greatly on material security and, with the Tiger always job-hopping, the Rat will fret over money. To endure, both must remember the initial reasons which drew them together. They have lots to talk about and agree on many things. If the Rat can recall how the Tiger roared attractively into his or her life, and the Tiger can continue to appreciate the Rat’s powers of seduction, there is hope for an exciting, long-lived marriage.",Ox:"Disastrous. No matter how you slice it, this combo is in for a rocky ride. Both possess an iron will, backed by the power to exert it. Equally self-possessed and determined, the obstinate Ox and temperamental Tiger are better known as rivals than accomplices. Frankly, this quarrelsome duo is best off entangled at the center of a boxing ring. Often, the Tiger jump-starts the Ox’s tranquil day by stirring up trouble. The stoical Ox wants only to stay close to home and plod on. He must exercise much patience with the rambunctious Tiger. And the Ox finds that exhausting. The rebellious Tiger roars off to a trade union demonstration, complaining bitterly about the humdrum, dreary Ox, while the Ox bullies the Tiger, accusing him or her of everything from incurable restlessness to insanity. If round three takes place under the covers, there is hope for reconciliation. The Tiger’s raw sensuality thaws the Ox’s glacial resistance. With the Tiger, the inhibited Ox feels free. Twenty-four-hour truces may result. Even so, the union is best-suited for friendship or business partnership, where dual iron wills can effect real progress. The Tiger/Ox emotional match is a tug of war. It is not romantically promising.",Tiger:"Two Tigers? Bum-out alert! Tigers believe fervently in love at first sight and may pounce on each other with gusto. Yes. A Tiger tandem is full of instant enthusiasms, quick fix plans, and clever strategies. But there is a basic problem. While both Tigers are out changing the world, who’s watching the store? Candlelight dinners. Vibrant, witty foreplay. Banter and excitement. “My place or yours?” decisions rapidly executed. Groans, sighs, crackings of zippers, and tearing of clothes, twin tigers are so turned on, they never make it to the bed. They consume each other. Afterwards, they’ll sip champagne and pore over the world's fate. Their torrid embraces become passionate arguments. Forever in combat, the Tiger twins are messily content. Come morning, two Tigers regain their respective lairs, freshen up and dash off to work. No time lost, and no extra romantic palaver to cloud the clear purpose of a busy day. Tigers are inveterate meddlers, always shoving their paws in where they ought to abstain. Two Tigers will contradict and wrongly advice each other all over the place, leaving no other alternative than to swim around in boiling water for the rest of their lives. Help! Perhaps they should forego marriage. A love affair will be played out in fast-forward mode and promises to be ultra dynamic. But this marriage is unlikely to be either peaceful, long-lasting or productive. And…God help the Tiger cubs. The insecurity! The ever-changing domiciles and decors. Arrgh!",Rabbit:"A style clash. This couple might very possibly enter into a so-called “marriage of convenience”, but underneath roils a mute tension that screams, “Get me outta here!” With a Tiger/Cat union, it’s the Tiger who’s doing the silent shrieking. What then? The Cat usually has the money, and the Tiger, who married the Cat for the loot, is busy having a nervous breakdown. Tigers live for change and victory. Cats dream only of peace and quiet. Get the picture? No common ground. Trying to outwit each other, these two felines stealthily compete for the household throne. The Tiger goes at it with typical self-serving vengeance and the Cat skulks around the house seeking opportunities to entrap the Tiger. Imagine, two wily cats under the same roof. They merely tolerate each other. An occasional playful interlude can degenerate into a clawing, hissing brawl. Cats require security and build their nests with refinement and taste. The Tiger might enjoy these surroundings but, unlike the Cat, the Tiger craves change and favors a more Bohemian lifestyle. The seductive Tiger might be tempted to grab some of the Cat’s dough and dash off to the Amazon, leaving only a deep skid mark outside the Swiss bank. Even in bed, this pair is not apt to be compatible. The Tiger is aggressive, possessing such a raw, frank, pushy sexuality that the Cat’s delicate sensuality is overwhelmed. Cats require coaxing, seductive, slow-moving lovers and Tigers are ill-suited to satisfy this need. I see the Cat/Tiger match as either an intense summer romance, or perhaps a long-lived “loving friendship” wherein they get together in bed once in a blue moon for old times’ sake. Marriage? Only if the Cat has a private income and protects it from the Tiger’s spendthrift clutches.",Dragon:"Sexed! The Tiger/Dragon love relationship bears serious consideration. Combined, their strength is almost excessive. And energy! Enough to fuel several large power plants. There is EGO flashing in red neon all over this couple. Overbearing and self-propelled, they are both a bit too much. But as a pair, they can succeed. Despite an excess of commando muscle, this combo lives peaceably together. Mutual respect and admiration offsets the expected clashes. The dashing Dragon begs for constant flattery and applause. However, the strong-minded Tiger finding the pontificating Dragon tiresome and teases the spotlight away. The Tiger is undaunted by fire-breathing antics. In fact, the intrepid Tiger loves a good shouting match and respects a worthy opponent. The generous Dragon is amused by and tolerates the Tiger’s love of danger and precipitous behavior. In short, these two get along. Tiger with Dragon is not only a sensual match. They carry themselves with bravado and flair. An air of madness colors everything they do. People flock to their home to bask in their aura and share in the high of their hazardous love. Not afraid to share power, they take turns sitting on the throne, complicity taking precedence over their individual roles. This relationship is good for marriage. Battles will be waged, but at the end of the day the force of their attraction ensures they will be lovers for life. Entwined in their own whirlwind of passion and steamy sex, this couple knows the road to heaven. The Dragon sets the tawny Tiger alight and the rapacious Tiger devours the dashing Dragon’s scalding hot fire. Enjoy!",Snake:"The elusive Snake and the tempestuous Tiger are irresistibly drawn to each other, but this union is not advisable. A Tiger/Snake pairing can be a disastrous alliance. As different as black and white, yin and yang, the Tiger/Snake combination simply does not blend. Should either of you be unfortunate enough to fall for the other, a preliminary restraining order could save you from catastrophes. If not, here is what to expect: The slow-moving Snake will inflict tremendous frustration upon the energetic Tiger's psyche. Initially, the jungle predator mistakenly perceives the enchanting serpent as quiet and submissive, and attempts to dominate. But reptiles do not respond well to bullying; they retaliate. Snakes are aloof, independent-minded, and strategic masterminds. Haughty indifference and disdain are among their sharpest weapons. They are also prone to repeated instances of infidelity, which will certainly shatter a Tiger mate's considerable ego. The impressive tantrums of the Tiger can make the Snake's calm, reflective, philosophical life miserable. Equally magnetic, Snakes and Tigers compete for attention. The Tiger does so aggressively, and the Snake slyly bewitches. At their own cocktail party, Tiger/Snake hosts may appear quarrelsome. The Tiger recounts stories about its days in the Sinai desert. The Snake subtly encroaches on the Tiger's territory, captivating the company with the Dance of the Seven Veils, learned (coincidentally) in the Sinai desert. Outmaneuvered, the Tiger loudly outdoes the Snake, recounting further desert expeditions. Subdued, the Snake joins the applause, but adds, in a cultivated, soft-spoken voice, that everything the Tiger knows about deserts was learned from the Snake. Tigers are fast and alert, while Snakes are quiet and deliberate thinkers. Tigers are impulsive and may act heedlessly. Snakes rely almost solely on intuition and take things slowly. These creatures may cohabit for sensual pleasure, but they do not see eye to eye. Sexual intimacy? The Snake's need for beautiful, romantic foreplay is denied by an aggressive Tiger, who simply gets down to business. It is best to abstain!",Horse:"Auspicious, to say the least. Both parties have unruly natures. Individually, they are independent. They might clash, but the attraction between them is strong and so is the mutual respect. In love, they become wilting passion flowers of vulnerability. As a loving pair, their passion knows few bounds. The Tiger and the Horse are equally inventive and creative. In family matters, the Horse’s conservatism curbs the Tiger’s hotheadedness. They work hard together to raise a fine family in a proper way, yet, thanks to the Tiger’s rebelliousness, the kids will get some relief from the seriousness of Horsey’s approach. Both are optimistic and strong. Usually, if a depression comes along, the Horse is up and the Tiger is down, or vice versa. And no boredom here either. These two are active, lusty life-grabbers. Unless one learns to be practical with money, they may have financial crises. Both know how to earn and both love to spend. The initial sexual attraction is volcanic and they are both imaginative and faithful enough to keep sex exciting over the long haul. This relationship can endure.",Goat:"This union is among the worst possible known to Chinese astrologers. Although the couple may make a fabulous start (in bed), from there on it's all downhill. The practicalities just don't work out. Goat is charming, beautifully seductive and loving. Tiger is passion and mettle. But who will bring home the bacon? In this family, nobody wants the job. No concessions are made. The Goat remains laid back while the ambitious Tiger bombasts a hole in the kitchen ceiling. What was a great passion ends in lifelong misunderstanding and acrimony. Affairs? Yes. Marriage? Abstinence is advised.",Monkey:"These two make eager lovers. Initially, they will leap frequently on each other’s bones, accomplishing astonishing feats of extreme passion, but in the long run, the ardor may die a natural death, because Tigers hate to be clung to—and innately neurotic Monkeys don’t know how not to cling. The strong intellectual tug between Tigers and Monkeys frequently keeps them together, anyway. The Tiger admires the Monkey’s keen eye for strategy and the Monkey enjoys and applauds the Tiger’s feisty wit and temerity. Monkey gives Tiger plenty of presents and kudos. Tiger gives Monkey spunk and encouragement. These two have an easy common viewpoint, and, even if they cannot keep the love flame burning, will go far together as lifelong pals. Except… the Chinese say that the Tiger should beware. Traditionally, the Monkey is Tiger’s natural enemy. I don’t advise marriage.",Rooster:"I don’t recommend this pair for marriage. Both parties are aggressive and opinionated; neither will back down easily. The atmosphere will be taut and most arguments one-sided. Conflicts and collisions are guaranteed to hinder the harmonious progress of this couple. Tigers bounce back and forget every nasty word that was said. But Roosters carry grudges and cannot forget how badly they were treated by a Tiger last time they had a row. Impasses are common. In bed, there may be some fairly exciting fireworks, as the Rooster is imaginative and energetic enough to keep the demanding Tiger interested. They are both impetuous and uninhibited lovers capable of grand gestures and profound intensity. Unless the disagreements of the day carry over into the bedroom, this couple is well aspected for a long, healthy sex life—without marriage.",Dog:"Harmony incarnate. Dogs and Tigers just plain get along. They have common causes and common philosophies. But they are very different. The Tiger is overly optimistic, the Dog pessimistic. Each helps the other to understand these basic character differences. The Chinese call this pairing a happy alliance of muscle and heart. The Tiger has the strength to put the Dog’s ideals across to the public. The disquiet Dog keeps watch and prevents the Tiger from leaping into the wrong frays. They are, simply, a great couple. Harmony reigns right from the start. And because Dog and Tiger respect each other’s deepest convictions, mutual admiration sticks them together like super glue. In bed, the Tiger usually takes the lead, which is felicitous for the tense, nervous Dog, who often needs to be thawed out before engaging in any heavy intimacy. With time, this couple learns to blend eroticism with affection to achieve physical fulfillment. It is rare that such a marriage ends in divorce.",Pig:"The basic characters here are vastly different. Pigs are scrupulous and peace-loving. Tigers strategize every move and carry banners for their own noisy causes. Yet with the proper amount of gentle understanding from Piggy and the sort of generous reasonableness for which Tigers are famous, the pair can make a real go of marriage. The Pig admires the Tiger’s punchy gall and the Tiger respects the Pig’s guilelessness and purity of spirit. Pigs are mostly even-tempered and good-natured, while Tigers are pathologically changeable. Pigs find Tigers too mobile but they don’t mind staying at home and holding the fort white Tiger rushes about being self-important. Instead of clashing, these two complement one another. Their physical relationship is full of tenderness and mutual understanding. The Pig is sensual, adores pleasure and is lavishly generous. Tigers need a lot of affection and cherish the sort of warmth and homeliness the Pig offers their restless nature. Steamy cuddling sessions abound in the Pig/Tiger household."},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"As you undoubtedly already know, the Snake consistently desires influence. In relationships, in business, or in government, the Snake aims to dominate. Now, for you Tigers, this particular Snake characteristic is both unsettling and extremely irritating. You do not necessarily wish to be in control of many things; answering phone calls and emails in an office all day, waiting for people to attend tedious meetings, would bore you immensely. However, the Snake does not necessarily understand this about you. You appear so strong and self-assured that the cautious Snake feels threatened. Consequently, your life in the Snake year may prove to be less than delightful. The Snake might attempt to obstruct even your most innocent desires for leadership, belittle your most ingenious ideas, and may even sabotage your plans. You see, the Snake not only desires power; it also seeks security and is a meticulous accumulator and saver. You are the more extravagant, carefree individual who believes that money is abundant and that if you keep seeking new opportunities, there will always be more available to you. Conflict will arise between your spending habits and the Snake's desire to accumulate. My advice? Plan to travel this year and remain out of public sight. If you do not threaten the Snake in any way, it will do you the favor of completely ignoring you."},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"Many people believe Horses and Snakes do not harmonize. Many people are correct. This year will be challenging at best for Snakes, as the Horse is not even-tempered and does not particularly care about its subjects’ well-being. Horses are intensely pragmatic; they simply want to do things their way. They are talented and shrewd, and they are artistic, but not necessarily altruistic. You Snakes are motivated by compassion and philanthropy; you sincerely believe in your ability to contribute to the betterment of humankind. So, Snake dissatisfaction is common in the ego-centered Horse year environment. You will feel as though you just cannot make progress on any project and maintain it without obstacle after obstacle being thrown up and roadblocks appearing at every turn. You might, moreover, become entangled in a legal battle over a contract or real property. As the climate in Horse years is unfavorable to a positive outcome for Snakes, you will not have much chance of winning. It would be better to try some cunning tactic to delay the lawsuit until next year when the gentle Goat will rule—a more lenient climate for Snakes involved in legal disputes. Obviously, this year will not be your favorite. Take your frustration on a long holiday somewhere warm and tropical with your significant other in tow. Should your significant other be (for some strange reason) a Horse, I advise that you leave him or her at home. Perhaps you should consider seducing someone more philosophically inclined."},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Yin Fire",prediction:"Tigers generally fare better under the Goat’s influence this year; however, they also have to strive harder to achieve their desires. The Goat and you do not perceive life in the same manner. Fundamentally, Goats enjoy being confined to fertile areas where they can exercise their creative abilities without the concern of having to exert themselves independently. You are quite the opposite; you are inherently independent. You do not enjoy being restricted anywhere, ever. As a consequence of this significant difference in approach, in Goat years, you often feel disapproved of. Not that you care in the slightest whether or not you are liked or accepted by the Goat. But you do wish it would not try to curtail your style. Ideally, in these years, you will engage in more travel for both business and pleasure. You will enjoy the wandering. Meeting some new like-minded individuals will help keep your energy levels high for the twelve rather unhurried months ahead. The financial deities are on your side in Goat years. This may not signify that millions will be bestowed upon you, but it does indicate that you are doing something correctly, that is, traveling!"},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Yang Earth",prediction:"No frivolous behavior! These next twelve months will offer you a burst of activity, precisely to your liking. Multitasking, numerous meetings, and multiple proposals for work, cultural, and sports experiences. Accept the Monkey's invitations for all these propositions. You, more than any other sign, are certainly capable of managing such a diverse array of ongoing activities. Where other people might feel overwhelmed by such an abundance of new things to learn and do, you revel in the novelty of it all. A change in your work environment is also forthcoming this year. You are an individual whose enthusiasms require alteration as frequently as you change your shirt. So, start diligently searching for that unusual job immediately this year. You will not regret doing so. Love life? Medium rare. I say that because the romantic situation you have been in for so long is, by this time, well done. Overdone, in fact. Hence, it is time to make significant changes. Now, briefly pursue new romantic interests. See how it feels to enjoy the thrill of seduction again. Change is the central theme of the Monkey year for Tigers. P.S. Your current partner will most likely be overjoyed to see you depart."},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Yin Earth",prediction:"Allow the Rooster to manage the proceedings. Or at least give him or her the impression that they are in a position of leadership. Roosters prefer to act swiftly, enjoy themselves, and (unlike yourself) prefer not to leave a trail of casualties behind. As you probably have a new romantic interest by this time, you will be busy devising new strategies to retain this prize. However, you need to apply yourself diligently to work this year. Roosters expect people to be actively engaged in their various projects and are not amused by idlers. So, maintain a prominent presence. When you are laboring under the hot sun or mining coal deep underground, groan frequently and sweat profusely to convey to your superiors just how demanding a Tiger's life can be. Otherwise, if you are not attempting to overshadow him, the Rooster will leave you to your countless independent pursuits. Travel and visits to relatives in distant cities are favored now. There is a family member you have been avoiding. Make it your priority to pay them respect. It is in your financial interest to be kind to them now and make amends for any past neglect."},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Yang Metal",prediction:"Phew! There is relatively little that can go utterly wrong for a Tiger in Dog years. You and Dogs get along well together because you share similar beliefs and adopt a global perspective on even the most minor events. Differences of opinion arise when you sense the Dog's inherent paranoia surfacing unexpectedly. Dogs possess a unique understanding of Murphy's Law; they instinctively know that if something can go wrong, it will, and they are more than willing to announce it beforehand. Hence, in Dog years, an atmosphere of pervasive anxiety lingers, which drives Tigers to distraction. My advice to Tigers in this otherwise somewhat challenging year is to enjoy the goodwill that the Dog offers you as its protective companion. Relax a bit. Ease off the accelerator at work. Spend some enriching downtime simply socializing with friends or family—or both. In Dog years, you can also enjoy engaging in cultural excursions. Take tours of exotic lands you have always promised yourself you would visit. Go see the Pyramids or visit Niagara Falls. Do something wonderful for yourself, but leave the Dog and its paranoia at home."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Yin Metal",prediction:"Pigs admit to a certain wide-eyed admiration when confronted by you restless Tiger individuals. Pigs are strong, knowledgeable, and culturally adept people. But they do not comprehend your exaggerated need for change. You are constantly bustling about, never settling long enough to accumulate capital, amass riches, collect art, or acquire luxurious homes—whatever it is the Pig considers wealth. Nevertheless, the Pig and you can be close companions. You admire the Pig's purity and authenticity of spirit. What it does not understand about you is what will hinder you this year. The atmosphere of abundance will lead you to assume you can spend, give, and squander your money, and so—in a word or two—you overspend. If you are not more careful about where your money is going in the first part of this Pig year, by September, you will find yourself in a difficult financial situation. So, tighten your resolve, Tiger. Control your desire to be overly generous to those you love or those you feel are in need. Hold onto your financial reserves and do not sell the family jewels to acquire a fancy new car to impress your beloved. Put yourself on a budget. Give your love freely, but take fewer financial risks. Slow down. Sit still. Read. Knit. Go to the countryside. Sit under a tree and reflect."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Yang Water",prediction:"This year, the Rat’s influence may be detrimental to Tigers. Rats love to dominate, and you do not particularly enjoy being told what to do. The atmosphere in Rat years can be tense for Tigers as well. You will need to travel this year, and you may also need to do so in the company of a Rat whose political views are not at all in harmony with your own. As Rat years are all about power, this will be a good time for you to avoid seeking promotions or asking for a raise. Maintain a low profile. Do not attempt to be the leader of anything you cannot fully control, as the Rat will be waiting to seize any opportunity to undermine your authority. I would not advise that you and your romantic partner or spouse take any lengthy journeys together, as the stress of the year will cause both of you to be irritable. If you can take separate vacations, do so. In general, your romantic life this year should be put on hold until a more favorable period. Your health is generally good. There is no need for you to undergo any plastic surgery or cosmetic procedures."},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Yin Water",prediction:"I must caution you against attempting to earn a significant amount of money or securing the prestigious job you desire in an Ox year. Why? It is not merely because the Ox does not wish for your success, but also because your rapid, opportunistic methods exasperate the Ox. As a long-term planner, the Ox becomes disoriented simply observing your quick acceleration and swift movements. Ox individuals possess great talent for leadership; they often become autocratic figures. However, they are not particularly quick on their feet, and they are even slower in their intellectual processing. Their minds operate in an unhurried fashion. Do they linger and adopt a leisurely approach to managing their year or their domain? Absolutely not. But they persevere steadily, and you act impulsively. Therefore, in an Ox year, it is advisable to preemptively temper your intensity so as not to appear threatening or to bewilder the deliberate, task-oriented Ox. You will not need to humble yourself to advance. However, you will need to agree with those in positions of authority. Since you detest being anyone's subordinate, you may experience digestive issues, migraines, and other stress-related ailments as a consequence. Maintain the well-being of your romantic life by making a special effort to perform loving acts of kindness and deference towards your beloved or spouse (or both) in this rather challenging, unaccommodating Ox year. You need all the approval and affection you can gather from those who cherish and admire your spirited demeanor."},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Yang Wood",prediction:"This year is your year. You are in charge. You must, therefore, be vigilant and ensure your subjects do not overthrow you. Do you recall that last year, you were able to spend your time peacefully managing your projects and were not subject to any sudden changes or unexpected events? Well, this year promises to be quite the opposite. The Tiger is an extremely volatile individual who enjoys a thrill a minute. You can handle the chaos, but you will not appreciate having to frequently revise your meticulously planned timetables. Tigers thrive on constant change, and you... well, you do not. I would like to be able to advise you to travel and avoid this hectic atmosphere. Unfortunately, the Tiger and the Ox are traditionally at odds. So, you must remain on guard. If you are not present and vigilant, your enemies will seize the opportunity to usurp your authority. Do not take risks. Do not change jobs or move to a new house. Do not buy a new car. Do not have a baby. Do not invest your money. The only advice I can offer you is: stay where you are, and do not make any significant moves."},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"You will need to maintain a low profile in this Cat/Rabbit year. They do not enjoy the chaos and general disorder that you Tigers create in your professional lives. However, if you are discreet and cautious, you can accomplish a great deal. The Cat/Rabbit will ignore you if you do not make a lot of noise. Your health will be good, and your romantic life will be passionate. As the Cat/Rabbit is a homebody, you will feel the need to remain close to your family and friends. This is an excellent year for home renovation projects, building a new house, or constructing an addition. You will be able to manage these projects without much interference from outside sources, but do be careful not to make any foolish investments. The Cat/Rabbit is very shrewd about money and will be watching you closely. If you appear to be squandering your finances, the Cat/Rabbit will not hesitate to report you to the authorities. So, if you are not up to date on your tax returns, I suggest you get them in order."},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"Dragons love you Tigers. They adore your spirit and admire your courage. They will do everything in their power to assist you in your endeavors. So, this year, you can anticipate success in all your projects. You will be able to travel, and you will be able to earn a significant amount of money. You will also be able to find a new romantic interest, and you will be able to maintain your current relationship without much difficulty. The Dragon is a generous individual who will not interfere with your personal life. However, you will need to be careful not to take on too many responsibilities. The Dragon is a very demanding individual, and you will need to be able to keep up with his or her pace. If you can manage to do so, you will have a very successful year. If not, you will find yourself in a great deal of trouble. The Dragon does not tolerate failure, and you will be held accountable for any mistakes you make. So, be careful, and do not make any foolish decisions. If you can manage to do so, you will have a very successful year."}}},a={introduction:`Ah, Virtuous Cat/Rabbit, you seek harmony. You are cautious and practice discretion in all matters. When you sense a conflict approaching, you quickly retreat and hide. Distinguished, diplomatic, and well-mannered, you are also as nervous as a cat. Culture and refinement provide you with comfort. You do not dislike money either; you instinctively know how to earn and preserve your fortune without ostentation or display. You prefer traditional antique furnishings over contemporary chrome and glass. You are a soft-stepping go-getter—ambitious but never aggressive, strong but never rough.

Your particular brand of wisdom suggests, "He who fights and runs away lives to fight another day." You are hypersensitive—even squeamish. You are somewhat of a hypochondriac: an innocent hangnail on your big toe alarms you. "Call an ambulance, get me to the emergency room!" Chronic illnesses—migraine, asthma, hay fever, lower back pain, warts, hives—you have experienced them all. Purchase a large house in the countryside, then fill it with brilliant, well-behaved children and pets. Choose a partner from among gentle Goats, scrupulous Pigs, or loyal Dogs. If you are feeling generous, remember that Snakes are delighted to recline on Cats' velvet sofas. Avoid Tigers, Roosters, and Dragons; their relentless flamboyance threatens your tranquil existence. You plan your life to proceed smoothly, and usually it does. But should spontaneity enter the picture and events go awry, you panic. Take my advice and relax, not only on yourself but, more especially, on the rest of us.`,elements:{Wood:`A birth in a Wood year bestows additional stability, wisdom, generosity, and altruism upon the already responsible Cat/Rabbit. This individual can work tirelessly without showing a hint of fatigue or nervousness. This steadfastness and strength of purpose are often demonstrated by its extraordinary endurance and composure when assisting in the care of elderly or ill individuals. The Wood Cat/Rabbit is that widely recognized good Samaritan whom everyone commends, remarking, "He was so supportive during his mother's prolonged illness."

This Cat/Rabbit is also meticulous about having things done precisely its way. It can be demanding and even unyielding, especially if it is contradicted. It cannot tolerate any teasing or even gentle criticism. It is difficult to get along with when harmony is disrupted, which presents a significant challenge for those who live with it. Creating a perpetually pleasant atmosphere around the house is no easy feat, yet that is what the Wood Cat/Rabbit desires and even insists upon.

Its sexual drive cannot be described as passionate, but this individual can be aroused to a high degree of sexuality if properly stimulated by an enticing, sensual partner. As for romance, it is neither adept at nor interested in Valentine's Day or sentimental gestures like hearts and flowers. It prefers to approach love in a civilized, rational manner so that it can maintain control.

For the most part, this Cat/Rabbit will do almost anything to preserve equilibrium, maintain peace, or avoid causing trouble. It is hindered in its interactions with others. It cannot be entirely honest for fear of disrupting the prevailing tranquility. Though not dishonest, the Wood Cat/Rabbit is cunning and shrewd about concealing its feelings.

This adaptable person will be accepted almost anywhere it goes due to its open-handed and easy-going nature. These traits may not always work to its advantage, as others might misinterpret its kindness as weakness. If it is wise, it will choose a strong lifelong partner who will serve as its constant shield against life's harshness and difficulties. Then it can relax and pursue its many artistic and literary interests.`,Fire:`Fire often introduces instability to the reserved Cat/Rabbit, yet it also adds vigor to its overly proper and fastidious nature. It cannot be described as aggressive, but the Fire Cat/Rabbit is generally somewhat more spirited than its fellow felines.

Genius flourishes in this Cat/Rabbit. Many great writers and musicians, painters and poets were born in Fire Cat/Rabbit years. Emotionally intuitive, it can perceive extrasensory messages in others and frequently knows how to transform them into poignant works of art. This Cat/Rabbit will also possess a sharp sense of humor and knows how to charm people with it. Others typically enjoy its company and find its wit intelligent and readily applicable to real-life situations. The Fire Cat/Rabbit is the least shy of all Cats/Rabbits. It can handle fame and competently deal with the public without needing to retreat from the spotlight.

However, it is not an altruist. It is supremely self-centered and desires its own way in most relationships. It can be strong in the face of opposition—if necessary, it will bare its claws and hiss loudly to ward off attackers—but it would prefer to play a waiting game, using cunning tactics to avoid confrontation and circumventing most difficult issues. The anguish the Fire Cat/Rabbit experiences during a waiting period can cause it serious health problems. It is not naturally well-equipped for dealing with internal conflict. Yet, it creates such conflict by suppressing its true feelings while waiting for the opportune moment to act. If it could learn to be more compassionate, set aside its ego, acquire knowledge of how to care for others, and express its feelings more readily, it could avoid developing complex chronic health problems such as depression and neuroses later in life.

People accuse Fire Cats/Rabbits of arrogance. It may initially seem reserved and aloof. Mostly, it attempts to present an amiable facade, but sensitive individuals are not deceived. It is overly confident and self-important when it comes to intellectual matters.

The Fire Cat/Rabbit reads extensively. Its memory is vast, and its information is well-organized. In discussions, it can be sarcastic and pedantic, causing its friends and family to endure many tedious evenings listening to it expound on obscure subjects of no interest to anyone else. Others, again, do not matter much—and their opinions, frankly, bore it.

Government jobs and administrative positions attract and suit the Fire Cat/Rabbit. It will feel at home in the snobbish, opulent atmospheres of embassies and diplomatic missions around the world. It also makes a wonderful business executive. Not only is it capable of brilliant management, but the Fire Cat/Rabbit has a way of infusing its workplace with that special Cat/Rabbit flair and elegance, and it can detect problems before they arise. No budget-conscious, caution-loving, self-respecting, ambitious Fire Cat/Rabbit would ever allow a small financial deficit to grow into a looming red figure on the bottom line.`,Earth:`Observation and a keen sense of style characterize the Earth Cat/Rabbit's nature. It is also inventive, capable of impressive creative feats, and often responsible for the planning and execution of aesthetic projects of vast scope. The sharpest intelligence resides in this person, and it consistently knows how to utilize its keen mind to great advantage. In leadership positions, its style is passive and understated. Nevertheless, it rules with an iron paw.

The Earth Cat/Rabbit is both critical and conservative. It is meticulous about its surroundings and selects its friends and associates with the utmost care. Socially, it is also somewhat awkward. Because it feels different from its peers, it often travels to distant places for work and may even become an expatriate. The typical Earth Cat/Rabbit is always seeking to relocate itself, to move to a new place or society more suited to its personal tastes and sensitivities. It imagines life will improve if only it can live somewhere it feels it belongs, is better understood, and is less pressured to maintain a high degree of social decorum.

The Earth Cat/Rabbit's equilibrium depends on maintaining a realistic approach to life. It does not enjoy any pursuit that is not clear-cut. It is candid in speech and action, not mincing its words or shying away from confrontation, unlike most other Cats/Rabbits.

Earth Cats/Rabbits also demonstrate a profound interest in the meaning of death. Somehow, it is convinced that we do not cease to exist when we die. It is a spiritual type of person who believes in an afterlife. Near-death experiences, reincarnation, and spiritualist theories intrigue it. It is also drawn to the esoteric and perhaps metaphysics and extrasensory perception.

The Earth Cat/Rabbit is the most sensual of all Cats/Rabbits. It obviously does not possess the expansive sexual drive of Goats or the full, gentle sensuality of Pigs. But the Earth Cat/Rabbit is reputedly a voracious participant in sexual activity. Its style may be a bit overly refined. Cats/Rabbits rarely surrender to complete self-abandon, but the list of its conquests can be impressively long.

The Earth Cat/Rabbit is a willing learner. It is eager to listen and understand its shortcomings. Professional assistance with anxiety and sleeplessness will certainly work wonders for the stability of this sometimes mildly neurotic Cat/Rabbit person.`,Metal:`Metal bestows a steely resolve and more courage than we typically observe in Cat/Rabbit behavior. It is not a world-beater in direct confrontation, but unlike some less spirited Cats/Rabbits who flee, it can hold its ground if and when it encounters an obstacle. Due to this ability to defend its viewpoint, it is more optimistic than other Cats/Rabbits. It is even slightly aggressive. Still, Metal Cats/Rabbits remain cautious. They do not take significant, frightening risks. They rarely act on impulse, think every detail through, and scrutinize the particulars of every new situation as if searching for flaws. Until each element is perfectly clear, Metal Cats/Rabbits will avoid investment, commitment, marriage, and intimacy—even with loved ones. Metal Cats/Rabbits require their lives to be orderly and prefer to stay out of the confusing waters of indecision.

If its projects do not succeed, the Metal Cat/Rabbit may not only stumble and fall but also face ruin. This individual is a strong believer in adhering to its ideals. Unfortunately, it is rarely able to do so because it aspires to precarious positions and is easily defeated by ruthless adversaries. Its downfall often takes the form of a persistent depressive attitude towards advancement and a fatal loss of self-confidence. Sometimes the Metal Cat/Rabbit anticipates its failures and deliberately undertakes a project that it knows exceeds its capabilities. This way, it can foresee and deflect the pain of the inevitable failure.

The Metal Cat/Rabbit's word is as good as gold. Once committed, it makes a point of honoring its promises and always supports them with reliable informational data. It considers disloyal people and unfaithful friends or relatives unworthy of its time. It is impatient with all untidiness in human endeavors and insists on clarity and a hundred fail-safe clauses and procedures before signing any document.

This creature may well possess special gifts that allow it to read other people's minds. It tends towards introversion. Although it can be deliberately charming, the Metal Cat/Rabbit is never quite as amiable and outgoing as it could be. The darker, hidden aspect of its nature resides in ambiguous areas and mysterious realms where ghosts and spirits reside. It is more than occasionally drawn to participate in séances where tables turn and spirits return to seek communication with their loved ones.

The Metal Cat/Rabbit possesses refined taste. It may well become famous in professions such as decoration or architecture, art history, or even painting or drawing. It is an avid collector of art objects and, due to its eye for detail, rarely falls into traps or is deceived by dishonest dealers. Its astute sixth sense perceives deceit through almost any disguise. At an auction, when it senses authenticity, its elegant paw reaches directly for its checkbook. With lightning speed, it acquires all the bargains in a single swift action.

This highly refined aesthete does not have many casual acquaintances or companions. It is not someone to "hang out with" or invite in merely for idle conversation. The Metal Cat/Rabbit is a serious individual with earnest intentions and goals. It allows almost no one into its private life and rarely shares intimate information—even with its spouse or romantic partner.`,Water:`The Water Cat/Rabbit is a more "feminine" type than most other Cats/Rabbits. Its sense of taste and love of refinement for its own sake are exaggerated by the gentle influence of water. It is also more squeamish than other Cats/Rabbits and will recoil and turn its head away from all physical illness, disability, and emotional and mental instability. It cannot tolerate the sight of blood and indeed nearly faints at the thought of an injection.

This Cat/Rabbit, no matter if it protests its preference for the joys of living on the edge, lives solely for security. Despite an endearing inclination for associating with peculiar individuals or dating eccentric art students or flamboyant dancers, the Water Cat/Rabbit does not envision itself departing from the norm to live any type of bohemian or even freelance life. Not only does it enjoy making money; the Water Cat/Rabbit requires luxury to survive. It cannot bear squalor, prefers to meticulously control and discipline all its food intake, and must have the proper bath and toilet facilities complete with all the suitably appointed cupboards and shelves to keep its finery safely housed. Without a well-established plan and a rigorous infrastructure, the Water Cat/Rabbit soon becomes fearful. Order provides it comfort. It fears everything from poverty to its own idleness. It strives to maintain clarity and a rational point of view because, deep down, it is afraid of losing its way, and perhaps even its mind.

True love often eludes this individual's grasp as well. It falls in love easily and is captivated by romance. Yet, the Water Cat/Rabbit will not fight for its rightful position in relationships, rarely speaks of its innermost feelings, and keeps its own counsel when confronted by the threat of conflict. Its dream of love is so idealized and vague that it often makes serious errors when seeking a mate.

The Water Cat/Rabbit is a daydreamer. Aloof and seemingly detached from it all, it frequently resides in a dream kingdom where it is the master and monarch of the entire realm. It longs for excitement but does not dare indulge in adventure. It imagines being brave enough to escape the monotony of a nine-to-five lifestyle. It would love to be a spy, an international journalist, or a philosopher, but deep down, it prefers the safety of material gain to the danger and adventure of passionate or romantic endeavors.

This person desires a showplace for a home. If it can, it spends much time there, in elegant rooms surrounded by collections of antiques, first edition books, and classical music. This Cat/Rabbit reads voraciously, cares little for gourmet foods, but drinks only the finest wines (in moderation) while contemplating its next financial triumph on the stock market. The Water Cat/Rabbit is attracted by all that is ethereal and intangible, yet it will always remain attached to creature comforts. It is a rare Water Cat/Rabbit who dashes off, scornful of convention, disconnected from society for the pure joy of participating in some exciting fling. It is too staid and "fraidy-cat" for that.

Charming and amiable, it has many acquaintances but few genuine friends. The Water Cat/Rabbit is also known for its rare intellect. It is usually highly educated and wishes to be regarded as both cultured and wise. It often cultivates people for their social standing and is attracted to those it feels come from the "right" families. It has a tendency to exploit artistic or unconventional acquaintances, living vicariously through them rather than risking a life outside the system.

This person is a great conversationalist and a skilled storyteller. It is well-respected in its work, as it is undaunted by decision-making and can outmaneuver practically anyone. It is a formidable strategist and a keen planner of schemes for advancement. Water Cats/Rabbits are always employed in lucrative careers and, due to their cunning and caution, almost always live to a dignified old age amidst elegance and abundance.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"This game of Cat and Mouse is one I would resist playing. Although both the Cat and the Rat have some similar traits, they are not very compatible. Both have strong needs for a home. One might imagine them rummaging through the IKEA catalogue together or co-choosing wallpaper for their new kitchen. But unfortunately, Rat and Cat disagree on just about everything. In conflict, they will forever elude each other: neither prepared to make concessions or take steps towards reconciliation. The Cat will be hissing and the Rat sulking. This testy relationship grows pickier and pettier by the day. However dissonant a chord they strike, once joined, it will be hard for this team to separate. They both cling to security. Divorce would lead both of them into the unknown. As they find the familiar reassuring, they would probably prefer to be mildly satisfied together than partnerless. Sexually, they tend to be excited by sadomasochistic games, tearing out each other’s hair in the midst of a passionate embrace. In time such practices will lead to a sexually destructive relationship. Prolonged commitment is unadvisable.",Ox:"A cozy pairing. Nestled against a rock-solid Ox, the Cat will have plenty to purr about. The Ox provides the anxious Cat with security, allowing the Cat to dedicate time to creative activities without having to worry about finances. In return, the Cat, naturally endowed with refinement, provides its more unrefined counterpart with much-needed sophistication. The Ox's bossiness is easily managed by a Cat, who typically chooses to avoid conflict. Quiet and submissive, the Cat is content to take a secondary role and allow the Bull to assert dominance, feeling secure in the presence of a strong, forceful mate. To show gratitude, the Cat showers the Ox with affection. Of course, the self-sacrificing Ox finds excessive displays of affection difficult to tolerate and may avoid gestures of tenderness or mock them. This attitude could prove frustrating for the affectionate Cat, who adores cuddling. With luck, in time, its feline companion will melt the Ox's icy resistance and perhaps even teach it a romantic trick or two.",Tiger:"A style clash. This couple might very possibly enter into a so-called “marriage of convenience”, but underneath roils a mute tension that screams, “Get me outta here!” With a Tiger/Cat union, it’s the Tiger who’s doing the silent shrieking. What then? The Cat usually has the money, and the Tiger, who married the Cat for the loot, is busy having a nervous breakdown. Tigers live for change and victory. Cats dream only of peace and quiet. Get the picture? No common ground. Trying to outwit each other, these two felines stealthily compete for the household throne. The Tiger goes at it with typical self-serving vengeance and the Cat skulks around the house seeking opportunities to entrap the Tiger. Imagine, two wily cats under the same roof. They merely tolerate each other. An occasional playful interlude can degenerate into a clawing, hissing brawl. Cats require security and build their nests with refinement and taste. The Tiger might enjoy these surroundings but, unlike the Cat, the Tiger craves change and favors a more Bohemian lifestyle. The seductive Tiger might be tempted to grab some of the Cat’s dough and dash off to the Amazon, leaving only a deep skid mark outside the Swiss bank. Even in bed, this pair is not apt to be compatible. The Tiger is aggressive, possessing such a raw, frank, pushy sexuality that the Cat’s delicate sensuality is overwhelmed. Cats require coaxing, seductive, slow-moving lovers and Tigers are ill-suited to satisfy this need. I see the Cat/Tiger match as either an intense summer romance, or perhaps a long-lived “loving friendship” wherein they get together in bed once in a blue moon for old times’ sake. Marriage? Only if the Cat has a private income and protects it from the Tiger’s spendthrift clutches.",Rabbit:"As long as they have loads of money, Cats can adore each other. Both need material comfort and love order. They are not deliriously reproductive: kids mess up the household and break the porcelain vases, are damned inconvenient, and expensive, too. Mr. and Ms. Cat are mutually cautious about cash. However, they usually live lavishly. They collect cruise brochures and set up trips to the safest, most luxurious zones of the globe. Switzerland, New Zealand, Arizona or the Cotswolds will do nicely. No danger, conflicts or funk, thank you very much. The Cat couple’s idea of fun at home is to snuggle in duvets, on a bed strewn with books about home decorating and gardening. They love to be pampered and may invite the chiropodist, hairdresser, masseur and yoga teacher to service them at home. Cats demand such perfection and find fault in so many areas that no one (least of all each ether) ever measures up. Reciprocal nitpicking is usually at the center of any dissonance between them. They do however make a cozy pair and so long as they have sufficient means at their disposal, a generally happy (and even sexy) couple.",Dragon:"The flamboyant Dragon’s exaggerated pizzazz does not suit the Cat ‘s need for discretion. The fire-breathing monster goes about wowing crowds with his pyrotechnic displays while the Cat sits by disdainfully, deeming the Dragon’s antics vulgar. The classy Cat finds all grandiose public exhibits absurd. He would much rather stay at home and polish the silver coffee urn. Although a Cat/Dragon marriage usually proves unfulfilling, there can be a positive aspect to this duo: a wise Dragon sometimes chooses a gentle, sensible Cat as savior. With much patience and forbearing on Kitty’s part, their marriage might work. Unfortunately, the gentle consideration the Cat lends to a tempestuous Dragon partner can never really be reciprocated. The Dragon needs to be in the limelight, to lead a gregarious life, careering around, currying ovation, and the domesticated Cat is often left at home, tending the household, where overly sensitive to the Dragon’s indifference, poor Kitty sits alone by the fire, doing a slow bum.",Snake:"The intuitive Snake and the philosophical Cat find each other reciprocally interesting. Both have keen minds and are deep thinkers. Should they run into trouble, this couple can rely on their mutual innate wisdom to steer them out of difficulties. The spendthrift Snake makes weekly shopping appointments with salespeople at Cartier and Dior. This upsets the careful, tradition-bound Cat, who doesn’t approve of the Snake’s penchant for the extravagant. Conflicts are easily resolved if the Cat is allowed to be in charge of the loot. However, unless the Cat learns to understand the Snake’s desperate need for the grandest accessories and surroundings, a powerful python partner may become a listless garden Snake. A Snake deprived can also be a hostile reptile. These two bons vivants can usually resolve their differences, whiling away an evening over a bottle of Pommard. As a couple, this pair oozes charm. They make excellent guests and can expect invitations to all the best parties. In, public, the Cat fears the Snake’s incessant flirtations, finding the Snake’s open, raw sexuality difficult to deal with. But Snakes have their irresistible ways with reticent Cat lovers. Both are potential psychics: if all else fails, they can always become traveling soothsayers.",Horse:"The very name of this union is catastrophe. Cats are sedate, laid back and reserved. Horses are pushy, antagonistic and outspoken. Clashes in everything from decorating style to sexual frequency will stand in the way of this lopsided couple’s happiness. Although both are devoted to pragmatism, each has a different way of dealing with material issues. Cats are cautious, even tightfisted with money. Horses flaunt their wealth openly and try to impress with their generosity. No meeting of minds ever occurs on this touchy subject. Cats are not much on public display. Horses love to show off. Cats like quiet, traditional surroundings. Horses adore bold fantasy settings. The Cat wants to stay at home listening to Brahms. The Horse wants to get up and boogie at the best disco in the funkiest section of town. Hard work is the Horse’s religion. The Cat seeks ways to live and work in luxury without disturbing one immaculately coiffured hair. Does this sound like a harmonious pair? Hardly. Moreover, in sexual settings, the Cat needs soft music, satin sheets and filmy negligees, while the Horse prefers a no-nonsense loft bed sans pajamas and plenty of loud marching music to reach ever-greater heights of fancy sexual athletics.",Goat:"Although initially they may seem ill suited, this pair will undoubtedly develop a solid love relationship. Cats and Goats are complementary. The Cat provides the dependent, creative Goat with just the right amount of down-home security, and the hypersensitive, capricious Goat amuses and keeps the Cat interested. Cats are serious and steady. Goats hardly ever follow the rules. Although normally disconcerted by such nonchalance, the Cat finds it disarming in a love partner. The Goat respects the Cat’s sound judgment and takes solace in Kitty’s ability to cope in a routine fashion. The Goat’s capacity for total surrender in love situations melts the sexually resistant Cat’s little heart. Their romantic life is dense with passion. Tenderness and marathon caressing sessions are the order of the day. The fewer children this couple has, the better. The Goat requires so much personal attention and caring from a Cat spouse that a brood of children who distract the Cat might make the Goat cranky and jealous.",Monkey:"These two people are intellectually well matched. They both enjoy being in cultural venues, seeking out new exhibitions or museums and learning about subjects of particular interest to one or both of them. The meeting of two like minds can be the basis of a lifetime of wedded harmony. Emotionally, however, there will be snags. The Cat hates change and does not enjoy surprises. Discretion, for the Cat, is nine-tenths of the law. Monkeys live for change, enjoy leaping about from place to place and adore being in the limelight, amusing cronies and carrying on high in public. Moreover, the Cat takes him- or herself very seriously. Not too many jokes allowed. Monkeys make fun of everything (including their mates) and think of the world as a giant silliness. The success and longevity of this relationship depends on the degree of passion the couple can extract from their intensely cerebral friendship. Neither lends much belief to the idea of syrupy romance, keeping their respective cynical distances from all “sentimental” notions. They may require a push from an outside source (e.g. Dicey love triangle, savvy therapist, good friend etc) to accept to surrender to the natural human impulse to love and be loved—no matter what!",Rooster:"This couple should think twice before taking the lifelong plunge into matrimony. The sex is mediocre at best. Although Cats are initially attracted by the haughty Rooster’s natural nobility and aura of reserve, they may be misinterpreting the Rooster’s real methods and motives. Basically, Roosters want to be free to roam and race about following the peripatetic bent of their roller-coaster existence. Cats like to stay at home, work long and hard at quiet jobs, get and stay rich. Lifestyle would quickly become a problem for this pair. With their individual approaches being so gapingly different, who, I ask you, would take out the garbage? Certainly not the refined Cat, who is too busy reading philosophical tomes and decorating magazines on a Louis XV chaise longue. As for the Rooster—he’s hardly ever home long enough to create any garbage, or babies. If the pair has the means (and nothing prevents them from earning money, as they are both hardworking, serious types) to hire help for the baser human chores, they can establish a solid, functional family life.",Dog:"In Chinese astrology, Cats and Dogs traditionally get on with each other. Although sexual intimacy is not the most salient point of contact here, companionship is. Everybody knows how important companionship is to an animal Dogs. Cats like to be safe and well housed too. This couple’s marriage is based on profound mutual affection and respect for each other’s opinions and aesthetic choices. Both Cats and Dogs have a marked tendency to mood swings. Both are critical and easily discouraged by the realities of everyday life and its various injustices. Although Dogs are more pessimistic, Cats can be testy and crotchety when the chips are down. Their complicity will be based largely on their mutual mistrust of human nature. Their shared cynicism is their consolation for putting up with an imperfect world. Both parties are dutiful and unafraid of working hard. Money should not be an issue. Mutual participation in professional and paraprofessional projects will lend strength to their union. The Dog’s spontaneous expressions of lapping affection might get on the Cat’s taut nerves. But one thing is for sure: the Cat can depend on the Dog’s loyalty which, in the cautious Cat’s heart, counts for a lot.",Pig:"Here’s a pair tailor-made for successfully carving out a bucolic country life together. Both creatures love nature and thrive in rural, bourgeois opulence. They both covet ownership of the finer things in life. With time, the Cat/Pig couple can expect to lead a civilized, charming life together in peace and tenderness, without suffering want or lack of mutual respect. The Cat, of course, has an artistic side, and will be the one to maintain decorum, keep neat flowerbeds and establish house rules. The Pig, an earthier character given to rustic manners and relaxed—even sloppy—habits, will appreciate the Cat’s attempt at forging a pristine existence for them. These people are both malleable enough to accept the other’s shortcomings and honor their partner’s needs. Piggy is lavishly sexual. Kitty is not. Piggy is rampantly erotic. Kitty is borderline prudish. At first, there may be some misunderstanding in this area, but in the long run, the Pig’s sensuality and open-mindedness about sex will break down the Cat’s hesitancy, and a good old sexual entente can be established for life."},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"This is a favorable year for Cat/Rabbits to make progress. The Snake admires your quiet charm and shares your identical taste in the finest luxuries. You, of course, might prefer castles on the Loire, and the Snake may fancy diamond necklaces from Cartier, but the similarity in taste is evident. Snakes are also philosophical and can work discreetly behind the scenes to achieve a great deal in a very short time. You enjoy tranquility and are comfortable with the kind of enduring beauty that belongs solely to the Snake. Hence, the atmosphere of this year does not clash with your aesthetic sensibilities. You will have time in the Snake year to assess what has been happening in your own personal life as well. Meditate or compose poems. Some emotional crisis will arise before the summer that threatens disappointment involving someone you care deeply about—a relative or an old friend. The event will shock you, and it concerns thoughtless comments or remarks made about your character. Try not to take it too seriously or allow it to ruin your friendship or mar the harmony in your family. Sometimes thoughtless people make terrible mistakes, but they do not realize how damaging those blunders can be for their closest and dearest."},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:`Horse years are renowned for their rapid pace and astonishing speed. Some might describe these years as 'dynamic'; I tend to think of them as wild and unpredictable. A great deal is happening, and it is usually related to work. Unlike the sedate, rather leisurely Snake, the Horse is a large, restless, muscular creature whose capacity for labor is legendary. Horses can cultivate their own food, construct their own houses, bake their own bread, and raise children and pets—all while simultaneously juggling three plates on sticks above their heads. They are remarkably talented and constantly busy. This, of course, is quite the opposite of you Cat/Rabbit individuals who enjoy quietude and seek (as long as there is someone to do the gardening and clean the stables) the tranquility of the countryside. So you will undoubtedly find the pace of the Horse year irritating. You may be surprised—even shocked and frightened—by the degree of impulsive interference that occurs in your personal space during this Horse year. You might be reading a book under a tree in the park and suddenly be startled by someone "working" there. Or you could be sunbathing on the beach and, out of nowhere, be instructed to "move along" by the lifeguard. Horse years are famous for encroaching on people's peace and quiet. Do not be alarmed. Be cautious. And if you do not want your life meddled with in an aggressive manner, do not cause any disturbances.`},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Yin Fire",prediction:"The Goat is one of your most fervent allies. Not that Goats are as refined or high-strung as you, but your characters complement each other—like how beige pairs with tones of brown or sage green. The atmosphere in the Goat year suits you. And even the most successful, wealthy, or famous of Goats desires to have the practical aspects of their life managed. Cat/Rabbits make excellent caretakers who look after their own and other people's possessions with a cautious eye. Hence, the Goat feels secure in your company and is more or less willing to rely on you to handle the organizing, so that he or she might frolic through a workday confident in the knowledge that their financial situation is being overseen by someone competent. You tend to complain a bit and suffer from physical ailments that are more imagined than real. The Goat understands you, listens to your laments, and even takes you seriously when others will not. You should spend this year not only accruing interest from your valuable offshore bank accounts but also gaining ground in your personal life. The issues and unresolved problems that you were encountering early in the Goat year will dissipate as if by magic after the month of March. Things will quiet down in your home life because you can breathe easier and feel less anxious and defensive than you did last year."},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Yang Earth",prediction:"One of the most prominent characteristics of Monkeys (and consequently, of the years in which they govern us all) is that, deep down, they truly do not care. You Cat/Rabbits care intensely—about everything. So, sometimes during Monkey years, you feel frustrated. You wish people would do something about the chaos, reinforce the bridges, repair the roads, improve the schools, and establish some form of properly functioning public transport system. As you are somewhat of a meticulous person when things do not work as they should, you are an easy target for experiencing this year in a state of heightened irritation. This will be a year of social disruption for a variety of reasons. One of these is the fact that Monkeys can solve most problems for others, but rarely for themselves. So, when it is their turn to govern and the problems become theirs, they want no part of it. It is too complex, too difficult, too much visibility. Monkeys dislike all of that. They simply want to be free to be entertaining and intelligent. The Monkey prefers to continue its cheerful life independently with its loved ones and desires no part of the authority that comes with ruling countless people. Needless to say, the Monkey’s carefree, hands-off attitude toward governance irritates you Cat/Rabbits. Yet, because you never engage in conflict, you remain in the background, stewing. To alleviate this general feeling of irritation, I suggest twelve months of bed rest, hot water bottles, silken sheets, and a gentle, loving companion."},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Yin Earth",prediction:"Your inclination for luxury will need to be curtailed this year. Roosters expect us to behave economically and adhere closely to our budgets. As a general rule, Cat/Rabbits do not scatter money carelessly as if it were autumn leaves, but they do tend to part with large sums of money at once for significant purchases such as expensive antiques, sterling silver tableware, porcelain dinner services, paintings by old masters, and castles in Spain. This year, you should not acquire any of the aforementioned items. Simply rely on what you already possess. Organize your stock portfolio and ensure your bank has not made accounting errors while you were resting with your gentle companion from last year's break. Use the time you are not spending at auctions and antique shops to converse with your family. Discover what they have been thinking about you and perhaps even about what portion of your funds they have had their eye on. You always have enough; they almost never do. Do be cautious. Do not let anyone's sad stories persuade you to open your safety deposit box. Address any physical symptoms that you cannot seem to alleviate with your customary dietary supplements, homeopathic remedies, and/or general alternative cures. Sometimes—only sometimes—doctors can be helpful."},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Yang Metal",prediction:"Traditionally, in the West, Dogs and Cat/Rabbits are perceived as adversaries. In Chinese astrology, however, this is not the case. You Cat/Rabbit individuals appreciate the dutiful, anxious Dog, and it, in turn, admires your calm, quiet, and generally gentle nature. The only aspect of the Dog year that might adversely affect you Cat/Rabbits is the aura of liberalism and near-revolution that clouds the political scene in almost every country on the planet. Dog years are fraught with dissent. Cats dislike disagreement and avoid disputes. Hence, the highly charged atmosphere prevalent in this Dog year may leave you with a severe case of nervousness. You fear upheaval and revolution because you generally comply with the system and enjoy the benefits of its privileges. Should the government be overthrown, you might well lose some of these advantages. The mere thought of having to hand-wash your table linens from Porthault or grant the household staff a raise gives you goosebumps. You will enjoy this Dog year only if you can overcome the fear of loss and accept that social change is necessary for the good of all. Besides, you hardly ever host those lavish dinner parties for twelve anymore because they are simply outdated."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Yin Metal",prediction:"The Pig admires your discretion and tact. Nevertheless, the year may bring emotional upsets. These will concern family and (of course) money. In late Spring, there will be an inheritance or a gift bestowed upon a single family member. If you are the recipient of this good fortune, keep it confidential. Boasting by someone less discreet will ignite serious conflict. You dislike dramatic scenes and will undoubtedly suffer a panic attack. Excuse yourself and remain absent until tempers have cooled. This year is one of abundance, so you will feel inclined to invest some money. Any real estate you purchase must be structurally sound and not require too much renovation, as in Pig years, the work tends to cost more than the actual house. Beware of dishonest financial advice. This year, many deceptive stock schemes are circulating. In matters of the heart, the Pig will bless you with a highly charged, passionate romance with someone you have always known. Your health is generally sound in Pig years. All in all, this will be a quiet, prosperous year for the cautious Cat/Rabbit—as long as you remember to disappear when family crises arise."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Yang Water",prediction:"This is not the most encouraging of years for you Cat/Rabbit individuals. Why? Because the Rat is envious of your settled, secure lifestyle and would not in the least mind disrupting it. Rats thrive on drama and excitement. You prefer safety and time for quiet pursuits in the countryside. Of course, you are the wiser of the two signs, but you prefer not to have to fight to achieve your desires. Rats seek power; they want to dominate and are not afraid of confrontation. Do not perform any public stunts that will attract attention to you during this sharp-edged year. It is not the time to run for mayor of your town or even to seek the presidency of your French conversation class. Nor is it the year to splurge on frivolous items, showy vehicles, or mansions in upscale neighborhoods. Your finances could come under scrutiny from tax authorities. It is better to maintain a low profile and spend weekends listening to classical music, reading history books, or polishing your antique clocks. You might enjoy a brief romantic encounter or two with someone charming and openly sensual. Take care to protect your reputation for refinement and good taste."},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Yin Water",prediction:'In Ox years, you Cat/Rabbit individuals tend to feel out of place. You are not inclined towards strenuous labor; you despise the very notion of hauling barges down muddy riverbanks or lifting bales of cotton all day long in the blazing sun or biting cold. You are an indoor sort of person who, for sport and adventure, might take a stroll in your garden among the hydrangea and heliotrope beds. The Ox is a formidable worker; it willingly exerts itself in any weather whatsoever in the name of "hard work." Exertion and everything related to industriousness and labor are integral to its belief system. Your reluctance to soil your hands or dishevel your attire in the name of toil tends to irritate the Ox. So, this year, you will need to evade the taskmaster and expect to be heavily criticized for any unnecessary displays of snobbery or excessive refinement. Your home life (unless you are married to an Ox) should not be seriously affected by the adverse atmosphere. Stay close to family. Tinker in your wood shop. Teach yourself to knit, tat, or do needlepoint. Whatever you do, do not attempt to compete with the powerful Ox in any project where brute force is a deciding factor.'},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Yang Wood",prediction:"Tiger years are characterized by impulsive, rash moves and risky changes of direction. In the early part of the year, you might still be recovering from the impact the last couple of challenging years have had on your gentle spirit. Once you are back on your feet and feeling energetic and well, you will be pleasantly surprised at how lenient, easygoing, and carefree the atmosphere is in this Tiger year. Many of the significant events occurring this year will directly affect you. An individual or group of people whom you did not know until now will approach you at various times for your assistance or involvement in their projects. Remember, you work best with Pigs and Goats. Whatever you do, do not become involved with a headstrong Horse or a daring Dragon; their very style irritates your delicate nervous system. By year's end, you should be feeling wonderful and perhaps even a bit sentimental. Why not spend some quality time with old friends from school or take your mother or father on an exotic trip somewhere where you can stroll along a beach and learn more about your childhood. Health looks relatively good this year for Cat/Rabbit individuals. Adhere to your diet and exercise routine, or you will spend the better part of next year trying to lose excess weight."},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:'Some aspects of your romantic life require attention. Either you or your significant other is dissatisfied with certain elements of your relationship. Are you bored? Is he or she too busy to be available when you are? Is one of you suspicious of the other’s extracurricular activities? More than likely, you have allowed too many issues to be ignored, and now they are subtly emerging and filling the air with tension. Nothing is worse than silent mealtimes and unspoken differences of opinion. If you (who dislike confrontation) cannot discuss the problems at hand, seek professional counseling and bring your beloved along. Financially, you are in better shape than you have been in ages. This is your very own year in which to plan the next twelve years of your life. Ask yourself seriously, "Where do I want to be in 2047?" Then, formulate a plan of action to reach that goal, one year at a time, over the next ten or twelve years. You would be much happier if you lived outside of the city. Should you find yourself in an urban environment, acquiring a secondary residence in the countryside might be a good place to begin your plan. You need birdsong and antiques, refinement and natural surroundings to keep your hypochondria at bay.'},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"The Dragon's atmosphere of boisterous parties and spirited conversation does not do much for you discreet Cat/Rabbit individuals. You are always better off in the quiet of your own comfortable home or at a cultural event or concert in the park. The Dragon harbors no grudges against the Cat/Rabbit species, but its demands are not few. Dragons want everyone to pay attention to them, to follow their rules, and applaud their antics. Generally, you Cat/Rabbit individuals are too busy devising quiet ways to take over a giant corporation or buy a winery in Bordeaux to bother attending all the Dragon-like festivities available in this noisy, celebratory year. The Dragon year is yet another good reason to have purchased that country retreat. Go there as often as you can. Travel when there is no traffic and return to town when others are already back. Or better still, seclude yourself all year in your manor house in the remotest Bavaria and write that book you have been meaning to start. Dragons, frankly, are not your most rewarding companions. If you choose to remain in the thick of things, they will do everything in their power to draw you into their flamboyant lifestyle, where you will be tempted to overindulge, drink too much, and party until you collapse. Where will your twelve-year plan be then? One year behind schedule."}}},i={introduction:`Magnificent Dragon, self-assured, dynamic, and rarely inconspicuous, you are a born master of ceremonies. Be it fireworks, parties, festivals, holidays, or rallies: you know how to initiate events and keep them lively. You are spirited and endowed with power and good fortune.

People admire you. You can be flamboyant—and a bit of a braggart. When you believe you are correct, you are unyielding. In business, you appear formidable. You are shrewd and not easily deceived. But even you, dauntless Dragon, are not invincible. All those flames are merely camouflage. Beneath, you are easily influenced, a pushover. You are deeply moved by the sight of a weeping willow. Sentimentality lies just beneath the surface of that scaly green exterior. You cannot resist its emotional pull.

Faithful to friends and loyal to family, you are sometimes less so in romantic matters. You are devastatingly attractive, and romantic too. You long to retreat into one cave after another with a series of passionate lovers who simultaneously excite, challenge, and thrill. You dream of a lifelong moment of ecstasy.

Engage in flirtation with a hard-driving Rat or a clever Monkey. But when you choose a mate, select a reliable Rooster or a Tiger (your accomplice). Do not bother with taciturn Oxen. Outspoken Dogs will both attract and challenge you. A regulated, disciplined family and school life in childhood may frustrate your need for applause and unearned attention, but it may also set you on a more realistic path than one you would have chosen yourself. Your mid-life crisis will be spectacular! But if you are still alive at age fifty, your hard work will begin to yield rewards. You know how to learn from your mistakes. Dare I offer you advice? Do not let your ego overpower your intellect. Practice laughing at yourself in the mirror. Lower your profile. Consume plenty of humble pie.`,elements:{Wood:`The Wood Dragon is the most amiable and sociable of all Dragons. He is a ray of sunshine, full of goodwill and helpfulness, freely offering advice and assisting his friends whenever called upon. He is a devoted partner, never shirking duty or responsibility once accepted.

This Dragon also possesses a special capacity for profound philosophical thought. His ability to handle abstract concepts and synthesize ideas from them is well-known and highly regarded among his peers.

The Wood Dragon is also a peacemaker. He can swiftly defuse a potentially explosive situation with his clever tongue, injecting humor and light-hearted logic into stressful circumstances. His counsel is often sought by influential individuals, as he has an uncanny talent for seeing through ambiguous situations and uncovering the truth. Although he does not consciously intend to cause pain, his incisive comments often strike a sensitive chord.

Wood Dragons are so perceptive and open-minded that they could become seers or spiritual leaders. Concepts from realms beyond our world seem to reach this individual, and the Wood Dragon often knows what will happen before it occurs. This gift enables him to pursue astrology, study metaphysics, or become a prophet or healer. A Wood Dragon could also enter the medical and religious professions or even politics and government. Because he is multi-talented, he might choose painting, sculpting, writing, or acting, but whatever his choice, the Wood Dragon will never be bored or boring. His life is filled with activities and hobbies. As long as he can sew or build, plant and pot, paint and decorate after work, the Wood Dragon is content.

This artistic inclination diminishes some of the stigma of fussiness that characterizes so many other Dragons. Wood Dragons have a Bohemian streak that allows them the freedom to live in a relaxed manner, to forget to replace the barbecue cover, or to resist the urge to straighten every painting in someone else's house.

All Dragons are fun-loving and festive, but the Wood Dragon is the master of dramatic parties. Wherever he finds himself, the Wood Dragon ensures he is the center of attention. Salvador Dali was a Wood Dragon—recall his penchant for spectacle. He was no recluse; a true Wood Dragon, Dali yearned for company, lived for theatricality, and exhibited himself shamelessly. From his outlandish costumes to his shockingly wild sweeping statements, Dali was the quintessential Wood Dragon.

This Dragon is not particularly courageous or enduring. Adversity throws him off course, disturbs his sensitive core, and causes him to retreat. As the Wood Dragon is not aggressive—one might even call him a reluctant Dragon—he shies away from conflict, preferring diplomacy to aggression and love to hate. Because he is a philosopher and wishes to be regarded as an instrument of harmony, the Wood Dragon becomes involved in the most convoluted discussions over simple issues. The important thing for him is to appear knowledgeable: do not hesitate to suggest he cease speaking if he distracts you from the matter at hand. He may be furious—but his rage will not last long.`,Fire:`Fire is the Dragon's inherent trait, making this the most quintessential Dragon. It is certain of its superiority, blatant about its lofty ambitions, and entirely self-driven. Fire Dragons rarely require assistance or seek a loan, because when they desire something, they take it.

This energetic, spirited, dynamic individual is always someone to be reckoned with. Whether a Fire Dragon is born into humble beginnings or enters the world with immense privilege, it stands out from the crowd. It makes a name for itself and causes significant trouble for anyone in the immediate vicinity who does not wish to comply with its plans.

It is also exceptionally generous. Devoted family members and favored friends praise its loyalty and open-handedness. It is intelligent, quick-witted, and gregarious. A wry smile often accompanies its brisk remarks, as it perceives the irony in everything. An innate natural authority lends it an air of grandeur and compels it to behave in an irritatingly condescending manner. It inflates itself like the worst kind of dictatorial monarch, appearing simultaneously to look down its nose and inspect you for flaws.

Even so, the Fire Dragon is one of the most attractive, charismatic creatures in the Chinese zodiac. Its personal magnetism is legendary. People cannot leave it alone. It is bafflingly contradictory. It is intensely sensual and full of wisdom. It constantly offers advice and is not afraid of taking major risks or embarking on eccentric campaigns to achieve the impossible. It can be warm-hearted and giving, but when crossed, it is ruthlessly vindictive.

The Fire Dragon is impressive. Upon meeting it, we are initially taken aback. It presents an image of courtesy coupled with masterful hospitality, a kind of inherent nobility. But make no mistake: it may be fabulous to behold and imposing to encounter, but it is also vulnerable. The Fire Dragon's ardor to achieve and succeed is born of true passion.

Likewise its sentimentality: despite its apparent armor, the Fire Dragon's feelings are easily hurt. Its skin is thinner than those green scales would have you believe. And, like many great people, it is a victim of emotional highs and lows which keep it in a dangerous state of nervous tension. It must be wary of overextending itself, of diluting its cohesive forces by having its finger in too many pies, and of being toppled by a craftier, less generous soul than itself.

One of the greatest strengths of the Fire Dragon is its ability to acknowledge its mistakes. Although it is always making sweeping gestures, involving itself in grandiose schemes, and craving attention, it is not afraid of the criticism its behavior often attracts—it seems to fuel its fervor. Its determination to dominate frequently places it in the public eye, and its earth-shaking decisions often put it on the public firing line. But the Fire Dragon can handle criticism. Its ego (unlike many Dragon egos) never obstructs its desire to be king. A composed individual, it understands the necessity of diplomacy and knows how to withdraw gracefully from untenable positions to clear the way for a comeback at a more opportune time. Obviously, politics suit this Dragon perfectly.

The Fire Dragon adores engaging in vast projects. It is enterprising and will not involve itself in anything trivial or that is not guaranteed to reward its efforts with world renown. Although it truly wishes to be effective and use its intelligence wisely, it is not interested in thankless behind-the-scenes work that might not lead it to leadership and celebrity.

Does the Fire Dragon desire a better world? Yes, it does. But it also wishes to create it itself, name it after itself, and rule over its obedient subjects.`,Earth:`The Earth Dragon is the most ego-driven of all Dragons. It requires flattery, applause, and the brightest spotlight under which to manifest its magic. When its ego is nurtured, its mind becomes vibrant. Tell it how magnificent it is, and it will preen and swell to larger-than-life proportions, capable of achieving astonishing feats. Compliments and approval are the fuel of its daily existence, and without them, it is lost, desperate, and susceptible to depression and even addiction.

Earth Dragons possess abundant charm. They effortlessly attract more members of the opposite sex than they can manage. Their captivating physical presence commands every eye. People never disregard an Earth Dragon, who shines like a beacon in any crowd, drawing hordes of admirers.

The Earth Dragon desires to help. It is always willing to involve itself in the problems of others, offering aid and assistance to friends, family, and even those it does not know well. The Earth element bestows an uncommon gentleness upon the spirited Dragon nature, and this Dragon is easily affected by the pain and struggles of others. It offers sympathy and even financial assistance to those it feels need its helping hand. As it is completely ego-driven, it will also give its shirt to anyone who pays it tribute.

I would not advise anyone to confront this Dragon over personal policies or ideals. The Earth Dragon is not only serious about its convictions, but it can become passionate and even dangerous if crossed—especially by people it considers its friends. Friends are its lifeline: family is necessary, and business acquaintances are pleasant, but what truly matters are friends. The Earth Dragon pampers and caters to them. It invites them to dinner, takes them to lunch, and brings them along on its extensive fishing trips. Wherever there is an Earth Dragon, you will find a host of fine, seasoned, genuinely loyal companions on whom it can rely and for whom the feeling is mutual.

Career choices for this Dragon should always consider the necessity of the spotlight. Money alone would never be enough to motivate this Dragon to work: no Earth Dragon will be content performing accounting tasks in an unseen office somewhere. Even if it decides to be a philosopher or a poet, it must be given top billing and abundant visibility.

This Dragon will never be solitary. It will always choose to be married or at least committed to someone it loves. It will probably not be capable of sexual fidelity, as it is so captivating and outrageously charming that people fall at its feet for the potential delight of a one-night stand or an afternoon of stolen bliss. But its unfaithfulness is not treason. It will never abandon its family, as no matter how mischievous it knows itself to be, it understands that its family reveres it most and will provide it with more adulation than a thousand fleeting encounters. The Earth Dragon is level-headed and will never sacrifice security for superficiality.

Strangely enough, this Dragon is also somewhat of a Bohemian. Although it requires constant attention and depends on its public's applause for its sanity, it would prefer to live as an outsider, a rebel, a non-conformist. It delights in eccentricity: no Earth Dragon is happy as a middle-class bourgeois living in the suburbs. It desires flair, seeking out the unconventional and hunting down the rare. Sometimes it leans towards laxity, forsaking discipline in favor of indulging in peculiar pastimes such as associating with idlers, drinking, gambling, or taking drugs. This can be its downfall, and it should monitor its bad habits from an early age to enjoy a long, healthy life.`,Metal:`This Dragon allows nothing to impede its work. It is a Doer. Projects abound—the more challenging and demanding, the better. Metal Dragons dislike being idle; they always choose activity over inertia. No sitting on the sidelines for this Dragon, who never accepts a secondary role. Like time, Metal Dragons wait for no one.

Astrologers say that, of all Dragons, those influenced by Metal are the least favored by the gods. They often encounter situations where the atmosphere (and the company) is unsavory, and are then drawn into intrigue and, ultimately, misfortune. Perversion and even sadistic tendencies are common among Metal Dragons. Their type puzzles even the most astute psychoanalysts, as they appear so strong, stable, amiable, and gentle.

Even the politest, nicest Metal Dragon often finds joy in deviant behavior. Its salvation lies in being clever enough to know how to use this inclination constructively—otherwise, it may fall victim to its own (real or imagined) demons.

The Metal Dragon is tough and believes in mind over matter. Thanks to its power, it need not be afraid or shrink from asserting its way out of unpleasant circumstances. It is both knowledgeable and determined where its work and ideals are concerned, and will always know how to extricate itself and rise to the top—even if it chooses not to.

This Dragon is ambitious beyond all our dreams. It desires to be someone significant, and it earnestly wishes everyone else to notice. It is happiest when involved in some lofty cause. Anything from orphans to orchestras will suffice, but the Metal Dragon should always have a favorite charitable cause that keeps it absorbed and interested enough to stay out of trouble.

It needs to travel to distant lands. Jobs in public relations or international banking or politics will suit its restless nature. It is very observant and gifted with a prodigious memory. Journalism or scholarship will suit its passion for collecting facts and extrapolating knowledge from them. Traveling outside its normal environment provides just the challenge the Metal Dragon needs to feel that its mind is being kept sharp. Also, it is attracted by cult religions, which allow it to deviate from its childhood ethics and explore new ways of solving philosophical problems. The Metal Dragon might undertake a pilgrimage to the highest regions of Tibet where it dines with monks in rarefied atmospheres and returns renewed, quiet, and calm. The Metal Dragon is perpetually seeking new approaches to old problems.

The Metal Dragon is responsible and makes an excellent parent. It will usually prefer to be married or at least committed—even though it strays occasionally, if only for novelty and perhaps an unusual learning experience.

Metal Dragons typically earn substantial money in stable, sensible jobs. They can assume management positions and bring order out of the worst corporate chaos. They can handle the most challenging issues and invigorate any group with their wise and humanitarian leadership policies. Elect it president, yes, but do not hand over the purse strings. The Metal Dragon spends money like a drunken lottery winner. And it dislikes being told to be more economical. It desires no back talk or criticism from its subordinates and will display its superiority—even at the expense of its composure.

Its temper control is very sensitive. The Metal Dragon erupts into wild fits of anger and will direct them at whoever happens to be brave or foolish enough to confront it. These tantrums do not last long, yet they are so impressive that more rational people may question the perpetrator's sanity or at least find it difficult to forgive it. It should be warned against having these outbursts when not among friends.

Above all, the Metal Dragon loves money. Its work is important to it, and so are its family and friends, but most of all, it desires to live lavishly, be waited on and deferred to, have meals prepared and be cared for, to laugh and joke with its adored friends, to gaze at beauty, and to curl up in the comforting lap of luxury. It will be happy to work towards this goal, but it will also be greatly annoyed if it does not reach it. A Metal Dragon who fails in this regard would be capable of marrying for money, living as a courtesan, or settling down in a posh nunnery for the rest of its days.`,Water:`Are Water Dragons contradictory? And contrary? You can be sure of it! But even though influenced by water and seemingly relaxed, this Dragon is exceptionally sensual and sexual. It is an inveterate show-off throughout its life. Its Dragon-like dynamism is only slightly tempered by the influence of Water. It does not present itself like other spirited, noisy, sometimes arrogant or bombastic Dragons. Instead, it gives the impression of high-born gentility. It appears well-mannered, well-bred, scholarly, and informed.

You can rely on this individual: friendship is its exceptionally strong point. When it takes a liking to someone, and the feeling is mutual, the Water Dragon vows to involve itself forever in that person's welfare and well-being. It is thoughtful, calls its friends weekly, cheers them when they are down, and gives them a boost or even a loan in a difficult situation. The Water Dragon is home-loving, adores having a large house, a supportive mate, and many offspring, pets, and other comforts. It revels in inviting companions over for drinks and dinners, card games, a round of badminton, or simply a long, pleasant conversation. It is also possessive, showing off its property, boasting about the new trees it has planted, and the special blossoms of its flaming yellow lilies.

It is also a curious person—like all Dragons, but more so. The Water Dragon is nosy: it cannot glimpse a slip of paper lying on a table or desk without intensely desiring to know what is on it. "Where did you get this letter? Who wrote it? Are you going to answer? What will you say?" are just a few of the questions that Water Dragons can devise to insinuate themselves into every corner of your private life.

The Water Dragon's contradictory nature often makes it unsure of its ambition. On the surface, it seems driven with clear goals for success, but underneath, it is not as energetically involved in "getting there" as it appears. If having money and achieving success means conformity, you can count this Dragon out. If being a star depends on kowtowing to a bunch of witless, cigar-smoking producers, the Water Dragon will back out before it begins. Either success comes because of its talent, its unusual gifts, and its remarkable brilliance, or it simply cannot be bothered. It would rather go live in the country and raise goats.

This Dragon is intuitive and can advise you on almost anything. If it does not know an answer to a direct question, it will say so. But it will always have an opinion and will probably know where to look for any facts it is missing. It has the capacity to be a true seer. It can sense coming events that will occur in the future for others.

Love is its main objective. Even though it has affairs and flings galore, and seduces and captivates lovers far into its old age, what truly matters for the Water Dragon is genuine love. Family, children, and long friendships are the mainstay of its emotional stability. It lives for improving the structure of its family and thrives on the approval and gratitude it receives from them.

Most of all, the Water Dragon is creative. Its ideas are innovative. It knows how to combine the new with the established and devise plans that surprise us with their improvisational yet solid practicality. It is also economical—even penny-pinching. It likes to be careful with money so it does not have to work at that dreadful office where conformity threatens to spoil its enjoyment.

The greatest dilemma facing any Water Dragon is caused by its multitude of talents: it finds it difficult to eliminate any in favor of a single pursuit. Most Water Dragons can paint, write, invent, dance, and even sing. They are amusing, attractive, and easy to like. Early on, when it becomes obvious to the young Water Dragon that it will be forced to choose one discipline over another, it may hesitate. It wants to imagine, because of its vast stores of energy, that it can one day do it all, have it all, and be everything to everyone. If it does not make some definite choice before the age of twenty, undertake a course of study that offers it a solid future or profession, it had better inherit a lot of money from its rich Uncle Harry. A clever Water Dragon can happily spend its formative years as a professional creative genius or even as an idler. But when age thirty arrives, bringing with it responsibility, children, and the desire for security, an under-educated or unemployed Water Dragon whose finances do not match its self-image may indeed end up dissatisfied.

My advice? Structure. Discipline. Focus.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"This is an absolutely delicious marriage: the Chinese claim it as one of their best-arranged unions. The restless Rat will be warmed by the heat of the dashing Dragon and the Dragon will bask in the Rat’s generous applause. These two will complement each other beautifully. Guaranteed bliss. With the strong-willed Dragon around, the Rat will be happy to give up total control: anxieties slowly subside, bringing peace and comfort. The Dragon is so emotionally effusive that the burden of worry will be taken off the poor little Rat’s shoulders. Bigger and bolder, the Dragon will carry the weight of the loving Rat’s turmoil. The Rat will not feel competitive about the Dragon’s position of strength in this couple, happy to stand in the shadows of a fervent friend/mate. The Dragon and Rat team will feel like king and queen. In the Rat’s eyes, the Dragon does no wrong. All the better for the lucky Dragon who loves to shine. The dazzling Dragon is so bright and exciting that even the Rat’s usual hearty appetite for sex may be overwhelmed and suddenly wane. Despite his innate wisdom, the proud Dragon may fail to see the problem (The Dragon’s ego can be bigger than his brain at times.) and place blame on the Rat. A relaxed, rational discussion will clear the air, and in no time, the Dragon’s conversational fireworks will re-ignite the Rat’s temporarily diminished sensuality.",Ox:"Be prepared for plenty of late-night squabbles in an Ox/Dragon combo. Both believe they are righter than right. The Dragon dictates his will over the opinionated Ox and the Bull bullies back. The Ox has little patience with vanity. The Ox’s indifference to the Dragon’s fiery appearance is a perpetual disappointment to the Dragon’s ego. The glamorous, extravagant Dragon loves to spend money but, with the Ox counting pennies, feels hampered and ill at ease. The Dragon’s wandering eye unsettles the faithful Ox who rarely strays from a good sexual union – he just doesn’t have time! Too busy working. With so much conflict, how can this duo reconcile? Their mutual love of home and family could save them from total despair. Both enjoy sex, although the Ox’s routine techniques may bore the Dragon, whose sentimental nature yearns for puffy clouds of pink cotton candy to enhance lovemaking. He won’t often see fireworks with the Ox. Also, the methodical Ox expects a regular living schedule. The Dragon, however, favors a more erratic time code, exorbitant stormy sex for a week followed by peace and quiet for three. An excellent business partnership, this union is not recommended for either marriage or romance—unless the Dragon can be free to roam and hunt excitement elsewhere.",Tiger:"Sexed! The Tiger/Dragon love relationship bears serious consideration. Combined, their strength is almost excessive. And energy! Enough to fuel several large power plants. There is EGO flashing in red neon all over this couple. Overbearing and self-propelled, they are both a bit too much. But as a pair, they can succeed. Despite an excess of commando muscle, this combo lives peaceably together. Mutual respect and admiration offsets the expected clashes. The dashing Dragon begs for constant flattery and applause. However, the strong-minded Tiger finding the pontificating Dragon tiresome and teases the spotlight away. The Tiger is undaunted by fire-breathing antics. In fact, the intrepid Tiger loves a good shouting match and respects a worthy opponent. The generous Dragon is amused by and tolerates the Tiger’s love of danger and precipitous behavior. In short, these two get along. Tiger with Dragon is not only a sensual match. They carry themselves with bravado and flair. An air of madness colors everything they do. People flock to their home to bask in their aura and share in the high of their hazardous love. Not afraid to share power, they take turns sitting on the throne, complicity taking precedence over their individual roles. This relationship is good for marriage. Battles will be waged, but at the end of the day the force of their attraction ensures they will be lovers for life. Entwined in their own whirlwind of passion and steamy sex, this couple knows the road to heaven. The Dragon sets the tawny Tiger alight and the rapacious Tiger devours the dashing Dragon’s scalding hot fire. Enjoy!",Rabbit:"The flamboyant Dragon’s exaggerated pizzazz does not suit the Cat ‘s need for discretion. The fire-breathing monster goes about wowing crowds with his pyrotechnic displays while the Cat sits by disdainfully, deeming the Dragon’s antics vulgar. The classy Cat finds all grandiose public exhibits absurd. He would much rather stay at home and polish the silver coffee urn. Although a Cat/Dragon marriage usually proves unfulfilling, there can be a positive aspect to this duo: a wise Dragon sometimes chooses a gentle, sensible Cat as savior. With much patience and forbearing on Kitty’s part, their marriage might work. Unfortunately, the gentle consideration the Cat lends to a tempestuous Dragon partner can never really be reciprocated. The Dragon needs to be in the limelight, to lead a gregarious life, careering around, currying ovation, and the domesticated Cat is often left at home, tending the household, where overly sensitive to the Dragon’s indifference, poor Kitty sits alone by the fire, doing a slow bum.",Dragon:"This relationship is almost too volatile for any long-term good to come of it. What we have here is a lifetime battle royal for supremacy. In competitive situations, neither Dragon can allow the other’s gigantic ego to prevail, so whether it’s a pitched combat over who gets to manage the TV remote or a tussle about who drives the car on the next trip to the supermarket, the air will always be full of strife. At first, all this emotional power play may seem to the Dragon couple like a love storm of glorious emotion. They are not ill suited sexually and, even when they are furious with each other, may have some of the most exciting sex of their lives together. Yet, day-to-day living threatens to be so highly charged, so noisy and fraught with shouting and name-calling, that one wonders if a few moments of occasional earth-shaking sex is worth it. Unless it’s irreversible, I advise against this marriage. Two giant uncompromising, fire-breathing beasts may well be doomed to set each other’s hearts ablaze, but they are patently unsuited to keeping the home fires burning.",Snake:"In Chinese astrological parlance, these two are considered kissin’ cousins. The Dragon adores sporting a gorgeous, attractive, sexy Snake partner and the quiet, subtle Snake admires the Dragon’s world-beating flamboyance and style. In turn, Dragon protects Snake. Snake coddles Dragon’s ego and lets Dragon blab away without so much as a hint of criticism. Of course, no relationship with any Dragon can ever be calm, but the Snake/Dragon duo comes close to being a levelheaded, harmonious union. Wisely, the Snake never confronts the Dragon’s ego head-on. Snakes deal subtly with clashes, slithering and examining all sides before striking at just the right spot to get results. Sexually—with the Snake’s huge capacity for erotic activity and the Dragon’s giant appetite and innate talent for same—you can just imagine ... the chemistry is sublime. They agree on living luxuriously, too. The Dragon buys endless scrumptious accessories for the Snake’s pleasure and the Snake allows the Dragon—within reason—to indulge in filling the house with gadgetry. Their home life is peachy. They make a handsome couple. It’s truly a match made in heaven.",Horse:"This couple will, no doubt, boast vociferously of having fallen in love at first sight. Both of these effusive people are firm believers in falling in love as a way of life. The sex meter will be permanently set to hot and heavy mode. They won’t be able to keep their hands off each other. Fact is, sex is about the only thing that distracts these two from a full-time war of wills which inevitably besets their relationship. Horses are authoritarian and don’t like to be told what to do. Dragons like to dominate and hate to be bossed around. Each one is proud, touchy, irritable, self-centered and headstrong. Neither is acquiescent. The Dragon, at least, is sentimental, but the Horse is hard-nosed and tough-minded and knows how to make the Dragon cry. The Dragon is the less conventional of the two and will not hesitate to embarrass the socially correct Horse in public for revenge. I also see money conflicts here. The Dragon and the Horse like to spend. If allowed to have their way, they’ll be broke and in debt ail the time. This ill-suited couple is only happy during the initial, sexy infatuation stage. From there on it’s all downhill. No marriage plans? Keep it that way.",Goat:"In Chinese astrological circles, this is said to be a sound marriage. Goats are essentially dependent. They are easily swayed and don’t mind being bamboozled and manipulated by their loved ones. Dragons need to command direct operations and dominate. Goat’s good-natured passivity. The acquiescent Goat inspires the Dragon to protect and be chivalrous and thrives in the security provided by Dragon’s authority. Their sexual life together will be as near to an erotic dream as you can get. Dragons like to take charge and Goats like to lie there and be loved. Being two very sentimental as well as sensual beings, these two will know instinctively how to blend sex with affection. Their intimacies will be satisfying and frequent.",Monkey:"Despite the obvious differences in their characters, these two have a lot going for them. The Dragon is bombastic and needs to be adored, yet reveres the Monkey’s keen intelligence and ability to see around corners. Monkeys love spectacle and invariably enjoy the show Dragons put on. Dragons get themselves embroiled in world problems. Monkeys are born solvers of problems—big and little. There is plenty of room for personal evolution in this couple. Impressed by the efficiency of the Monkey’s exceptional mind, the Dragon (atypically) will become almost dependent, let up on the accelerator from time to time and even take an occasional back seat to Monkey’s brilliance. Monkeys enjoy being appreciated for their skillful talents, are not particularly interested in the number one position, and let a Dragon bask in the footlights. As a result of this clever balance, the Dragon/Monkey match becomes a strong bond, built on compromise and mutual respect. Sex, however, may not be the strongest element that binds these two. The Monkey’s normally healthy appetite seems moderate by comparison to the Dragon’s voracious and conspicuous need for consumption of his or her mate’s intimate favors.",Rooster:"Both passion and glamour are missing from this otherwise well-balanced relationship. It is workable. Dragon protects with gusto and Rooster obeys with serious intent to do the right thing. Neither is ecstatic in this arrangement but, then, neither is blatantly unhappy. Roosters recognize and respect the Dragon’s need to shine, to assert superiority over others and go out and beat the world at its game. Despite sometimes flamboyant outward appearances, the Rooster is a rank conservative. Roosters do want to voice their truths and implement their ideals. But they don’t show off. With a brave and daring Dragon partner, the Rooster can carry on being quietly cocky while the Dragon plays the conspicuous role. I’m afraid the Dragon’s exorbitant sexual needs may prove overwhelming to the less sensual Rooster. Rooster’s rebuffs may destroy Dragon’s ego. The solution will only be found in frank discussion with an objective third party. A therapist? A clergyman? A family friend?",Dog:"Polarized outlooks might find happiness, providing the sex is sensational. But with the Dragon/Dog duo, this is plainly not the case. According to Chinese astrologers, few relationships are less likely to withstand the test of time. Dragon/Dog bickering and barking prevail. Dragons and Dogs are full of enthusiasm, energy and vigor. But their styles are so different as to make them near enemies. Dogs hate making a fuss over nothing. Dragons intentionally create daily scenes complete with flames, smoke and noise. Dragons deem the moralizing, pessimistic, stern Dog a downright bore. Dragons live primarily for themselves. Dogs live for others. The Dragon will wish the Dog a more obedient mate. But the freethinking Dog will never buckle under to oppression. While the Dragon boasts of successes, the Dog gloats over his or her mate’s resounding failures. I have to agree with the Chinese soothsayers. Dissonance reigns. No marriage here please.",Pig:"Most Dragon/Pig marriages last forever. The two have just enough in common and just enough differences to keep them both interested. The Pig is compliant and easygoing, always gives the benefit of the doubt to the other fellow and admires gutsiness and audacity in a mate. The Dragon needs an ally, a helpmate, a shoulder to cry on and someone nice to boss around—preferably someone who forgives easily. The Pig amply fills the bill. Both characters adore opulence—the more gilt sconces they can stick on the walls of their châteaux, the happier they will be. The Pig applauds Dragon’s successes and turns a blind eye to all chicanery. In turn, Dragon protects and admires the Pig’s scrupulousness. In short, Pig helps Dragon maintain the shine on an overactive ego. Dragon adores being put on a permanent pedestal and makes it clear that Pig’s homemaking talents are all he or she has ever dreamed The sex is good. The Pig cleaves to sensuality and the Dragon just plain loves sex—lots of it. Piggy wants romance so Dragon must temper crudity and learn a thing or two about the value of hearts and flowers."},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"You will be compelled to cease your playful escapades and quell those party instincts this year. The Snake is not a slave driver, but he/she requires all the attention. You also fall squarely into the attention-seeking category, but you are not fond of competition. You prefer floodlights and marching bands. The Snake prefers soft Debussy and fragrant bathtubs surrounded by flickering colored candles. One may be equally attractive as the other. However, this is not your year; it belongs to the quiet, unobtrusive, philosophical, but powerful Snake. So, what will occur between you and the Snake year is a clash of styles. It is your turn to don a bushel basket to cover your head and scuttle along walls so as not to be noticed. This may cause you some degree of indigestion because when the limelight fades, you grow despondent and sometimes even pity yourself. Self-pity is unbecoming to dauntless creatures like you. So, check yourself before you sink into your self-made oblivion. Keep in mind this is the second year of your twelve-year cycle, and you need to have a plan. Where did you put that list I suggested you write last year? Find it. Add to it. And implement each step one by one so as to stay on track."},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"Dragons can easily find themselves bewildered by Horse years. First of all, these years are notoriously fraught with tension. The Horse is often a strong yet troubled soul whose sense of self can be easily disrupted by the slightest setback. You, Dragon, might just be part of one of those setbacks, as you are not daunted by the prospect of conflict with anyone—least of all a Horse. You sense the Horse’s strength, but sometimes you do not intuit the Horse’s skittish fragility. Horses are powerhouses of talent, but they do not always seek to shine. They are not as interested in monopolizing the stage as you are, but they do want, need, and actively seek recognition. This year, I suggest you relax. Hold back a bit. Look around in your own life and reflect on how much progress you have been making over the past couple of years. Then, cautiously, return to the fray without causing disturbances or provoking the Horse’s aggression. You will be able to make enormous progress in Horse years and enjoy significantly more time with your family... if only you can suppress your flamboyance. Horses need understanding. Sentimental people like you are capable of generosity and compassion. Utilize those talents this year, and you will navigate smoothly and unhindered."},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Yin Fire",prediction:"You are a star with Goats. Why? Because they need your power and are willing to go to almost any lengths to be able to depend on it. Goats are all about creativity and eccentric, whimsical notions. They love ease and yearn for comfort. They dream of languishing in abundance. But they are not always able to secure those dreamed-of luxuries by themselves. So when a big, strong, capable Dragon comes confidently along, Goats perk up their ears and remain vigilant for opportunities so they might benefit from the Dragon’s willingness to lead them forward. Goats have many more good ideas per second than a Dragon can contain within its proud, scaly head. Goats do not mind being humble and even modest. But they do not ever want to have to compete or impose their wills in the challenging world. They prefer to support strong leaders. So your role in a Goat year, as one of those same strong leaders, is to take the reins without appearing to. Manage the show from behind the scenes and let the Goat have its moment. He or she will thank you forever after and shower you with love and devotion for a lifetime."},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Yang Earth",prediction:"No frivolous behavior! These next twelve months will offer you a burst of activity, precisely to your liking. Multitasking, numerous meetings, and multiple proposals for work, cultural, and sports experiences. Accept the Monkey's invitations for all these propositions. You, more than any other sign, are certainly capable of managing such a diverse array of ongoing activities. Where other people might feel they have been overwhelmed by such a plethora of fresh things to learn and do, you revel in the novelty of it all. A change in your work environment is also forthcoming this year. You are an individual whose enthusiasms require alteration as frequently as you change your shirt. So, start diligently searching for that unusual job immediately this year. You will not regret doing so. Love life? Medium rare. I say that because the romantic situation you have been in for so long is, by this time, well done. Overdone, in fact. Hence, it is time to make significant changes. Now, briefly pursue new romantic interests. See how it feels to enjoy the thrill of seduction again. Change is the central theme of the Monkey year for Dragons. P.S. Your current partner will more than likely be overjoyed to see your scaly rump slink out the door."},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Yin Earth",prediction:"Let the Rooster manage the proceedings. Or at least give him or her the impression that they are in a position of leadership. Roosters prefer to act swiftly, enjoy themselves, and (unlike yourself) prefer not to leave a trail of casualties behind. As you probably have a new romantic interest by this time, you will be busy devising new strategies to retain this prize. However, you need to apply yourself diligently to work this year. Roosters expect people to be actively engaged in their various projects and are not amused by idlers. So, maintain a prominent presence. When you are laboring under the hot sun or mining coal deep underground, groan frequently and sweat profusely to convey to your superiors just how demanding a Dragon's life can be. Otherwise, if you are not attempting to overshadow him, the Rooster will leave you to your countless independent pursuits. Travel and visits to relatives in distant cities are favored now. There is a family member you have been avoiding. Make it your priority to pay them respect. It is in your financial interest to be kind to them now and make amends for any past neglect."},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Yang Metal",prediction:"Phew! There is relatively little that can go utterly wrong for a Dragon in Dog years. You and Dogs get along well together because you share similar beliefs and adopt a global perspective on even the most minor events. Differences of opinion arise when you sense the Dog's inherent paranoia surfacing unexpectedly. Dogs possess a unique understanding of Murphy's Law; they instinctively know that if something can go wrong, it will, and they are more than willing to announce it beforehand. Hence, in Dog years, an atmosphere of pervasive anxiety lingers, which drives Dragons to distraction. My advice to Dragons in this otherwise somewhat challenging year is to enjoy the goodwill that the Dog offers you as its protective companion. Relax a bit. Ease off the accelerator at work. Spend some enriching downtime simply socializing with friends or family—or both. In Dog years, you can also enjoy engaging in cultural excursions. Take tours of exotic lands you have always promised yourself you would visit. Go see the Pyramids or visit Niagara Falls. Do something wonderful for yourself, but leave the Dog and its paranoia at home."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Yin Metal",prediction:"Pigs admit to a certain wide-eyed admiration when confronted by you restless Dragon individuals. Pigs are strong, knowledgeable, and culturally adept people. But they do not comprehend your exaggerated need for change. You are constantly bustling about, never settling long enough to accumulate capital, amass riches, collect art, or acquire luxurious homes—whatever it is the Pig considers wealth. Nevertheless, the Pig and you can be close companions. You admire the Pig's purity and authenticity of spirit. What it does not understand about you is what will hinder you this year. The atmosphere of abundance will lead you to assume you can spend and give and squander your money and so—in a word or two—you overspend. If you are not more careful about where your money is going in the first part of this Pig year, by September, you will find yourself in a difficult financial situation. So, tighten your resolve, Dragon. Control your desire to be overly generous to those you love or those you feel are in need. Hold onto your financial reserves and do not sell the family jewels to acquire a fancy new car to impress your sweetie. Put yourself on a budget. Give wantonly of your love but take fewer fiscal risks. Slow down. Sit still. Read. Knit. Go to the countryside. Sit under a tree and think."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Yang Water",prediction:"Here comes a bonanza year for you Dragon people. Nobody admires your dashing self more than the astute Rat, and the feeling is often mutual. You will be inundated with proposals for new projects and asked to direct (an activity you simply adore!) everything from the village orchestra to the Neighborhood Watch. You are a Star in this Rat year—and what's more, you can feel it. A rush of approval and freedom comes over you around mid-March and will not dissipate until the end of January. Take wise advantage of the opportunities presented to you because they are almost all excellent chances for the betterment of both your financial and personal life. A romantic interest appears about halfway through the year. If you are in a committed relationship, beware of temptation; this person is highly attractive and drawn to your charismatic personality. If you are unattached, pursue it. Family members' needs may impinge on your time in the Rat year. Offer some of your moral support to those in need, but do not be tempted to shower them with your newfound wealth. You have better things to do with your money than bail people out of gambling debt or lend your new BMW to your irresponsible brother-in-law who lost his license for drunk driving."},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Yin Water",prediction:"Provided you keep a lid on your notoriously flamboyant nature, the Ox will not interfere with your progress this year. What most irritates the Ox is your tendency to concoct disorder and create chaotic celebrations out of everything from the dog’s wedding anniversary to your wife’s sister-in-law’s menopause. Ox years are about hard work and order. Oxen are not always fond of anything or anyone who deviates from the established norms in life. They love tradition and social structure. You do too, but you need to make a fuss about it, and the Ox does not. Oxen, too, are assertive; they enjoy giving orders and do not accept them very graciously. As you are a more natural leader—a beloved despot—you may find conflicts arising where you least expect them. I am not suggesting this will be a difficult year for you—unless, of course, you forget to lower your voice and keep your vociferous opinions to yourself. Because of the conservative atmosphere in this Ox year, let me suggest that you take a closer look at your accounting strategies. Pay down your credit cards. Wild spending sprees occasioned by last year’s elation are not favored in Ox years. Adopt a more conventional approach to budgeting, or you are in for some unsettling surprises."},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Yang Wood",prediction:"There are several aspects of your character that irritate the spirited Tiger. First of all, he detests snobbery and name-dropping. The Tiger finds your casual boasting about the famous person you saw at the fancy restaurant, or which celebrated author gave you her estimable autograph, or who you sat next to at the Academy Awards, irritating. Big talkers’ words fall on his deafest ear. Tigers do not care much about who's who, and they deplore pretensions of all kinds. So, no matter if the Pope attends your funeral, do not engage in any bragging or attempts to impress during this Tiger year. The same applies to your famous sentimental displays and your tendency to want to steal every show. Basically, this can be an excellent year for you financially. All new and unusual projects are favored. The Tiger is your ally; he admires your spirited nature, and your words of sensible advice are always welcome. As long as you do not spout any flames through his bedroom window or steal his beloved with those seductive swishings of your scaly tail this year, the Tiger will encourage all your pursuits and applaud most vigorously when you succeed. Be as subtle as you know how, and do not show off. Tigers dislike braggarts."},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"These tranquility-seeking Cat/Rabbit years are never your favorite and frankly get on your nerves. You are constantly searching for excitement, seeking sources of joy, and igniting your own fireworks displays. The Cat/Rabbit perceives this boisterous Dragon-like behavior as rowdy and disruptive. Face it, you Dragons are a noisy bunch! Cat/Rabbits are quiet and even secretive. So the overall atmosphere in this current year will aim to temper your life. Frustration is in store because you genuinely feel sad when the fireworks cease and the last of the Roman candles lies sizzling at your feet. How to manage it all? Reflection is not your strong suit, but you can do it when pushed. This year you will not be pushed; rather, you will be summarily removed from the main stage and find yourself in the quiet backstage of most of the action (which in Cat/Rabbit years usually occurs in banks and other such esteemed institutions). So why not learn to meditate or join a Dragon support group where you might learn to keep quiet and engage in deep, deep thinking? Why? Because you need a plan. Make lists. Set goals. Build new dreams. Next year is the Dragon year. You had better be ready to go!"},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:'The year is all yours! For Dragons, the words "all mine" are particularly meaningful. You like to have control of your own existence and are not disinclined to taking control of a few other lives along the way. You have just had eleven long years to complete your previous twelve-year cycle, and now you are embarking on a new one! But of course, you are in the rebirthing stage of the cycle, the very first year indeed. So you may find yourself uncharacteristically childlike again. Louder than ever. More flamboyant and outspoken. Increasingly self-important and just a touch on the boisterous side. Never mind. Go ahead and frolic and enjoy the party. But, when you wake up each morning, do remember to add something substantial to your list of accomplishments you want to be proud of over the next dozen years. Ask yourself: "Where do I want to be in 2 years? 5 years? 9 or 10 years?" How do you intend to live out your dreams and with whom by your side? All of these considerations are key to a person’s success as a significant human being. Do not plan to fritter away a couple of years in sabbatical mode. You cannot afford to miss a single opportunity to shine. A Dragon’s life is always a barrel of monkeys. Make the best of it.'}}},n={introduction:`Oh, Tempting Snake, how does it feel to be irresistible? It must be wonderful to know that the whole world is captivated by you, with your enchanting allure, your silken scarves, and your glamorous accessories. Everyone is in awe of your appearance. And you, in turn, are in awe of how adoring your admirers are. You truly love to please. Some consider you to be the quiet type, but you can be very talkative when there is something important to convey.

People value your sagacious advice. Those seeking peace of mind are drawn to you for counseling and wisdom. You can always sense what is about to happen before it does. One wonders if you receive messages from other realms. If you do, do not resist it; listen to the spirits and learn. With money, you are both frugal and extravagant. Rather than raising the thermostat a few degrees, you will wrap yourself in sable and curl up with a good lover. You are famous for demanding exclusive rights to your partner while casually maintaining your own busy private life on the side. Security is your all-time favorite source of happiness. Marry a resourceful Rooster or a stabilizing Ox. The first two phases of your life will be hectic and nerve-wracking, but old age suits you. Enjoy it.

Some advice? Be generous with your glory. Try to decline the spotlight when someone who needs it more than you is present.`,elements:{Wood:`This Snake is the public speaker, the actor, the skillful communicator, and presenter of grand-scale ideas. Its exquisite articulation of information guarantees it success. It instinctively knows what place in society it wants to carve out for itself.

Although the Wood Snake experiences more than its share of setbacks, it will make a million comebacks, valiantly returning to the front lines to begin again, perhaps in a different manner, to climb the golden ladder of success. The Wood Snake, like all Snakes, has to combat a tendency towards laziness and an exaggerated love of luxury for its own sake, but because of its intense desire to reap applause, renown, and great wealth, it will always overcome its negative inclination for idleness.

It is a dreamer and often has to force itself to be practical. But unlike some Snakes who are incapable of disciplining themselves, when it comes to earning money, the Wood Snake can be downright pragmatic. If it cannot succeed as a painter, it will try illustrating children's books—and if that does not work, it will go into advertising or commercial design. The objective is to achieve success; any means to that end is valid. The Wood Snake may be vain, but it is not proud. It is always able to discern winning from merely getting by—and it knows that what it desires most is to win.

As a genuine Snake, it is conscious of a deep-seated, subtle desire to enjoy all the pleasures of life. It is not one to refuse the joys of taste, sight, sound, and whatever else it can experience physically. No matter how immense its projects or how public its image, the Wood Snake is always furiously involved in seeking new ways to enjoy itself.

The Wood Snake's drive to achieve fame and fortune is powered by its ambition to please, to win approval, and to convey its ideas and persona to its audience or public. It loves praise; being admired is its preferred stimulant. It is a perfectionist in its work and stops at nothing to learn more, constantly challenging its intellect to break through new territory and find novel means of transmitting both its charismatic image and powerful ideas to the world.

All Wood Snakes fear rejection and abandonment. It is difficult for them to accept flaws in others. They want their partners to be wholly attentive to and responsible for their well-being. They require constant attention and large doses of compassion and understanding to survive. They also need security and a calm environment to thrive. If the object of their affection cannot provide these or does not measure up to the stringent criteria set forth by this demanding lover, the Wood Snake's heart may be broken—and it frequently is.

Although it demands intellectual freedom for itself and is scandalously flirtatious—even sometimes unfaithful—it is jealous, exclusive, and monopolistic when it comes to love. It will never take a secondary role or allow total freedom to the other person. For the sake of its love for another, the Wood Snake is not above dissembling and employing emotional blackmail. It will make its loved one feel guilty until they either conform to its ideal or give up and leave. Emotional involvement with the Wood Snake is anything but simple: the rules are hard to follow for anyone who has outside interests. Extricating oneself is even harder. The process of detaching the Wood Snake's stubborn tentacles of unconditional love and devotion from someone it loves is a horrible, painful spectacle to observe.

As being left alone is precisely what this Snake fears most, the loss of a loved one can mean physical as well as nervous collapse. Serious illness and depression may overcome the poor, bereft creature. The road back will be long and arduous, but it does recover, and once restored in body and mind, it enjoys renewed stability, rekindled ardor, and belief in the all-powerful emotion for which it truly lives—love.

People adore this charming individual. Its presence is always desirable, as it converses easily and possesses a quick sense of humor. The Wood Snake genuinely enjoys social interaction; it is happiest when surrounded and adored. It is friendliest when it knows it is liked and is a wonderful companion whose wise advice is invaluable to its many acquaintances. It is a fervent advocate of the arts, spending much time and money promoting cultural activities. Its homes are showcases of precious works of art and antiques. It entertains with generosity and style. Its manner is obliging, and as long as its own advancement and personal interests are in no way compromised, it will go to great lengths to accommodate those it cares for.`,Fire:`The deep-thinking Fire Snake is not only brilliant; it is power hungry. When it wants to succeed, it is capable of gigantic, masterful strokes that will propel it into the public eye, eliminate the competition, and, with a flick of its tail, bestow upon it a title it can be proud of. This Snake means business.

The Fire Snake's will is stronger than that of its fellow Snakes. It can glide in and out of social gatherings with panache. It sidles up to important people and turns them into putty with its inimitably subtle charm. It makes contacts and uses them to its own benefit, leaving, if necessary, the contact behind. Fire Snakes are ruthless, glamorous, and profoundly learned. They are unafraid of scholarship, know how to concentrate, and assimilate knowledge the way other people soak up sunshine.

Friends and acquaintances play a significant role in the Fire Snake's life. It makes friends easily and keeps them interested because of its charm and willingness to participate in their lives. It will always help out a friend or even give a leg up to a person it has just met, because the Fire Snake believes avidly in the goodness of humankind and in its ability to rectify its own wrongs. To this essentially altruistic person, nobody is entirely foolish or criminal.

Unlike their somewhat reticent counterparts, Fire Snakes have strong opinions that they are not afraid to express with vehemence and clarity. This gift makes them keen politicians, actors, singers, writers, poets, and filmmakers—professions that give them the chance to put their strong ideals into action.

One drawback to the Fire Snake's charm is its unquenchable thirst for sexual intimacy. Its overactive sensuality is so forceful and directive that it is almost hindered by it. Sex is omnipresent in its thoughts. Its propensity for promiscuity is so great as to constitute a danger to its personal safety. It so needs to be found attractive, to make love, to be courted, admired, hugged, kissed, wooed, and smothered in love that it can forget its usually excellent manners and commit acts of foolishness that threaten its reputation and even its personal safety. It usually curtails its murky private involvements sufficiently so as not to tarnish its public persona. But if it is not careful, it may be blackmailed or attract negative newspaper coverage. Scandal sheets seem to sense the vulnerability of the Fire Snake.

Although it usually marries for love, the Fire Snake will not often remain physically faithful for long. Inconstancy comes with its nature. It is incapable of resisting the pull of sexuality that keeps it constantly on the prowl, hunting for new encounters. Its mate, however, should not interpret this as disloyalty. The Fire Snake is fiercely devoted to its family. It spends a lot of time with them, nurtures its children, and dotes on its partner. It depends on its family to anchor its fickle heart and keep it from drifting off into uncharted territory forever.

The Fire Snake enjoys traveling and is at ease in all social gatherings. Its manner is sardonically subtle and secretive. Although it is a deep thinker, when it comes to relationships, it is not profound. It can be counted on to keep a confidence or to uphold its end of a bargain. It is sometimes too judgmental and not indulgent enough with those it feels are insufficiently socially responsible. But the Fire Snake is a gentle sort. Its sterling integrity informs its every act—except, of course, in the bedroom, where no holds are barred and the sky is the limit.`,Earth:`Here, in the Earth Snake, is the very lightest of Snakes. The Earth element lends frivolity to the already delicately constructed Snake and gives it an extra dose of feminine charm.

More than any other, this Snake feeds on dreams. It is often lost in reverie and seems to be floating above the clouds. The baser aspects of life, such as violence, raw sexuality, squalor, and poverty, upset the Earth Snake so much that, to survive, it must always remain at a safe distance. Its cozy swarm of illusion serves as a cocoon for this fragile creature's sensitivities and protects it from harsh reality.

The Earth Snake is, nevertheless, an intelligent person, full of wild ideas and exciting plans. But, no matter how it works, it is not always able to carry through with its plans because of its curious, self-defeating habit of self-deception. It is a potentially marvelous magician who knows how to twist and turn facts and create its own version of the truth, but it fails to apply this talent to the outside world where it might need it to make a deal or navigate some difficult stage.

Instead, it tells itself that everything will be all right as long as it believes its own fabricated version of what is truly happening. This Snake ends up with a reputation for lacking perseverance and stability. It is perpetually joining forces with people who are even better at deception than it is, and finding itself lost and without an anchor for the duration.

To counteract this tendency, the Earth Snake is a marvelous seeker (and finder) of rock-like mates to shelter it from the harsh world and who know how to appreciate (and perhaps even exploit) the Earth Snake's brilliant deceptions.

I renovated a ruined house in a Provencal village some years back. My mason was a fantastically inventive Spanish craftsman named Juan who built me a fabulous four-bedroom house out of a ten-room dump. Juan always told me the truth—his truth. But sometimes his truths were just fantasies about how it could be so much more beautiful if I had a mezzanine here or a terrace there.

"I prefer to work on a house," he explained, "that I create myself, rather than just execute some foolish plan made by a mere architect!" Juan was a typical dreamy, inventive Earth Snake. Sometimes his wild dreams were feasible; sometimes not. When I didn’t have the necessary funds to meet his need to build me a roof garden or install a wrought iron staircase instead of a simple wooden one, Juan pouted or simply didn’t come to work for a few days. The fact is, he took my practicality as a slight—a desire to hinder his creativity.

As long as this Snake is well married or still in the safe embrace of its parents' home, it will not encounter too many disasters. At home, it is a kind of genius: it is tenderhearted and makes an excellent family person who always listens and understands the miseries of other members. It is an excellent parent and a superior host. Its warm welcomes and pleasantries infuse its guests with joy and a feeling of warmth from the moment they cross the threshold. It is generous and spontaneous, giving of its possessions and itself for the sake of friendship or loyalty to its clan.

The Earth Snake is more dependent than the other Snakes. It is very hard-working and clever at resolving difficult issues. Ideally, it should be employed by a large corporation or at least a solid small company or even the government. An insecure job where money and stability are not part of the package would cause it too much inner turmoil and lead to its departure or failure to uphold its responsibilities. It is not hard-hearted enough to boss others around, but because it is so exceptionally creative, it has plenty of trouble following orders.

The nature of this gentle soul is so pleasing, and its temperament so even and cheerful, that people with selfish motives, who criticize it for its timidity, its love of luxury, its easy-going attitudes, and its pure joy in living, often take advantage of it. It must be careful not to attach itself to those who do not have its best interests at heart. Those who associate with it must know how to appreciate its easy charm and be able to leave it at that. It cannot be hurried, pressured, or changed.

If alerted to the dangers surrounding it, the Earth Snake can usually identify the predators who seek to control and torment it. It is more than wise; it is cunning and exceptionally clever at understanding reality. It may become cynical and crudely aware of what is, but it tries to remain oblivious. It prefers to dream, plot, and scheme than to get up every morning and contend with the truths of the hard life ahead.

Aware of its frivolous nature, this Snake is often attracted to conservative types. Somehow, it is able to discern, through its haze of fantasy, that the best way to survive is by locating people more down-to-earth than itself and cultivating their friendship and love. It will often seem very creative and even silly by comparison to its steady mate. You might wonder why it chooses to live in a secluded area when it seems more like a typical Bohemian. The truth is, it is happier among the middle class, who demand only that it gossip or shop, cook or dispense love. And... it is happiest in a natural setting where trees, woods, and flowers provide a constant refuge from aggression. By staying out of the way, it is not obliged to leave its cozy nest of fantasy and can indulge in its dreams all day in complete safety.

The wise Earth Snake knows what it needs to survive and uses its innate charm and cheerful demeanor to obtain it. Perhaps in the context of suburban bourgeois security, or as a country gentleman, it will energetically fundraise for museums or restore a lovely old mansion, feed the starving millions from its brocade armchair, or even adopt unfortunate third-world babies. But do not count on the sensitive Earth Snake's willing participation in any projects requiring scrambling in challenging conditions. Even though its governing element is Earth, this Snake will fade and be miserable if it has to dip so much as its delicate big toe in the mud.`,Metal:`This type of Snake yearns for a grand life and even greater wealth. It is an individual with grandiose ideas—one might even say, delusions of grandeur. It is ambitious and desires notoriety. It seeks to display its talents to capture the attention of the entire world. Because of its intense need for public acclaim, it often succeeds in becoming something of a star, wherever it may live or practice its profession. The life of the exceptionally talented Metal Snake is marked by difficulty. It often experiences significant setbacks, losing fortunes or loved ones, succumbing to drug excesses, or cultivating misguided religious beliefs, both of which lead to disaster and cause it to lose precious time in its quest for fame and fortune. But it always regains its composure and resumes its pursuit.

Like all Snakes, because of its deep desire to please and be accepted, the Metal Snake is vulnerable, but it is even more so because it does not hesitate to openly express its emotions, to voice its opinions, and to open its heart to the general public. It melts with joy at thunderous applause. But it is unwary of the fickleness behind the applause of a public quick to lose interest, to grow critical and unkind towards the unprotected Snake whom they have admired. Negative publicity or an unappreciative audience can defeat this unguarded genius and drive it to suicidal thoughts.

Although it is insufficiently cautious of its public, this Snake is usually suspicious in its private life. It does not trust easily and will search for a long while before committing to marriage or family life. It wants to be sure it is not taken for a fool. It needs to know that its partner will be faithful and uphold its ideals. It must be assured of security before agreeing to bear the responsibilities of family. Of all Snakes, it is the most naive and believing in the fundamental goodness of humanity. It tries to be a good person, to emulate those it admires, and to advocate for humanitarian causes. Because the Metal Snake is sincere, it is easily deceived by unscrupulous characters who do not have its best interests at heart, accept its favors, use it, and then discard it. I would not go so far as to say it is attracted to undesirable individuals—but perhaps it is.

The Metal Snake takes delight in the chase and may not be able to remain faithful forever to a sexual partner. It knows that one day it will break the covenant of good faith that marriage demands. It does not necessarily enjoy this aspect of its character and even perceives it as somewhat of a handicap. Nonetheless… it was born with a restless urge and sometimes acts on it.

When it becomes aware of its imperfections, conflicts arise within the Metal Snake's responsible, stable mind, and it is not always comfortable in its own skin. It may experience periods of self-doubt. Or, more likely, it may do what it is so gifted for: rationalize. It will tell itself that it needs freedom to be creative, or that it must be at liberty to roam so that it can help humankind, or that a few infidelities will ultimately benefit the marriage. This Snake is highly deceptive but means no harm.

Ironically, Metal Snakes are chronic truth-seekers. They may be superficially sociable and desire to succeed in the world, but they secretly dream of solitude, of living in a state of blissful detachment with an unlisted phone number. In their daily life, they sometimes simulate a desert island anonymity by choosing not to answer personal questions, evading reality to maintain an aura of mystery about and for themselves.

There is none so opportunistic as this incisive and intuitive person, whose creative genius usually finds a lucky star on which to ride to the top. The Metal Snake can perceive an opportunity for success in everyone it meets. It cultivates contacts the way farmers grow cabbages. Its method of operation begins with charm and ends with seduction. One day, it will secure a partnership with the perfect sponsor, and before you know it, you'll be reading about its superstar status in everything from the tabloids upwards.

Despite its vulnerability and desire for fame and positive cash flow, this Snake is somewhat of an intellectual. It is curious and interested in the inner workings of the mind and will spend much of its spare time reading and studying, listening, or discovering new things. It may choose to specialize in history or even delve into obscure fields of philosophy and exotic Eastern religions. It keeps its own counsel, is superbly self-confident, and manages to remain remarkably independent—for a Snake.`,Water:`Great minds characterize these eminent Water Snakes. Their advantage over other, less logical and more thoroughly sensory Snakes, is that they are meticulous planners. Before embarking on any far-reaching project or moneymaking scheme, the intuitive Water Snake designs a sound, well-thought-out schedule with specific parameters and follows it precisely. It is a world-beater, a force to be reckoned with.

The Water Snake is wildly imaginative. It spends much of its time meditating on new ways to solve old problems or speculating on inventing new ones. It is devoted to childhood's fairy-tale world and cannot ever climb completely out of the comfortable cradle of infantile fantasy. An active imagination can be a marvelous asset, but the fertile mind of the Water Snake may exaggerate events, interpret them too vividly, and muddle reality. If this trait overwhelms it and it succumbs to exaggerated mental wanderings, the Water Snake may become paranoid and suspicious, fearing aggression or threats that are not truly present.

This person can be gainfully employed as an astrologer, soothsayer, or psychologist. Its psychic abilities are appreciated by friends and clients alike, who do not hesitate to call on it for advice. Its cool, reserved personality inspires confidence, and its soothing voice calms the shattered nerves of many who consult it. It knows so well how to soften harsh realities that it can make even the most afflicted person feel better.

The Water Snake preserves its good looks long into middle age. It takes care of its body and its diet. Vanity plays a part in this, but so does common sense, of which, despite its penchant for the fantastic, it possesses a good measure.

The Water Snake is socially responsible and cares deeply for the outcome of human events. It worries a great deal and is anxious by nature. Unfortunately, it also suffers from a mini-martyr complex and would rather play the victim than be the aggressor in its partnerships. This attitude may lead to self-pity, which, again, borders on paranoia. With luck, its tendency to whine and feel sorry for itself will always be discouraged and managed by the good sense with which it was born.

The Water Snake can never be accused of maliciousness. It is kindly and tries to comprehend the legitimate motives of people who hurt it. It is never unnecessarily judgmental or cruel. It boasts numerous friends who enjoy its sweet nature and approve of its methodical approach. It is generous—except when it has to pay for necessities—and can be a lavish spender. It is often an excellent cook, too, and prepares feasts at a moment's notice.

It is drawn to professions where music and art play an important role. Beyond that, anything from architecture to advertising or telecommunications would suit it. Like other Snakes, it seeks power and money, but unlike them, it is not conniving. It knows how to go about achieving its goals in a reasonable and honest fashion. It usually studies diligently at school and graduates with decent grades. It is able to conform to the norm sufficiently to make itself liked by its classmates as well as respected by its teachers.

The Water Snake is an active, serious person who lives life to the fullest, yet remains more than most other Snakes on the marital straight and narrow. It might enjoy the occasional dalliance with a stranger, but knows that such a transgression might jeopardize its overall plan and confuse its already complex psyche. It convinces itself that such dangerous temptations are not for it and finds comfort in its fantasy world, drawing, painting, or listening to music while reinventing the wheel.

Because it is dreamy, the Water Snake exposes itself to huge disappointments. It often overvalues a person or gives too much credit to an event and then discovers it was wrong. Its views are clouded by its desire to improve on reality. This sets it up for emotional or sentimental decision-making, which can be disastrous. It should always perform a severe reality check before embarking on any important, new plan.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"Although this alliance can often lead to an interesting friendship, I would not recommend it as a romantic relationship. Rat and Snake may be sexually attracted to each other, but ideally, their connection should remain purely social. On a daily basis, life for a Rat/Snake couple will be filled with upheaval, disagreement, and disappointment. After the initial physical attraction, the Snake will withdraw and keep aspects of its life securely private. The Serpent's inclination for flirtation will be even stronger if the Snake is attached to a clingy Rat. The Rat will grow uneasy and fearful about security. The Snake's investments may not prove profitable, and the restless Rat will have to take charge of the family's finances. Tempers will flare, especially the Rat's, who struggles under the burden of trying to maintain the crumbling foundation. The Snake? It will storm out of the house to the nearest Dior boutique to add to an already extensive wardrobe of fine lingerie. The only moments of tranquility in this union will be spent intimately, passionately entwined for hours. The Rat will appreciate the sexual attention the elusive Snake provides and, ever generous, will be forgiving. Be cautious, gentle Rat, of your enchanting Snake. If you are not careful, even you can become a victim. Snakes will draw you in with promises, love you intensely, then metaphorically consume you whole for breakfast.",Ox:"A nimble Snake entwines itself around an Ox's yoke and accompanies it on its journey. The Ox welcomes its agile passenger and steadily progresses through life with contentment. A Snake feels comfortable in the Ox's presence. Yet, the fickle Snake possesses an appetite for new experiences—especially those yet unexplored. Oxen are devoutly monogamous. Deep down, of course, the Snake is devoted to the Ox, whose stability is crucially important for the Snake's survival. If the Ox can learn to curb its suspicious nature and control a jealous temper, this creature can retain an appealing Snake partner better than anyone else. After all, the Ox possesses all the money, power, and patience, and Snakes adore all those qualities. Should the Ox begin to worry over failed ventures or depleted reserves, the Snake must subtly lead it to bed. The Ox is happy to comply with lusty quantity, but to prevent the reptile's attention from wandering, it must develop more imaginative foreplay. This union can be a good one if the Ox can remain courageous and undaunted by a challenging (yet fascinating) Snake mate.",Tiger:"The elusive Snake and the tempestuous Tiger are irresistibly drawn to each other, but this union is not advisable. A Tiger/Snake pairing can be a disastrous alliance. As different as black and white, yin and yang, the Tiger/Snake combination simply does not blend. Should either of you be unfortunate enough to fall for the other, a preliminary restraining order could save you from catastrophes. If not, here is what to expect: The slow-moving Snake will inflict tremendous frustration upon the energetic Tiger's psyche. Initially, the jungle predator mistakenly perceives the enchanting serpent as quiet and submissive, and attempts to dominate. But reptiles do not respond well to bullying; they retaliate. Snakes are aloof, independent-minded, and strategic masterminds. Haughty indifference and disdain are among their sharpest weapons. They are also prone to repeated instances of infidelity, which will certainly shatter a Tiger mate's considerable ego. The impressive tantrums of the Tiger can make the Snake's calm, reflective, philosophical life miserable. Equally magnetic, Snakes and Tigers compete for attention. The Tiger does so aggressively, and the Snake slyly bewitches. At their own cocktail party, Tiger/Snake hosts may appear quarrelsome. The Tiger recounts stories about its days in the Sinai desert. The Snake subtly encroaches on the Tiger's territory, captivating the company with the Dance of the Seven Veils, learned (coincidentally) in the Sinai desert. Outmaneuvered, the Tiger loudly outdoes the Snake, recounting further desert expeditions. Subdued, the Snake joins the applause, but adds, in a cultivated, soft-spoken voice, that everything the Tiger knows about deserts was learned from the Snake. Tigers are fast and alert, while Snakes are quiet and deliberate thinkers. Tigers are impulsive and may act heedlessly. Snakes rely almost solely on intuition and take things slowly. These creatures may cohabit for sensual pleasure, but they do not see eye to eye. Sexual intimacy? The Snake's need for beautiful, romantic foreplay is denied by an aggressive Tiger, who simply gets down to business. It is best to abstain!",Rabbit:"The intuitive Snake and the philosophical Cat find each other mutually interesting. Both possess keen minds and are deep thinkers. Should they encounter difficulties, this couple can rely on their shared innate wisdom to guide them out of trouble. The extravagant Snake makes weekly shopping appointments with salespeople at Cartier and Dior. This upsets the cautious, tradition-bound Cat, who disapproves of the Snake’s inclination for the lavish. Conflicts are easily resolved if the Cat is permitted to manage the finances. However, unless the Cat learns to understand the Snake’s desperate need for the most opulent accessories and surroundings, a powerful python partner may become a listless garden Snake. A deprived Snake can also be a hostile reptile. These two pleasure-seekers can usually resolve their differences, spending an evening over a bottle of Pommard. As a couple, this pair exudes charm. They make excellent guests and can expect invitations to all the most desirable parties. In public, the Cat fears the Snake’s incessant flirtations, finding the Snake’s open, raw sexuality difficult to handle. But Snakes have their irresistible ways with reserved Cat lovers. Both are potential psychics; if all else fails, they can always become traveling fortune-tellers.",Dragon:"In Chinese astrological terms, these two are considered very close relatives. The Dragon adores having a gorgeous, attractive, and sensual Snake partner, and the quiet, subtle Snake admires the Dragon’s world-beating flamboyance and style. In turn, the Dragon protects the Snake. The Snake pampers the Dragon’s ego and allows the Dragon to speak freely without even a hint of criticism. Of course, no relationship with any Dragon can ever be entirely calm, but the Snake/Dragon duo comes close to being a levelheaded, harmonious union. Wisely, the Snake never directly confronts the Dragon’s ego. Snakes handle conflicts subtly, observing and examining all sides before striking at precisely the right moment to achieve results. Sexually—with the Snake’s immense capacity for erotic activity and the Dragon’s vast appetite and innate talent for the same—you can just imagine... the chemistry is sublime. They also agree on living luxuriously. The Dragon buys endless delightful accessories for the Snake’s pleasure, and the Snake allows the Dragon—within reason—to indulge in filling the house with gadgets. Their home life is excellent; they make a handsome couple. It is truly a match made in heaven.",Snake:"This relationship is characterized by drama, sexual intensity, luxury, promiscuity, passion, and potential ruin. Two Snakes could be doubly indolent. Both tend to dissimulate and desire to be surrounded by beautiful things and unusual friends. The couple’s life will be fraught with intricate complexities and unexpected occurrences. A Snake couple is artistic. Together, they will enhance their cultural existence, regularly attending exhibitions, concerts, and theater. As they also tend to be philosophical and are drawn to the metaphysical, they will often engage in exciting New Age activities and hold conversations that last far into the night. This sexually compatible pair will entwine upon first meeting and subsequently have great difficulty disengaging for even the most important practical matters. Tenderness, romance, and passion are the very cornerstones of their intimacy. Although the financial aspect of their joint life might be a real mess, an overwhelming physical attraction binds them together. Despite a tendency towards infidelity on both sides, no jealousy will cloud their lovemaking. In fact, these two may hardly emerge from between their smooth satin sheets long enough to allow the live-in, full-time maid to wash them.",Horse:"These two are strongly attracted to each other. The Horse admires the Snake’s natural ease with people and appreciates its considerate, charitable nature. The Snake, on the other hand, likes and respects the Horse’s spiritedness and innate enthusiasm. Their social life will be rich and full. Trouble begins when the Horse realizes that its adored Snake mate is 'running around.' Promiscuity does not sit well with the straightforward, faithful, devoted Horse. So, the Horse shifts into a mode of recrimination, which forces the Snake to conceal any extracurricular activities more cleverly—but not necessarily to abandon them. The Horse does not handle duplicity well, and storms ensue. The Snake has a generous heart. The Horse is more conservative with money. This disparity will cause some significant arguments. It is best to let the Horse manage the finances and dispense money to the Snake for trivialities. But do not expect the money-loving Snake to accept that arrangement; it wants to spend! The Horse may bolt. Almost everyone is happy with a sensual Snake person in their bed. Horses have little confidence in their sexuality, but Snakes have more than enough to share. They make good, considerate teachers. The match can work if the Horse can learn not to fall apart when the Snake embarks on sensual, romantic interludes, and the Snake can learn to curb its inclination for minor indiscretions.",Goat:"Charming and graceful, this pair of artistic, creative people can have the world eating out of their hands. The Goat’s inherent beauty and seductive appeal, when combined with the Snake’s elegance and sensuality, form an enviably synergistic couple. Theirs will be a delicious complicity. Unfortunately, neither of these gloriously attractive people is very adept with a calculator. They are both equally improvident, luxury-loving, and even extravagant with spending. Unpaid bills will accumulate, and each will accuse the other of being a spendthrift, leading to a stalemate. Do not expect the Goat to find solutions. Snakes may overspend, but they also provide. Goats are determined to be dependent and provided for. The Snake will only tolerate so much of the Goat’s indolence and will soon find the poor Goat a high-paying job and compel it to arrive at the office on time and perform its duties well until death do them part. Once again, the Snake’s incurable infidelity enters the equation. Goats tend to be fickle too. But, even though the Snake understands the Goat’s occasional need for a fling, the more stubborn Goat dislikes sharing its possessions and will react strongly to the Snake's infidelity. But never mind; arguments are a part of these people’s lives: both are addicted to passionate drama. Romantically, this couple is sound. But when the harsh, overhead light of reality penetrates the veneer of their relationship, the cracks and flaws may prove too numerous for its survival.",Monkey:"Auspicious beginnings encourage these individuals to unite and operate as a team. The versatile Monkey finds wisdom and consideration in the Snake’s personality. The Snake enjoys the Monkey’s charm and energetic spirit. They are truly a complementary pair. After a time, however, they will realize that all they have in common is a desire to help others, a charitable inclination that binds them ever so loosely together. The Snake, of course, always embarks on extramarital adventures. The Monkey? Well, the Monkey could not care less: if affairs arise, so much the better. If not, it can take them or leave them alone. Snakes value elegance and desire their lives to be carefully accessorized. Monkeys are bored by the very idea of accessorizing anything and prefer casual attire to dressing up. Monkeys are spontaneous; Snakes are deliberate. The Snake is romantic, the Monkey logical. The Snake is sophisticated, the Monkey bohemian and carefree. Monkeys love to converse, but dialogue becomes difficult because Snakes find it hard to reveal their inner feelings. A breakdown in communication might be the demise of this relationship. Their sex life usually compensates for much of the strife between them. Although sexual intimacy is not always the Monkey’s strongest suit, Snakes succeed in exciting them greatly. The complicity of elaborate sexual games may provide a foundation for this pair to strengthen their union—despite their essential differences.",Rooster:"A perfect love match, if ever there was one! The Rooster is rather conventional and traditional. Snakes are aesthetic and desire to appear attractive at all times. Although, at first glance, it may seem that the Snake is too sophisticated and elegant for the plain-living Rooster, the opposite is true. Roosters and Snakes form some of the best couples. They are both quite secretive and prefer to keep to themselves. Yet, when together, they are constantly engaged in intense discussion and consideration of every detail, from the quality of light inside their refrigerator to the leather on the soles of their expensive shoes. Roosters are mostly forgiving, indulgent people whose loyalty knows no bounds. Snakes may engage in some casual social and sexual dalliances, but they are careful never to become deeply involved with their conquests and hardly ever betray or leave their Rooster mates. Why? Because they truly love them. In this marriage, the Rooster should manage the finances. Snakes often waste money; Roosters keep closer tabs on their pennies. The cultural side can be handled equally well by both. Sexual intimacy should definitely be left to the seductive Snake. Snakes know how to arouse hesitant Roosters and make their bodies sing. Roosters are basically reserved about sensual matters. The Rooster who finds a Snake as a mate will have much to boast about.",Dog:"This partnership is imbalanced. We are dealing with two disparate types of people. Dogs are pessimistic, prone to depression and worry. Snakes are naturally relaxed, less anxious, and certainly less sarcastic. Sometimes the doubting Dog even mistrusts a companion Snake’s charm and will whine and snap about it, criticizing the Snake for both frivolity and an easygoing nature. Basic personality differences do not have to destroy relationships. But the Dog dislikes society, has few friends, and stays at home a lot. Snakes are just the opposite, yet they need a home to return to after their numerous forays into the wider world. Returning to the comfortable Dog home after experiencing society's greed can be refreshing for the sociable Snake. Even though they snarl and threaten, Dogs always forgive, are loyal to a fault, and never waver in their devotion to their loved ones. Both parties are sensitive to causes, feel strongly about combating injustice, and believe in right over might. This similarity of purpose can serve to harmonize their relationship and smooth out some potential rough edges. The problem is, their sexual selves are very different. Dogs are physically conventional and direct. Snakes are highly adventurous in bed and enjoy intricate sexual play. The two may not clash over this issue, but the Snake may eventually grow bored, resume a natural inclination for flirting, and irrevocably damage the Dog’s tender-hearted soul.",Pig:"This is the Pig’s nemesis. Chinese sages always advise against this relationship. They say that the rapacious Snake will eventually strangle the unsuspecting Pig. It is interesting because Pigs are earthy, warm-hearted individuals who are easily swayed by beauty and cultural sophistication. So, inevitably, the first gorgeous, sex-loving Snake to come along completely captivates the Pig, who cannot resist. Superficially, the luxury-loving Pig has much to offer a Snake lover. Pigs are scrupulous and mostly honest. They usually know how to earn a lot of money, which the Snake loves to lavish on their joint lifestyle. They both adore traditional things like antiques, vintage wines, and castles in Spain. The problem here revolves around a shared weakness: neither the Snake nor the Pig is a world-record decision-maker. The Pig changes its mind as readily as the Snake changes its outfit. The Snake procrastinates. The Pig wallows and wonders. They are sexually compatible to a fault, but little is accomplished in life by lying about intertwined in each other’s limbs. Pigs do not care much about appearances, making rude noises and smacking their lips when they eat. Eventually, a fastidious Snake grows critical of a Pig’s sloppy habits. The Snake’s sarcastic remarks bring out the worst in the Pig, who whimpers, which only makes the Snake more impatient and even cruel. The gracious Pig can never please the demanding Snake enough. It finally just sadly withers away and leaves all its money to the voracious beauty it could not resist marrying."},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"As you will be in the driver’s seat this year, you can expect to be supercharged and cheerful most of the time—except when events accelerate and too many demands are made on your time. You prefer to live your life at your own pace. This year, you will be compelled to follow the hectic rhythm of the world and its drastic politics. In Snake years, the planet’s geopolitical climate generally intensifies to full throttle by about July and does not calm down until well after the following January. I know that being a member of the ruling class sounds terrific in theory, but in practice, it is an entirely different matter, with everyone vying for top status. You will need ample rest and relaxation this year if you want to remain in good health. Ideally, you would take one day off a week, but of course, almost nobody—not even you relaxed Snake people—can do that with a clear conscience. Instead, tune out. Wear earphones and blinders. Turn off the house phone, the cell phone, the TV, and your computer so you can take a few short naps here and there. If you are still without a life partner (rare for the irresistible Snake), this year will present you with a couple of serious options. Stick to Roosters and Oxen if you can. If not, dare to marry a Tiger. OR... why not hitch your wagon to a Dragon?"},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"Many people believe Horses and Snakes do not harmonize. Many people are correct. This year will be challenging at best for Snakes, as the Horse is not even-tempered and does not particularly care about its subjects’ well-being. Horses are intensely pragmatic; they simply want to do things their way. They are talented and shrewd, and they are artistic, but not necessarily altruistic. You Snakes are motivated by compassion and philanthropy; you sincerely believe in your ability to contribute to the betterment of humankind. So, Snake dissatisfaction is common in the ego-centered Horse year environment. You will feel as though you just cannot make progress on any project and maintain it without obstacle after obstacle being thrown up and roadblocks appearing at every turn. You might, moreover, become entangled in a legal battle over a contract or real property. As the climate in Horse years is unfavorable to a positive outcome for Snakes, you will not have much chance of winning. It would be better to try some cunning tactic to delay the lawsuit until next year when the gentle Goat will rule—a more lenient climate for Snakes involved in legal disputes. Obviously, this year will not be your favorite. Take your frustration on a long holiday somewhere warm and tropical with your significant other in tow. Should your significant other be (for some strange reason) a Horse, I advise that you leave him or her at home. Perhaps you should consider seducing someone more philosophically inclined."},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Yin Fire",prediction:"Goats usually find you Snakes alluring, but in another way, they cannot stand to be near you. Why? Because you are so quietly strong, capable, and attractive, and Goats are so dependent and pessimistic. Deep inside, they sincerely wish that you would take care of them. You, of course, are not very willing to take care of anybody except your good looks, your favorite charities, and your beloved family. So the atmosphere in this Goat year is lukewarm for Snakes, and if there is anything Snake people dislike, it is tepid affection. Snakes prefer it hot; Goats prefer it comfortable. So, watch out for the possibility of someone younger or weaker than you who will try to crawl into your life, eat from your fridge, soak up your central heating, and generally just settle there until you force them out. It might be a relative or an ex, a niece, or just a nice person you feel sorry for. You invite them to stay until they get back on their feet. After only a few months, they now live with you and your family, and the entanglements are many. Take advice from your significant other or a wise close friend who will show you how (diplomatically) to get rid of the intruding guest without having to either create scenes or witness a very unpleasant houseguest tantrum unfold."},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Yang Earth",prediction:"You will need your indomitable strength this year to withstand the onslaught of the Monkey’s intricate antics. Monkeys crave attention and will perform almost any type of outrageous act to get it. Perhaps you will not be drawn in by the Monkey’s neurotic charm, but if you are—beware! You provide an excellent audience because you simply love spectacle. This characteristic puts you in considerable danger in Monkey years. Because you find entertainment so attractive, you can be deceived. Monkeys are tricksters who do not care much whom they are performing for, as long as the public rewards them. So, in this year of the Monkey, Snakes must guard their finances, secure their purse strings tightly, and avoid temptation. Do not even think about entering a casino or going near a card game. Remain aloof by undertaking a major creative project that keeps you grounded and in one place. Your romantic life may also provide a safe haven—provided, of course, that you are not married to a Monkey. Should this be the case, consult a Dog or Ox psychiatrist, or else—move to Tibet—alone!"},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Yin Earth",prediction:"Snakes and Roosters make excellent companions. You appreciate each other’s energies and can both easily understand the other’s point of view. Being naturally able to glimpse into almost anyone’s private life, you Snakes do have a distinct advantage over us mere mortals. Roosters live their lives and play their cards very discreetly. Hence, being capable of subtly understanding them (as all self-respecting Snakes can) constitutes a huge advantage for you in Rooster years. As the Rooster is so comfortable in your presence, you can also count on this year to provide you with the financial security you so long for and deserve. What’s more, this Rooster year gives you the opportunity to ascend to new and more prestigious heights in your professional life. All doors seem to open at once. Executives who until now refused to receive you suddenly call you to inquire if they can make an appointment. Promotions come your way when you least expect them. It’s a great year for Snakes to make progress in every area of their existence. The ups and downs created by this new commotion will surely land you at the doctor’s office once or twice during this twelve-month period. But never mind; the rewards will be worth any anxieties or upsets you may suffer because of the Rooster’s demanding pace."},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Yang Metal",prediction:"The Dog protects its charming Snake companion and, like all dogs, loves you unconditionally. Both Snake and Dog individuals have humanitarian goals. The Dog is more spirited and vocal about desiring justice for all, but you do see eye-to-eye when it comes to believing that something can and ought to be done about the innumerable examples of human cruelty prevalent in the world today. You may not form a perfect team, however, as you and the Dog both prefer to be in charge. But each in his or her own way is constantly vigilant for signs of bias and unfairness. The Dog is slightly more paranoid about evil being perpetrated against its own person. You are cool-headed and confident in your ability to rectify wrongs. But no matter; you will be appreciated for who you are and, of course, admired and adored for your natural beauty. In this favorable climate, you should dare to undertake new projects, establish your own business, or build yourself a dream house. Whatever you create will be solid and well-received. Dogs emanate anxiety vibes. As the year progresses, this fretfulness will most likely affect you, as it is contagious and can undermine your peace of mind. Take time out; practice yoga, tai chi, or meditate to quell the unease."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Yin Metal",prediction:"Take advantage of the Pig’s profound adoration of you to make progress this year. Nothing is more attractive to a plump, trusting Pig individual than a slender, worldly-wise Snake who (to Pigs) seems to possess all the answers. Pigs are sweet, innocent, and tough. Snakes are not so sweet, never innocent, and… they are far tougher than Pigs. Pigs, however, possess something that all Snakes desire: money. For some peculiar reason, Pigs attract wealth. They moreover covet and acquire everything authentic in sight—from rococo antique tables to old masters’ paintings and gilded Louis XV sconces, and castles and palaces and gold. Snakes certainly do not disdain that sort of asset and will sometimes vigorously pursue and even conquer the poor, unsuspecting, vulnerable Pig. But that’s another story. This year, Snakes thrive. You can count on everything from passion to a reprieve from your allergies and skin ailments. The only dark aspect of this year’s forecast will reveal itself if you try to make rapid decisions. Stay away from people who ask you to participate in their schemes. Adhere to your own work ethic and do not partner with anyone except your good self."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Yang Water",prediction:"Your health and well-being are in excellent condition this year. All the ailments you were suffering last year will dissipate in the beneficial atmosphere of the protective Rat. Trouble may be brewing, however, in your financial sector. Although you will begin the year with a sense of abundance and continue it with ample sufficiency, you may encounter some unexpected financial difficulties towards the end of the year. You should start saving money for the future and curb your buying sprees. Shopping may be calming for you while it is happening, but when those alarming credit card bills and excessive mortgage payments start flooding your mailbox, it will be goodbye to serenity and hello to stress and late-night anxiety. Much emphasis has been placed on your family situation for the past twelve months. Now it is time to pursue career goals and achieve them for your and your family’s benefit. The Rat is a nervous type, and that intense atmosphere emanating from the very core of this year causes you anxiety. Secure your finances more tightly and accumulate security. Invest only in what you can genuinely afford. Otherwise, you will be struggling against the current for twelve long, frazzled months."},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Yin Water",prediction:"Snakes are the Ox’s best friends, and vice versa. You are both deliberate and slow-paced, and your energies are similar in character. So, this coming Ox year for Snakes will be beneficial, productive, and personally valuable. You will return to your natural rhythm and enjoy the kind of relaxed mood in which you always devise your best schemes and are able to complete projects that needed finishing or enhancing. Last year truly slowed your progress to a subtle crawl, but the Ox appreciates your quiet sense of aesthetics and is always there to help you realize your dreams. Love is also back. You will be feeling more romantically intense than you have been in a while. The reason? Your financial and health troubles are behind you. Do remember, though, that the Ox is a demanding individual and does not tolerate idleness. One must demonstrate a willingness and ability to labor under pressure in Ox years, and even though the Ox favors you and considers you its companion, you will still have to apply yourself diligently and begin working on projects and problems left undone in previous (less benevolent) years."},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Yang Wood",prediction:"The Tiger wishes you only the best. Its influence, however, is an entirely different matter. Tigers have a reputation for stealthily prowling the world's jungles late at night, stalking their prey. This animal portrait does not quite fit the profile of the restless Tiger individual. Tiger people are extremely active; they leap and bound and rush about searching for new and different experiences. They adore change and prefer it to happen quickly. You Snakes prefer to recline in silken repose on chaises longues, reading novels with intricate, winding plots, expansive detailed geographies, and complex characters. Let’s just say your styles are different, and your goals are not the same either. You wish to reflect and philosophize; Tigers act first and think second. Because of their immense charm, Tigers are frequently chosen to lead, but they rarely lead far without the wise counsel of someone like you. How could they? They have change for brains—loose change at that. So this Tiger year will be a challenge for Snakes. You will be called upon to advise friends and foes alike. You will be in charge of wisdom. Minor accidents and small setbacks will annoy you, but you are not in danger. In the hands of a Tiger, a Snake can feel a certain thrill. But do not look for security this year, because there isn't any to spare."},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"You Snakes will need all your cunning skills this year because the Cat/Rabbit and you are traditionally at odds. You are not inclined to conceal your feelings and almost never spare us the details of your moods. The Cat/Rabbit is a master of secretive and covert behavior. He or she never wishes to attract much attention or confront conflict. The prevailing mood of Cat/Rabbit years is anything but direct. Instead, it is quiet, effective, and exceedingly calm. You are constantly moving and scurrying about in an attempt to control and manage things your way. Your very restlessness irritates the Cat/Rabbit. This will be an excellent year for investment. Make it your priority to conduct business, but keep your sharp little eyes peeled for trickery and theft. If you are not in a committed relationship, you could very well fall deeply in love this year. If you do, then whisk your new beloved away to a secluded island where the two of you can daydream about next year, which promises to bring far more favorable vibes your way."},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"Relax, my little Rat friend. The Dragon and you are long-standing allies. You respect the flamboyant Dragon’s need for attention and never threaten to overshadow its brilliance. Your intelligent handling of Dragons is, in fact, legendary. You understand how to let it shine while quietly building your own empire in the background. The mood of the Dragon year is celebratory. These magnificent creatures enjoy hosting large gatherings for thousands at numerous festivals and events of all kinds. Any excuse for a grand commemoration is welcomed. It is the Dragon’s way—the more ceremonial the event, the more it enjoys watching people have fun. You do not mind playing the charming guest among the Dragon’s countless friends, all the while planning your own networking strategies. Play hard this year and make the most of opportunities while the Dragon’s brilliant sun is shining on your life. Enjoy this hectic but fortunate year; it is guaranteed to be one of your most memorable and best."}}},s={introduction:`Distinguished Horse, high style is your style. Self-possessed and proud, you dream of forging your own unique path through life, moving mountains, and transforming the existing order. You are active and energetic. Yet, unless you feel inclined, you may stubbornly refuse to do anything at all. Nobody can make you budge an inch. You are not lazy; you simply do precisely as you please. Nonetheless, Horse individuals are doers. You are a resolute achiever who cherishes your goals. You fear failure and will labor tirelessly to safeguard your career. Money is important to you, and you never let sentimentality impede your progress. You are even willing to step over a few obstacles to achieve what you desire from life.

Passion is the only emotion that can melt your ruthlessness into tenderness. It may even cause you to surrender the keys to your innermost soul, turn your back on family, abandon friends, and erase your past for the sake of pursuing an idyllic future with the object of your affection. Beware! Such exclusive devotion can be the ruin of an otherwise hardy and practical Horse.

Beneath a facade of near dandyism, you are oddly conservative. Your standard-striped ties may feature a shocking pink background, but they are still standard-striped ties. Your basic black dress may boast a sexy off-the-shoulder neckline, but it is still basic black. You perceive yourself as a reliable, straightforward individual. But verbally, you are outrageous, outspoken, and often inappropriate. To belong (and despite your rebellious streak, you yearn to belong), you will spend much of your life learning to control your outbursts. You are irritable and arrogant when provoked—and you are frequently provoked.

Childhood is easy for you; children are expected to be spirited and turbulent. Young adulthood will be a stormy, reluctant period. Although fitting in appeals to you, responsibility dampens your high spirits. Maturity arrives late for Horses. But once it has its common sense under control, the Horse progresses smoothly. Here's a piece of advice: do not break rules. Crime is not your strong suit. Your happiness lies in your work.`,elements:{Wood:`Perhaps the most opinionated of all Horses, the Wood Horse, although a sociable, convivial person, gives little quarter to weakness, either in others or in himself. This Horse, governed by the verdant Wood element, has a tendency to judge others by his own standards, making him intolerant, harsh, and, at times, impossible to get along with.

Although he can hardly be considered as giving as Mother Theresa or as self-sacrificing as Albert Schweitzer, the Wood Horse is capable of great altruism. He is often known for his generosity towards those less fortunate—but only those he deems worthy of his gifts. He thrives on influencing others and enjoys watching people pull themselves up by their bootstraps to finally take charge of their lives. The Wood Horse will gladly help the strong grow stronger but is not apt to sponsor fragile souls who want to depend on him for life. So the Wood Horse is charitable, but not philanthropic.

Wood Horses may suffer from the blinding light of their own brilliance. From birth, they feel different and special. At home and then at school, they are applauded for their fine intelligence and hailed by teachers as more willing to take chances than the other kids. Once out in the world, the Wood Horse, a sociable and likeable person, is again encouraged by the praise of bosses and superiors. He seems to know instinctively how to rise to the top without half trying.

As a born over-achiever, the Wood Horse may arrive at the age of thirty holding three doctorates and a master's degree in four different subjects. Being the type to try anything once, he may suddenly decide that what he really wants is to become a writer, singer, actor, painter, or dancer! He may reject job offers, close his ears to worn-out accolades, and take up residence in a freezing cold garret where he will sculpt until he gets really good at it. Then he may grow bored and decide to further his study of nuclear medicine.

If he is not careful to manage his talents, focus on his aims at an early age, and find his social niche before he reaches thirty-five, this Horse may find himself burnt-out by age forty, a jack of all trades and master of none. There are worse fates than being forty and knowing how to fly airplanes, do brain surgery, and tap dance, but it is wise to have some idea of who one is and where one is going before the onset of middle age. This is the Wood Horse's toughest challenge. Not only is he so good at everything, so adventurous, and such a hearty risk-taker that he feels tempted to have it all, but he is also highly susceptible to praise and greedy for the thunderous applause all this achievement brings him. It’s difficult for him to get off his own roller-coaster.

Wood Horses hate authority and refuse to yield to those who claim to rule them from a position of hierarchy. If the Wood Horse feels that the person telling him what to do is not equal to him in brains and brawn, he will walk away, leaving the boss to listen to his own ratings. He is bold and, at times, foolhardy. Important jobs will be awarded to him because of his excellent academic record and affable personality, but sometimes he loses them or is demoted because he refuses to be dominated by fools.

The Wood Horse is an excellent self-promoter. He knows every trick to get himself noticed. He usually sports a very pleasant demeanor. He is, for example, gifted in holding the attention of an audience and has good luck in careers where public speaking or performing are prerequisites. Wood Horses can excel at politics, as they are both bright and persuasive. They are also very funny, with a sharp, biting sense of humor. Unfortunately, they don't usually know how to laugh at themselves; their jokes almost always poke fun at others. Male Horses can be extremely sarcastic.

The Wood Horse is not only intolerant of those he considers less clever than himself, he is envious of those who are better established or more successful. Jealousy is a terrible curse, and its presence in the life of this otherwise sunny soul gnaws away at his nervous system, eats at his equilibrium, and causes him both emotional and physical distress. Ordinarily he looks before he leaps, but in an attempt to eliminate anguish, the envious Wood Horse is capable of making rash moves and committing foolish, warlike errors which may cause him to lose both ground and face with those who hitherto respected him for his wisdom.

On the surface, the Wood Horse is easy to get along with, charming, and friendly. He loves novelty and is attracted by new ways of approaching old problems. He is a jolly companion who longs to be the center of attention. In love, Wood Horses make fun-loving sexual partners who enjoy the game of seduction. They are good-looking, innovative, and never boring in bed. Wood Horses, though, do tend to be a shade on the selfish side; they may seek their pleasure first and, if there's time, will then consider that of their partner.

In general, Wood Horses try to be cooperative. They may be head and shoulders above the crowd, but they still want to fit in. Yet compromise is not their strongest suit. They bridle at the notion of keeping their opinions quiet, as they like to think of themselves as authorities on many matters. If consulted, they may swell with pride, make grandiose pronouncements, give untimely or overbearing advice, and even become meddlesome with friends and family.

There exists in this creature a lack of intuitive perception. If you have dealings with a Wood Horse, no matter how his aura of genius impresses you, remember that exceptional intelligence does not compensate for a lack of feeling and insight. He is smart, elegant, glib, and fun-loving. He is witty and multi-talented. He can talk the pants off anyone who will listen and is afraid of no trick. But this Horse has about as much second sight as an earthworm. If the Wood Horse is wise, he will try to learn the trick of true human understanding by trying to learn (through the gentler hearts of those he trusts) to feel and intuit more effectively.`,Fire:`Oh, la la! The most challenging sign of all to define. Before I attempt to describe the Fire Horse's character, let me state that whatever I have previously mentioned about Horses in general (brilliant, rebellious, attractive, stubborn, self-centered, socially obsessed, etc.) can now be multiplied tenfold in intensity and applied directly to this mystifyingly irritable and lovable personality.

Fire Horses do not do anything by halves. Every Fire Horse is a walking magnifying glass for ordinary experience. In the mind's eye of a Fire Horse, every tiny gesture is a world-class event, every sigh a howl, every friendly kiss a meaningful experience. Fire Horses transform every tear into an ocean of sorrow and convert every titter into an uproarious belly laugh.

In dealing with Fire Horses, you cannot win for losing. If you make any attempt to get close to this adorable monster of temperamental behavior, you will end up confused and bewildered, wondering what you have said or done that could cause such an unmanageably inappropriate reaction in what, two minutes before, seemed a normally balanced human being.

When it comes to discussing himself, the Fire Horse is a sealed tomb. He is a master at deterring interlocutors with sullen glares and sarcastic remarks. He obstructs all probing conversation and stops progress before it begins. The Fire Horse is unable to engage in normal discussion or argument, dares not exchange a few sociable remarks, or indulge in verbal sparring with friends. Life itself is amplified for the Fire Horse. Whatever happens, he almost always over-reacts. He might get so angry that he could hurt someone or blurt out a cutting remark that will end a friendship.

Wise Fire Horses learn early how to stop the battle before the first shot is fired. They simply take the initiative and eliminate their adversary. Conversing with these volatile Fire individuals is dangerous to one's self-image. So, if you are planning an affair with a fascinating Fire Horse, prepare for a constant volley of rapid-fire put-downs—and do not say I did not warn you. Fire Horses are formidable individuals.

Yet even at their most smoldering, Fire Horses are among the most endearingly genuine souls on Earth. All of their antics and exaggerated behavior make them extraordinarily interesting to be around. They are oddly naive and, at the same time, amazingly sophisticated. They can kiss you one minute and try to annihilate you the next. They may taunt or tease you into striking out at them and then be deeply sorry and claim that they wish they were dead because they hurt your feelings. They are deliciously funny and playful, too. Their incisiveness is remarkable, and their talents are myriad. To know a Fire Horse is to love a Fire Horse—or else!

But, like the fickle element that governs them, Fire Horses get so swiftly out of control as to be in constant danger of setting their own precarious world on fire. These are rebellious, difficult, hard-working people. It is impossible for most normal mortals to comprehend what Fire Horses are really doing because: (1) they are not natural sharers of private or emotional information; (2) they prefer only to project vibes about what pertains directly to them and their own ambitions, hopes, and dreams; (3) they have practically no capacity for compassion; (4) they have little sense of family or loyalty to it; (5) they are excessive and unstable; (6) they are ruthless, selfish, and proud.

Fire Horses have some dreadful faults, but they also possess a multitude of good qualities: (1) Fire Horses are splendid to look at; (2) they are exciting; (3) they are creative geniuses; (4) they have limitless energy for achievement; (5) they are solid citizens; (6) they are ingenious; (7) they are exceptionally clever; (8) they love with burning intensity.

The Fire Horse lives with a volcano inside him, which threatens to erupt if he opens his mouth even slightly. At an early age, he becomes aware that his reactions are considered excessive. He cries louder than other babies, laughs harder, and eats more. Soon, his parents begin to perceive him as a perilous pot of simmering milk about to boil over. They handle him gingerly, as though he might explode. Yet, despite the inner volcano, our subject is, first and foremost, a Horse. He wants to fit into a group or social unit. He desires popular acceptance and needs to be cared for and about by his peers and family. But if he cannot discipline his explosiveness, the Fire Horse can remain misunderstood and may end up a social outcast.

The young Fire Horse's life is a series of attempts by himself, his peers, and his entourage to control the flames, to stay close to the warmth without being scorched, and to keep the home fires burning without having to call the fire department. This sensitive lifestyle is hardly conducive to stability. In this atmosphere, the young Fire Horse often grows more and more remote, rigid, and unapproachable. His own family feels left out. His friends find him impenetrably sulky and withdrawn. But the Fire Horse suffers most from his unbreakable spirit. He encounters many obstacles to controlling his own rage and tempering his fervor. He finds normal expression pale and even dull when compared to what he truly feels inside. He even begins to think of himself as a misfit.

Usually, feeling ill at ease among his wary friends and overly deferential relatives, he rebels and leaves home early to make his own way in his own time. As a result of this departure, the Fire Horse directly confronts his extravagant self in the real world of work and moneymaking, spending, and responsibility. The new challenge is enormous and more to his liking. He may feel burdened when asked about his headaches in the confining intimacy of his home; but competing to become a first-rate opera singer in New York does not deter him for a second. He believes in his own capacity for greatness.

Fire Horses try to bring about change through sheer force of will. They push hard until the obstacle yields or walk away in a huff and go it alone. They do not have patience with long-term solutions or power games, refusing to willingly engage in either.

The life of a Fire Horse is never simple. He struggles uphill against his own internal resistance, suffers from envy, and seeks revenge against his enemies. He is enormously talented, and his gifts are usually recognized early by teachers and specialists alike. But he lacks perseverance, refuses authority, and often abandons a brilliant future in favor of solitude and independence.

Virtually all Fire Horses have difficulty with personal relationships. They want to believe that others are as perfect as they imagine themselves to be. When things do not turn out as they hope, they are stricken with disappointment and despair. Many Fire Horses suffer from depression and may have nervous breakdowns. They grieve over losses that less dramatic souls would consider moderate; they languish in netherworlds of silent rage where they feel lost and lonely but from which they are unable (and sometimes unwilling) to escape. Then again, they may suddenly feel wonderful, wake up on the right side of the bed for years at a stretch, and dwell for a period in euphoric happiness. During these good spells, Fire Horses often make positive things happen. "Genius" is not too strong a word to describe their creative talent. Even in love, Fire Horses are rapacious and abstinent, greedy and generous, selfless and selfish. Commit yourself to one of these volatile characters, and you will never experience a moment’s boredom.`,Earth:`In the Horse born in an Earth year, we encounter a better-natured and more easy-going Horse than the rest. The Earth provides a solid base to the otherwise skittish and nervous Horse individual. He is less impulsive, more level-headed than his counterparts. The Earth Horse is a straightforward person with sound ideas that he puts into practice either alone or under the guidance of some serious superiors. He works well in groups and is able to add an element of fantasy to even the most mundane work situations.

For a Horse, he accepts authority graciously. As an employee, he instinctively knows how to be innovative and competitive without committing immature acts of insubordination. Although he may be excitable, and even inconsistent, generally his work style is positive. Just as he is willing to take orders, he is also able to give them. He handles people well, is never too bossy or critical, and, as he has a congenial nature, he is usually well-liked. The Earth Horse has fewer problems with relationships than his fellow Horses, as he is perhaps the most compassionate and altruistic of them.

The Earth Horse is often an artistically talented person whose special gifts preclude the necessity for routine jobs. He would much prefer to be a film director than vice president of a bank. He'd rather perform cabaret than work in an office. He is far more gifted for singing or acting or dancing than he is for practicing medicine or reading law. The Earth Horse knows how to take a back seat and put his ego aside. Compromise and diplomacy come easily to him. His financial picture is generally healthy too. Thanks to his reputation as a competent budget manager, the Earth-born Horse is frequently called upon to restore failing businesses to profitability, to resolve messes created by incompetent individuals in the building trade, or even to troubleshoot in the military.

Although he can be excitable and excessive, the Earth Horse is capable of toning down his extravagance. He is a fighter and will go to the front for what he believes in. But he is a born advocate of the adage, "He who fights and runs away, lives to fight another day." The Earth Horse will only struggle to a certain point. If he can foresee that a battle might deplete his resources, he will turn tail and race back to the safety of the stable. The Earth Horse doesn't mind losing face by losing a single battle, as his true aim is to win the war.

Less self-involved than other Horses, the Earth Horse often engages in activities that seek to remedy society's ills: feminist politics, adopting orphans, helping the elderly claim their rights, cleaning up messes after natural catastrophes.

Even though he rarely appears timid or acts like a shrinking violet, the Earth Horse is hypersensitive. He may weep at the slightest provocation—sob at a stranger's wedding or sniffle through an entire movie. This hypersensitivity may cause him to be grouchy or at least testy. He loves growing flowers and tending to animals and may even perform delicate handiwork such as building furniture or quilting.

The Earth Horse loves the countryside. His mood is often deeply affected by feeling confined in an urban environment. Running wild and breathing fresh country air fuels his artistic bent and frees up inhibitions. His best choices for a career are in art or art-related fields. Painting or any graphic art will suit the Earth Horse. He can be outstandingly successful in all areas involving the theater and cinema. He is a creative person whose ideas are not merely new and exciting but, because he is a Horse, practical—and, as an Earth Horse, even his grandest projects are always grounded, sensible, and safe.

Writing is a less obvious profession for this Horse because he doesn't enjoy sitting still for long—he needs activity and movement to be happy. If he likes to write, he might want to try journalism or copywriting, where he can remain active. This talented character can also flourish in music. He can become a maestro in almost any field where a musical inclination is required. He might be a producer or an instrumentalist, a singer, conductor, or composer. The Earth Horse has a special musical gift. Even if he doesn't opt for music as a profession, he can always take it up as a hobby.

The Earth Horse, like all the other Horses, falls in love intensely. Once he has found the person he feels is right for him, he is likely to stay where he landed for the rest of his life. The Earth Horse is faithful and traditional: he enjoys family life—especially if he is the parent who manages everything—and insists on well-behaved, happy children. He has intense and long-lasting friendships that he cultivates as carefully as his garden. If, however, he is betrayed by someone he cares about and trusts, he will seek revenge and demand retribution. When wronged, he can be vindictive and blind to his own faults. Nonetheless, he's a saner, more reflective, and certainly more commonsensical Horse than most.`,Metal:`Outstanding talent and a knack for basking in the spotlight without developing an inflated ego are two of the Metal Horse's special qualities. It is adroit, forceful, and combative in its driving ambition to achieve success in life. People usually perceive this individual as a true "fighter," someone who is definitely assertive, ready for action, and armed with a strong personal sense of self-belief. Though not truly pugnacious, the Metal Horse prefers to remain vigilant and rarely lowers its guard. Metal Horses carry themselves with confidence, which deters others who might try to obstruct their path.

You might assume that this bravura is merely a defense to conceal sensitivity or a lack of confidence, but it is not. The Metal Horse maintains strict control over its emotions. It must hold itself in check to sustain a dignified and respectable public image. It is always well-dressed in a conservative, tasteful manner. It lives in the "right" neighborhoods, buying or renting in the most proper suburbs or keeping a stylish temporary residence in the more exclusive areas of all the best cities worldwide. The Metal Horse is careful to engage in acceptable, noble sports activities: tennis, golf, sailing, or fencing. It usually marries individuals from "good" families, joins the most prestigious clubs, sends its children to the "right" schools, and dines at the "in" restaurants recommended by the "best" critics.

Yes, our Metal Horse is somewhat of a snob. But it has a solid reason to disdain poor quality and common sports. The Metal Horse thrives on material comfort, which it knows it can only secure for itself and its family if it associates with the right circles, pursues the most lucrative jobs, and is perceived as better-mannered, educated, and dressed than its rivals. The Metal Horse is more ambitious than intelligent, more self-driven than a scud missile... and tougher than tungsten.

It is not entirely fair or accurate to condemn this eager individual so hastily, recklessly categorizing it as a thoughtless, blindly ambitious go-getter. The Metal Horse is nobody's fool. It is unusually quick-witted, bright, and agile. It likes to stay within the boundaries set by society, pays its taxes on time, and rarely cheats. It is always punctual, well-dressed, and often has perfect teeth. Its children never use drugs, and its dog does not bite the postman. You must know at least one Metal Horse; it is that infuriatingly well-put-together person who lives in the lovely flat on the second floor of your building, about whom nobody ever knows anything except that it appears to do everything correctly.

Obviously, the Metal Horse is far from perfect. It has faults, but it conceals them. It has troubles, but keeps them to itself. It has a heart, but it's kept under wraps. The Metal Horse guards its secrets carefully because it fears both pain and the guilt of shame. It's skittish of messy emotional situations and flees every intimate discussion. Its cupboards are in perfect order and its kitchen sink shines. It is wary of what others may think. Its dinner parties are timed to the last toothpick and its car never breaks down. It is determined to appear to be in control in the eyes of its peers. The Metal Horse is also terrified of disorder and even avoids spontaneity. If everything isn't planned in advance—something might go wrong. When the dishes are washed and the sink is scrubbed and the fire's laid then (and only then) the Metal Horse will allow his compulsive little head to lay itself upon the pillow for a well-earned snooze.

This Horse is inherently clumsy. It is constantly tripping over things and almost drowning in its own bathtub. The result? From an early age, it starts polishing its image, planning its time slots, and setting up calm facades to hide its inadequacies. It is a walking time-bomb of potential mistakes and a master of camouflage.

The Metal Horse is a rather robust lover. Though its technical skills may be excellent, it never seems to be doing much more than performing a task well. It's not cold or without physical passion, but it never completely lets go. As its sensitivities must remain hidden, it eschews tenderness and recoils from gentle caressing. If you love one of these effective, ambitious creatures, you will be forced to employ cunning to keep him in bed after lovemaking. No post-coital cuddling or spooning for this individual. The Metal Horse is more likely to make love, then leap up to do the laundry, make a phone call, or turn on the TV.

Of course, it is a serious worker. All professions requiring good social skills, group dynamics, and team integration are perfectly suited for the Metal Horse. It can be an efficient boss or a junior employee, but the Metal Horse will not stay an underling for long. It loves hierarchies and thrives on the challenges of climbing the sturdy ladder to success. It adores material wealth and has an obsession with acquisition. Quality items with pedigrees and historical references line the walls of its house. You never eat from cheap dishes in the Metal Horse's home, and the flowers are always fresh too.

Paradoxically, this Horse deplores routine and dislikes confinement. It is a restless soul who requires change and movement. I do not advise it to take any job that does not require travel. Action is its best friend. The more it does, the healthier and happier the Metal Horse will be. Its need for motion can sometimes hinder the Metal Horse’s enjoyment of a family life. It can make a commitment—but not to anything that doesn't readily evolve. If it feels trapped in a static relationship or family situation where there’s no room for improvement or change, it may bolt. The Metal Horse would prefer to live alone than feel trapped in a no-win marriage or love affair. Some turn to drink when struggling in bad marriages or relationships. For this Horse, divorce is preferable to drugs, gambling, or lifelong depression.

The wise Metal Horse will try yoga and meditation to temper its fever-pitch existence. Otherwise, the stress it generates by living through one of its packed days might push its delicate nervous system over the edge. Emotional collapse is not uncommon in the Metal Horse. Vitamins and a steady diet of grains and vegetables are recommended to aid its sometimes acidic stomach and sluggish digestion. It usually chooses to remain fit, as it adores sport and exercises obsessively.

When at its best, this Horse is productive and active. It is even thrilled by adversity, considering setbacks mere hurdles. Then, when the moment is just right and the multiple endeavors it is pursuing are all ready, the Metal Horse will leap all obstacles with grace and style…and it always lands smoothly and elegantly victorious from its Herculean efforts.

Lastly, this Horse is very kindly—even charitable, dedicating its time and money for communal and group events. Often these activities are Church-oriented, but they might also have to do with philanthropic or philosophical movements. Unusual for a Horse, the Metal Horse can be spiritual. It is attracted not only to religion but capable of expanding its mind in search of philosophical truth. It can succeed in even the most obscure metaphysical realms as a clergyman, teacher, or physician.`,Water:`Here we have the most generous of Horses, who dotes unconditionally, bestows fabulous gifts, and showers loved ones with old-fashioned practical favors. It is hospitable, full of sound, practical advice, and brimming with energetic attention. It is superbly intelligent and talented. But the Water Horse is different—mellower, calmer, and more socially inclined than the others. It likes to belong, but it doesn't care if it belongs to the country club and can settle for belonging to its family, or to a group of good friends. Because its days are incredibly busy, it has neither time nor talent for brooding or analysis. Thanks to the Water element, this Horse is not as neurotic, self-involved, nor as angry as other Horses.

In fact, this Horse is a real winner. Every young Horse is drawn toward adulthood by a beacon of ambition. Early awareness of the desire to stand out and rise above its environment, spurs it to leave its family to make its own way. The Water Horse is slightly modified.

Like other Horses, Water Horses also leave home early, but they tend to return before the age of thirty, bearing the fruits of their adventures, to share their good fortune with the family they left behind. A Water Horse may always need to keep a safe distance from its home turf because it doesn't function well when encumbered by standards which are not its own. But it will always be there for its parents, ready to pick up the pieces for siblings in distress or rescue a struggling cousin. Water Horses feel the suffering of others intensely and are not afraid to show their devotion in practical ways.

The Water Horse is gregarious and loves to be surrounded. It likes having many children, enjoys working in groups, and having admirers who watch and applaud while it performs its wondrous tricks of bravura and brilliance. It might get together a tasty dinner for a troop of tired girl scouts or pile everybody into the car for a swim in the nearest waterfall or belt out a few jazz ditties on stage at Carnegie Hall, but whatever it does, the Water Horse is happiest when performing for an adoring audience. It needs to feel wanted and loved—which is what he is really all about. APPLAUSE. APPROVAL. ADORATION.

It would be pleasant if these Horses were duly rewarded for their generosity and compensated for their affability, but that is often not the case. Mostly, the Water Horse goes on giving while his entourage receives but does not completely return the favors. People do not rush about telling each other how selfless their Water Horse friends, parents, or colleagues are. They may be impressed that a Water Horse took on the baking so that twelve hundred schoolchildren could have cake on their picnic. But they are usually baffled when it comes to knowing how to approach the Water Horse with gratitude.

Why? The Water Horse emanates a hard-edged aura of competence and self-confidence which puts people off. Once we have watched him in action and applauded, we would like to throw our arms around the Water Horse's neck and kiss him to death. But something about his demeanour discourages us. He’s a bit standoffish. He makes us feel small. Or are we afraid of disturbing him? Maybe he would rather we applaud and then go home and leave him alone.

As kind, giving, and generous as the Water Horse can be, he is distant and doesn't take kindly to gushing gestures of affection or tenderness. He is (like most Horses) afraid of intimacy. He wants to be admired but hates admitting it. He craves adulation but doesn't believe he deserves it. He goes out of his way to do giant love favors for people and has difficulty accepting a hug for his trouble. He needs to maintain distance from those he helps out. I suspect that the Water Horse is locked inside himself in typical Horse fashion and cannot allow himself the luxury of receiving his share of tenderness. Perhaps he fears he will look silly.

If you love a Water Horse, this aloofness may throw you off your feed. You may feel rejected, unloved and obliged to perform some fancy tricks to get close to this character. Not to worry. The seduction, the ruses and emotional slaloming that the Water Horse demands are worth any self-doubt you may feel. Once you are allowed into the cozy sweet heart of a big old Water Horse, you will feel safely loved back forever ... plus, you will have gained the best friend you could want—for life.

The Water Horse is not introspective. He is practical and is not drawn to the metaphysical. He hates abstraction. He thinks intellectuals are idlers who get paid for doing nothing. He cannot abide laziness—either in himself or in others. He likes his life (and the lives of those who surround him) to be lived on the surface. He enjoys material things and is happy working with his hands, making curtains or re-covering a sofa, building an attic room or driving around the countryside hunting down antique glass or ceramic figurines in obscure little shops. He doesn't require luxury but he likes his comforts to be more than adequate.

The Water Horse is funny too: his jokes are always acute and, when it comes to sarcasm and satire, his comments are right on the button. He has usually mastered the art of seeing through artifice. If you want an opinion on good taste or authenticity, whether with regard to a person or an object you found at a flea market, consult a Water Horse. These folk have impeccable taste and a flair for everything visual from decorating to evaluating old paintings.

Water Horses were born to be bosses. Holding down mundane jobs is a problem for the over-achieving Water Horse. He cannot be subjugated to anyone for long and is especially sensitive to taking orders from bosses he doesn’t respect. He comes off beautifully in any job interview so he gets the job right away. But although he may remain polite and answer dumb requests courteously for the first few weeks, he will soon commit an act of blatant insubordination which usually ends in his early resignation. Job choices for this creature are simple—he can be the boss of anything. Independent careers are what he excels at and he is good at everything from medicine to cuisine, from real estate to accounting, from law to photography, acting, singing or film making. Musicians abound among Water Horses, as do graphic artists and writers. He will certainly be artistic and might even be a genius.

Luckily for him, the Water Horse is among the most adaptable of the zodiac's creatures. When he's down he doesn't lie there for long before getting up and starting to run again towards goals of his own making, leaping hurdle after hurdle and finally making it. Project after project may fail but, one day, because of his strong belief in self and remarkable ability to zero in on his goals and stick to routine, the Water Horse will triumph. Because he likes change and rarely uses the same tactic more than once, he may be exhausted by the time he reaches his goal but whatever gain or joy he derives from his major success will be richly deserved.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"In China, even the corner grocer shudders at the mention of this unlikely pairing. The Horse is far too self-centered for the Rat’s kindly giving, dependent nature. Although initially attracted by their differences, they should not marry. Beyond a shared love of money and all it can afford them, no common ground exists between these two. The Rat is likely to be mistreated by the haughty Horse. The Horse is moody, causing the Rat to feel unstable, and so individualistic that he will not even consider the Rat’s feelings, which will unnerve the already anxious rodent. Ultimately, the Horse will not feel sufficiently challenged by a Rat partner. To show his disappointment, the Horse may criticize and attack the Rat who, because marriage is so basic to his security, will keep on keeping on trying to please the nagging Horse. This only makes things worse. Now the Horse despises the Rat for his “weakness”. The Horse’s impatience can lead to a search for pleasure elsewhere and subsequent merciless infidelity. In short, all the negative aspects of the Horse’s personality will be drawn out by the Rat’s frailties. The usually strong Rat will be starved for security. A family and children could temporarily return Rat to his or her whimsical self. But when the children grow up and leave home, the Rat parent will become depressed and lonely. Yet no matter his unhappiness, the Rat, fearing disruption, will not be able to leave the punishing Horse and will only grow bitter and vengeful. A definite marital no-no.",Ox:"Exhausting! These two get along so poorly that the effort which goes into trying is hardly worth the result. What a struggle! The conventional Ox wants to tame the wild, independent Horse, whose only urge is to gallop far away from an authoritarian Ox mate.. Horses like to make their own decisions and abhor meddlesome suggestions. The obstinate Ox never stops bossing and advising. If the Ox interferes too strongly with the Horse’s single-mindedness, the haughty Horse will take every opportunity to mortify the unsuspecting Ox—in public! Best thing about this marriage is the work ethic. It’s very high. Both partners will labor and tote barges and bales without complaint. That’s the plus side. But the Horse will simply not conform to Ox’s ways. He drives the Ox mad with hyper-fanciful ideas of painting the house pink, getting married in black pajamas or taking home a STOP sign from in front of the police station. Ox steams and pouts. The Horse just laughs, convinced he or she is married to a dullard. Sexually, this willful combo will already be dissatisfied on their honeymoon. The Horse, like a wild bronco let loose in a corral, makes mincemeat out of the Ox’s reserve. The slow-paced Ox is still in a state of undress when the Horse is riding the great white way. No harmony will cloud this union.",Tiger:"Auspicious, to say the least. Both parties have unruly natures. Individually, they are independent. They might clash, but the attraction between them is strong and so is the mutual respect. In love, they become wilting passion flowers of vulnerability. As a loving pair, their passion knows few bounds. The Tiger and the Horse are equally inventive and creative. In family matters, the Horse’s conservatism curbs the Tiger’s hotheadedness. They work hard together to raise a fine family in a proper way, yet, thanks to the Tiger’s rebelliousness, the kids will get some relief from the seriousness of Horsey’s approach. Both are optimistic and strong. Usually, if a depression comes along, the Horse is up and the Tiger is down, or vice versa. And no boredom here either. These two are active, lusty life-grabbers. Unless one learns to be practical with money, they may have financial crises. Both know how to earn and both love to spend. The initial sexual attraction is volcanic and they are both imaginative and faithful enough to keep sex exciting over the long haul. This relationship can endure.",Rabbit:"The very name of this union is catastrophe. Cats are sedate, laid back and reserved. Horses are pushy, antagonistic and outspoken. Clashes in everything from decorating style to sexual frequency will stand in the way of this lopsided couple’s happiness. Although both are devoted to pragmatism, each has a different way of dealing with material issues. Cats are cautious, even tightfisted with money. Horses flaunt their wealth openly and try to impress with their generosity. No meeting of minds ever occurs on this touchy subject. Cats are not much on public display. Horses love to show off. Cats like quiet, traditional surroundings. Horses adore bold fantasy settings. The Cat wants to stay at home listening to Brahms. The Horse wants to get up and boogie at the best disco in the funkiest section of town. Hard work is the Horse’s religion. The Cat seeks ways to live and work in luxury without disturbing one immaculately coiffured hair. Does this sound like a harmonious pair? Hardly. Moreover, in sexual settings, the Cat needs soft music, satin sheets and filmy negligees, while the Horse prefers a no-nonsense loft bed sans pajamas and plenty of loud marching music to reach ever-greater heights of fancy sexual athletics.",Dragon:"This couple will, no doubt, boast vociferously of having fallen in love at first sight. Both of these effusive people are firm believers in falling in love as a way of life. The sex meter will be permanently set to hot and heavy mode. They won’t be able to keep their hands off each other. Fact is, sex is about the only thing that distracts these two from a full-time war of wills which inevitably besets their relationship. Horses are authoritarian and don’t like to be told what to do. Dragons like to dominate and hate to be bossed around. Each one is proud, touchy, irritable, self-centered and headstrong. Neither is acquiescent. The Dragon, at least, is sentimental, but the Horse is hard-nosed and tough-minded and knows how to make the Dragon cry. The Dragon is the less conventional of the two and will not hesitate to embarrass the socially correct Horse in public for revenge. I also see money conflicts here. The Dragon and the Horse like to spend. If allowed to have their way, they’ll be broke and in debt ail the time. This ill-suited couple is only happy during the initial, sexy infatuation stage. From there on it’s all downhill. No marriage plans? Keep it that way.",Snake:"These two are strongly attracted to each other. The Horse admires the Snake’s natural ease with people and appreciates its considerate, charitable nature. The Snake, on the other hand, likes and respects the Horse’s spunk and native enthusiasm. Their social life will be rich and full. Trouble sets in when the Horse realizes that the adored Snake mate is “running around”. Promiscuity does not set well with the straight arrow, faithful, devoted Horse. So Horsey flips into recrimination mode. Which forces the Snake to conceal any extracurricular activities more cleverly—but not necessarily give them up. The Horse does not deal well with duplicity. Storms ensue. The Snake has a generous heart. The Horse is more conservative with money. This disparity will cause some world-class rows. Best to let Horsey take over running the finances and doling out money to Snake for fripperies. But don’t expect the money-hungry Snake to sit still for that arrangement. He wants to spend! Horse may bolt. Almost everybody is happy with a sensual Snake person in their bed. Horses have little confidence in their sexuality, but Snakes have more than enough to go around. They make good, considerate teachers. The match can work if Horsey can learn not to fall apart when Snake takes off on sexy, romantic interludes and Snake can learn to curb its penchant for the peccadillo.",Horse:"Not a perfectly harmonious couple. The Horse is self-centered. Two Horses may initially be attracted by their similarities. Merely sharing so many things in common will cement a solid friendship between them. However, unless they can agree to slough off convention and each remain free to go their own way, excitement will be lacking and boredom will smother this hardworking couple in its own hair shirt. These two are open-minded, so, with an extra dose of flexibility, they can function as a productive team. However, the hotheaded, headstrong, willfulness of two Horses can threaten their marriage with discord. As both are gamblers, financial instability can also weaken the marriage. For money matters to tick along as they should, these two should hire an accountant and try to keep their social life active. The influence of softer, gentler souls, will improve the Horse team’s effectiveness. Individuality however, is not always the best ingredient to ensure the success of a team. The Horse couple’s tempestuous sex life will reflect excessive egocentricity on both sides, which may cause the eventual demise of this otherwise diligent, hardy couple.",Goat:"This apparently odd combination sometimes works extremely well. Horses are strong-minded hard workers. Goats are languorous, creative and oh-so-dependent. The Horse in this pair will always feel protective of the Goat mate. Horses like to feel superior and Goats know exactly how to inflate their egos. When decisions are to be made or actions taken, the Goat goes all flabby and swoons, “Honey, you’re so clever. I just know you’re better at this than I am,” and the Horse rides off into the night to play hero. The Goat’s romantic side appeals to the stodgy Horse’s need to learn about love. Even though their sensitivities are not too similar, Horses find ethereal Goats decidedly sexy. They complement each other. Goats are pessimistic; Horses are not. Goats are flaky. Horses are solid conservatives. Goats depend and Horses willingly provide. Horses like things their way and, as long as there’s money in the bank, Goats are supremely flexible. These two are so different that they will never be bored together. Of course, friction might occur, because the Goat can be jealous and possessive and the Horse needs to feel free. But usually, the Goat’s sense of what is most practical for the future will win out and, aside from some mild disapproval, he or she will not tax their partner sufficiently to cause the Horse to bolt.",Monkey:"A mutual desire to stay abreast of events, mingle in society and be part of what’s happening in the outside world will constitute the initial attraction between these two. Monkeys are so versatile, imaginative and amusing that Horses have trouble resisting their charms. Monkeys feel that serious Horses need cheering up and are inspired to make them laugh. Monkeys also appreciate the Horse’s strict sense of duty and ability to endure hard work. They love to join forces and solve problems together. Communication may not be their strongest suit. Monkeys are inveterate neurotics who cherish their unhealthy behavior patterns and although they chatter, they don’t open up easily. Horses are guarded and conservative about speaking up on their own behalf. Much tension may build. They should agree (before reaching the ulcer stage) to see a therapist regularly. Otherwise, unexpressed emotions will cause the death of their union. A brilliant sex life is in store for the Monkey/Horse couple. They are mutually energetic and fanciful about romance. Horse may want more sex than does Monkey, but Monkey’s fertile imagination will more than compensate for lack of appetite. As long as these two don’t sit around complacently, patting each other on the back about how well their couple “works”, they can create a lasting bond.",Rooster:"Unless stimulated by the right partner, both Roosters and Horses become stodgy and work-obsessed. This couple would need a professional or family connection in order to be thrown together in the first place. There is not much charisma on either side at the outset. But, with some work, the relationship can grow and endure. Once together, the Horse will be flattered by the Rooster’s possessive streak, but in time will resent it and dissension will set in. Horse wants to go out and play and Rooster wants them both safely at home – even if it’s only to share the Sunday crossword puzzle. For this relationship to succeed, the Horse must learn to be less outgoing and the Rooster more tolerant of the Horse’s need for social interaction. Roosters are so conservative that, although Horse’s occasional outrageousness appeals to their rebellious side, they will worry nonstop about the negative outcome of their mate’s follies. A Rooster’s best bet is to give the Horse a longer and longer rein, and wait sanely by the fireside till Horsey comes cantering back for dinner. At first, their sex life may be limited by Rooster’s excessive conservatism. The practical Horse will rise to the occasion and prod Rooster to be more innovative. In time, when they learn to satisfy each other’s needs, their sexual rapport can become nigh unto perfect.",Dog:"If this pair hires a nanny and a housekeeper, a laundress and a cook, they can establish a very sound love relationship. Neither these two effective, active, project-oriented people is enchanted by a career as a house drudge or nose-wiper, staying at home waiting for the other to appear. Horses are characteristically profligate with money. They gamble away and take chances others would not. This risky trait fills the disquiet Dog with fear. The Horse hates to be reminded of profligacy but the sarcastic Dog cannot keep quiet for long. Fights—yes, I said fights—ensue. As harmony reigns in their bedroom, these two usually end up being friends after vibrant lovemaking sessions wherein each lavish pleasure on the other. The Dog is giving and the Horse is loving. It’s a good sexual match. The lovemaking may be salutary, but what will ultimately hold this pair together is their deep respect for each other’s integrity. They are mutually honorable people with a refined sense of social and loyalty. Time will round off whatever sharp angles this pair encounters. A durable, solid relationship is assured.",Pig:"Poor Piggy! Horses are notoriously headstrong and willful. The Pig simply cannot say “no” to the Horse’s winning ways. And even though a right-thinking Horsey knows better than to walk all over an acquiescent mate, he cannot help himself. Because they are often very striking, Horses attract Pigs in droves. In their turn, Pigs win the hearts of Horses because they are so willing, generous and tantalizingly compliant. Sexually, these two are well matched. The Horse finds the Pig’s overt sensuality liberating. Pigs like the forceful side of Horse’s sexual nature and are turned on by his handsome appearance. Pigs attract money. Horses work hard and know how to make money, but often gamble it away. The Pig is a natural homebuilder and nurturer. The Horse is an outside person. They complement each other. Providing the Pig can endure the Horse’s frequent absences and accept the outgoing side of his personality, this couple can create a sound basis for a felicitous and prosperous family."},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"This is not the easiest year for Horses. Your new family (read: in-laws) demands much more from you than you are willing to give. Their needs will create dissension and, if you are not careful, could lead to a nasty breakup of your relationship. The Snake’s influence can be laden with half-truths and even fantasies that do not quite align with reality. The Snake longs to believe only its own vision of a given situation and is often reluctant to surrender to reality. So, you may encounter some real obstacles this year in your attempt to get your marriage or long-term live-in relationship off the ground. New beginnings usually sweep clean, but as they age, some of the dirt begins to be swept under the rug or even altogether neglected. The same holds true for a new relationship. Whatever messes are troubling you or your partner must be resolved. And first, they have to be brought out into the open. Sit yourselves down—alone or with a marriage counselor or therapist—and discuss things thoroughly. You will both need to decide where your loyalties lie this year, and it had better not be with the in-laws. A couple is a couple; no intruders are necessary, thank you."},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"According to Chinese legend, the Horse year is not an excellent one for Horses. Most other signs benefit from their own years, but not the Horse. This will be a troubled and sometimes even dangerous year for you Horse individuals. The perils are not your fault; they are simply present, like bad luck. The best way for you to handle this situation, of course, is to exercise caution in all your activities. Opt out of risky business deals. Do not go trekking in the Himalayas. Cancel your subscription to the Bungee Cord Club and renege on all plans for ski holidays in avalanche season in the Andes. In other words, keep it simple. Stay around home a lot. Busy yourself with domestic projects like baking Christmas cookies or working in the garden—and even then, watch out for household accidents. You could pierce your palm with a tomato stake or dent someone’s car on the way to the market to buy flour and chocolate for cookies. Just be careful; you are walking on eggshells this year. Now, please do not go sulk somewhere and not emerge until this year is over. Do understand that the reason for such a difficult time in your life is so you will learn new lessons; it’s all about helping you to see what it’s like to be a Horse of a different color."},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Yin Fire",prediction:"It is about time you received a break from learning new ways to behave and stopped having to be so cautious all the time. Goat years are a breeze for Horses. They bring sunshine into your previously dreary life and encourage you towards ever more intriguing acts and ambitious endeavors. Goats do not demand much from Horses—except that you be strong enough to provide them with a generous back to ride on. You do not mind supporting others; you can handle being depended upon by someone vaguely artistic or too brilliant to be simply idle. The Goat spends its life seeking a pot of gold at the end of the rainbow. He or she knows that you might just be the vehicle to transport them there. This is your chance to go to extremes again. Time to embark on that hike in the Himalayas. Or why not try out several different gambling casinos around the world? Or marry your Cousin Charlie? Do something outrageous. One way or another, under the Goat’s Horse-friendly influence, everything will work out for the best. Even your health will be excellent—as long as you maintain your fitness routine and stick to lean meats, fish, vegetables, and of course… OATS."},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Yang Earth",prediction:'Being of a pragmatic nature, you are not often drawn into shady schemes or led down winding paths where outcomes are not clearly visible. But Monkeys are agile individuals; they are nimble of foot and mind. If you are ever tempted to get involved in anything that deviates from the straight and narrow, it is likely to happen this year. Watch your step. Horses need to work hard to make progress and achieve success. Horses usually do not take shortcuts. Therefore, should you be tempted away from your usual strict adherence to the rules of striving and toil, you may indeed fail—miserably. When presented with attractive "quick fix" plans to avoid taxes by sheltering your yacht in Panama or opening an offshore bank account, just say NO. There are no free lunches for the hard-driving Horse. Monkey years also threaten your waistline. These nimble-minded creatures cannot keep their hands off food, and if you are not extra careful about monitoring your diet, this year can expand your girth to twice its normal size. In fact, the general message for Horses in Monkey years is: Stick to routine and keep your nose clean.'},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Yin Earth",prediction:'If there is one thing you hate more than anything, it’s being held back or restrained in any way. You are a doer, an active person with more irons in the fire than a roomful of blacksmiths. You are a runner, a worker, and a striver. Nobody should ever attempt to hold you down. Yet, you do have to live through this Rooster year where we all feel somewhat constrained by the Rooster’s firm grip on his pocketbook and his disapproval of our wildest dreams. Roosters are serious, single-minded individuals; they cling to conservative ideas and prefer the traditional to the outlandish in life. The atmosphere this year, then, inclines us all to adhere to rules, be thrifty, and stick to tried and true methods. You might, however, be tempted this Rooster year to travel afar to visit tombs and museums, churches, temples, and monuments. The Rooster doesn’t usually disapprove of travel—especially if the journey leads to somewhere instructional and is not just for "fun." I wouldn’t advise you to make any major purchases this year (houses, cars, boats, buildings, farms, etc.) because money will be generally tight and interest rates quite high. All your favorite outspoken and outrageous extreme behaviors should be curbed. Do not try dabbling in clandestine love affairs either. Romantic indiscretions are simply not advisable for Horse people in Rooster years.'},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Yang Metal",prediction:"Horses and Dogs belong together. You gallop gaily about the countryside along with scads of children and cats and chickens and ducks. You two have a natural affinity, and although of different breeds and species, you could easily be thought of as siblings. This year, then, will be a gracious year for Horses. You will, however, be called upon to demonstrate a side of yourself that we do not frequently see. The Dog requires that we involve ourselves in world issues. Dogs want justice and will do almost anything to see that justice is done. They care about the future of the human race. As being engaged in political goings-on has never appealed to the Horse’s free-wheeling, outspoken character, you Horse individuals will be hard-pressed to show that you care who gets to be president or, for that matter, leader of the entire Planet. Why? Because you do not care a fig. You know in your heart that all politics is corrupt, and you want no part of corruption anywhere in your straightforward existence. My advice for you this year is to attempt to try to care. Just do it for your pal, the Dog’s, sake. Be more generous of heart, more giving, and loving to others. Remember, you get out what you put in. That’s the rule in the benevolent Dog year."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Yin Metal",prediction:"Pig years are not among your favorites. Horses insist on working long and hard and being visible about it. You want to be seen as industrious. You need us to know what a good person you are—and how honest and forthright as well. Pigs are not slovenly or lazy; they also work, and sometimes they work extremely hard. But Pigs like a good time. They enjoy inviting people in for a meal, drinking a bit too much, and eating delicious culinary concoctions (often of their own making). You do not mind a good time, but you are not one to waste hours lounging about at table over a final glass of wine or two and some scrumptious cheeses or dessert. The atmosphere of conviviality prevalent in the Pig year, then, might irritate your restless nerves. You want action. Doing, going, working, and being busy keeps your mind off more ponderous, irritating, soulful matters. So this year, you need to slow down and relax. Take a lengthy journey in your new sailboat or buy yourself an old barn to renovate in the country. Be busy, but be relaxed as well. Watch out this year for symptoms of depression or other illnesses caused by stress. You have needed to ease off the accelerator for too long. Take a break and enjoy some of the good, clean fun associated with all Pig years."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Yang Water",prediction:'Do not expect any miracles to appear on your path this year. Rats and Horses are well-known adversaries. There will be an initial attraction, a brief honeymoon period, and then a swift descent into bickering and eventual separation. Rats desire power; you dislike being told what to do. Do you understand the dynamic? Rats need to surround themselves with people they can feel protective of, look after, and guide. There is nothing worse for Horses than to feel smothered by some meddling outsider who interferes in everything the Horse does. Horses value freedom and independence; they do not wish to be held accountable. So, in this Rat year, you Horse individuals had better relax. Remain in the background. Do not attempt any grand stunts or public displays of your talents. Of course, you probably will not follow my advice any more than you would follow the Rat’s instructions. Horses can be led to water, but we cannot make them take even a tiny sip if they do not want to. No amount of coaxing, blackmail, or guilt trips will make them ingest a drop. So, Horses… this Rat year will be a struggle. You would be better off retreating to the countryside for the duration. But as you will not heed my good counsel… as they say for good luck in the theater, "Break a leg."'},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Yin Water",prediction:"Things are looking up. Oxen admire your stamina and ability to undertake hard labor without a complaint or a grumble. This then should be a terrific year for Horses. No interference. No meddling in your business. No directives. However, Ox years are not brilliant for the Horse’s romantic life. You may indeed fall in love this year. And when you fall, you crash—thunderously. But this year, the more passion you direct towards your chosen significant other, the less that person seems to want to become intimate with you. You can avoid being disappointed in love by simply leaving your emotions aside and pursuing your goals independently. Your professional outlook promises nothing but success. As long as you apply consistent effort and demonstrate persistence, the Ox will not only stay out of your way but will applaud you, encourage you, and when it can, will highly recommend you to any influential people you may need to know to advance your career. Health? Nothing serious or life-threatening is imminent. But you really ought to look after yourself better. Horses tend to think they are invincible and rarely, if ever, bother consulting doctors or visiting other health practitioners. Avoiding the symptoms you have been experiencing for far too long without a medical opinion or two could lead to a chronic illness that will remain with you for at least the next twelve Chinese years."},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Yang Wood",prediction:"You are in for some major alterations in everything from your romantic situation to your actual lifestyle. Tigers require change; it’s in their genes. Horses and Tigers are the best of companions. In the Tiger year, you will feel free to be entirely yourself—the real you: the headstrong, spirited, talented, outspoken you. You see, Tigers do not mind your playfulness and strong will. They, in fact, approve of how Horses manage their lives and are themselves ultimately independent and free-spirited. What you do have to watch out for in Tiger years is being drawn into crazy schemes, urged to take eccentric trips to far-flung destinations, or dragged into nutty real estate projects without a backward (or forward) glance. Be cautious of feeling too unrestrained. Avoid departing for some fantastical place from which you will not be welcomed upon your return. You might instead be severely criticized for being irresponsible, as Tigers tend to encourage eccentric behavior. Discreetly observe your own surroundings this year. If you do, you will be pleasantly surprised to find that a surprising romantic interest lurks in your immediate vicinity. Someone you have known for a while will suddenly take a liking to you. Do not retreat; this could be The One."},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"You are favored by the Cat/Rabbit who never wants to get in your way. You are all action and brisk movement, always rushing headlong into projects both new and old. The Cat/Rabbit is a more deliberate, reflective sort who, contrary to you, does little to draw attention to him or herself. Provided you demonstrate your usual ability for hard work and dedication to it, the Cat/Rabbit will stay completely out of your way. This is a good year for you to expand your business, open some franchises, buy land, refurbish or renovate a property or two. Devote some of your free time to your art as well. Drawing and painting. Singing and dancing. Filmmaking or photography or sculpture or ceramics… any and all artistic pursuits will thrive under the influence of the refined Cat/Rabbit. One small blemish on the otherwise pristine face of this Cat/Rabbit year… you may lose confidence in yourself. This sudden slide into melancholy or self-doubt could be caused by boredom. This is not an exciting year. No great new romance. No terminal illnesses. Not much high living. Just work and art. But consider yourself lucky because those are the two things you do best."},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"Here is yet another year in which the ruler maintains a hands-off policy regarding you. Dragons do not meddle much with Horses. If you have the good sense never to attempt to steal the spotlight this year, you will be surprised how positive this twelve-month period will turn out to be. First of all, there is a hint of marriage—or at least a long-term live-in relationship—in the offing for Horses. You are not usually inclined to live full-time with anyone. But when you fall for somebody, you fall hard, and this year is favorable for just that kind of passionate abandon. Dragon years are famous for celebrations and festivities. One of those gatherings might just be your wedding or, at the very least, your engagement party. Before you get too involved, however, I must warn you that part of the Horse’s problem with intimacy stems from the fact that you cannot be happily confined for long. Make absolutely certain that your significant other or future spouse is aware of your penchant for trotting off from time to time into your own realm or even into the ethereal. Marry someone whose independence quotient harmonizes with your own: a Tiger or a Dog would be best. Second best? Who wants second best?"}}},r={introduction:`Oh, Gracious Goat, your sign is the most creative. You are truly gifted, possess a flair for the aesthetic, and enjoy being in tune with nature. You are artless, hardworking, and intuitive. When you’re relaxed, you could teach "take it easy" courses. But before you do anything, you must be provided with security. You need to feel loved, protected, and be grazing safely in a fertile field. Without structure, you're uncomfortable.

You are an eccentric, and something of a winner, too. You don't mind struggling and striving in an effort to reach a noble or tangible goal, but you hate adhering to schedules or performing repetitive, routine chores. You need lots of ready cash, yet you scorn budgets.

A formidable ambivalence divides your basic need for security and your longing for total freedom from stressful limits. Goats are generally very delicate. Your good manners, wiles, and charm will go a long way towards finding that person, group, or profession that offers you maximum protection and allows your talent to thrive. Try your hand at poetry, research, or, better still, just lie back, relax, and embrace a bohemian lifestyle. You would make a perfect hippie.

Try courting an eloquent Horse. Horses know how to work hard for others. Bat your eyelashes at a refined, home-loving Cat or—better still—grab yourself a scrupulous, competent (and often rich) Pig to lean on and love for life. Avoid Tigers and Oxen; they don't approve of your capriciousness.

You don't mind the role of dependent, so you'll probably enjoy a peaceful childhood. As an amorous and fanciful young adult, you may experience some devastating romantic disappointments. But luck shines in the third part of your life, bringing love and security to coddle your tender soul. A bit of practical advice: find your "fertile field" at a young age and force yourself to graze patiently. Your fortune can often be found in somebody else's bank account.`,elements:{Wood:`The influence of Wood on the Goat's whimsical behavior is definitely beneficial. Here we see a strengthened and supported Goat individual. Instead of indulging in frivolous caprice, this Goat manages to maintain a healthy balance between lightheartedness and stability. Of all Goats, this type is most likely to be able to overcome harsh setbacks and carry on valiantly as though nothing untoward had occurred. This Goat is exorbitantly creative, yet more ambitious than many of its counterparts.

The necessity for security and moral support from its immediate circle is still very much present in this Goat's life. Take just a few of the above-mentioned famous men as examples. Arthur Murray, the celebrated dance instructor who gave his name to thousands of ballroom dance studios throughout the world, was typically Goat-like: tall, graceful, and slender. Dancing is a perfect career for a Goat; and Arthur Murray was an excellent, innovative teacher. He was not, however, a manager. He always said that his wife Katherine was the brains behind the expansion and management of the Arthur Murray operation. Without her, he claimed, "I would still be swirling around a summer pavilion dance floor looking gorgeous." Knowing his Chinese sign, I believe him.

Wood Goats are indeed so talented and innovative that marriage and a stable home life often serve as the necessary springboard for them to dare to venture out into the challenging world and make their fortunes. They need to know that they can always come home and feel safe where they live.

The Wood Goat is young at heart. Even under pressure, he manages to keep a smile or a joke on his lips. Because of this gift for optimism (exceptional in Goats), he confronts adversity more readily and extricates himself more gracefully than most Goats who are likely, in their frustration, either to crumble or surrender.

Given to mood swings, the Wood Goat gets depressed from time to time. These sinking spells or periods of gloom are often caused by the hormonal fluctuations common to all Goats, but particularly severe in this Goat. Careful monitoring of endocrine gland function is advised.

The Wood Goat lives in a permanent state of moral dilemma. He is, like all his Goat counterparts, a hedonist, a potential lifelong pleasure-seeker. However, the Wood Goat wants to achieve. He does not choose to remain in the herd, and he knows that to reach the lofty goals he imagines, he might have to commit himself to a life of both hard work and protracted routine effort. This prospect, for any Goat, is daunting. The Wood Goat can handle it.

To satisfy his desire for success, the Wood Goat, in his inimitable resourcefulness, learns young how to choose effective friends and associates. First, he cultivates their affections, then trusts them implicitly to assist him in getting where he wants to go. I would not go so far as to call this Goat a "taker." He doesn’t use people to his own ends. Rather, the Wood Goat is a jolly parasite. He is easy to have around—a joy and an inspiration to those who will generously surround him with essential comforts, calm, and sustenance. And hard work delights him, so influential people willingly give him a hand to get almost anywhere he wants to go.`,Fire:`The Fire Goat is a walking emotional maelstrom. Passion governs its existence. No matter how it tries, it cannot react calmly to stimuli, remain composed in the face of insult, or appear aloof when provoked. Mind you, this Goat is no pouncing Tiger who devours its adversaries before they have a chance to finish their sentences. Its methods are more akin to theatrics. It is prone to dramatic displays and erupts into rages or succumbs to nervous collapse. The Fire Goat is excessively sensitive and requires a stronger emotional restraint than most to keep its volcanic sentiments in check. A steady partner can make all the difference to the success or failure of the Fire Goat's life.

This individual is renowned for its charm and ability to influence others through a quality we might call refinement. Its sensitivity is almost palpable, causing the very hairs on forearms to rise. People are drawn to it and instantly admire its uplifting style. The Fire Goat's ability to reach masses of people with its words or to touch their emotions with its talent for seizing the moment or interpreting a role is legendary. It is exceptionally talented but requires top-notch guidance to ensure its perseverance.

This individual must not be compelled to manage its own finances. The mere thought of balancing a checkbook is enough to trigger one of the Fire Goat's fainting spells. If success comes knocking, it is well advised not to open the door until it has summoned its resident accountant to stand by. The Fire Goat is a reckless squanderer of money—its own and other people's. If you know and love one of these ethereal creatures, you are hereby warned to maintain strict control over joint accounts and impose limits on credit cards. The Fire Goat is not dishonest, but it is both thoughtless and inconsequential about spending. Fortunately, it is also incredibly lucky. I certainly do not advise gambling, but the occasional raffle ticket couldn't hurt, could it?

This Goat can enjoy some degree of superiority in a hierarchy but must not assume too grand a role. An excess of responsibility can lead to the onset of chronic ailments such as migraines or ulcers. A Fire Goat has a short fuse. When angered, it does not know how to keep its antagonistic feelings suppressed. Leadership demands self-control; the Fire Goat is deficient in that commodity.

Charisma is the Fire Goat's strong suit. Its gentle manner and aura of mystery attract others. The best professions this person can choose will involve theater, movies, music, mysticism, philosophy, the subconscious, occult science, or perhaps physics or other mind-liberating sciences.

It follows, then, that the Fire Goat is drawn to causes that seek to improve the quality of our inner as well as our outer lives. Fire Goats can take the lead in such areas as acting, directing, singing, ecology, health professions, nutrition, or alternative medicines. A smart Fire Goat can make a handsome fortune in these and other New Age pursuits. But it must surround itself with honorable and sympathetic associates who will never give it the key to the safe.`,Earth:`There is genius in the Earth Goat's makeup. Given the proper circumstances, skill and business may combine to help this Goat create a superlative and luxurious (just the way it likes it) lifestyle.

But the Earth Goat is perpetually erratic. Half the time it cannot decide what it wants to do, and the other half it suddenly becomes determined and pursues a difficult-to-achieve goal. Sometimes it succeeds, and things go swimmingly, provided it is well protected and insured against its own worst enemy—itself.

The Earth Goat tends to be argumentative. Its talent for talking things through is more pronounced than that of other, less naturally verbal Goats. But it often bases its arguments on illogical premises or fleeting dreams that happen to be circulating in its psyche and catch its fancy. As it does not always think things through to their logical conclusion, the tone of these discussions is often chaotic. If it is not careful, people eventually grow to mistrust its judgment, and it becomes the subject of some ridicule among its peers. Studying logic in college and participating in school debating teams would provide a sound basis for the Earth Goat to spare itself disrespect in later life.

Despite its tendency to bicker over trivialities at every turn, the Earth Goat has one of the most manageable Goat natures. It knows very well that its survival depends on the goodwill it can generate among those who surround it. It hardly ever pushes its disputes too far, causing rifts or break-ups. In fact, it displays almost no follow-through urge to assert its rights, demand its due, or seek reparations. However, if it feels it has been wronged, it will resort to lawyers. The image of a lawyer "standing up" for it where it cannot and will not do so for itself is tempting to this kind of Goat. Life with the Earth Goat is usually suffused with a spirit of cooperation and gentility—unless it feels betrayed; then, it loses its temper.

Its lack of objectivity gets it into scrapes, however, particularly in the work hierarchy. Because of its inherent passivity and gift for concession and compromise, the Earth Goat is sometimes blamed for wrongs it did not commit. More ambitious, ruthless colleagues will happily take advantage of its laid-back, semi-unresponsive nature to leap over its desk in pursuit of their own selfish ends.

Ultimately, the biggest challenge to the Earth Goat is simply to endure, but not necessarily to prevail. More than anything, it wishes to be left to its own devices to follow its lucky stars and dream its impossible dreams without interference from more down-to-earth folk who feel that they are doing it a favor by bringing truth into its life.

It's a tricky and perilous management challenge both to remain dependent on the support of others and still maintain intact one's integrity and dreams. The tightrope it walks may cause a feeling of imbalance in the Earth Goat's inner self. Physical symptoms may result that are solely manifestations of this lack of equilibrium. Epileptic seizures, spells of weakness, and dark, gloomy depressions may crop up. When this happens, a good lover or lifelong companion or caring boss needs to be right there for its Earth Goat. Nothing short of sitting it down with some old-fashioned straight talk and reassurance about its security will clear up the messy muddles into which this Goat's elusive psyche can lead it. When properly handled, the Earth Goat's startling talents can afford it the highest accolades. Its imagination knows no bounds. It is sympathetic and understands even the most incomprehensible human behavior. It is often a brilliant, sympathetic soul. But it has to watch out for its own scatterbrained tendencies. If not, it may well tarnish its image in the eyes of those who respect it.`,Metal:`Goats appear in the most unexpected places! I tell you that they are dependent and sometimes frail and super artistically creative, and then someone major and powerful like Gorbachev or Rupert Murdoch turns out to be a Goat. The Metal Goat seems, to the uninformed outsider, a gentle pushover. Its unassuming, disheveled, casual style suggests only simplicity and innocence. But beware: although the influence of Metal does enhance the gentle Goat's resolve, it also hardens its heart, causing it to become unnecessarily combative when dealing with others.

Goats are generally non-confrontational and are known to have to depend on the kindness of strangers for their survival. At all costs, they must appear to be compromising and easy-going. This is true of the Metal Goat: it cannot and does not risk open conflict. Yet, as it is temperamental, it often feels interfered with and imposed upon. To avoid being visible and therefore doubly vulnerable, the combativeness in this individual goes underground. Metal Goats delight in secret manipulation and subterfuge, and perform their most skillful string-pulling from behind the scenes.

For this reason, the Metal Goat makes an easy-going friend but is a daunting adversary. It will never speak its mind in any controversy. It categorically refuses to deal one-to-one in open conflict. It will not take stands on any controversial subject, nor will it brave danger for the sake of a good cause. The Metal Goat favors underhanded means and is quite capable of lying and justifying even the most amoral behavior to itself if it does not get its way. The wronged Metal Goat is consumed by the need for revenge and will stop at nothing to gain ground against its (real or imagined) enemies.

At home in the hidden depths of the collective unconscious, the Metal Goat can readily pursue careers where knowledge of the inner workings of the human mind is a prerequisite. It will make an excellent forecaster and interpreter of human behavior: a soothsayer or psychiatrist, an incisively charismatic actor or film director, a politician, a brilliant writer or singer, or, more simply, a willing courtesan. Alternatively, it might choose to stay at home and become an inventor, trying to concoct a gourmet elixir of youth, to make gold from aluminum foil, or improve on some secret eavesdropping device.

Of all the Goat types, this one is perhaps the most elementally lacking in a sense of urgency. It will not hurry. It insists on moving ahead in a leisurely way and hasn't got a clue how its lackadaisical behavior affects others.

This Goat can rise to great heights by advancing steadily at its own unhurried pace. But because the subconscious is always pulling at it, it often falls victim to self-deceiving bad habits, such as drug, alcohol, or diabolical religious addictions.

A well-nurtured Metal Goat's talent can bring it enormous rewards, but it must watch out for a dangerous tendency to self-congratulatory boasting. Metal Goats suffer from an excess of pride. Sometimes their vanity gets in the way of their common sense and thwarts the possibility of reaching a desirable goal.

The remedy? Lots of tough love and no-nonsense nurturing may help to bring reality out of the basement of the Metal Goat's mind and put its thoughts into better perspective.`,Water:`The Water Goat's claim to fame is its skill at using its intuition. Of course, all Goats are sensitive and easily pick up on feelings—but Water bestows a special talent for intuiting the flavor and tone of even the most subtle of life's situations on this fluid variety of Goat. Where hints of danger, twinges of fear, or suggestions of sexuality or extraterrestrial activity may pass unnoticed by less perceptive folk, every nuance is picked up by the supremely impressionable Water Goat. It seems able to understand without learning and to know certain things instinctively without necessarily having first comprehended them.

Although compassion is the emotion that can be most profoundly felt by it, the Water Goat is oddly egocentric and quite unable to escape from its golden bubble of preoccupation with itself long enough to relate to those it might feel sorry for. It is neither a natural care provider nor is it very altruistic. Rather, the Water Goat senses the way things are moving, then zigzags through the loaded minefields of life, relying solely on its inner radar to guide it. It seeks more to stave off danger and predict events for itself than to warn others of potential harm.

Water Goats are intensely charming and sensual. They love being needed and adore having an audience. Adulation and applause provide approval and help to keep them moving. Appreciation serves to push them to heights they might not aspire to without external urging. Their inner emotional structure is somewhat shaky, so being encouraged, cheered, and inspired by friends and family is of great assistance to them in making decisions, accomplishing tasks on time, and overcoming hurdles without the usual Goat-like pessimism or hesitation.

There is a kinky side to this Water Goat's sexual character. The male of the species is amorous and romantic and requires abundant physical attention from females. In her geisha-like way, the sensuous woman Water Goat also comes on very strong. Although quiet and unassuming, the Water Goat lady is a true siren whose amiable sexual prowess is never a well-kept secret. In fact, hardly a day goes by that this Goat does not engage in sexual activity or fantasy. There is a strong propensity among Water Goats to engage in group sex and other forms of unconventional and promiscuous activity.

When you get to know this Goat well, you rapidly understand why this has often been known as the sign of the hippie or Bohemian. Water Goats don't care to heed the rules and regulations of the standard social system. They prefer to remain outside, looking in, enjoying a certain detachment from the mainstream, and managing to hover about three feet above their own and others' heads.

Water Goats, like their brothers and sisters of the other Goat signs, frequently possess genius. When they put this to practical use, the road ahead may quickly lead to stardom because, of all Goats, this one knows best how to use its influence to make contacts, open doors with its sexual charms, and eagerly seize opportunities. It knows instinctively how to move in the "right" circles, get itself known to the "right" people, and find ways to be noticed by influential types who can get it where it wants to be. This Goat is never too pushy or boastful but, rather, plays its hand deftly by maintaining tight relations with influential people who can put it where it thinks it ought to be.

Although it doesn't usually assert its will aggressively, the Water Goat does not like being thwarted or interfered with. If it doesn't get its way, or feels it has been shunted aside, its well-developed sense of martyrdom rises straight to the surface. Its whining can be heard for miles. The "Poor me" side of the ultra-sensitive Water Goat is absolutely its worst fault. If it can control this tendency, it will be a true charmer, a delightful, well-mannered individual, and a terrifically amusing friend. But when that "Why me?" refrain rises from the depths of the silken chaise longue, I advise you to head for the hills and hide under an anonymous rock until the sniveling is over. And don't feel guilty. If you don't take care of poor little Water Goat in his deepest chagrin, he will make it his business to see that somebody else does.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"This is a tricky one. The Goat enjoys the loving Rat’s company but finds his nervousness unappealing. The Goat’s peaceful nature appeals to the snuggly Rat, but the Goatly lack of interest in the menial tasks of everyday life will cause the Rat to fret and worry. The Goat’s fey, lackadaisical nature will strike the industrious Rat as rank laziness. The Goat will spend too much money on unnecessary items. The Rat will suffer anxiety about debt, fiscal responsibility and pervasive insecurity. This household is in a constant state of cold war. The Rat worries quietly and the Goat lacks the necessary initiative to loosen up his troubled mate. All their battles will be fought with underhand tactics and vicious stares. The Rat will long for a partner with more oomph. The gracious Goat, not courageous enough to confront the Rat, will resist lethargically—but not emphatically enough to suit the Rat’s need for challenge. Their mutual feelings of inadequacy will be put to rest when they have sex. The Goat is ultra sensual and can exert an almost magical power over the Rat. Thrilled by such intense sexual excitement, the Rat (for once) will be happy to surrender power. The Goat may gain confidence from the Rat’s submissiveness and see an opportunity to discuss some of their differences. If the physical union is strong, this couple may eventually iron out their discord on the pillow.",Ox:"In the beginning, the delicate Goat seems like a great catch for a domineering Ox. But we must never judge a Goat by appearances! Although gentle, Goats are not easily bossed. I caution all Oxen against this union. First, you’ll feel a surge of power next to this dainty mountain creature. But after several shared hikes, your puffed-up ego will flop like a tired soufflé. The Goat complains endlessly and you (slowly but surely) lose interest. The patient Ox puts up with the Goat’s lackadaisical attitude for a while, but soon comes to believe that the Goat is not only lazy, but directionless. A hard-working Ox simply can’t understand the Goat’s inertia. Happy to be dependent on others, the Goat just doesn’t feel the need to work himself to death. Doesn’t the dedicated Bull bring home more than enough bacon? After a while, as the Ox is so tame and responsible, the Goat finds him just plain dreary. The Goat likes to sleep on different sides of the bed every night just for the fun of it, which exasperates the rigid Ox, who can’t bear the thought of breaking routine. Even in bed, the stodgy Ox has trouble keeping up with all the different Goat positions. This is a clumsy couple. Each will be better off without the other.",Tiger:"This union is among the worst possible known to Chinese astrologers. Although the couple may make a fabulous start (in bed), from there on it's all downhill. The practicalities just don't work out. Goat is charming, beautifully seductive and loving. Tiger is passion and mettle. But who will bring home the bacon? In this family, nobody wants the job. No concessions are made. The Goat remains laid back while the ambitious Tiger bombasts a hole in the kitchen ceiling. What was a great passion ends in lifelong misunderstanding and acrimony. Affairs? Yes. Marriage? Abstinence is advised.",Rabbit:"Although initially they may seem ill suited, this pair will undoubtedly develop a solid love relationship. Cats and Goats are complementary. The Cat provides the dependent, creative Goat with just the right amount of down-home security, and the hypersensitive, capricious Goat amuses and keeps the Cat interested. Cats are serious and steady. Goats hardly ever follow the rules. Although normally disconcerted by such nonchalance, the Cat finds it disarming in a love partner. The Goat respects the Cat’s sound judgment and takes solace in Kitty’s ability to cope in a routine fashion. The Goat’s capacity for total surrender in love situations melts the sexually resistant Cat’s little heart. Their romantic life is dense with passion. Tenderness and marathon caressing sessions are the order of the day. The fewer children this couple has, the better. The Goat requires so much personal attention and caring from a Cat spouse that a brood of children who distract the Cat might make the Goat cranky and jealous.",Dragon:"In Chinese astrological circles, this is said to be a sound marriage. Goats are essentially dependent. They are easily swayed and don’t mind being bamboozled and manipulated by their loved ones. Dragons need to command direct operations and dominate. Goat’s good-natured passivity. The acquiescent Goat inspires the Dragon to protect and be chivalrous and thrives in the security provided by Dragon’s authority. Their sexual life together will be as near to an erotic dream as you can get. Dragons like to take charge and Goats like to lie there and be loved. Being two very sentimental as well as sensual beings, these two will know instinctively how to blend sex with affection. Their intimacies will be satisfying and frequent.",Snake:"Charming and gracious, this pair of artistic, creative people can have the world eating out of their hands. The Goat’s inherent beauty and seductive appeal, when combined with the Snake’s elegance and sensuality, forms an enviably synergistic couple. Theirs will be a delicious complicity. Unfortunately, neither of these gloriously attractive people is very handy with a calculator. They are both equally improvident, luxury-loving, even profligate about spending. Unpaid bills will pile up and each will call the other a spendthrift. Stalemate. Don’t expect the Goat to find solutions. Snakes may overspend but they also provide. Goats are determined to depend and be provided for. The Snake will only take so much of the Goat’s indolence, will soon find the poor Goat a high-paying job and force him to get to the office on time and perform his job well till death do them part. Once again, the Snake’s incurable infidelity slithers into the equation. Goats tend to be fickle too. But, even though the Snake understands the Goat’s occasional need for a fling, the more stubborn Goat hates to share his goodies and will freak out at the Snakey’s infidelity. But, never mind. Rows are the stuff of these people’s lives: both are addicted to passionate drama. Romantically, this couple is sound. But when the harsh, overhead light of reality pierces the veneer of their relationship, the cracks and flaws may prove too numerous for its survival.",Horse:"This apparently odd combination sometimes works extremely well. Horses are strong-minded hard workers. Goats are languorous, creative and oh-so-dependent. The Horse in this pair will always feel protective of the Goat mate. Horses like to feel superior and Goats know exactly how to inflate their egos. When decisions are to be made or actions taken, the Goat goes all flabby and swoons, “Honey, you’re so clever. I just know you’re better at this than I am,” and the Horse rides off into the night to play hero. The Goat’s romantic side appeals to the stodgy Horse’s need to learn about love. Even though their sensitivities are not too similar, Horses find ethereal Goats decidedly sexy. They complement each other. Goats are pessimistic; Horses are not. Goats are flaky. Horses are solid conservatives. Goats depend and Horses willingly provide. Horses like things their way and, as long as there’s money in the bank, Goats are supremely flexible. These two are so different that they will never be bored together. Of course, friction might occur, because the Goat can be jealous and possessive and the Horse needs to feel free. But usually, the Goat’s sense of what is most practical for the future will win out and, aside from some mild disapproval, he or she will not tax their partner sufficiently to cause the Horse to bolt.",Goat:"Immediate synergy! In bed, this couple performs well. They are so alike that everything flows naturally. Romance flourishes as they are both loving, sensitive and unusually in touch with and open about their emotions. At first glance, it would seem that these two might be able to live on love alone. Later on, however, when they have settled into a routine, a pair of Goats will cause each other much mutual pain. Being alike in temperament, their sins and grievances will be similar. Each will learn quickly how to push the other’s panic buttons. The immaturity and pessimism of dual Goats could be their undoing. Neither wants responsibility for the finances, for the future of their emotional bonding or for the workaday continuity of the household. Neither is able to depend on the other. When things go wrong, each will dream of having a stronger partner. The best way for this union to work well would be if one party (or better still, both) had a private income. Then, they could hire a “take-charge” domestic staff and have all the time in the world for creative joint projects. Infidelity is another Goat trait. Imagine two randy Goats running loose in the same marriage. Awful rows, pouting and shrieking occur. Moreover, Goats are possessive and jealous. Each, in his turn, will be devastated by the other’s betrayal. An “iffy” marriage at best.",Monkey:"A mutual lightheartedness will draw these two creatures into a joyous relationship. The Monkey’s energy alone can carry the couple and, as the Monkey is very generous, he or she will not mind being the sole provider. If Monkey is doing well, their whole existence can consist of fun and games. The sex will be less than wonderful, though, because Monkey isn’t the same sort of sensitive lover as the Goat. Goats need constant caresses, are romantic and sentimental, while Monkeys are practical lovers whose lovemaking resembles a healthful gymnastic more than a swooning match. The Goat’s moral dependence may become irritating to the Monkey, who longs to move about freely without undue constraint. Having to stay at home, coaxing a grumpy Goat out of pessimistic moods and rousing him from inertia may be more than the independent Monkey can bear. If this couple has a family, it may help to hold them together. Goat can stay securely at home while Monkey wanders free. It’s a sound combination, providing the Monkey can eventually support Goat in leisurely style.",Rooster:"This is a dicey combination. Roosters are conservative and individualistic. They deplore laziness and cannot tolerate lackadaisical attitudes in others. Goats like to take it easy. They don’t believe in work for its own sake, would rather sit still than move about, and are ever ready to get someone else to take care of their basic needs. As the Rooster often had great difficulty scratching out a living, he or she will be impatient with the idea of anyone living off the fat of the land and will wish the Goat would find a “real” job, like a normal person. Goat’s feelings are readily hurt. Tensions can mount in this household and very little will be talked through, because the Rooster hates discussing his emotions. The fickle Goat may wander sexually, causing the staid and faithful Rooster untold pain. Trouble is, the Goat needs more than just the Rooster’s perfunctory affections. Knowing this fact creates feelings of inadequacy and a lack of self-confidence in the Rooster. If Goat could be persuaded to stick around all the time and teach the willing Rooster how to be more sensual, their relationship might have a good chance at success. At least it would give more purpose to the otherwise idle Goat’s home life. Goat with Rooster is far from an ideal marriage.",Dog:"Not much love is lost between these two. The Dog is all moral standard and high-mindedness. Very often, the Goat’s ideals begin and end with where the next meal is coming from. Goats are on the side of the person carrying the wallet. Dogs deplore pandering. Goats know no other way of life. As a couple, unless the Dog decides, uncharacteristically, to shoulder the burden of changing a poor misunderstood Goat whom he or she believes to be a hidden genius, they will be two very different people going in opposite directions. The Dog likes things to be clear, just and fair. The Goat doesn’t even know what those terms mean. Goats are dreamers whose ephemeral plans often go up in smoke. Dogs dream too, but their dreams are founded in concrete and seek real solutions to real problems. Goats, of course, love sex and favor open relationships wherein they have full freedom. Dogs wouldn’t think of being disloyal. They may stray—but only for a minute or two. To a Dog, devotion and loyalty come first. To a Goat, blind devotion and loyalty are for fools who don’t know which side their bread is buttered. It would be too optimistic to expect harmony from this essentially unbalanced romantic equation.",Pig:"In this pairing we find one of the happiest possible combinations. The atmosphere between Goat and Pig is mellow and smooth. They may have minor differences of opinion over small things, like taste in furniture or which sort of friends to frequent most, but the Goat likes the security he finds with Piggy and Piggy, in turn, enjoys the creative nuttiness of the charming Goat. Pig is lucky in money matters so he can support the gentle Goat, allow him free rein to dream, aimlessly inventing and reinventing his daily life. Pigs have endless patience and seem to be composed of goodwill and indulgence for the capricious Goat mate. Goat could not be better matched where emotional stability is concerned. The Pig usually stays in the country, away from madding city life, where the Goat can safely cavort, unhindered, in fertile fields. The sexual side of this affair is also enviably harmonious. The parties have similar sensitivities. Noble Piggy will undoubtedly be jealous of the Goat’s incessant dalliances and disapprove of his unfortunate tendency to try to take up with almost every attractive person who comes to call (the flirtatious Goat lacks tact). But, never mind. Once Piggy’s pain has passed, the darling Goat will be forgiven and both will return to their familiar devil-may-care, bucolic existence."},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"Still moving along in a completely free-spirited way, you will discover a fresh sense of luxury and social acceptance by the conclusion of this Snake year. While Snake individuals aren't known for being the most outgoing people, they frequently seek out the gentle, artistic companionship of Goats. You are currently operating on your own unique wavelength, approaching your activities at a notably unhurried pace. This calm and deliberate manner of yours appeals greatly to the Snake, who prefers to navigate life smoothly and without haste. Your easygoing company provides warmth and comfort to the otherwise reserved Snake. You can anticipate being invited to a great number of elegant dinner parties and various events in exotic locations, possibly even on yachts or at chateaux in France or Spain. Take time to prepare your most sophisticated car, update your wardrobe, and certainly remember to use your finest French colognes and other appealing cosmetics. Naturally, all this personal grooming and socializing will lead to an abundance of romantic adventures. You'll find yourself courted by so many new and diverse individuals that keeping track will become quite a challenge. Enjoy these romantic experiences while they last, as by the end of the year, amorous pursuits will come to an abrupt halt. If you're considering marrying one of your recent conquests, I suggest you reconsider. Marriage is not currently foreseen in your immediate future."},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"Goats generally feel quite comfortable during Horse years, because the diligent atmosphere created by the Horse provides a comforting sense of security and safety. This year, it would be beneficial for you to solidify your position within any organizational structure where you currently find yourself established. Now, you might argue that you don't belong to any such structure, perhaps identifying as a freelance magician, a self-employed dog walker, or a renowned plastic surgeon who practices independently. However, if you do work on your own, I would wager that you are either deeply married to a stable, responsible individual who handles the finances—or perhaps both! If you aren't married, then it's likely you live at home, where you can depend on regular meals and a warm bed. Goats rarely operate entirely alone. This brings us back to the Horse year: you will appreciate the general mood of this year because it supports your need for dependability. You can truly rely on the Horse. Indeed, we can all rely on Horses; they are consistent, reliable, and practical beings. Therefore, this year, you will continue to progress smoothly with good fortune on your side. Consider investing some money in real estate this year. Perhaps acquire a cottage or a bungalow to renovate. You are very skilled with your hands, and this year, hands-on projects are on everyone's agenda."},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Yin Fire",prediction:`Finally, you are in charge! Although this isn't exactly your preferred style, as you'd likely feel more comfortable being named chancellor of the exchequer or serving as the King's or Queen's jester. You typically feel more secure when you are stably employed and protected by the society in which you reside. But never mind; you hold the position of power this year, and you will manage it—your way. As fate is on your side, this year will grant you everything you've ever envisioned in terms of freedom and the resources to create, accomplish, invent, and bring into production all the wonderful ideas you've conceived over the past three years. This is also the crucial year when you must formulate a plan for the next twelve years. It should outline something like: "2027, Innovate. Be the leader. 2028, Get the production line moving. Hire new people. Make changes, but avoid public attention. 2029, Economize," and so on, until you reach 2039 when your own year cycles back. The Chinese organize time into sixty-year cycles, each comprising twelve-year periods, and this marks the beginning of your current cycle. By 2031, you should have decided whether to get married or remain so. Make a clear decision now about where you want to be in twelve years, what you wish to be doing, and with whom. Beyond leading the world this year, you must actively begin drafting this twelve-year plan.`},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Yang Earth",prediction:"This year promises to be a bit too chaotic for your personal liking. Monkeys are constantly bustling about, devising intricate schemes and planning ways to entertain the world while simultaneously resolving all its issues. The truth is, Monkeys are rather disorganized individuals who present themselves as orderly. You won't find that crucial sense of security from Monkeys, and for good reason. They are incredibly neurotic and frequently imagine that others might be plotting against them. They devise strategies and manipulate situations, neither of which you are typically guilty of. You prefer to confront problems directly—even if you don't succeed in resolving them. The Monkey's deliberate chaos will unnerve you and cause you to doubt yourself. Since you don't possess an abundance of self-confidence to begin with, this perplexing year will make you extra anxious, highlight your pessimistic tendencies, and more than once leave you feeling foolish and cornered. Why? Because you insist on being direct and transparent about your intentions. Monkeys don't grasp that; they prefer complex mazes to straightforward paths. If I were you during this Monkey year, I would seriously consider a complete change of profession. Perhaps ask a wealthy friend to purchase a restaurant for you, or seek bank sponsorship for a career as an opera singer. Remember, your priority is security. Do not fund ventures yourself. If you fail, let someone else bear the consequences."},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Yin Earth",prediction:"In this period, you will find yourself in a year where you get the distinct impression that opportunities are tightly restricted, and progress is not flowing smoothly. Roosters are demanding individuals who are almost never as adaptable as one might wish. This lack of flexibility, however, is only part of the challenge. Roosters do not appreciate sacrificing their own independence for the benefit of another. They enjoy being in control of their own lives and the lives of those important to them, but their generosity extends no further. Furthermore, they cannot tolerate anyone who is not fully contributing their share. You, as a Goat, need to be nurtured and understood; you long to feel secure. This year, you might have to set aside all those desires and aspirations. Perhaps you should consider taking a sabbatical or finding passage on a wealthy lover’s yacht. Your health outlook is positive; those symptoms you experienced last year have subsided. They might have been related to stress and anxiety, as the chaotic influence of the Monkey year can affect Goats in that way. Romantic prospects will be uncertain in the Rooster year. While there won’t be an abundance of serious commitment available, there should be plenty of passion on the agenda. However, ample sexual activity offers little compensation for the fact that you won’t be accumulating gold either. The Rooster is cautious about spending and does not encourage extravagance or waste. Since your favorite pastime is acquiring lavish, often unnecessary items, you may experience disappointment. This year does not promise any designer gowns or luxury watches for gentle Goat individuals."},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Yang Metal",prediction:"The Dog tends to guide Goats, yet Goats do not appreciate being directed or compelled to participate in activities that are not of their own choosing. Nevertheless, in Dog years, we are all more or less obligated to join the fight for universal justice, to work diligently for the common good, and to voice our objections against all that is cruel and inhumane in our complex world. Fortunately for you, Dogs have a soft spot in their hearts for Goat individuals. Why? Because Dogs are fond of all forms of companionship. Goat people make excellent companions. When they are not working excessively long hours without eating or napping, Goats are very present and engaged. You can always count on a Goat friend to call for a chat, spend an evening watching television with you, or accompany you to a movie or a bistro. Consequently, this will be a good year for your social life. You will be asked to go on dates and attend community functions. You may even be invited to take an active role in the local political scene. What might appeal to you least about this Dog year is the Dog’s tendency to criticize your methods and sometimes even say hurtful things. At times, you will feel closely scrutinized. Try not to take these observations too seriously. The Dog cares deeply for you and worries that you cannot take care of yourself. Be patient; you are loved."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Yin Metal",prediction:"You can finally relax. Goats are among the Pig’s most favored individuals across all types of people. This year, you will be pampered, cared for, and made to feel exceptionally comfortable in your own skin. You desired security? You have it. A full calendar year of safety and admiration is available for Goats during the Pig year. What should you do with this sudden sense of well-being? Get out there and perform. Make your voice heard. Showcase your numerous talents to the world. Create movies, write books or poetry, sculpt, invent, act, or dance… but DO something significant for your career and your future NOW. In this benevolent year, you can make enormous strides towards success in your chosen field. Do not hesitate to present your innovative ideas to superiors, exhibit your work in galleries, or submit multiple manuscripts. You will be making all sorts of deals and contracts and signing agreements within the generous atmosphere prevalent in this Pig year. You may also get married. Yes. And/or you may indeed have a baby (or even two!) because this is the year in which things simply work out for Goats. Take full advantage. Next year is not quite as promising."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Yang Water",prediction:'As the Rat seeks power and desires to protect and influence people, Goats find it difficult to express much of a personal statement this year. Being pressured or crowded does not have the desired effect on you carefree individuals. You are always willing to cooperate and be pleasant when asked to perform. However, when someone literally pushes you and orders you to get moving, you instinctively retreat in fear and aversion. You may feel misunderstood and sulk, but you certainly won’t feel inspired to paint the Mona Lisa or reinvent pizza. Furthermore, when you feel unwell, you often spend money as if there were no tomorrow—which is not a healthy way to react, but a typical Goat-like method of "dealing" with discomfort. You can still be creative this year. Work diligently on your personal projects in a protected environment where you feel safe and cared for. However, Rat years are not the time for building up your reputation as the genius you often are. Love will emerge to spare you from excessive misery this year. Someone sweet and strong (perhaps a Pig) will appear who will love and admire you. This person will genuinely appreciate how exceptional you are and will encourage you in your artistic and inventive endeavors. This romantic interest will materialize unexpectedly… perhaps at a restaurant, a public beach, or even on an escalator going in the opposite direction. Do not miss this opportunity. When the initial glance proves intriguing—seize the chance to connect with this charming individual.'},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Yin Water",prediction:'While the Rat previously tried to motivate you to perform under the guise of offering protection, the Ox takes a distinctly different approach. The Ox dictates directly, with no pretense necessary. You will either work alongside him and complete tasks his way, or you will find yourself excluded. Goats typically voice their loudest complaints in Ox years, feeling misunderstood by those in authority, and indeed, they often are. Goats dislike being told what to do no less than anyone else, but they might willingly comply if the Ox were to say, "Go frolic over there and graze on the fresh green grass, and I’ll call you when we’re finished working here." Ox years signify a period of diligent effort, and that work can manifest in many forms. It might involve manual labor like ditch digging, or it could necessitate significant changes in the Goat’s personal plans, such as: "You are going to buckle down and complete university, achieving straight A’s this year." Alternatively, the Goat might be called upon to serve in his or her country’s armed forces, or be ordered to assist in disaster relief after a tsunami. The bottom line is that demanding work awaits Goats wherever they look this year, and no matter where they attempt to hide, they will be discovered and pressed into service. Fortunately, despite all this pressure, your romantic life is progressing splendidly. You have either found someone (or they have discovered you) on whom you can depend for defense and protection, without any bossiness or tyranny. Hold onto this person; you require security to sustain your actively inventive existence.'},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Yang Wood",prediction:"Keeping pace with Tigers is a challenge few enjoy. Tigers leap and bound, pounce, and roam about like hyperactive grasshoppers—and they consistently emerge looking triumphant. If the only issue were the pace that the Goat cannot maintain, that would be one thing. However, the truth is, the Tiger also possesses outlandish ambition and an intense drive to succeed. Goats are simply unable—and unwilling—to keep up. So, when it’s the Tiger’s turn to dominate the world, the Goat mostly retreats into hibernation or else feigns admiration for the chaotic energy, applauding the countless curtain calls without genuine conviction. In either scenario, Goats and Tigers frequently clash. Not only do they have different approaches to tasks, but they also disagree on the desired outcomes. These disagreements do not imply that the Tiger doesn't want you to succeed. Fundamentally, Tigers are indifferent to your success or failure—as long as you are not hindering their progress. Therefore, in Tiger years, I suggest that Goats work and engage in leisure activities as much as possible independently. Take solitary walks. Paint pictures. Write a book or sculpt a piece of art. But stay out of the intense Tiger fray. You were not designed for coexistence with this impulsive creature. Use this year to build your own career or your own house, or to learn to cook, sew, knit, crochet, practice judo, or yoga. However, do not attempt to compete in the challenging wider world during the Tiger year."},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"Having endured two rather challenging years, you can finally relax and lighten up in the benevolent, refined atmosphere of the Cat/Rabbit year. Not only will you feel more vibrant and open to meeting new people, but your social life will also significantly improve. You might only be invited to tea or an intimate cocktail party, but these are precisely the types of gatherings that appeal to you. There, you can confidently express yourself and display some of that famous Goat-like charm. This year is particularly favorable for you to meet an important new individual. Perhaps a romantic interest, though not definitively. It could be someone you will collaborate with on a new project, or someone who knows a person capable of providing precisely what you need (whether it's money or influence) to launch your business or acquire a country residence. If you have tasks to accomplish and prefer to do them at your own speed, this Cat/Rabbit year is the one you have been anticipating. There will be no external pressures forcing you to intensify your efforts or criticizing you about how long it takes to thread a needle. You are not comfortable with other people’s deadlines. A project might take you a few days, or it could require weeks of concentrated effort. And for most of that time, you will likely get no sleep, not eat regularly, or converse with many people. But the job will be completed correctly. You have no inherent sense of time; it’s simply your way. The Cat/Rabbit will not interfere."},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"Before I neglect to remind you: begin now to save up a few months’ salary during this Dragon year. You will find it necessary. In Dragon years, the pace intensifies, but the favorable disposition towards Goats continues steadily. You will not only feel liberated and unburdened by intrusive influences, but you will also be entertained by the pervasive sense of celebration and festivity that permeates every aspect of our lives in Dragon years. You Goats often require that extra spark of energy (or a push) to navigate the challenges of daily life. You can be prone to both pessimism and defeatism. The Dragon desires no part of your negative attitude and will exert all its power to keep your spirits high. Throughout the year, you will be able to claim minor victories over adversity. You won’t contract the prevalent flu, and you will win the lottery and successfully find the exact drapes you wanted for your TV room. Nothing earth-shattering, but the triumphs will be frequent enough to keep you prancing towards the future with your head held high. Towards the end of the year, you will likely experience a financial setback. Take care not to panic. Instead, find comfort in knowing that you have set aside enough money to see you through until next year, when your fortunes will definitely improve."}}},l={introduction:`Merry Monkey, you're a delightful person who never misses an opportunity and who, despite an undeniable inclination towards cunning and trickery, rarely disobeys rules. Is this contradictory? Yes, indeed, and more so. Monkeys are astute and enjoy being involved in everything. You grasp concepts long before the punchline, but you never laugh until you are truly ready. You are a meticulous plotter and planner. When faced with a seemingly impenetrable haze of human complexity, you, with your nimble spirit, will always discover the means to restore order. You are an invaluable assistant, employee, and helper. You would make an excellent vice-president. Titles and positions hold no significance for you, as you instinctively recognize that, no matter how high up you are seated, you will still merely be sitting on your posterior. Without drawing attention, you manage to skillfully orchestrate affairs from behind the scenes. You refuse to age. If you possess the financial means, you will be among the first to undergo a facelift, nose job, hair transplant, or all three!

In selecting a partner, treat yourself to a magnificent Dragon, a driven Rat, or even an impulsive Tiger, who will keep your problem-solving talents actively engaged. The initial and final periods of your life will unfold smoothly. Around the age of thirty-seven or thirty-eight, you may experience a sudden loss of confidence stemming from a significant mid-life romantic crisis. This period of despondency will pass after the age of forty-five.

My advice? Being cleverer than others is not sufficient. Knowing precisely when to take a chance and when to refrain is the secret to winning at the games you so enjoy. Refine your sense of timing through careful, patient observation. You will live longer and better on less if you learn to conserve your valuable energy (and your money) for high-stakes opportunities.`,elements:{Wood:`A fundamental characteristic of the Wood Monkey's personality is its belief in the future. This individual is constantly active and involved in everything, always engaged in some endeavor. It is perpetually constructing and creating, meticulously planning and strategizing to enhance its productivity, improve its personal environment, or contribute to making the world a more pleasant place to reside.
Wood Monkeys are inherently social creatures. They respond enthusiastically to interactions with their peers and are always seeking novel methods and locations to discover new friends, form acquaintances, and broaden their social circles. The Wood Monkey is a creative participant in social gatherings. It is the smiling individual who effortlessly navigates through any chattering crowd, meeting and greeting people with a cheerful "Hi" and "How do you do?" as if gracefully swinging from tree to tree in a lively jungle. When it comes to interacting on a purely sociable, superficial level, the Wood Monkey is unequivocally exceptional.
The less positive aspect of the Wood Monkey's high degree of affability is that it often struggles (or fails) to maintain long-term, meaningful friendships. Somehow, the good-natured charm that this Monkey exudes in public simply doesn't possess enough depth to sustain and strengthen lasting relationships. It suffers from a profound lack of genuine intimacy, often pondering why people find it so captivating and alluring, yet cease to be its friend after only a brief acquaintance. It is convinced that its intentions are honorable. It strives to be helpful and generous. Where, then, does the Wood Monkey go wrong?
Perhaps it doesn't make enough effort to truly get to know its friends and companions. Although it intends to be charitable and genuinely cares about the welfare of others, the Wood Monkey cannot remain still for long. It aims to be useful in the world and genuinely desires to cultivate many friendships, but it doesn't take the time to sit down and truly engage with friends, to listen to their troubles. It dislikes waiting for things to develop naturally, always believing it knows best. It is restless and talks excessively. It is perpetually in a hurry and shows little compassion for individuals it considers weak. If devoted friendship is what it seeks, the communicative Wood Monkey is missing the crucial point. Either it fails to truly absorb what it hears, or it simply doesn't listen in the first place.
The Wood Monkey becomes frustrated when it realizes that others cannot always keep up with its fast-paced lifestyle. It is compulsively impulsive and is sharply critical of slow-moving, single-minded individuals and those who prefer to approach life at a relaxed pace. Although it values efficiency, it fails to recognize that a slower, methodical approach can be just as effective as rapid action.
This particular type of Monkey is a social climber, a name-dropper. It feels secure when surrounded by influential people who offer both social standing and resources. It is inclined to seek romantic partners among those it perceives as socially superior, as it fears being excluded if it is not accepted by equals or superiors. This gregarious individual requires ample external reassurance that it will be included, loved, and, most importantly, permitted to remain within its peer group for an extended period.
A commendable quality that consistently saves the day for this impulsive creature is its good nature. This resilient individual knows how to be the subject of jokes and still maintain a cheerful demeanor. It gets teased because of its obvious desire to be liked, but it possesses a strong grasp of its own self-image. It is difficult to wound the ego of this amiable person.
Wood Monkeys are driven achievers. They need and desire to advance. They envision themselves ending up far beyond where they began in life. To accomplish their ambitious goals, Wood Monkeys constantly analyze the competition for weaknesses and strategize to win in the most socially acceptable manner.
For the Wood Monkey to truly succeed, it must learn to relax, to slow down, and, most importantly, to delve deeper into friendships and embrace intimate human connection. Unless it can learn to listen attentively to the needs of others, all the superficial chatter and back-slapping in the world will not lead it to its desired destination. If it applies itself, the Wood Monkey can learn to share and exchange its deepest thoughts and ideals, rather than merely presenting them, like a bundle of ripe bananas, to everyone it encounters and then continuing on its cheerful but solitary path.`,Fire:`Fire Monkeys enjoy being dominant in all their undertakings. Unlike most Monkeys, these types remain very much focused on their personal goals, creating and shaping their enterprises as they progress. Fire Monkeys are driven and ambitious. They desire results and are not afraid to seek the means to achieve them. The Fire Monkey is a self-starter whose enormous energy, although sometimes inconsistent and uneven, propels him speedily through life.
As the Fire Monkey's mind is fertile—his imagination is teeming with projects and innovative plans—he is doubly blessed. His capacity for hard work, coupled with his gift for invention, should make him a professional wizard. This Monkey will initiate trends, establish a new fashion in clothing or food, invent a novel literary style, or launch a new film project. But even with his myriad talents and dynamic personality, if he isn'tcareful, he may exhaust himself before he is halfway to his goal.
Although Fire Monkeys possess all the vigor, drive, and authority necessary for high achievement, they also crave the baser thrills of "having a good time." Over-indulgence in gambling, late nights in clubs, and engaging in frivolous activities may deplete their strength; indeed, these pursuits may take precedence over their initial lofty ambitions. Though not inherently excessive, Fire Monkeys are driven by the promise of excitement. They also have a dangerous taste for perversion. Some accuse them of being outright corrupt. If not curbed, Fire Monkeys can easily overload their systems and ruin their lives.
Fire Monkeys are deeply passionate, driven individuals. They respond to every experience with lightning speed and emotion. They bravely contend with the complexities of accomplishing tasks and seem almost inspired by setbacks—stimulated by adversity. To the agile-minded Fire Monkey, nothing is impossible. He seeks out and discovers solutions to the most challenging problems. He's cunning and resilient, flexible and sharp. The Fire Monkey is always willing to take a chance or embrace a new opportunity.
Though adaptable in spirit and free-wheeling, Fire Monkeys enjoy controlling others. You will often find them drawn to or living with partners of lesser willpower who need them for support or who look to them for emotional stability. Fire Monkeys may choose their lovers because of their own need to dominate someone less forceful. Yet the tables often turn on this would-be dominator, and, through an odd system of emotional manipulation and unavoidable entanglement, the Fire Monkey dominator becomes the one controlled by the mate he imagined was the weakling.
Fire Monkeys are born cynics, too. In youth, they possess a disarming air of candor, but as they mature, they grow wiser, less credulous, and sometimes even embittered. They have difficulty trusting anyone, especially their colleagues and associates. Gradually, they lose their respect for morality and begin to wear a jaundiced, knowing smile. Raw ambition provides little comfort against disappointment, but once he has lost his youthful charm and earnest beliefs, ambition is frequently all this Monkey has left.
The Fire Monkey doesn't take kindly to being made to look foolish. He is jealous in both his romantic and professional lives. He is competitive and can be vindictive, even vengeful. Speculation is his favorite game. He may take on many partners, form corporations, or assemble groups for projects, but no matter how equitable the terms of any agreement, the Fire Monkey will always insist on remaining the boss.
This Monkey is by far the most power-hungry of all Monkeys, yet he may not always be the most visible. Much of his true essence remains hidden or operates behind the scenes. Outwardly, the Fire Monkey is scornful of naive dreams and loudly dismisses ideals as trite, childish, and insipid. But the resilient Fire Monkey also yearns for a better world and would go to even greater lengths than all other Monkeys if only he believed that his wonderful dream could come true.`,Earth:`This Monkey is calmer, more sentimental, and a deeper thinker than most. Altruism is well developed in its character, and it is notably less carefree than its counterparts. It genuinely ponders both the past and future of humankind and attempts to comprehend the shape of things to come. Earth Monkeys love all types of people and can embrace the problems of others as if they were their own.
The Earth element bestows upon the Monkey solid natural wisdom and insight. Because it is so perceptive, it is painfully aware of certain harsh truths about life from an early age. It may speak out in family or school situations, surprising adults with unnaturally astute comments. Although silence is not its strong suit, study is. It will be capable of reaching lofty social positions through education. In China, the Earth Monkey is known as the teacher Monkey. Not only is it learned, but it is also able to impart knowledge and demonstrate devotion in the pursuit of a professorial career. Its students will be faithful admirers. They will adore its cheerful manner and are instructed and amused by the Earth Monkey's imaginative presentation of inherently difficult or dull material.
This Monkey's best attribute lies in its ability to interact with its peers: people like it immediately. It is affable and jolly, optimistic and inspirational. It's bright and witty, and so smart and intuitive that it seems to possess foresight. Even better, the Earth Monkey knows how to make us laugh. It won't waste time on gloomy reruns of its difficult childhood or tedious school exploits. It is fun, spontaneous, and full of life. It is strong without being overpowering, and yet it remains a serious, even profound, thinker.
The biggest flaw in the Earth Monkey's character is its desire for perfection. This sociable and pleasant individual seems so easy-going and fun-loving that we sometimes wonder if it can truly be taken seriously—but this Monkey is worse than serious—it's nit-picking—obsessed with perfection. It longs for a home that operates flawlessly, a family to be nothing but proud of, a designated place for everything, and everything in its place.
However, the family life of the average Earth Monkey is never a paradise. Its need for order in the inherently disorderly atmosphere of home and children leads to problems for it and its poor, subjugated offspring. Either the children and spouse become terrorized by all the obsessive fussing, or as time goes by, the meticulous Earth Monkey parent becomes a subject of family ridicule and has to seek refuge in the basement or is forced out of the nest.
This Monkey is fatally attracted to the opposite sex. An imaginative lover, it cannot resist the urge to engage in romantic play. It adores the intrigue, the chase, the seduction. Extramarital affairs are common in the life of this highly sensual Monkey. Usually, fear of scandal (the specter of imperfection again) prevents it from confessing its indiscretions to a passing newspaper reporter. It hates to acknowledge its own mistakes, yet is quick to point out those of its family. Living intimately with the Earth Monkey is not for amateurs: it requires more than patience—even a spirit of masochistic self-sacrifice. Yet this Monkey is kind and can be reached through a large, tender window of guilt. If reminded of how difficult it is, the Earth Monkey will rally. Beneath its challenging, superficial nature, it is devoted to those it loves and can always be counted on to provide and maintain order.
The Earth Monkey is blessed with good health and a sturdy constitution. It will live to a ripe old age. With its innate talents for study and concentration, it could work in scientific research, law enforcement, or history. Because of its ability to work independently, it can pursue a career in the arts as an independent filmmaker, a literary scholar, a painter, or sculptor.
If an Earth Monkey could improve one aspect of its character, it should definitely be its perfection-seeking tendency. It could and should partake of some of life's simple pleasures. Earth Monkeys need to relax their overly traditional side, break down personal barriers that prevent them from enjoying a relaxed lifestyle, and rid themselves of the need to show off their brilliant achievements in public. Developing the spiritual side of this neurotically driven perfectionist is a sure way to loosen those inhibitions for something more profound than clandestine extracurricular sex.`,Metal:`The intellectual aspect of this Monkey helps it to be a creative, self-made individual. It typically prefers to forge its own path alone, working contentedly at a profession that leads it into elevated realms.
This independent person will encounter numerous obstacles on the journey to discovering its unique niche. However, it will certainly find it—or perish trying! This is the fighting Monkey. When uncertain, it confronts issues, battles inner demons, and fiercely attacks adversaries. It often triumphs through persuasion, reason, and logic. But, if the situation demands it, it is unafraid to engage in physical confrontation and decisively defeat its opponent. The Metal Monkey's strength is not like the stormy, fiery bravado of a Dragon, nor can it match the Ox or Rooster for perseverance and endurance. The Metal Monkey appears resilient and aggressive. It simply annihilates challengers through intellectual might and a twist of spirit. Then it leaves the defeated behind and moves forward, as spirited as ever, to challenge the next contender. It's tough—but in a commendable way.
The Metal Monkey's personal life is never a romantic novel. It is determined to achieve a significant position in its career, make its mark on society, and push its creative ideas through established systems, leaving little time for family or emotional space. As a major innovator, it must possess unconventional ideas. It is neither obedient to norms nor overtly revolutionary, but it requires the thrill of achievement, advancement, and status. It desires to be where the action is, and if its associates do not understand, then that is their problem.
It is, of course, possible for this individual to marry and maintain a semblance of family life. Metal Monkeys are usually financially secure and make good providers, but they may not be inclined to spend much time at home. This person needs an independent, loving, and patient mate, unafraid to take sole responsibility for the home, family, and marriage.
Metal Monkeys possess sociable, gregarious personalities. They converse extensively and (although they are Monkeys) are often capable of learning foreign languages. They enjoy travel and are quite likely to move abroad early in adulthood, relocating to start anew in a different place to satisfy their desire for self-sovereignty. The Metal Monkey dislikes criticism, does not wish to be compared to siblings and/or cousins, and deplores the existence of relatives who insist on burdening it with unsolicited advice. The Metal Monkey desires to be distinct, officially unattached—an individual. It forges its own path and refuses to credit its frequent successes and financial gains to anyone else.
The Metal Monkey is intelligent. It is argumentative, yet possesses a charming, winning demeanor. The close relative who lives with this captivating person knows just how irritable and particular it can be, and resents all the extra affection and praise that the Metal Monkey receives from its numerous admirers. For the Metal Monkey, family situations are often tense and fraught with animosity. Metal Monkeys are the kind of people who try to seize the family home from sisters and brothers to convert it into an elderly care facility which, naturally, bears the Metal Monkey's illustrious name.
The Metal Monkey can be prone to melancholy. If this person (who would perform amateur open-heart surgery on friend or foe to achieve their goals) does not succeed, they may succumb to despair. All that pushing, shoving, and strategizing is so exhausting, and the stakes are so all-or-nothing, that the fatigued Metal Monkey sometimes cannot muster the energy to begin all over again. Its flaw lies in its inflated self-image—its pride. It can handle setbacks as long as it emerges victorious. Too many losses, and it retreats, dejected and hopeless. One sometimes wonders how many struggling individuals are Metal Monkeys who simply gave up.
When and if despair sets in, the Metal Monkey may attribute its failures to its upbringing, its family, friends, or associates who were jealous and tried to undermine it. This "poor me" attitude is characteristic of an undeveloped personality that cannot accept its own shortcomings, will not assume responsibility for communication breakdowns, and can only perceive itself as a victim. Truly, this attitude leads to a dead end.
The remedy for despondency in Metal Monkeys is structured group therapy. Although I don't often recommend it, I view the Metal Monkey as so oblivious to its own errors and so unwilling from an early age to consult with or take advice from elders or peers that it cannot help but benefit from a group experience. Metal Monkeys do not realize that they cannot always be right. They need to learn early on to accept feedback from those around them.
This Monkey makes an excellent salesman or TV talk-show host, newscaster, or disc jockey. It is so articulate and quick-witted that it could sell fur coats to bears. Whatever verbal challenge arises, it meets it with composure and a smooth-talking manner. It makes strangers feel comfortable. It exudes confidence and competence even when it has no idea what it's doing.
Finally, expect nothing but the best from the brilliant side of this person. Leonardo da Vinci was a Metal Monkey, as is Pope John Paul. These Monkeys are profoundly individualistic. This signifies achievement and versatility. Metal Monkeys can learn how to do almost anything.
However, if Metal Monkeys experience too many failures, their mental and physical health will deteriorate. They are born with more pride than resilience. The fracturing of this fragile surface can destroy their cheerful demeanor, and they may quickly begin to crumble into oblivion.`,Water:`A sublime blend of cooperation and genius, the Water Monkey is truly exceptional! Inquire around; everyone agrees. It is one of the world's most spirited individuals.
Although Water Monkeys can always be relied upon to defend their own interests, they are generous individuals, willing to lend a hand or share whatever abundance they possess. Water Monkeys are never careless friends who casually walk through your living room, grab a piece of fruit, and quickly depart without leaving more than a faint scent of patchouli. They take friendship and love seriously. Not that they become overly effusive about their affection, but from the moment they decide to welcome a friend into their circle, their devotion is genuine, their willingness to assist when someone needs help is constant, and their loyalty is unwavering.
Water Monkeys are clever and witty without being cynical. There is a sweetness to their affability, and they are always seeking to help others realize their dreams. They possess an innate ability to care deeply without being overly sentimental. They do not mind relinquishing the spotlight in favor of someone they admire, and except for a basic need to maintain a modicum of security, they are extravagantly generous with everything from hospitality to money, praise, and affection.
The Water Monkey possesses an elfin or lively quality. A whimsical energy permeates everything it does. It is constantly radiating vibes of ironic cheerfulness, which blends perfectly with its natural tenderness towards others. Consider the teasing cartoons of Sempé, the lyrical films of Milos Forman, or the biting yet humane works of François Truffaut. There's something both socially commendable and subtly sarcastic about the way Water Monkeys view life. They are critical and caring simultaneously. They don't mind pointing out the flaws of friends and relatives, but they wouldn't hurt them for anything, because they care so intensely about their happiness.
Water Monkeys do not always fare as well as their friends. They tend to be unnecessarily neurotic. They are easily overcome by worry and become bewildered when minor things go wrong—they may grow anxious when the hall porter forgets to say good morning. Perhaps the porter is having a bad day and forgot to greet him—but it will trouble the Water Monkey, who may not be able to let himself, or you, forget it for weeks. The insignificant incident is exaggerated out of all proportion, and the Water Monkey suffers. It is always he who apologizes and makes amends.
Water Monkeys are ingenious problem-hunters—and solvers. They do not want to hear the word "impossible." For a Water Monkey, navigating a dense thicket of thorns means devising a way around it—and the Water Monkey makes an excellent mediator, troubleshooter, or organizer. It is a great motivator—it can spend its life urging, scolding, monitoring, identifying, and rectifying flaws, and be contentedly fulfilled with that secondary role.
The Water Monkey is never a prima donna or an egomaniac. The innovative talents of this warm, loving person would not suit continuous talk show appearances. The Water Monkey's ego is contained within the clever mind of a generous soul. Even Elizabeth Taylor, with her astonishing beauty, has never become a captivating siren like Zsa Zsa Gabor or a delightfully simpering Marilyn Monroe. She's always married to some man with a giant ego whom she's trying to cure of alcoholism (and perhaps getting caught up herself) or helping to combat prejudice about AIDS. Liz Taylor is a failure as a prima donna because she simply wasn't born selfish enough.
Gloom and depression can cause the Water Monkey's buoyant spirit to plummet. If its minor neuroses or others’ demands close in on it, and it's made to feel guilty, its high spirits may crash. The idea of being wrong unnerves it, and as it blames itself for much that goes wrong anyway, it is ill-equipped to defend itself against accusations. Water Monkeys are easy targets for manipulative individuals who ruthlessly exploit their sympathies.
There is something of the cheerful meddler in the Water Monkey. Sometimes it becomes intrusive. Water Monkeys enjoy gossip, which contributes to their reputation as sociable companions and excellent friends. But occasionally, they reveal someone else's secrets when they might be better off choosing to "speak no evil."
Water Monkeys are intensely sensual. They adore engaging in the act of love. They revel in all the imaginative ways to play the oldest human game. Unfortunately, they are rarely cool-headed in their choice of lovers and cannot resist becoming involved with complex and difficult individuals. Perhaps it is natural for the problem-solver to take on problematic people. Water Monkeys consistently find unyielding, challenging partners with irritable tempers and precarious emotional foundations. Individuals whom you or I might happily remove from our lives, Water Monkeys adopt as cherished companions. They are irresistibly drawn to experiencing perplexing scenarios in the hope that they will play a key role in untangling the most stubborn knots.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"If all else fails, these two can go on the road as a comedy duo. Humor, games, parties, and friends! What fun you’ll have! How lucky you are to have been brought together! Shared, your lives will be a never-ending roller-coaster ride. The amusing Monkey, incessantly grimacing from the top of the jungle gym, has the Rat in perpetual stitches. Amid guffaws, the Rat suggests funnier, more clever antics, fueling the witty Monkey with ever more hysterical moves. It’s a matrimonial picnic. The sometimes-repressed Rat will become a tiresome chatterbox alongside a mellow Monkey. But the Monkey never tires of the clever Rat. For him, it’s like owning a walking radio show. Both so personable, they will always be dining out or entertaining at home. They have a multitude of friends and spend little time alone. As neither is afraid of hard work, money comes easily to them. The Monkey sometimes uses characteristically diverse interests to justify a desire for sexual promiscuity. Should Monkey betray the ever-devoted Rat, the relationship will become strained. But terminal dissension is rare. Mostly, this gleeful couple lives in an amusement park of joy.",Ox:"If the Ox can relinquish stubborn conformism and trust his beloved Monkey, the Monkey can greatly improve the quality of an Ox’s life. In return for the Monkey’s gift of freedom, the Ox will lend security to his Monkey mate. Much to everyone’s surprise, the Ox, usually incensed by any disturbance of routine, is fascinated by the tricky Monkey. Monkey, in turn, tries harder to amuse and enchant his faithful mate. Both are basically practical and project-oriented. Moreover, Monkeys can teach Oxen to step outside themselves, be willingly kind to others, to help out the less fortunate. Charity gives the Ox a special thrill. He is grateful to the Monkey for opening his eyes to the needs of the poor. Under the covers, expect the imaginative Monkey to spice up the Ox’s humdrum technique. With the Monkey’s agile tutelage the Ox can expect to learn much more than a few dancing techniques. He may even learn how to fly!",Tiger:"These two make eager lovers. Initially, they will leap frequently on each other’s bones, accomplishing astonishing feats of extreme passion, but in the long run, the ardor may die a natural death, because Tigers hate to be clung to—and innately neurotic Monkeys don’t know how not to cling. The strong intellectual tug between Tigers and Monkeys frequently keeps them together, anyway. The Tiger admires the Monkey’s keen eye for strategy and the Monkey enjoys and applauds the Tiger’s feisty wit and temerity. Monkey gives Tiger plenty of presents and kudos. Tiger gives Monkey spunk and encouragement. These two have an easy common viewpoint and, even if they cannot keep the love flame burning, will go far together as lifelong pals. Except… the Chinese say that the Tiger should beware. Traditionally, the Monkey is Tiger’s natural enemy. I don’t advise marriage.",Rabbit:"These two people are intellectually well matched. They both enjoy being in cultural venues, seeking out new exhibitions or museums and learning about subjects of particular interest to one or both of them. The meeting of two like minds can be the basis of a lifetime of wedded harmony. Emotionally, however, there will be snags. The Cat hates change and does not enjoy surprises. Discretion, for the Cat, is nine-tenths of the law. Monkeys live for change, enjoy leaping about from place to place and adore being in the limelight, amusing cronies and carrying on high in public. Moreover, the Cat takes him- or herself very seriously. Not too many jokes allowed. Monkeys make fun of everything (including their mates) and think of the world as a giant silliness. The success and longevity of this relationship depends on the degree of passion the couple can extract from their intensely cerebral friendship. Neither lends much belief to the idea of syrupy romance, keeping their respective cynical distances from all “sentimental” notions. They may require a push from an outside source (e.g. Dicey love triangle, savvy therapist, good friend etc) to accept to surrender to the natural human impulse to love and be loved—no matter what!",Dragon:"Despite the obvious differences in their characters, these two have a lot going for them. The Dragon is bombastic and needs to be adored, yet reveres the Monkey’s keen intelligence and ability to see around corners. Monkeys love spectacle and invariably enjoy the show Dragons put on. Dragons get themselves embroiled in world problems. Monkeys are born solvers of problems—big and little. There is plenty of room for personal evolution in this couple. Impressed by the efficiency of the Monkey’s exceptional mind, the Dragon (atypically) will become almost dependent, let up on the accelerator from time to time and even take an occasional back seat to Monkey’s brilliance. Monkeys enjoy being appreciated for their skillful talents, are not particularly interested in the number one position, and let a Dragon bask in the footlights. As a result of this clever balance, the Dragon/Monkey match becomes a strong bond, built on compromise and mutual respect. Sex, however, may not be the strongest element that binds these two. The Monkey’s normally healthy appetite seems moderate by comparison to the Dragon’s voracious and conspicuous need for consumption of his or her mate’s intimate favors.",Snake:"Auspicious beginnings encourage these characters to join forces and operate as a team. The versatile Monkey finds wisdom and consideration in the Snake’s personality. The Snake enjoys the Monkey’s charm and peppy energy. They are truly a complementary pair. After a time, however, they will see that all they have in common is a taste for helping others, a charitable bent which binds them ever so loosely together. Snake, of course, always takes off on extramarital adventures. Monkey? Well, Monkey couldn’t care less: if affairs turn up, so much the better. If not, he can take them or leave them alone. Snakes like elegance and want their lives carefully accessorized. Monkeys are bored by the very idea of accessorizing anything, and dress down rather than dressing up. Monkeys are spontaneous. Snakes ponderous. Snake is romantic, Monkey logical. Snake is sophisticated, Monkey Bohemian and carefree. Monkeys love to converse, but dialogue becomes difficult because Snakes find it hard to divulge their inner feelings. Breakdown in communications might be the death of this relationship. Their sex life usually compensates for much of the strife between them. Although sex is not always the Monkey’s strongest suit, Snakes succeed in turning them on in a big way. The complicity of elaborate sex games may ensure a basis for this pair to consolidate their union—despite their essential differences.",Horse:"A mutual desire to stay abreast of events, mingle in society and be part of what’s happening in the outside world will constitute the initial attraction between these two. Monkeys are so versatile, imaginative and amusing that Horses have trouble resisting their charms. Monkeys feel that serious Horses need cheering up and are inspired to make them laugh. Monkeys also appreciate the Horse’s strict sense of duty and ability to endure hard work. They love to join forces and solve problems together. Communication may not be their strongest suit. Monkeys are inveterate neurotics who cherish their unhealthy behavior patterns and although they chatter, they don’t open up easily. Horses are guarded and conservative about speaking up on their own behalf. Much tension may build. They should agree (before reaching the ulcer stage) to see a therapist regularly. Otherwise, unexpressed emotions will cause the death of their union. A brilliant sex life is in store for the Monkey/Horse couple. They are mutually energetic and fanciful about romance. Horse may want more sex than does Monkey, but Monkey’s fertile imagination will more than compensate for lack of appetite. As long as these two don’t sit around complacently, patting each other on the back about how well their couple “works”, they can create a lasting bond.",Goat:"A mutual lightheartedness will draw these two creatures into a joyous relationship. The Monkey’s energy alone can carry the couple and, as the Monkey is very generous, he or she will not mind being the sole provider. If Monkey is doing well, their whole existence can consist of fun and games. The sex will be less than wonderful, though, because Monkey isn’t the same sort of sensitive lover as the Goat. Goats need constant caresses, are romantic and sentimental, while Monkeys are practical lovers whose lovemaking resembles a healthful gymnastic more than a swooning match. The Goat’s moral dependence may become irritating to the Monkey, who longs to move about freely without undue constraint. Having to stay at home, coaxing a grumpy Goat out of pessimistic moods and rousing him from inertia may be more than the independent Monkey can bear. If this couple has a family, it may help to hold them together. Goat can stay securely at home while Monkey wanders free. It’s a sound combination, providing the Monkey can eventually support Goat in leisurely style.",Monkey:"These two make great companions. They love in a hands-off fashion. Neither interferes with the other’s progress merely looking for ego-strokes. Two Monkeys usually create a project-oriented family atmosphere wherein each member of the group has individual responsibilities and householding belongs to everyone. Cooking and washing up, shopping and even ironing may be shared equally. The male Monkey is never too proud to do laundry. And Ms. Monkey doesn’t mind changing the oil in the car. Monkeys are race, creed and color blind. Sexually slanted competition doesn’t exist between these two. Problems (and there aren’t many that two Monkeys can’t solve better than one) will arise in the financial arena. Neither Monkey likes doing accounts, writing checks or letters protesting gas and electricity bills. As a couple, they may fall behind and ruin their reputation. As both are work and people-oriented, this couple will need to hire a bookkeeper to hold their finances together. Sex is not often the foremost consideration between two Monkeys. They both enjoy it and even prefer having sex with each other. But they are not overly preoccupied by the intensity or endurance of their sexual lives. If and when it happens, they are excited and happy. Without it, neither curls up and dies. Promiscuity might be a dot on the horizon, but dalliances are of no consequence, as Monkeys make committed couples who believe in personal freedom.",Rooster:"Not much is going on sexually between these two characters. Roosters are possessive and anxious about their position in relationships. Their instinct is to anchor their prey. Monkeys need miles of rope to feel good about themselves. They have to roam amid people, jabber with others and find solutions to ever more important problems. Roosters are conservative thinkers. Monkeys are all for liberation, gentler laws and personal liberty. This couple may be constantly at odds over policy. Decisions become difficult. Tensions rise and Rooster suffers—because Rooster makes the untenable scenes that send the Monkey packing. Roosters must accept Monkey’s devil-may-care side to enjoy the benefit of his or her humor. It’s up to the Rooster to be more flexible. And that is a tall order. So these two are not exactly Romeo and Juliet. Monkey is interested in sex, but he’s also fascinated by life’s other aspects—above all its practicalities. Rooster is also practical and appreciates Monkey’s delight in solving concrete issues. But Rooster needs softening, romancing, loving and cuddling to appreciate the joys of sex. Now it’s Monkey’s turn to adapt, to become more languorous and spend time petting and nuzzling. Or Rooster (God forbid!) might begin scratching around in another barnyard for sexual understanding.",Dog:"The Dog is a blazing idealist. The Monkey lives for the opportune moment. They may well meet up and fall in love when engaged in a social struggle together. Each possesses qualities lacking in the other. Although this might make them seem perfectly matched, it takes more than dovetailing qualities to make two such impervious individualists communicate. Each is so accustomed to living on his own wavelength that they have real trouble shifting gears to make themselves understood to someone on another plane. The remedy is talk. These two nervous souls must sit and yammer for hours, days and months before they reach comprehension. The Dog will have to give up blurting nasty remarks and the Monkey must accept being tethered for at least part of the time. Although they can be guilty of it, Dogs don’t take kindly to philandering. But Monkeys like sexual freedom. Monkey seems carefree and Dog laughably frustrated. Being of basic good intention, if they wish to stay together, this pair can work out a harmonious sex life together. This relationship’s harmony is possible but will not be won without effort. Unless the union is inevitable, I advise imagining it can work forever.",Pig:"Piggy! The Pig must treat this relationship with less blind indulgence for the opposite party. Monkeys can be ruthless when necessary. The Pig’s naïveté is no help when it comes to dealing with a beloved, yet sometimes unscrupulous, Monkey. Unlike the Snake, whose intentions in the Pig’s regard are plainly lethal, the Monkey means no harm. Pigs’ and Monkeys’ tender hearts are mightily compatible—but their thinking processes are worlds apart. The Pig must adapt to the Monkey’s ways or the couple is doomed. As Pigs are very malleable, adaptation is not an unreasonable demand. But Piggy must be careful not to lose his or her purest ideals in Monkey’s constantly expanding bag of tricks. Pigs live by intuition. Monkeys cleave to logic. If they can teach their mutual talents to cooperate, it will assist their union’s progress. If not, there will be major rows. An angry Monkey is a hopping mad mini-volcano who forgets about it two minutes after the eruption. A mad Pig is fearsome, relentless, dangerous and vengeful. Monkey should accept and enjoy Pig’s smothering and homely charms. And Pig should try to see how innocently the Monkey needs room to wander and squander. If these concessions are made, they can have a lovely, long-lasting life复工"},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"This period is not precisely a time of ideal comfort for Monkeys; Snake years will require you to perform some intricate adaptive maneuvers. The Snake is a composed and collected individual, characterized by a no-nonsense and philosophical demeanor, and Snakes do not require or desire constant entertainment. Of course, they appreciate a high-quality professional show or concert, where they can dress appropriately in their finest attire and enjoy the play or music at a suitable, socially acceptable pace. However, Monkeys riding around on unicycles or playing trumpets in their bathrooms while dressed as scarecrows or nuns? That is met with very little enthusiasm, and only in extremely small, carefully measured doses. Fundamentally, the Snake disapproves of the Monkey’s eccentric approach. Therefore, in this year governed by the sober Snake, you should temper your slapstick humor. Refine your comedic routines so they convey a more serious tone, and reduce your physical comedy. If you manage to quiet yourself down, you will discover the company of the wise Snake to be extremely beneficial. Listen to the Snake’s advice. Make the necessary adjustments and changes to adapt to the prevailing mood of this year, and you will be free to advance swiftly in all your endeavors. Since you enjoy giving presents as readily as others change their socks, feel free to lavish gifts! Be generous with your giving this year—and particularly choose beautiful accessories; handbags, jewelry, scarves, gloves, hats, ties, and cufflinks of the finest quality will be greatly appreciated by the recipients. Snakes have an intense fondness for accessories."},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"The Monkey’s fundamental problem-solving nature holds strong appeal for the practical Horse. This year, the Horse will not obstruct the Monkey’s progress. On the contrary, Monkeys will be encouraged to utilize their diverse skills and manage affairs in their own clever way. Do not interfere. Do not attempt to take control. When the situation begins to falter and threaten to derail, simply close your eyes and hum a cheerful tune. Horses do not appreciate being helped, confined, restricted, or criticized. This, of course, is a significant challenge for Monkey individuals, who can discern the intricacies of almost any situation and always wish to offer assistance in a crisis. Horses frequently find themselves in difficult predicaments. My advice to Monkeys? Stay out of it. Unless the Horse year begins to become unstable and threaten to bring down your own household, absolutely refrain from offering any advice or inserting yourself into complex situations. (If you are an in-law, this advice is particularly directed at you.) Allow this year to resolve its own difficulties. Attend all the parties you are invited to. Entertain enthusiastically. But do not attempt to steal the spotlight or try to take over where others have already established themselves (this applies to deals, relationships, business projects, inventions, etc.). Your role this year is to keep pace with the swift and winding Horse year’s hectic rhythm and avoid losing your composure."},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Yin Fire",prediction:"Your inherent generosity must be restrained during the Goat year. You tend to see someone in need, and when you can, you instinctively reach into your pocket or purse. It’s not that you are careless with money, but you possess an open-handed attitude regarding what you have to spare. You give many presents, and you enjoy treating your friends and family to delightful meals in charming restaurants or taking them on trips to interesting new places. The Goat year may exert just a little too much pressure on your finances. You will perceive opportunities for charitable or altruistic acts and impulsively fall headlong into their tempting demands. Hold back. Watch your pennies carefully. Goats love Monkeys and are particularly drawn to their ability to be creative in so many different areas. In this respect, you two are quite similar. However, caution is advised. Goats are perpetually seeking someone to lend them money, provide assistance, offer housing and sustenance, and well… take care of their everyday needs so that they can continue with whatever they are currently engaged in. Monkeys simply cannot afford to take on Goats. Therefore, this year, be especially cunning when some unfortunate individual asks you for a handout or a loan. Smile, claim financial hardship, and firmly say NO."},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Yang Earth",prediction:"During your travels this year, you will encounter someone who will exert a profound influence on your career. This could be an older person who takes a particular liking to one of your brilliant ideas. Alternatively, it might be a contemporary who is willing to partner with you, either in business or in love. Pay close attention to this person’s Chinese astrological sign and compare it with your own. If the compatibility is harmonious, seriously consider pursuing a joint project or a marriage together. This is your year to shine, to preen, to assert yourself, and to dance on tables if you feel inclined. However, do remember to return to Earth occasionally, because this is also the year for you to plan the next twelve years of your life. The Chinese calendar does not use ten-year decades; instead, it employs twelve-year periods. Each year holds a particular significance for every zodiac sign. When your own year arrives, you are obligated to sit down with pen and paper (or a computer) and outline the next twelve years of your life. Where do you wish to be in 2040? What do you envision yourself doing? How might you meticulously plot the path to this objective, year by year, to ensure you are more or less certain to achieve that goal? Is this an easy task? No. But it is a necessary exercise for constructing your own life. Take charge of your destiny in this auspicious Monkey year. Do not simply sit back and allow life to dictate your path."},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Yin Earth",prediction:"In this year, Roosters consistently take a liking to Monkeys because they recognize that Monkeys are the most amusing individuals around, and Roosters genuinely need to be entertained. Furthermore, Roosters are greatly impressed by your ability to resolve even the most intricate problems. You two are not at all similar. Roosters tend to be somber, rigid, and serious individuals. You Monkeys, by contrast, are quick-witted and agile in both body and spirit. Nevertheless, in this Rooster year, you will benefit from considerable goodwill. You can earn a significant amount of money, acquire numerous desirable items for yourself (such as cars, restaurant ranges, boats, houses, and—if you are so inclined—even an occasional winery or ranch). Best of all, in this unusually generous-to-Monkeys year, you will possess enough disposable income to lavish your loved ones (and even those you don't care for as much) with an abundance of presents. There will be days in this Rooster year when you return home laden with gifts for everyone. It will be like Father Christmas in July or Mother Christmas in September. Be vigilant for an overly cunning associate who (while you were on your shopping spree in Mendoza, Napa, or Burgundy) may have been embezzling funds. It could be your accountant, but it might also be your spouse or significant other. You will instinctively know how best to resolve this issue. Why? Because you’re a Monkey, of course!"},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Yang Metal",prediction:"Dogs are inherently mistrustful and prone to sarcasm. You Monkeys are well aware of corruption and savvy about the unsavory underbelly of the world. However, you would prefer to disregard all that and simply live for the present moment and enjoy something delightful to eat. The Dog year is not disastrous for Monkey individuals, but it is certainly not an easy period either. Firstly, financial difficulties may arise. In Dog years, money tends to be scarce. Dogs do not believe in waste and prefer not to live in lavish luxury or witness displays of excessive consumption. Dogs are champions for justice and are eager to see things done correctly. They are also remarkably blunt and critical, uttering disagreeable remarks without realizing how sharp and unkind they sound. You Monkeys want no part of this cynicism and do not care to join any movements aimed at improving the lives of homeless children in Brazil; it simply isn't your inclination. So, in Dog years, you will want to reduce your spending (which you needed to do anyway) and stay informed about current events. You will undoubtedly be called upon several times to participate in rallies advocating for the future of married Gay priests or to march for the right to life of all the litters of all the dogs in the thousands of animal shelters across your country. Do not be surprised. Maintain your amusing demeanor. Do not become depressed. Work diligently and frequently change your phone number to deter the do-gooders who will crowd your driveway if you allow them."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Yin Metal",prediction:"The pure-hearted Pig harbors little respect for you impulsive Monkeys. It's not that Pigs are joy-killers or wish to diminish your vibrancy; they don't. However, Pigs would rather luxuriate before a warm wood fire with a glass of the finest cognac, a Havana cigar, and engaging conversation than join a group of frolicking Monkeys on a noisy, smoky, and wild dance floor somewhere. Consequently, in this year, although you cannot rely on the Pig’s complete cooperation, you can depend on your own spirited nature to go out, earn money, and enjoy hobbies, sports, and other enjoyable activities. This would be an excellent year for you to join an amateur theater company or participate in some form of group therapy. You know how skilled you are at solving other people’s problems, right? Well, you are not known for being able to resolve your own. Monkeys are inherently neurotic. Somehow, you are blind to your own internal struggles and often simply stand there weeping and staring blankly at the challenges. All forms of talk therapy are recommended. You need to thoroughly discuss things to gain a comprehensive understanding of what is troubling you. If you can perceive yourself as others do, you will have made significant progress towards emotional health. The Pig is definitely on your side in this endeavor."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Yang Water",prediction:"After navigating through a couple of challenging years, you are finally in a space where you will be understood, celebrated, and admired for an entire year. Rats and Monkeys get along exceptionally well, like a perfectly matched pair. The Rat is an emotional individual who often struggles with making decisions. Should I buy a red car or a blue car? Marry a Dragon or a Tiger? Accept that new job offer or remain in my current position? How should I structure my life now that my parents are no longer around to influence me? What should I wear to the ball? By now, we all recognize that whenever one is grappling with a dilemma, whether large or small, the solution is to seek assistance from a Monkey. Monkeys cannot resolve their own problems very quickly, but they are masters at helping others make swift, practical choices. So, in a Rat year, you Monkey individuals will find yourselves frequently called upon to offer advice, to untangle complex issues, or to calm someone whose temper has them in a state of advanced agitation. You can always figure out the most graceful way to exit a difficult situation. Since you are not driven by power and never wish to be in the forefront, you are not in competition with the authority-seeking Rat. In other words, for Monkeys in Rat years, everything is proceeding smoothly."},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Yin Water",prediction:"Your preference for novelty and untested experiences can irritate the Ox. Oxen prefer things to remain (as much as possible) exactly as they were. So, you will confidently enter the Ox year, having just completed a satisfying Rat year where you pursued your own interests, and then—bam!—you will encounter the unyielding Ox temperament. However, there's no need to worry. Oxen can utilize some of your vibrant energy, so climb aboard the Ox’s strong back and progress through this year at its unhurried pace. For Monkeys, Ox years are periods of rest. The Ox protects you from your own tendencies and may even help prevent health issues by slowing you down and prompting you to thoroughly examine certain underlying concerns you've been needing to address. How is your relationship faring? What is the status of your career? How is your overall health? This is a time for medical checkups and dental examinations. Long conversations and strolls on the beach with your loved one (or ones) should help resolve any lingering grievances. Ensure your blood pressure is within a healthy range, and make sure to join a gym or take a tai chi class. Given your often erratic eating habits, the enforced slowdown in an Ox year could cause your body to expand significantly within a matter of weeks. Walk, run, jump—but avoid remaining stagnant."},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Yang Wood",prediction:'The Tiger consistently welcomes the presence of a Monkey in its midst, though not always continuously or for extended periods. In Chinese astrology, Monkeys and Tigers are traditionally considered adversaries. In practice, however, Tigers often befriend Monkeys, and vice versa. Nevertheless, what Tigers often do not reveal is that they frequently appreciate the company of Monkeys because Monkeys can resolve problems that Tigers cannot. Tigers enjoy Monkey humor and are somewhat entertained by their antics. But the true reason that you Monkeys will not face a difficult path this year is that the Tiger finds you useful. A business question? A travel predicament? Lost luggage? Lost love? Lost jobs? Simply "Dial-a-Monkey"—which is precisely what the Tiger year will prompt you to do. You will be called upon to advise and counsel others throughout this busy Tiger year. People may awaken you in the middle of the night just to ascertain your opinion on their church picnic for the following month. How should Tracey approach Nancy regarding the hard-boiled eggs? Who should cook the hot dogs? What types of games are safest for the children? Any kind of problem provides fodder for the Monkey’s agile mind. And people quickly realize that you can fix things for them. So you will be sought after and respected for your opinions in this Tiger year. However, you may not get married, become wealthy, or experience some grand passion this year, simply because there won’t be enough time.'},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Yin Wood",prediction:"Monkeys are widely known for gaining social or political influence during Cat/Rabbit years. The reason for this is quite straightforward when you consider that the Cat/Rabbit desires nothing overtly public to happen to him. He prefers to remain in the background while others perform and engage in activities on stage. You, as a Monkey, do not mind performing. In fact, entertaining others is one of your favorite pastimes. So, once again, you prove useful to the ruling sign, and what’s more, you are amusing. Cat/Rabbits often devise excellent strategies for earning or investing money, but they require a Monkey—a kind of engineer—to bring these plans to the attention of those in power. They also hold a monopoly on refinement and comfortable living. You, however, care very little about where you live and are about as refined as brown rice in a health food store bin. This disparity in styles might typically cause a rift between you and the sophisticated influences of this year. But it won't. The Cat/Rabbit employs your innate audacity to represent him, to be his spokesperson, to venture into society and present his case. That much you can and will gladly do. Therefore, this year, no tension will arise that could thwart any of your own plans. Seize the opportunity to reconfigure your life. Utilize your new contacts in high places to further your career and take pleasure from the Cat/Rabbit’s luxurious lifestyle."},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Yang Fire",prediction:"This year is perfectly suited for ambitious Monkeys who aspire to advance their careers and enhance their credentials. Dragons welcome Monkeys into their hearts, homes, businesses, and schools with a spirit of warm hospitality. Dragons love to laugh and enjoy a hearty chuckle over something amusing or unusual. Monkeys can conjure up jokes and stunts in an instant and perform pratfalls and eccentric visual gags without hesitation. Monkeys delight in entertaining their friends and brightening the atmosphere in any way they can. To those of us who prefer quiet over noise, repose over activity, and consistently choose seriousness over silliness, the Monkey’s need to divert and amuse is downright annoying. But for Dragons, who adore celebration, invent reasons to host parties when none exist, and willingly participate in all general merrymaking, the Monkey’s antics provide a welcome relief from boredom. This year, you will have the opportunity to earn a significant amount of money. Nobody or nothing will stand in your way. The fearless Dragon protects and admires Monkeys. Take full advantage of this benevolence; and for once in your life, bask in the spotlight, seize that microphone, and confidently create a better life for yourself."}}},h={introduction:`Jaunty Rooster, you were born to bounce back. Your life is a roller-coaster ride, a chaotic mix of successes and setbacks, periods of prosperity and hardship, trials, tribulations, and other emotionally draining or gut-wrenching experiences, yet you remain an irrepressibly steadfast and courageous spirit. Resilience is your defining characteristic. Regardless of the depth of despair, you simply pick yourself up, smooth your feathers, and confidently stride forward once more. You radiate enthusiasm. Your joy in experiencing new thrills is infectious. People eagerly seek your company, wishing to visit your places, see your sights, and share your exciting way of life. You will frequently hold positions of authority. You are naturally inclined to lead and excel at setting a positive example. You work exceptionally hard.

Despite a sometimes arrogant demeanor and a tendency towards conceit, you cannot be accused of being either overly aggressive or pedantic. You are a multi-talented, open-minded, yet curiously conservative individual. In matters of love, you are captivated by elegance and sophistication. Consider pursuing a glamorous Snake, or engage with an encouraging Dog. Even better, for the sake of a challenge, allow yourself to be charmed by a steady Ox. All of these pairings are capable of easing the difficulties and alleviating the strain of your exhaustingly busy life.

Listen closely. Heed my advice: you are too direct for your own benefit. Make an effort to be less candid. Your bluntness can be your downfall. Feel free to promote yourself, but try not to expose your own weaknesses in the process. Remember, a Rooster in trouble is nothing more than chicken soup.`,elements:{Wood:`This Rooster possesses a unique ability to persevere in areas where significant effort is crucial for achieving results. Its inherent vigor, conscientiousness, and meticulousness empower it to execute complex tasks that might intimidate less organized or "picky" individuals. However, do not ask the Wood Rooster to agree to spend a lifetime poring over yellowed texts in a dark attic room to produce an encyclopedic volume at the end of its life. Wood Roosters are only capable of exerting enormous effort for short-term undertakings. This individual is best suited for roles such as an efficiency expert, troubleshooter, or project manager, whose primary objective is to "get the job done well—now."

It is a sociable creature and enjoys being in friendly company where it can express itself, share some of its best stories, recount its travels, or listen attentively to the tales spun by its companions. Parties and festivals delight this naturally hospitable type, who will often host, do the cooking, purchase the wine, and (although it is far from wasteful with money) indulge its beloved guests with luxuries for the pleasure of ensuring they have a good time.

Some consider the Wood Rooster a superficial person because appearance holds paramount importance for him. It is important to understand that, on a personal level, he is preoccupied—even obsessed—with youth and fascinated by the "look" of things. Wood Roosters sincerely believe that one's appearance reflects one's essence. They cannot tolerate the idea of being old, irritable, wrinkled, or excluded from mainstream ideas. Even after middle age, the Wood Rooster is likely to continue dressing in youthful, form-fitting clothing and exert every effort to remain slender, agile, and self-assured. He seeks the company and intimacy of people younger than himself in an attempt to maintain his vitality. He often behaves in a manner not entirely consistent with his age—taking up roller-skating at forty, purchasing rock music at sixty, and dancing at seventy in noisy discos where no one else has yet reached their twentieth birthday.

As talkative and sociable as this creature is, the Wood Rooster has a significant emotional block when it comes to expressing his feelings. He can converse extensively about anything he considers polite conversation. In private, however, on subjects deeply personal to one’s heart and soul, he remains completely uncommunicative. If you love one of these emotionally reserved individuals, you will face a considerable challenge trying to encourage him to articulate what is on his mind. Whether this Rooster is angry or sorry, sad, glad, or madly, passionately in love, his exterior remains cool, sleek, well-groomed, nervous, and rather too serious. The Wood Rooster is the type of emotionally constrained person to whom it is necessary to ask a hundred times a day, "Do you love me, darling?" or "Honey, are you angry with me?" They require profound emotional events and insistent, heartfelt lovers to help them open up. Unless the Wood Rooster learns to directly address his feelings, an unhealthy accumulation of anger and resentment will almost certainly remain with him and his intimates for the rest of his days.`,Fire:`Complexity! And passion. Fire illuminates the Rooster in peculiar, exaggerated ways, causing him to be born tormented, difficult, and fiery! Fire Roosters are volatile, craving confrontation and confidently rushing from one head-on collision to another without sustaining so much as a tiny scratch.

This Rooster seems to thrive on exhilaration. He is enthusiastic about and involved in everything. Monotony and a lack of challenge bore and depress him. He desires to be right in the midst of the action, on the front lines. Regardless of how tough the dare, he will gladly undertake it. His capacity for work is monumental. His endurance is legendary. His cutting-edge brilliance at absorbing information is staggering. And, finally, his ability to organize others at work while still retaining their respect and affection is top-tier. Fire Roosters were born to be world-beaters, but, unfortunately for them, Fate simultaneously cursed them with a built-in emotional instability.

Fire Roosters should be more successful than they typically are. They are relentlessly ambitious, intelligent, and competent individuals. They make excellent lawyers, caring doctors, innovative scientists, and capable business people. However, because emotions play a primary role in how these individuals conduct business, they often create confusion. Whether they are deeply involved in a conference, eloquently presenting facts in a court case, or reciting crucial figures at a bankruptcy hearing, Fire Roosters remain vulnerable to emotional involvement. They can be swayed into submission if the boss’s wife has had a miscarriage, feel sympathetic because the accountant is overweight, or distort their plea because the other lawyer’s husband just lost his job—anything emotional that enters the Fire Rooster’s mind during business hours poses a potential danger to the outcome of his efforts. Objectivity eludes him.

This person is impulsive, headstrong, and cannot be easily reasoned with. Conjugal life with a Fire Rooster is a testament to friction and very often becomes explosive to the point of being unbearable. He can be tyrannical and despotic, too, especially if his pride is offended. The Fire Rooster believes strongly in absolute rightness and earnestly desires the truth to be revealed. But if voicing the truth involves revealing his own vulnerability or letting down his guard, the Fire Rooster may simply refuse and miss the point entirely: his promises are often little more than promises. He’s emotionally fragile, needing to be liked as well as to enjoy the thrill of victory. He fails because he's conflicted. He doesn't want to apply the rules of ruthlessness to his own advancement, yet because he is so intellectually gifted for clarity, he can perfectly well discern what is necessary to succeed.

On the positive side, the Fire Rooster is a fabulous friend, an amusing companion, and an honest, truthful colleague. In social settings, he enjoys his role as a non-conformist and is sometimes even exhibitionistically bohemian to make a point. He possesses a sound sense of morality, but will not go out of his way unless you go out of yours to champion causes or perform good deeds. He is a tit-for-tat person whose love of honesty and talent for being brutally frank carries him cheerfully along on the crest of his own enthusiasm. He falters when he confronts emotional imperatives with which he cannot reason. But, because he is a Rooster, even repeated failures and torrential setbacks do not deter his courage or dampen his spirit. He was born to bounce back.

As he is easily labeled puritanical in his approach to sex, this deeply troubled Rooster might be better off living in a cloister, adopting some ascetic course of action that does not demand emotional involvement. When effectively utilized, the Fire Rooster’s richly nuanced emotional capacity can produce excellent creative results. But if he chooses to become an artist, he will require both isolation and protection from the outside world.`,Earth:`A powerful intellect combined with a flair for the aesthetic, feminine side of life bestows upon this Rooster a talent for nuance and creativity that surpasses that of his more conventional Rooster brothers and sisters. Because of his gift for conversation, some find the Earth Rooster exasperatingly vague and accuse him of not sticking to the point when he delivers rambling speeches. His ability to engage with abstract concepts allows him great verbal freedom, but for those who value concrete facts, his mental meanderings can seem incomprehensible. There's no need to worry, however: this Rooster also has a firm grasp on factual information.

His thought processes can best be described as "penetrating," and his critical abilities as "dead accurate." When he needs to be precise, an Earth Rooster always gets straight to the point, recalling every single detail and date of what occurred previously. He will never allow his interlocutor to get away with fudging even a single detail. It's almost as if, to counteract his own tendency towards vagueness, he feels compelled to be ruthlessly factual in his recollections. Earth Roosters possess elephantine memories, minds like steel traps, and enough common sense to manage both Hungary and Yugoslavia single-handedly.

This is an uncommonly elegant person of regal bearing whose sense of humor—a twinkle, a wink, or a swift, ambiguous glance—always shines through his slightly forbidding facade. It is his great fortune to possess excellent health and frequently to live to a great age. Not only does he live a long time in good condition, the Earth Rooster ages gracefully, retains his agile, quick wit, and rarely suffers symptoms of senility. I know three 1909 Roosters and am certain that today any one of them could tackle a battery of the demanding exams we set our eighteen-year-olds. Earth Roosters grow old with poise, remaining steadfast and individualistic, but shedding the anxiety of their troubled youth to become serene and accepting.

The Earth Rooster only reaches his optimal performance once he has found true love. As he is somewhat timid in youth, he doesn’t always dare to be forward with the opposite sex. An air of naive embarrassment may deter others from attempting to seduce this reserved, conservative creature. He is unlikely to bring home some fleeting lover picked up at a singles bar, usually becoming involved with someone met through a cousin or at a family gathering or wedding. They often marry later than their peers, and because they choose carefully and wait for the right person, they rarely get divorced.

Sexual passion is not the strong suit of this deeply loving person. No tender pats on the head, overt signs of affection, poetic love letters, or exotic love potions for this no-nonsense individual. The Earth Rooster prefers to keep love pure and sensible, never allowing his pristine image to become muddled with sentimental scenes or sticky with emotion.

To succeed professionally, Earth Roosters require a support network. Working for a family business or a large corporation suits them, as they always enjoy playing an integral part in a communal effort. These individuals make excellent accountants, bankers, doctors, architects, and designers. They are meticulous with details and non-impulsive. Although they may experience some tough financial patches, Earth Roosters do not usually go bankrupt or lose their fortunes through foolish investments.`,Metal:`Here is a creature born to be on the stage, in the movies, or simply in the middle of his own living room, putting on a show for his family. The Metal Rooster is a performer, the life and soul of the party. People either like this fervent person immensely or find it difficult to tolerate him. Metal Roosters are sometimes boastful: they enjoy promoting themselves, sharing their success stories and those of their family, and generally letting you know how wonderful they are. Although this trait can be tiresome, the Metal Rooster’s purpose is neither egotistical nor greedy. He doesn’t want to impress anyone because he needs or wants something from them. Rather, it is part of his flamboyant nature. Although some find it irritating, others, because this person is usually funny and imaginative, adore being invited to witness the daily spectacle and manage to live happily ever after with this incorrigible entertainer.

If he doesn’t learn to temper it while young, this brash, confident person’s tongue can get him into trouble throughout his life. He is incapable of diplomacy and has a way of blurting out indelicate truths at the most inopportune moments, encountering failure and rejection where he might have found success and approval. When criticized for being too candid, the Metal Rooster may erupt into a short-lived fit of defensive rage. He isn’t the type to bear a grudge. But, given his inclination for speechmaking, his verbose outbursts of bad temper can be impressive enough to cloud an otherwise sunny afternoon.

The Metal Rooster loves organization: he needs to keep things neat and tidy—a place for everything and everything in its place. He doesn’t like to be interrupted when devising new tricks or engaged in his favorite hobby. He cannot tolerate having too much improvisation imposed upon him.

All of the above somewhat fastidious traits may cause a Metal Rooster to spend his adult life alone, without a full-time partner, children, or pets to disrupt the life he has so meticulously planned.

Roosters hold conservative political opinions. They make excellent policemen and, as they crave movement, thrive on travel, and enjoy being expatriates, may find lucrative, secure positions with organizations such as the FBI or Interpol. Of course, their inherent indiscretion might hinder their progress in jobs requiring top-secret classifications. But the Metal Rooster is intelligent and, with a little help from his friends, can certainly learn how to keep quiet in life-or-death circumstances.

The Metal Rooster is perfectly suited for jobs in theater, cinema, and TV. If he does not choose to perform, he should try to become involved in production. When he succeeds in this challenging profession, he will certainly have many fans and followers who will cheer him on and keep his career advancing. He is a natural for stand-up comedy routines, as a talk-show host, and might make a superb newscaster, roving reporter, and even war correspondent.`,Water:`Here we encounter the exceptionally multi-talented Rooster. Possessing all the most significant Rooster strengths and weaknesses combined, the Water Rooster might be considered the quintessential model for all other Roosters. He is serious. He is resolute and meticulous. He talks about himself quite a bit. He meticulously cares for his appearance as well as his wardrobe. He is a willing traveler and adores adventure. He knows how to work diligently and persistently to achieve a goal. He endures many setbacks, yet no matter how far he falls behind financially, this Rooster can always discover a new way to earn a living from nothing.

There are, however, a few distinct characteristics about the Water Rooster that set him apart. He is exceptionally adaptable. He’s not rigid but does hold conservative views on almost everything—except his rather inconsistent pattern of fidelity—which he accepts as his inherent right and privilege. Ironically, the Water Rooster is also jealous and possessive of his lovers and mistresses. For him, a double standard applies. Why? Because he says so. Water Roosters either get to be the boss, or they pack their bags and go home.

The Water Rooster loves to be surrounded by people. The more individuals who contact him on any given day, the happier he becomes. He actively seeks out the company of friends and family and will go to great lengths to succeed. He entertains frequently and is often an excellent cook and host. Possibly because he is so eager for companionship, he may, at times, lend assistance to someone less scrupulous than himself. If he is not careful, he may be exploited by ruthless individuals who profit from his goodwill and offer nothing in return.

The Water Rooster is thin-skinned. He cannot tolerate being advised, interfered with, or—heaven forbid—reprimanded. Even if he knows he has made mistakes or is about to encounter significant trouble, he does not wish to be reminded or warned of it. His reactions are not positive to even the mildest suggestion on how he might alter his approach or modify his thinking. If you don’t want to lose his friendship, do not attempt to play truth games with the Water Rooster. If you dare to utter one piercingly true statement in his presence, he’ll become unpleasant and hostile. He may only sulk for a period, but he might never call you again.

Essentially, the Water Rooster suffers from an inferiority complex. He often wishes that he were someone more fortunate whose parents had left him a fortune, a network of influential contacts in the world, or, even better, a chain of supermarkets to call his own. This Rooster often carries a chip on his shoulder about the injustices he feels society has committed against him, but, as he will not listen to the truth about himself nor squarely face his real place in the world, he often has to confront failure, which exacerbates his inferiority complex. As he grows older, this cycle of events becomes increasingly detrimental. If he cannot lower his guard and learn to accept advice, he may become so disgruntled that, by middle age, he may be permanently embittered, withdrawing from society and life as a cheerful hippie or a homeless person.

Despite his unflagging energy and industriousness, the Water Rooster secretly desires to be wealthy. He often envisions himself in a luxurious environment where satin sheets are commonplace and silk pajamas are essential. He even dreams of ample leisure time to recline and read novels and philosophical texts. Roosters are not adept at being idle, as they become bored when they have too much free time. Therefore, this period of idleness usually remains merely a dream.

It is not the Water Rooster’s destiny to become rich overnight. If he marries a wealthy woman whose father owns the biggest construction business in town, the old man will almost certainly go bankrupt the week after the wedding or die and leave all his money to some charity. If he enters into some get-rich-quick business deal where he feels certain to make a fortune in a week, the Better Business Bureau may shut him down or someone will report on TV that his products are defective. The Water Rooster is born to labor. He is both talented for and fated to earn a living from the most barren ground and, above all, to persist day after day, building a solid financial foundation until he has amassed a fortune. His lot may be demanding, but it is nothing to be ashamed of.

Water Roosters possess a seductive quality. Not only are they excellent conversationalists, but they also have a charming way with words that makes them irresistible as salespeople, lovers, advertisers, politicians, and teachers. Loving one of these masterful Water Roosters is a full-time commitment. They do not like to be left alone and cannot tolerate idleness. They require adoration and praise—but even if they receive more than their fair share of compliments, they still may not always be faithful to their partner.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"The Rat and the Rooster incessantly peck away at each other. They are equally jealous and possessive, as well as anxious about their combined future. One would expect this alliance to devote long hours to mutual accounts, carefully monitoring each debit. Nervous and impatient to pin down every detail, they’ve surely planned ahead, booking their flights to London and their trips to Morocco months in advance. Not so! Each considers that the other should be the adult in the relationship. Indeed, each wants freedom from burdensome responsibility. Rooster and Rat are forever arguing over money. Each deems the other too extravagant on the wrong items. The showy Rooster desires a shimmering new Jaguar. The Rat wants a crumbling stone house in the countryside. They will never agree. A lively Rat with an active social calendar makes a possessive Rooster turn green with envy. A socially active Rat paired with a conservative Rooster feels stifled. The rebellious Rat accepts prestigious invitations and leaves the jilted Rooster at home alone. Crushed by the Rat's frequent absences, the Rooster grows insecure and seeks new ways to confine the Rat. Using sex as a weapon, each deprives the other when they quarrel. Although fundamentally capable of enjoying each other, their mundane conflicts surface in the bedroom. This allows for only intermittent pleasure on the occasional peaceful Tuesday. The union is unstable, at best.",Ox:"Should you be fortunate enough to have found each other, remain together. People consistently notice an Ox/Rooster couple. 'Look how content they are!' they remark. Astrologers in China recommend this as one of the most favorable unions ever! Together, your lives will be enriched by a blend of effortless sociability and unwavering security. Individually, the Ox and the Rooster can be equally meticulous, anxious, and perfectionistic. One might expect this pairing to come together and then self-destruct. But, for some reason, they discover peace. This traditional couple lives strictly by the rules. The Ox performs everything correctly, and the Rooster follows suit. They purchase their first home at the appropriate stage of life, have children when expected, and retire to their beautiful country residence when they become wealthy—which often happens very quickly. Both are keen, capable workers. They are not particularly fond of social outings, preferring to remain close to home. Children will be more than welcome here. This stable pair provides great security for a family. Not known for passion or recklessness, their sexual intimacy reflects their practical lifestyle. No embellishments, just basic, normal lovemaking. Two naturally harmonious signs should ensure this happy marriage is long-lived and successful.",Tiger:"I don’t recommend this pair for marriage. Both parties are aggressive and opinionated; neither will back down easily. The atmosphere will be taut and most arguments one-sided. Conflicts and collisions are guaranteed to hinder the harmonious progress of this couple. Tigers bounce back and forget every nasty word that was said. But Roosters carry grudges and cannot forget how badly they were treated by a Tiger last time they had a row. Impasses are common. In bed, there may be some fairly exciting fireworks, as the Rooster is imaginative and energetic enough to keep the demanding Tiger interested. They are both impetuous and uninhibited lovers capable of grand gestures and profound intensity. Unless the disagreements of the day carry over into the bedroom, this couple is well aspected for a long, healthy sex life—without marriage.",Rabbit:"This couple should think twice before taking the lifelong plunge into matrimony. The sex is mediocre at best. Although Cats are initially attracted by the haughty Rooster’s natural nobility and aura of reserve, they may be misinterpreting the Rooster’s real methods and motives. Basically, Roosters want to be free to roam and race about following the peripatetic bent of their roller-coaster existence. Cats like to stay at home, work long and hard at quiet jobs, get and stay rich. Lifestyle would quickly become a problem for this pair. With their individual approaches being so gapingly different, who, I ask you, would take out the garbage? Certainly not the refined Cat, who is too busy reading philosophical tomes and decorating magazines on a Louis XV chaise longue. As for the Rooster—he’s hardly ever home long enough to create any garbage, or babies. If the pair has the means (and nothing prevents them from earning money, as they are both hardworking, serious types) to hire help for the baser human chores, they can establish a solid, functional family life.",Dragon:"Both passion and glamour are missing from this otherwise well-balanced relationship. It is workable. Dragon protects with gusto and Rooster obeys with serious intent to do the right thing. Neither is ecstatic in this arrangement but, then, neither is blatantly unhappy. Roosters recognize and respect the Dragon’s need to shine, to assert superiority over others and go out and beat the world at its game. Despite sometimes flamboyant outward appearances, the Rooster is a rank conservative. Roosters do want to voice their truths and implement their ideals. But they don’t show off. With a brave and daring Dragon partner, the Rooster can carry on being quietly cocky while the Dragon plays the conspicuous role. I’m afraid the Dragon’s exorbitant sexual needs may prove overwhelming to the less sensual Rooster. Rooster’s rebuffs may destroy Dragon’s ego. The solution will only be found in frank discussion with an objective third party. A therapist? A clergyman? A family friend?",Snake:"A love match if ever I saw one! The Rooster is rather bourgeois and conventional. Snakes are esthetic and long to appear attractive at all times. Although, at first glance, it may seem that the Snake is too sophisticated and elegant for the plain-living Rooster, the opposite is true. Roosters and Snakes form some of the best couples. They are both quite secretive and like to keep to themselves. Yet, when together, they are forever locked in intense discussion and consideration of every detail, from the quality of light inside their fridge to the leather on the soles of their expensive shoes. Roosters are mostly forgiving, indulgent people whose loyalty knows no frontiers. Snakes may run around a bit, both socially and sexually, but they are careful never to get deeply involved with their conquests and hardly ever betray or leave their Rooster mates. Why? Because they truly love them. In this marriage, the Rooster should look after the finances. Snakes often waste money. Roosters keep closer tabs on their pennies. The cultural side can be handled equally well by both. Sex should definitely be left up to the seductive Snake. Snakes know how to turn on hesitant Roosters, to make their bodies sing. Roosters are basically reserved about sensual matters. The Rooster who lands a Snake for a mate will have much to crow about.",Horse:"Unless stimulated by the right partner, both Roosters and Horses become stodgy and work-obsessed. This couple would need a professional or family connection in order to be thrown together in the first place. There is not much charisma on either side at the outset. But, with some work, the relationship can grow and endure. Once together, the Horse will be flattered by the Rooster’s possessive streak, but in time will resent it and dissension will set in. Horse wants to go out and play and Rooster wants them both safely at home – even if it’s only to share the Sunday crossword puzzle. For this relationship to succeed, the Horse must learn to be less outgoing and the Rooster more tolerant of the Horse’s need for social interaction. Roosters are so conservative that, although Horse’s occasional outrageousness appeals to their rebellious side, they will worry nonstop about the negative outcome of their mate’s follies. A Rooster’s best bet is to give the Horse a longer and longer rein, and wait sanely by the fireside till Horsey comes cantering back for dinner. At first, their sex life may be limited by Rooster’s excessive conservatism. The practical Horse will rise to the occasion and prod Rooster to be more innovative. In time, when they learn to satisfy each other’s needs, their sexual rapport can become nigh unto perfect.",Goat:"This is a dicey combination. Roosters are conservative and individualistic. They deplore laziness and cannot tolerate lackadaisical attitudes in others. Goats like to take it easy. They don’t believe in work for its own sake, would rather sit still than move about, and are ever ready to get someone else to take care of their basic needs. As the Rooster often had great difficulty scratching out a living, he or she will be impatient with the idea of anyone living off the fat of the land and will wish the Goat would find a “real” job, like a normal person. Goat’s feelings are readily hurt. Tensions can mount in this household and very little will be talked through, because the Rooster hates discussing his emotions. The fickle Goat may wander sexually, causing the staid and faithful Rooster untold pain. Trouble is, the Goat needs more than just the Rooster’s perfunctory affections. Knowing this fact creates feelings of inadequacy and a lack of self-confidence in the Rooster. If Goat could be persuaded to stick around all the time and teach the willing Rooster how to be more sensual, their relationship might have a good chance at success. At least it would give more purpose to the otherwise idle Goat’s home life. Goat with Rooster is far from an ideal marriage.",Monkey:"Not much is going on sexually between these two characters. Roosters are possessive and anxious about their position in relationships. Their instinct is to anchor their prey. Monkeys need miles of rope to feel good about themselves. They have to roam amid people, jabber with others and find solutions to ever more important problems. Roosters are conservative thinkers. Monkeys are all for liberation, gentler laws and personal liberty. This couple may be constantly at odds over policy. Decisions become difficult. Tensions rise and Rooster suffers—because Rooster makes the untenable scenes that send the Monkey packing. Roosters must accept Monkey’s devil-may-care side to enjoy the benefit of his or her humor. It’s up to the Rooster to be more flexible. And that is a tall order. So these two are not exactly Romeo and Juliet. Monkey is interested in sex, but he’s also fascinated by life’s other aspects—above all its practicalities. Rooster is also practical and appreciates Monkey’s delight in solving concrete issues. But Rooster needs softening, romancing, loving and cuddling to appreciate the joys of sex. Now it’s Monkey’s turn to adapt, to become more languorous and spend time petting and nuzzling. Or Rooster (God forbid!) might begin scratching around in another barnyard for sexual understanding.",Rooster:"Difficult at best, this couple’s inevitable clashes over everything from money to styles of clothing and which schools to send the children to are practically never worth sorting out. What we face here are two opinionated, ego-centered people. They are, first of all, victims of themselves and require jollier, more acquiescent partners than either can be for the other. Roosters need to be cushioned and coaxed. I hardly see any Rooster accepting to do the coaxing for another—unless in a war where the other Rooster was a fallen buddy. The war metaphor is suitable. Each Rooster engaged in a Rooster/Rooster couple wants to be the General. Each needs to feel superior to the other. Each is conservative and shy, unsure of his image and feisty beyond feistiness. Battles royal rage daily, viciously tearing harmony to shreds. Roosters often befriend each other. They think alike and have similar views. They can even work together—providing one takes a backseat. But romantic love between Roosters rarely produces equilibrium. The sex is lukewarm: neither is able to express passion without help from a more vigorously self-assured partner.",Dog:"Incompatibility reigns supreme in this couple. Dogs and Roosters are equally flinty and raw-nerved. Dogs are forever blurting criticism and bruising the egos of those around them. Roosters are cocky but deeply unsure of themselves. One yelp from the Dog’s storehouse of biting blatancies can put the Rooster under for days, depress him and undo his hard-earned image. Do these people fight? They never stop. Backbiting, carping, bickering over details. They don’t agree on anything. Dogs are classically left wing, kindly and trustworthy. Roosters are born conservatives who believe in the system, adhere to society’s basic tenets and cleave to traditional ways. This couple’s home life is a constant push-me pull-you of political unrest. Dog wants revolution. Rooster devoutly wishes for status quo. Dog thinks mismatched china and a pallet on the floor will do nicely. Rooster wants Spode or Limoges set with crystal grasses on an heirloom table. Dog wants to spend money on causes. Rooster wants to keep his money in the bank. Rooster demands more and varied sex than Dog has to give. Rooster needs to puff up his ego and preen his feathers. Dog couldn’t care less what he looks like in bed. He feels sex rather than performing it. Besides, Dogs are slightly puritanical. They don’t believe one should overindulge in pleasure. Leave the Rooster/Dog love relationship alone.",Pig:"This partnership can succeed brilliantly. Roosters who find themselves in bed with willing, sensual Pigs are truly in luck. My advice to this lucky Rooster is to hang on tight: you will not find such amiability, charm and easygoing service anywhere else in the zodiac. Pigs are willing to adapt and change, modify their personalities and lifestyles to suit the one they love. With all of your ups and downs, resounding successes and failures, you will definitely benefit from the presence of a kindly, nurturing, understanding Pig. As for the Pig in this relationship, you will gain much from the pure rigor and frank style of a Rooster partner. Roosters like things as they are. They are not revolutionaries. Pigs, too, enjoy tradition and respect the basic tenets of a good society. Your common interests will flourish and after the first few years will take you very far towards achieving dreams and goals you only dreamed of before meeting. Sex, too, is favored in this couple. The Rooster can take charge in lovemaking. Pigs appreciate being moved to exotic heights in bed, adore almost anything sensual and make excellent cuddlers for roughshod Rooster to learn to snuggle with. If I were a Rooster, I think I might seek a Pig mate. Your lifetime happiness and financial security (Pigs attract money) would be assured."},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Wood",prediction:"This year is a good one for you. Snakes and Roosters are allies. You can anticipate making good progress in your career and enjoying a stable love life. The Snake's philosophical nature will appeal to your own intellectual side. You will find much to discuss and may even embark on a joint project together. Financially, it’s a time of security. The Snake’s wisdom and your own diligence will ensure that you have more than enough. It's a good year for investing, particularly in areas related to art and culture. Romantically, you will be captivated by the Snake’s charm and sensuality. Your loyalty will be deeply appreciated, and you will find a profound connection with your partner. This is a year of harmony, intellectual stimulation, and personal growth."},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Fire",prediction:"This is a year of action and hard work. The Horse’s energy and your own diligent nature are a good combination for productivity. However, you may find the Horse’s pace a bit frantic. You prefer a more methodical approach. Professionally, your hard work will be rewarded, but you may have to adapt to new and faster ways of doing things. Financially, it’s a good year for earning money, but be careful not to get caught up in the Horse’s extravagant spending habits. Your natural conservatism will serve you well. In your love life, you may find the Horse’s need for constant excitement a bit tiring. You prefer a more settled existence. However, the Horse’s passion can also be invigorating. This is a year for adapting to a faster pace and reaping the rewards of your labor."},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Fire",prediction:"This will be a frustrating year for you. The Goat’s whimsical, and sometimes lazy, nature will clash with your own disciplined and hardworking personality. You will feel that no one is taking things seriously, and your efforts to impose order will be met with artistic temperament and emotional displays. It’s a time to be patient and to focus on your own tasks. Don't expect much from others. Financially, this is not a year for major gains. The Goat’s influence is not conducive to practical matters. It’s a time for conserving your resources. Romantically, you may find the Goat’s need for constant reassurance and its emotional volatility to be draining. Your straightforward nature may not be appreciated. It’s a year to practice tolerance and to lower your expectations."},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Earth",prediction:"This is a year of intellectual stimulation and strategic maneuvering. The Monkey’s cleverness will impress you, and you will enjoy the challenge of a good debate. However, be wary of the Monkey’s tendency to play games. You are a straightforward person and may not appreciate the Monkey’s love of intrigue. Professionally, this is a good year for problem-solving and for using your analytical skills. You may find yourself in a position where you have to outsmart the competition. Financially, it’s a time for caution. The Monkey’s influence can lead to risky schemes. Trust your own judgment and avoid anything that seems too good to be true. Romantically, the Monkey’s wit can be very attractive, but its lack of seriousness may be a source of frustration. This is a year for keeping your wits about you and for enjoying a good mental workout."},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Earth",prediction:"This is your year to take charge and to put your own house in order. You will feel a strong urge to organize, to budget, and to make plans for the future. Your natural leadership abilities will be in demand. However, be careful not to become too dictatorial. Your tendency to criticize can be off-putting to others. Professionally, this is an excellent year for management and for any work that requires precision and attention to detail. Financially, your conservative nature will serve you well. It’s a time for saving and for making sensible investments. Romantically, if you are with another Rooster, you will find a shared sense of purpose and a mutual understanding. However, the lack of spontaneity can be a bit dull. Make an effort to inject some fun and romance into your life. This is a year for being in control and for building a solid foundation."},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Metal",prediction:"This will be a difficult year for you. The Dog’s idealism and your own conservatism are at odds. You will find yourself in constant disagreement over matters of principle. The Dog will want to fight for justice, while you will want to maintain the status quo. This can lead to heated arguments and a general sense of unease. Professionally, you may find that your practical approach is not valued in a climate of social change. It’s a time to keep your head down and to avoid controversy. Financially, the Dog’s generosity will conflict with your own frugality. Don’t let yourself be guilt-tripped into supporting causes you don’t believe in. Romantically, your need for order will clash with the Dog’s more chaotic and emotional nature. It’s a year of conflict and frustration. Patience and tolerance are essential for survival."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Metal",prediction:"This is a very favorable year for you. The Pig’s good nature and your own sense of duty make for a harmonious combination. You will find that your hard work is appreciated and that your efforts are rewarded. Professionally, it’s a time for steady progress. Your diligence will lead to success. Financially, this is a very prosperous year. The Pig’s luck with money and your own sound judgment will bring you wealth. It’s a good time for enjoying the fruits of your labor. Romantically, the Pig’s sensuality and your own loyalty are a perfect match. You will find great contentment and security in your relationship. This is a year of peace, prosperity, and happiness. Enjoy it."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Water",prediction:"This year will be a period of conflict and stress for you. The Rat’s ambition and your own desire for control will lead to a power struggle. You will both want to be in charge, and neither of you will be willing to back down. This can lead to bitter arguments and a breakdown in communication. Professionally, you will find yourself in a competitive environment. It’s a time for being assertive and for defending your territory. Financially, there will be disputes over money. The Rat’s extravagance will clash with your own conservative approach. Be prepared for arguments over spending. In your love life, possessiveness and jealousy will be major issues. This is a year of tension and conflict. It will require all your skills of diplomacy to navigate."},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Water",prediction:"This is an excellent year for you. The Ox is your most powerful ally. You share a common work ethic, a love of order, and a conservative outlook. You will find great harmony and mutual support in this relationship. Professionally, your diligence and the Ox’s strength will lead to great success. It’s a time for building, for consolidating, and for achieving your long-term goals. Financially, this is a very secure year. Your combined efforts will lead to prosperity. Romantically, you will find a deep and lasting bond with your partner. Your shared values will create a stable and happy home life. This is a year of achievement, security, and contentment."},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Wood",prediction:"This will be a challenging year. The Tiger’s impulsiveness and your own need for order are a difficult combination. You will find the Tiger’s constant need for excitement and its disregard for rules to be very stressful. It’s a time for being flexible and for adapting to change. Professionally, you may find that your careful plans are disrupted by unforeseen events. You will need to be quick on your feet to respond. Financially, it’s a volatile year. The Tiger’s risk-taking can lead to both great gains and great losses. Be cautious. Romantically, the Tiger’s passion is exciting, but its temper can be frightening. This is a year for courage and for learning to go with the flow."},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Wood",prediction:"This year, you will feel at odds with the prevailing atmosphere. The Rabbit’s refined and gentle nature will seem frivolous to your practical mind. You may also find that your directness is not appreciated in a climate that values diplomacy and subtlety. Professionally, you may feel that your hard work is not being properly valued. It’s a time for patience and for not taking things personally. Financially, it’s a stable but uninspiring year. The Rabbit’s influence is not conducive to major financial undertakings. Romantically, you may find the Rabbit’s indirectness and emotional sensitivity to be frustrating. Your own conservative nature in love may not be enough to keep the peace. This is a year for practicing tolerance and for trying to understand a different point of view."},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Fire",prediction:"This is a year of opportunity and expansion. The Dragon’s energy and your own ambition can lead to great success. However, you will have to share the spotlight, which may not come easily to you. The Dragon’s flamboyance can also be a bit much for your conservative tastes. Professionally, this is a time for being bold and for taking on new challenges. The Dragon’s influence will help you to achieve your goals. Financially, it’s a year of extravagance. You will be tempted to spend lavishly. Enjoy yourself, but try to keep a rein on your spending. Romantically, the Dragon’s passion is intoxicating, but its ego can be overwhelming. This is a year for being confident and for enjoying the fruits of your ambition."}}},d={introduction:`Dear Doggie,  
Man's best buddy truly: you are truthful, loyal, and real. You provide true worth back for love. You are a nice pal—when you're feeling happy. To meet you is to like you, unless you toss out a mean remark or shoot quick jabs at us clueless folks nearby. You have a loud yap, Doggie, that makes even your worst chomp feel mild.  

But you kindly fix that. You trust in rightness for everyone and gladly pick up good fights and carry big loads against wrong rules. You honor old ways and prize respect. You find true joy in aiding an older person cross a crowded road. In life's grand cowboy tale, you surely sport a white hat.  

A sharp smart knack lets you spot tricks and chase down cheats. Problem is, this skill for honesty is so strong it sometimes makes you turn gloomy. Deep sadness and even gloom might follow.  

To guard against this drift to despair, try to hang out with fun friends whose cheer and zest keep you steady. Pair up with a bold Tiger, a dreamy Horse, or a warm, calming Cat. At a young age, you’ll start to see the world is a really unfair spot. You’ll jump into missions and aim to fix simple wrongs.  

My tip? Try not to be so stiffly proper. Welcome some give-and-take. Snuggle up here by the flames and picture brighter times.`,elements:{Wood:`With a huge heart, this Dog is very caring, gentle, and sweet. Once people figure out how to break through the Wood Dog’s tough shell, they adore him, and this time, he feels the same. Wood Dogs love meeting others. They wish to chat with all kinds of folks, grow varied friend circles, and mix with every sort of person out there. For this Dog, team fun, work buddies, and group tasks are not just okay but best.  

The Wood Dog often builds himself up. A natural edge comes from being super careful and stubbornly set. This mix pushes Wood Dogs to the top of nearly any job they pick. Plus, they’re great at managing everything, even themselves. They watch every little bit, track each task with close care, and can’t step away from hard work for long without feeling bad. This focus gives the Wood Dog a big lead in jobs needing deep study, exact plans, and pure grit.  

The Wood Dog can sniff out a phony, catch fibs, and dig up hidden stuff. He’s smart in a figuring-out way and has a firm style fit for leading. The Wood Dog has a talent for stirring crowds to big aims. This tough person holds very solid beliefs, too. Somehow, he thinks he can shift the world in just days. He won’t bend easy when pushed on a dream or value. He shows no mercy to fakes or flops and naturally knows how to pick helpers when given a big role.  

The top thing about the Wood Dog is his sense of trust. This guy can be counted on. If he says he’ll do something, you can bet it’ll happen, right when he promised, with no slack or wait. On the flip side, it’s wiser not to push the Wood Dog into stuff he hasn’t set up for. Like most Dogs, he dislikes shocks. Worse yet, he hates being caught off balance. He chases perfection and truly believes he must run every part of his (and maybe your) life to get there.  

Since this guy struggles to handle flaws, sometimes the Wood Dog loses faith in making a perfect world and quits work life way before age says to. Instead of dealing with a half-good fix, the Dog will just step away from the mess, head to the hills, tend goats, and drop thoughts of ruling all. He’s not often bitter, just settled.  

This Dog is clever, too. He has a sharp nose for the funny, a biting wit, and a gift for crafting short sayings. Bold jokers, like Alan Arkin, are often Wood Dogs. Their laughs poke at the dullness of everyday folks. They tease normal life and know how to get us chuckling at ourselves. If they pick poems or songs to share, their lines are often sharp, packed with big thoughts on people.  

Fixers love catching tricks, too. Ralph Nader built a life pointing out flaws in things we buy. His job fits a Wood Dog perfectly. He’s free yet works with a crew. He’s asked daily to judge and spot mistakes. He’s paid to be exact and honest.  

This Dog is so tender and frail, so big-hearted and loving that the only way he might dodge a breakdown is to pour his sad energy into a mission. See Shirley Maclaine’s quests and tales of mystery. Folks called her wild, but that didn’t halt her from wagging, yapping, and leaping at people till she got a crowd. Same with Kate Millett, women’s rights fighter, or Brigitte Bardot, who, though long done with movies, spends all her days and cash bettering animal lives in France. She backs pet homes, runs TV fundraisers for the SPCA, and pops up on shows to push kind care for creatures and fight hunting. Cash? She’s got plenty. Coins don’t really grab her. She’s not in it for profit. Bardot fights for the beasts.  

Wood Dogs are tender, sturdy, and charming, but with a hint of old-school ways, they often bloom late, stay choosy, and don’t dive into big romance till their mid-twenties or even early thirties. With so much warm love to give, they feel they must be super picky about where and how they share their deep, true care.  

The Wood Dog isn’t into stuff. In work and play, he’s a real plodder and worker. Yet cash flows easy to this busy soul. He toils hard, but usually not for gain, just to ease his busy mind. He thinks he should cheer up his neighbors and lift his kin to better goals by showing how. The Wood Dog, aside from his taste for judging folks too hard and his nosy streak, is a straight and able person.`,Fire:`Don’t bet on the Fire Dog to sit quietly still and pretty by your home’s fire. All Fire Dogs are lively. Their natural bounce and simple charm add a cute, kid-like spark to a bold spirit and make us warm up and trust them fast. Energy is the big word here.  

Since this guy is so real, serious even, we can’t help but want to hear, get pulled into his kindness, and enjoy his plain talk. “Why don’t we shield the Sahara folks? They live like long ago. Their ways should be safe.” is the kind of warm, good thought we might catch from him. Fire Dog thinking is so pure and basic you almost hope it’s true. Take my Fire Dog brother Peter’s latest smart note on the battle of men and women: “Ladies hate guys flipping TV shows all the time cause gals like to stay put, and guys love to roam.” It’s a sweetly easy take. The Fire Dog is open, and he’s spirited, but his views are often simple and off track. His good points are sweetly full of gaps.  

Fire Dogs are eager fans of their own dream lands. They can turn into lone pushers for fair but kinda basic goals. Since their listeners are usually more jaded and used to the world’s risks and twists, Fire Dogs often struggle to gather followers. Despite lots of flops in sparking big cheers for their dreams, they keep going. They trust their hopes. Really, their sky-high wishes are what pull them up each day. Every morning, they wish and plot for a nicer world. The Fire Dog is a brave dreamer who will rush into the fight and push hard for what he trusts in. We’re glad to have them around—most days.  

Sometimes, before he gets far enough against the tide, the Lone Ranger Fire Dog gets down from the tough facts he faces to hit his mark. Folks he counted on let him slip. Jaded lovers keep damping his sweet dreams. Messy games have fired him up too often. The fiery spark Fire Dog hates to lose. Yet lose he often does—even before he’s beat. In this spot, he might lift his paws and (worst case) turn to booze, pills, overeating, or some bad habit to dull the sting of loss and push-away.  

Though he lets himself slide into his own slips, the Fire Dog doesn’t have much room for his pals’ faults. The Fire Dog struggles to tame his wild spirit or get his act in line to shape his own ways. So, he’s an easy mark for clingy bad habits and must keep a sharp watch on his shaky state. When he’s mad at the world, the Fire Dog stops wanting to rein himself in and might pout or pick flaws in all and everyone near. Of course, as a Dog, he still wants to stay true to his buddies and keep faith in their basic goodness. So he often sits in a mix of mixed-up feelings. This up-and-down tug in his heart stirs inner trouble and brings aches to the Fire Dog. That hurt might quickly set him up for more risky self-soothing tricks.  

Fire Dogs make awesome reviewers, fixers, problem-solvers, and guides. They can spot a slip and find the weak spot in nearly any shield. But no matter how much they try, these hot-tempered folks can’t see their own flaws straight. They might call out “chubby” or “slow” or “tipsy” folks all around, but in the mirror, their own belly or laziness or heavy sipping magically vanish. They love the style of a sharp-dressed person and want to look good too, but they’re often stumped on trends. They feel odd in fancy gear and might even scoff at cool looks, arguing loud against fads or styles.  

Sour grapes? Not quite. It’s more a “who cares” vibe, coming from the Fire Dog once again feeling left out, misread, and mad at people.  

Though they often deal with hot tempers and short blue spells, Fire Dogs never look down. They are always friendly folks whose nice ways come straight from a true wish to help and love for others.  

Fire Dogs are driven go-getters and will push harder than most to rise and stay ahead of the group. Their real foes are: their fiery zeal, their struggle to handle how they react to wrongs, and their unlucky habit to huff, puff, and grumble.  

Since the Fire Dog is basically humble, his open anger fades fast. He thinks of others and would blush to be caught making big scenes. Still, bitterness digs deep into the Fire Dog’s warm little heart and muddles his knack for letting go.  

His recall for details is amazing. He can tell you what shirt his mom wore the night she skipped tucking him in and which shelf hid the candies at the summer cabin his kin borrowed in Maine. Yet this guy’s memory, like much of his makeup, rests big on heartstrings. He remembers the day he missed a tuck-in and recalls losing sweets. But the happy times might slip away.  

Since his deep feelings make the Fire Dog sense things so strong, he often soaks up the darkest bits of any moment. By grown-up years, the hurt might grow too big, and the Fire Dog might turn into a top-notch downer and Sad Sam. He must, for sure, fight this pull to see all in shadows and should stick with calm, bright, cheery folks whose feelings match his. He should also settle in quiet green places so kind Mother Nature can always ease his tender nerves.  

Fire Dogs aren’t quick to bend. They should dodge contests, power games, or trade deals. They aren’t super skilled for smooth talk or tough deals since they wrestle with greed and half-steps.  

Good jobs for the Fire Dog lie in healing or teaching, writing, or tunes. Though the shady ups and downs of showbiz might test the Fire Dog’s core kindness, he’s got a knack for speaking deep and can shine big on stage. Behind-the-curtain roles fit this touchy soul: he’ll make a top sleuth writer or quiet detective. Law or leading, as long as the fierce Fire Dog isn’t asked to haggle deals, give him a great shot to speak out on missions and use his fixer spirit.  

In love, the Fire Dog sees himself as the top one. He’s usually not bold or bossy in romance, though. He’s a careful type and always checks for hints of drift in his sweetie. In bed and out, he loves to be teased and wooed. Once in love, he’s soft and warm. His fretful yet kid-like outside doesn’t even hint at the wild passion he can let loose when sparked right. He’s not meaning to cheat. But he’s often mighty tempted to wander. The Fire Dog is a born love bug who needs steady comfort. Tell him often he’s cared for, and he’ll stick to you like glue on a post.  

Lively, free, and true to the end, the puzzling mix of the odd bold yet shy Fire Dog promises never to dull you.`,Earth:`The Earth Dog is quiet. Like other Dogs, he might trust in missions and push for fairness, might hope for a nicer world, but the Earth Dog isn’t a hothead. He’s calmer and more easygoing than his fellow Dogs, more careful and peace-seeking. Thanks to his sharp senses, the Earth Dog is quick to feel shifts in the breeze and can’t miss even the tiniest change around him. He’s super picky. His keen instincts catch the smallest jab or snip, giving him real heart pain. When he’s stung, he walks around in a steady wince. He’s so sensitive and breakable he’d rather stay out of the glow.  

Earth Dogs are artsy and soft, made to live in the wildest green lands, circled by plants and pets. They need a shield from harsh truth and do best with gentle pats and a safe feel.  

The Earth Dog is a maker who shines alone. Again, due to his finely tuned nerves, he has to store up strength, which he does by soaking in nature, keeping clear of crowds, and dodging the rush. Look at Michael Jackson, a star and live-wire on stage for sure, but fragile, lone, and open. He cuts a song or clip and slips back to his California hideout where he stays solo, with critters, helpers, and playthings as his only pals.  

Notice, too, that the list of big-name Earth Dogs is pretty slim. Dogs touched by the Earth often stick to quiet jobs forever. They surely aim for cash wins, and they might keep low, but they aren’t timid. Instead, the Earth Dog is naturally chill and super private. He wants his close moments to stay close and his messes to stay tucked away. If a loud career risks his quiet life, an Earth Dog might pull back for good.  

Since Earth Dogs usually skip the big buzz, they can float, watching how others roll. This gives them a great launch pad to kick off a path as a writer or news hound, peacemaker, or rule-setter. I’d bet not many Earth Dogs mess with power games, as they don’t like or stand for fake talk and fluff. The Earth Dog might turn into a fine builder or style maker, room fixer, or picture-taker. He gets the fine points of people’s ways and, as he’s naturally fresh, he’ll craft works of warmth and grace. Earth Dogs make top thinkers, too. If they turn to doctoring, they’ll likely thrive in study labs.  

This hushed, deep soul is also famed for his charm. Though he might not always flash it, the Earth Dog can sweet-talk leaves off branches. He’s shy, steady, and knows how to hear. He’s kind and gets other, busier, twisty, talky folks. The Earth Dog is real bendy of mind and, for a firm Dog, pretty ready to tweak his ways to match any spot.  

Like all Dogs, the Earth Dog can snap out sharp words when you least guess. Yet thanks to his soft heart and basic goodness, his words are less mean and rough than those of his kin Dogs. If he bites at all, the Earth Dog will likely make his point softly, hiding his sharp edge by nudging your neck or patting your bare legs.  

The Earth Dog is a homebody. He puts heavy thought and care into the happiness of his own clan. Always the helper of the kid who lost his ride or skipped his tasks, this guy makes a great teacher. He naturally knows how to blend big-heartedness with a steady push. He adores kids and tends to hold tight views on birth control and choice.  

Last, the Earth Dog is a jumpy, edgy person. He’s not often cranky, but when he is, he craves quiet, alone time, and rest. His body woes often tie to his slow belly, as he’s not exactly a zippy Dog. He should be nudged to munch lots of greens and fiber, sip tons of water, and get heaps of fresh-air play. If he tends his tender nerves and minds his meals, this guy can live to a grand old age.`,Metal:`This is the Dog who aims to fix the world—at least his own patch. He’s firm-minded plus big-hearted and giving. He’s a bold, noble soul whose only point for being here is to hunt the perfect prize. Metal Dogs live for their own quests. They’re clear, eager, orderly, and strict. They don’t buy into fights or chaos, feeling calmer, kinder ways can and do win. They reach for a dream with a drive that stuns the heads of less keen, less set folks.  

Oddly, though they sometimes seem hard to reach, Metal Dogs want more than anything to be known, loved, and looked up to by their crew.  

Metal Dogs are the sort most likely to nab a top award, scale a huge peak, find a fix for a skin itch, or reshape a land’s rules. They’re not just tireless chasing a high aim; they never quit, even holding a long grudge. They’re folks of big swings whose targets are rarely small or mild. When he hunts change, the Metal Dog won’t take less than a total flip.  

Metal gives a kinda me-first streak to this Dog. He can and will do grand things. He’s open and even sweet, but he wants the gains he earns through his own sweat to carry his mark and show his trusts. He’s deeply sure his dreams are finer, his goals more right, and his ways more solid than those of less able sorts.  

Metal Dogs get the need for teamwork. Most Dogs like going solo, but the Metal Dog won’t shy from close ties, especially ones that might speed him to his aims. He’s not scared to set his will on others and can build a work squad and keep it rolling as a unit to push his cause. He’s born with top smarts and can dig up fast, bright fixes to nearly any snag he hits. He’s me-focused and not past getting a smug buzz from the praise, nods, and claps of his work mates.  

He’s often wanted as a pal, teammate, or party guest. When it’s about big stuff, the Metal Dog is almost too deep a talker. Yet he doesn’t skip light chat with Madame La Comtesse, whose main worry might be her pup’s bare patch. He’s a high-driven, truly giving soul who can be leaned on to pitch in as he only wants to do right by all.  

As a parent, the Metal Dog can shine bright. He sticks to plans and naturally knows how to steer a home well. He’s me-first without being grabby. Kids won’t just gain from his big spirit and feel a grounding pull from him, but will never doubt their own worth. The me-focused Metal Dog doesn’t question his own or aim to dim his kids’ sense of self.  

Despite a deep care for others, this guy can be sharp and even harsh on weak spots he spots in outsiders. But his high-and-mighty air fades as, with years, the Metal Dog grows softer and milder. It’s young Metal Dogs who are so loud and stern with their peers, kin, and “the rules.” School heads often clash with Metal Dog kids, as they’re bold to call out plans or dislike strict moves. Since they’re usually top learners, the head might be stumped by this outspoken kid’s stand-off ways.  

Once he’s grown, though, self-control is a trait the Metal Dog handles easy. He can dive into law or healing or take up any thinker’s path as he can focus for hours on thick, dull pages the rest of us might hate even lifting off a shelf.  

To chase his aims, wrap up his learning, and climb to ever-higher spots, this guy needs to feel safe. He might stay home till thirty or set up a place young with a pal or sweetie. His crave for home order is key. The Metal Dog is a picky but true lover and mate. He won’t let home fights or fuss pull him from his trust or goal. He wants a calm, steady life and will stop at nothing to lock it down for him and his clan.  

Sometimes the aims of this driven heart rule out a family. Take Mother Theresa, whose call to aid the poor fills her days full. She smartly picked the safety and rhythm of a faith life: home life for such a driven giver would be too tough.  

There are few “famous” showbiz Metal Dogs, who never settle for the empty cheers of cash or fame alone. Metal Dogs want to hit big marks. Some, like Jacques Cousteau, Akira Kurosawa, Andre Agassi, and Sean “Puff Daddy” Combs, might’ve used the spotlight to share their plans and dreams, but they don’t just wish for a shiny, hollow star life. They aim to touch the whole earth.  

Thanks to his pull to go all-out, the Metal Dog often wrestles with up-and-down feelings. He might be chipper and playful one tick but the next drop into a pit of gloom. He needs folks to prop him up, cheer, and praise him in tough times as he might lose trust in his aim and need a morale lift before jumping back in.  

The Metal Dog has huge wonder and must dig to the root of whatever he takes on, checking every bit till he knows the real deal. Nothing slips this guy’s wide pull of sight, making him a detail nut, always sniffing around, hunting hints, and wildly shaping order from mess. When you pair the fixing giver with the snoop, you’ll see the Metal Dog makes a standout law keeper, sleuth, crime pro, or digger.  

Though he’s usually lean and long of build, the Metal Dog loves to eat hearty. He savors top-notch eats and is often a careful cook himself. He’s set on top quality yet cares little for cash piles or wins. If coins are there, he’ll know how to spend smart, grabbing only the best goods, dining at prime spots, and wearing fine, lasting threads. If he’s got no cash, the Metal Dog can still find a way to live comfy and proper. He might mingle, but he doesn’t give a lick what folks think of him or his yard’s shape.  

The Metal Dog is often a big talker. He’ll launch into a tale, tossing in bits and side stories, yapping with pup-like glee through twists of stray points. He very often (yawn) loses his listeners in a flood of loose details. The only fix for this quirk is to clock his chats, then tell him they run too long. He loves exactness and dreads looking silly. If you note his talk on old fish lasted sixteen minutes and thirty-five ticks, he’ll catch on quick. If that still flops and your top Metal Dog won’t stop droning, grab a debate rule book and a loud stopwatch that rings when time’s up. The Metal Dog loves order. He’ll fall right into the debate bell’s trick, and you might get table chat that doesn’t stretch from starters to sweets. If that still fails, drop me a note, and I’ll try to dream up a stricter fix.`,Water:`There’s a quirky crew for you. A big batch of writers, a sprinkle of tune-makers, lots of actors and actresses, a pair of movie bosses, and even a couple of power players—bright stars, all of them!  

The watery kind of Dog is tricky to know. Not only are they cool and distant when they first meet you, but they might even growl and flash their teeth. Bold? Yep. But the Water-born Dog is also gentle. He takes charge for those he feels life has hit hard, soothing their hurt feelings and boosting their own basic worth. He’s a “softer” type, milder and gentler than his fellow Dogs, able to show and grasp even the trickiest feelings.  

The Water Dog’s power sits in his knack to break down and blend info into art. He’s got a born gift for neatly sorting the leftovers of people’s ties into a bowl and baking them into a tasty, sharp, and fun treat. He’s a Dog, so he’s naturally super tuned-in. Yet he stays grounded and tough enough to hold up under push or knocks. His task here is to teach us to giggle, weep, feel, hurt, or wake up under the pull of his deep art work.  

The Water Dog never skips a beat. He’s born with skills that let him peek around bends, grab thoughts before they’re said, or catch a noise long before it hits our dull ears. Thanks to this extra sense, in a chat, he might seem to float off short into some hidden spot.  

Funnily, if the Water Dog weren’t so skilled as an artist, we might not spot him. He shows such a far-off air he might seem uncaring. The edge we sense in him usually comes from too much caution. Since he never feels sure of others and doubts new faces, the Water Dog might act distant out of care. He’d rather skip empty chatter, so he opts to stay apart. He’s watchful, but he’s not short on self-trust. He’s just born with a quiet, held-back way.  

Weirdly, once you know the Water Dog and turn into his tight pal, he almost never stops yakking. All Dogs have great recall for tiny bits, but this one’s a geyser of small stuff. He doesn’t just tell how he met his first flame; he spills it like a deep-dive reporter might track a growing cell over a day. He kicks off, “There we were at the thirty-seventh line at fourteen minutes and thirty ticks past seven. He wore a tan vest over a bluish soft shirt. His pants were rough weave, the kind with bumpy twists, not the angled sort. The air was muggy and warm, and he was sweating at the sides. A plane flew over. One motor sounded off. Maybe it was skipping or choking…” Water Dog lead-ins are wildly detailed. It feels like he’ll never hit the end.  

As a buddy, he’s warm and friendly, helpful, and giving. He dives into all you do and never drops a speck of your smallest worry.  

The Water Dog is a fair soul whose hot wish to see right done sometimes makes him poke in. You know how it goes when a kind-hearted type steps up for you when he thinks it fits and ends up catching a heap of flak. The Water Dog often gets this unfair payback. No matter how touchy the spot, the Water Dog can’t fight the urge to jump in with friendly meddling. Water Dogs make awesome, true pals, but they’re not slick peace-weavers, deal-makers, or smooth-talkers. They flash their growl before hearing the other side’s tale.  

These pretty beings are super alluring. Early on, tons of their time goes to wooing and bedding lovers. Since they’re Dogs, they do aim to stay true. But sometimes they can’t resist flaunting their tasty charm on someone fresh. Cheating brings the Water Dog awful guilt, which feeds his born gloom. His best move is to dodge the pull of side flings since his feeling frame is pretty frail, and too much guilt can drag him to dark lows.  

The Water Dog is never mean or nasty. Though he sometimes acts out his upset with a snap, he hardly ever breaks rules or swings fists. He doesn’t hunt excuses for his rare slip-ups. He’s a straight dealer, owning his faults and making up for them by crafting fine art, doing good deeds, and always hauling his load of the group deal.  

Another standout trait here is looks. We can’t help but see it. Male Water Dogs are sharp and classy. Their lady kin are stunningly pretty, mixing a crisp face shape with a moving hint of ache. Water Dogs try to live with grace, circling themselves with fine things and savoring nature’s gifts. Water Dogs are busy, but they’re also deep thinkers. They rarely jump before they peek. They push hard and hit big wins without fake swagger or self-pats. Water Dogs will spend a long, wild youth hunting a life mate and are likely to wed folks way older than them.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"This is a potentially happy marriage. Providing the cards are played fairly, Rat and Dog can be more than satisfied in each other’s company. But be prepared for long, heated discussions sorting out political, social and financial differences of opinion. The materialistic Rat can find it difficult to reason with a generous Dog. The Dog gives money away, sometimes forgetting to save enough for the rent. Dogs can’t resist the opportunity to salvage the needy. The Dog’s stability depends on being seen as the philanthropic good guy. Rat does not agree. He’s the hoarder, ravaged by anxiety about savings, unable to understand his puppy-faced mate’s desperate need to give it all away. Disagreements abound. But as each half of this couple feels deeply passionate about the other, true harmony is possible. The Dog’s love is unconditional, offering a gentle cradle for the Rat’s frenetic soul. The happiness you find together in and out of bed will be enhanced by the arrival of scads of kids and pets whom you will nurture and raise together as a team.",Ox:"Don't expect the loyal Dog to bay at the moon out of blind love for an Ox mate. They have polarized goals. Dog’s job—pleading a case for the homeless in Alaska—is bound to take priority. And, the Ox? He will be going to bat for a major corporation and grossing 50 per cent of the winnings. These two are so different in their philosophies that mini-battles form craters in their living room carpet. Despite a gentle, loving nature, a puppy Dog, graced with lucidity, knows that this is a Dog-eat-Dog world, yet believes only in justice and equality. The Dog wants no part of the Ox’s haughty domineering and answers only to the call of the wounded. The Ox believes that charity begins at home and will beg Doggy to leave the world’s problems behind. Both are devout moralizers. But they don’t see eye to eye: the Dog argues about starving children in India, trying to sway the Ox to contribute to the noble cause; the Ox fights for justice at home, complaining that the money used on creating a shelter for the homeless last month was really meant to pay for the children’s private school. Sex between them can be fun! This is the only place where an Ox's roll over command has clout. The Dog is tickled by and admiring of the Ox’s relentlessness and brutally frank style in bed. This is just an okay marriage. No sexual fireworks or undying passion will hold these two very different people together.",Tiger:"Harmony incarnate. Dogs and Tigers just plain get along. They have common causes and common philosophies. But they are very different. The Tiger is overly optimistic, the Dog pessimistic. Each helps the other to understand these basic character differences. The Chinese call this pairing a happy alliance of muscle and heart. The Tiger has the strength to put the Dog’s ideals across to the public. The disquiet Dog keeps watch and prevents the Tiger from leaping into the wrong frays. They are, simply, a great couple. Harmony reigns right from the start. And because Dog and Tiger respect each other’s deepest convictions, mutual admiration sticks them together like super glue. In bed, the Tiger usually takes the lead, which is felicitous for the tense, nervous Dog, who often needs to be thawed out before engaging in any heavy intimacy. With time, this couple learns to blend eroticism with affection to achieve physical fulfillment. It is rare that such a marriage ends in divorce.",Rabbit:"In Chinese astrology, Cats and Dogs traditionally get on with each other. Although sexual intimacy is not the most salient point of contact here, companionship is. Everybody knows how important companionship is to animal Dogs. Cats like to be safe and well housed too. This couple’s marriage is based on profound mutual affection and respect for each other’s opinions and aesthetic choices. Both Cats and Dogs have a marked tendency to mood swings. Both are critical and easily discouraged by the realities of everyday life and its various injustices. Although Dogs are more pessimistic, Cats can be testy and crotchety when the chips are down. Their complicity will be based largely on their mutual mistrust of human nature. Their shared cynicism is their consolation for putting up with an imperfect world. Both parties are dutiful and unafraid of working hard. Money should not be an issue. Mutual participation in professional and paraprofessional projects will lend strength to their union. The Dog’s spontaneous expressions of lapping affection might get on the Cat’s taut nerves. But one thing is for sure: the Cat can depend on the Dog’s loyalty which, in the cautious Cat’s heart, counts for a lot.",Dragon:"Polarized outlooks might find happiness, providing the sex is sensational. But with the Dragon/Dog duo, this is plainly not the case. According to Chinese astrologers, few relationships are less likely to withstand the test of time. Dragon/Dog bickering and barking prevail. Dragons and Dogs are full of enthusiasm, energy and vigor. But their styles are so different as to make them near enemies. Dogs hate making a fuss over nothing. Dragons intentionally create daily scenes complete with flames, smoke and noise. Dragons deem the moralizing, pessimistic, stern Dog a downright bore. Dragons live primarily for themselves. Dogs live for others. The Dragon will wish the Dog a more obedient mate. But the freethinking Dog will never buckle under to oppression. While the Dragon boasts of successes, the Dog gloats over his or her mate’s resounding failures. I have to agree with the Chinese soothsayers. Dissonance reigns. No marriage here please.",Snake:"This partnership is lopsided. We are dealing with two disparate types of people. Dogs are pessimistic, given to depression and worry. Snakes are naturally relaxed, less anxious, and certainly less sarcastic. Sometimes the doubting Dog even mistrusts a pet Snake’s charm and will whine and snap about it, criticizing the Snake for both frivolity and an easygoing nature. Basic personality differences do not have to destroy relationships. But the Dog hates society, has few friends and stays at home a lot. Snakes are just the opposite, yet need a home to go back to after their numerous forays into the big world. Returning to the cozy Dog home after imbibing a faceful of society’s cupidity can be refreshing for the sociable Snake. Even though they snarl and threaten, Dogs always forgive, are loyal to a fault and never waver in their devotion to their loved ones. Both parties are sensitive to causes, feel strongly about combating injustice, and believe in right over might. This similarity of purpose can serve to harmonize their relationship and round out some potential hard edges. The problem is, their sexual selves are very different. Dogs are physically conventional and direct. Snakes are highly adventurous in bed and enjoy intricate sexual play. The two may not clash over this issue, but the Snake may eventually get bored, resume a natural bent for flirting and irrevocably damage the Dog’s tender-hearted soul.",Horse:"If this pair hires a nanny and a housekeeper, a laundress and a cook, they can establish a very sound love relationship. Neither these two effective, active, project-oriented people is enchanted by a career as a house drudge or nose-wiper, staying at home waiting for the other to appear. Horses are characteristically profligate with money. They gamble away and take chances others would not. This risky trait fills the disquiet Dog with fear. The Horse hates to be reminded of profligacy but the sarcastic Dog cannot keep quiet for long. Fights—yes, I said fights—ensue. As harmony reigns in their bedroom, these two usually end up being friends after vibrant lovemaking sessions wherein each lavish pleasure on the other. The Dog is giving and the Horse is loving. It’s a good sexual match. The lovemaking may be salutary, but what will ultimately hold this pair together is their deep respect for each other’s integrity. They are mutually honorable people with a refined sense of social and loyalty. Time will round off whatever sharp angles this pair encounters. A durable, solid relationship is assured.",Goat:"Not much love is lost between these two. The Dog is all moral standard and high-mindedness. Very often, the Goat’s ideals begin and end with where the next meal is coming from. Goats are on the side of the person carrying the wallet. Dogs deplore pandering. Goats know no other way of life. As a couple, unless the Dog decides, uncharacteristically, to shoulder the burden of changing a poor misunderstood Goat whom he or she believes to be a hidden genius, they will be two very different people going in opposite directions. The Dog likes things to be clear, just and fair. The Goat doesn’t even know what those terms mean. Goats are dreamers whose ephemeral plans often go up in smoke. Dogs dream too, but their dreams are founded in concrete and seek real solutions to real problems. Goats, of course, love sex and favor open relationships wherein they have full freedom. Dogs wouldn’t think of being disloyal. They may stray—but only for a minute or two. To a Dog, devotion and loyalty come first. To a Goat, blind devotion and loyalty are for fools who don’t know which side their bread is buttered. It would be too optimistic to expect harmony from this essentially unbalanced romantic equation.",Monkey:"The Dog is a blazing idealist. The Monkey lives for the opportune moment. They may well meet up and fall in love when engaged in a social struggle together. Each possesses qualities lacking in the other. Although this might make them seem perfectly matched, it takes more than dovetailing qualities to make two such impervious individualists communicate. Each is so accustomed to living on his own wavelength that they have real trouble shifting gears to make themselves understood to someone on another plane. The remedy is talk. These two nervous souls must sit and yammer for hours, days and months before they reach comprehension. The Dog will have to give up blurting nasty remarks and the Monkey must accept being tethered for at least part of the time. Although they can be guilty of it, Dogs don’t take kindly to philandering. But Monkeys like sexual freedom. Monkey seems carefree and Dog laughably frustrated. Being of basic good intention, if they wish to stay together, this pair can work out a harmonious sex life together. This relationship’s harmony is possible but will not be won without effort. Unless the union is inevitable, I advise imagining it can work forever.",Rooster:"Incompatibility reigns supreme in this couple. Dogs and Roosters are equally flinty and raw-nerved. Dogs are forever blurting criticism and bruising the egos of those around them. Roosters are cocky but deeply unsure of themselves. One yelp from the Dog’s storehouse of biting blatancies can put the Rooster under for days, depress him and undo his hard-earned image. Do these people fight? They never stop. Backbiting, carping, bickering over details. They don’t agree on anything. Dogs are classically left wing, kindly and trustworthy. Roosters are born conservatives who believe in the system, adhere to society’s basic tenets and cleave to traditional ways. This couple’s home life is a constant push-me pull-you of political unrest. Dog wants revolution. Rooster devoutly wishes for status quo. Dog thinks mismatched china and a pallet on the floor will do nicely. Rooster wants Spode or Limoges set with crystal grasses on an heirloom table. Dog wants to spend money on causes. Rooster wants to keep his money in the bank. Rooster demands more and varied sex than Dog has to give. Rooster needs to puff up his ego and preen his feathers. Dog couldn’t care less what he looks like in bed. He feels sex rather than performing it. Besides, Dogs are slightly puritanical. They don’t believe one should overindulge in pleasure. Leave the Rooster/Dog love relationship alone.",Dog:"Seriousness and anxiety could cloud the union darkly between two Dogs who want to live together as a team. There exist, of course, areas of mutual understanding regarding causes and social ills, justice and humanitarian issues. But their abrasive Dog personalities and incessant caustic remarks could make pain the order of the day. There is however much reciprocity here. There are, after all, many breeds of Dog. One type of Dog will always help the other with everything from grocery shopping to projects. There are few, if any, artificial barriers about who is male or female and which tasks befit either. Both have respect for the other’s time and an understanding of his partner’s desire to be effective in the world. Trouble crops up in this relationship because of an age-old enemy—boredom. Both Dogs will be hyper-puritanical, chronically anxious, guarded, skeptical, cynical, critical and lacking in joy and lightheartedness. Life around the Dog house could be Gloomy Gus City. Stodgy moralities will be the rule rather than the exception. Self-righteousness will be knee-deep. But… if one Dog happens to be a Labrador and the other a Doberman—maybe a certain barking order will be established and the two Dogs can make a go of it. There is not much natural chemistry between Dog born people, so the act of love will be healthful but unimaginative. Intimacy frightens Dogs; they mistrust closeness. A second Dog sniffing behind them for a quick pop in the grass is about as much this couple can expect to have in bed.",Pig:"Intimacy between Dog and Pig people promises great enduring love, respect and passion. The Dog and Pig are complementary in thought and feeling. They both believe in the basic good of humankind. They both love the countryside and adhere to sanity as a fine way to live. Mind you, there are some basic differences to contend with: Pigs love opulence while Dogs couldn’t care less about luxury. Pigs tend to be conservative; Dogs are liberal. Pigs are sensualists—there’s nothing they love better than a good dirty story—while Dogs are puritanically-inclined. But all these differences are worked out between the Dog and Pig because they are each willing to respect and even admire the other for their individual tastes and preferences. Dog loves the cozy security Pig provides and Pig sees Dog’s politically active friends as perfect guests. He feeds them to death. Pig may at first be flummoxed by the Dog’s seeming sexual indifference. But Pigs have clever (sometimes devious) ways of getting people’s attention, and will always find a way to their Doggie’s heart. Pigs are infinitely patient. They know how to bide their time and cajole until they get what they want and need out of their cranky, but basically sweet-tempered Dog partner. Providing they husband and promote their mutual talent for goodwill, this pair will be blissfully content for a very long time."},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Wood",prediction:"This year, the philosophical Snake will make you anxious. The Snake’s tendency to speak in riddles will try your patience, and his love of luxury will strike you as downright wasteful. Dog years are frugal; Snake years are not. You may feel a bit out of place amid all the elegance and high-mindedness. You are likely to become embroiled in disputes with family or colleagues this year. Try to be less critical. Your frankness is not always appreciated, especially by the sensitive Snake. My advice? Spend more time alone this year. Take up a new hobby or learn a new language. This is a good time for personal growth. Travel is not particularly favored, so stick close to home and focus on self-improvement. Your love life may be a bit tumultuous. Be wary of making any long-term commitments. Wait until next year, when the atmosphere is more favorable for Dogs."},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Fire",prediction:"The Horse is your ally. This year will be a dynamic one, full of activity and progress. You will feel energized and motivated. It’s an excellent time for new ventures, career changes, or moving to a new home. The Horse’s practicality and your sense of justice make a powerful combination. Together, you can accomplish great things. However, the Horse’s independent nature means you won’t have to worry about being smothered. You will both respect each other’s need for space. Financially, this is a promising year, but be cautious of the Horse’s tendency to take risks. Your conservative nature can provide a good balance. Romantically, it’s a passionate time. If you’re single, you may meet someone who shares your ideals. If you’re in a relationship, it will be a period of renewed excitement and deep connection."},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Fire",prediction:"This will be a challenging year for you. The Goat’s whimsical, artistic nature clashes with your down-to-earth practicality. You may find the general atmosphere of the Goat year to be frivolous and unproductive. You believe in hard work and tangible results; the Goat believes in inspiration and dreams. This fundamental difference will cause friction. You may feel that no one is taking things seriously, and your attempts to instill order will be met with resistance. It’s best to avoid major conflicts. Focus on your own projects and don’t try to change the world—or the Goat. Your love life may also feel a bit unstable. The Goat is fickle and requires constant admiration, which you may find exhausting. Patience is key. If you can tolerate the Goat’s capriciousness, you’ll get through the year unscathed. It’s a good time for introspection and planning for the future."},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Earth",prediction:"The Monkey’s cleverness will both fascinate and irritate you. While you admire the Monkey’s ability to solve complex problems, you’ll be wary of its cunning and sometimes deceptive tactics. This is a year of intellectual stimulation. You may find yourself engaged in lively debates and strategic planning. However, the Monkey’s love of games and tricks can make you feel insecure. You prefer honesty and straightforwardness. To navigate this year successfully, you must rely on your strong moral compass. Don’t get drawn into the Monkey’s schemes. Professionally, it’s a good time for collaboration, as long as you can keep the Monkey focused on the task at hand. Romantically, it’s a playful period. The Monkey’s humor can be a refreshing change, but its lack of seriousness may frustrate you in the long run. Keep your wits about you, and you’ll find this year to be both challenging and rewarding."},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Earth",prediction:"This year is fraught with conflict. The Rooster’s vanity and your idealism are a recipe for disaster. You will find the Rooster’s need for constant praise and attention grating, and the Rooster will be deeply wounded by your sharp criticisms. Expect arguments over everything from politics to decorating. You believe in substance; the Rooster believes in style. This is a fundamental clash that will be difficult to resolve. Financially, it’s a tense time. The Rooster is extravagant, while you are frugal. Money will be a constant source of disagreement. In your professional life, you may find yourself at odds with superiors who value appearance over performance. It’s a frustrating period, and you’ll need to draw on all your reserves of patience. Your love life will be equally stormy. The Rooster’s possessiveness will make you feel trapped, and your need for independence will be perceived as rejection. It’s best to keep your distance and avoid making any major decisions this year."},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Metal",prediction:"This is your year to shine, but it’s also a time of great responsibility. You will feel a strong urge to fight for justice and right the wrongs of the world. Your leadership skills will be in high demand. However, be wary of becoming too self-righteous. Two Dogs together can create an echo chamber of pessimism and anxiety. Surround yourself with optimistic people who can provide balance. Professionally, you will excel in roles that allow you to advocate for others—law, social work, or politics. Financially, it’s a stable year, but your generosity may be tested. Don’t let your ideals lead you to financial ruin. Romantically, if you’re with another Dog, you’ll find deep companionship and understanding. However, the lack of lightheartedness can become oppressive. Make a conscious effort to have fun and enjoy life’s simple pleasures. This is a year for making a difference, but don’t forget to take care of yourself."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Metal",prediction:"This is a harmonious and prosperous year for you. The Pig’s good nature and your loyalty create a wonderful synergy. You will feel supported and appreciated, which will allow you to thrive. The Pig’s love of comfort and your practical nature will lead to a beautiful and secure home life. It’s an excellent year for family and friendships. Professionally, you will find success through collaboration. The Pig’s luck with money and your hard work will lead to financial gains. It’s a good time to invest, especially in property. Romantically, this is a blissful period. The Pig’s sensuality will help you to relax and open up emotionally. Your devotion will be deeply appreciated. This is a time of peace, love, and contentment. Enjoy it."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Water",prediction:"Though you and the Rat can find common ground, this year will be a test of your patience. The Rat’s ambition and desire for power will clash with your idealism. You may find yourself in situations where you have to compromise your principles for the sake of progress. This will be difficult for you. Financially, the Rat’s acquisitiveness can lead to risky ventures. Your cautious nature will be a valuable asset in preventing disaster. It’s a year for careful planning and avoiding impulse buys. Professionally, you may feel that your hard work is not being recognized, as the Rat takes credit for group efforts. Stay true to your values and don’t get discouraged. In your love life, the Rat’s need for excitement can be draining. You crave stability, while the Rat seeks novelty. Communication is key to navigating these differences. It’s a year of challenges, but also of growth."},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Water",prediction:"You will feel frustrated and constrained by the Ox’s rigid and authoritarian nature. Your desire for justice and fairness will be met with the Ox’s unyielding adherence to tradition and rules. This is a year of ideological conflict. You will want to fight for the underdog, while the Ox will defend the status quo. Professionally, you may find yourself in a stifling environment where creativity and independent thought are discouraged. It’s a time to lie low and avoid confrontation. Financially, the Ox’s conservatism means it’s not a year for growth, but it is a time of stability. Don’t expect any windfalls, but you won’t face any major losses either. Your love life will feel dull. The Ox’s lack of romanticism and your need for emotional connection will create a distance between you. This is a year for patience and perseverance. Endure it, and better times will come."},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Wood",prediction:"This is a year of great synergy and mutual respect. The Tiger’s courage and your loyalty make for a powerful alliance. You will be inspired by the Tiger’s optimism and energy, and the Tiger will be grounded by your practicality and wisdom. Together, you can achieve great things. Professionally, it’s a time for bold moves and new ventures. Your combined strengths will lead to success. Financially, it’s a prosperous year, as long as you can temper the Tiger’s impulsive spending habits. Romantically, it’s a passionate and fulfilling time. You will find a deep connection with your partner, based on shared ideals and mutual admiration. This is a year of action, adventure, and achievement. Embrace it with open arms."},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Wood",prediction:"This is a year for quiet companionship and mutual support. The Rabbit’s gentle nature will soothe your often-anxious soul. You will find comfort in a peaceful and harmonious environment. Professionally, it’s a good time for working behind the scenes. Your loyalty and diligence will be appreciated, even if you’re not in the spotlight. Financially, it’s a stable year. The Rabbit’s prudence and your own caution will ensure you have a secure nest egg. Romantically, you will enjoy a deep and affectionate bond with your partner. It’s a time for quiet evenings at home and for enjoying each other’s company. This is a year for finding peace and contentment in a stable and loving environment."},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Fire",prediction:"You will find the Dragon’s flamboyance and ego a bit much to take this year. Your down-to-earth nature will clash with the Dragon’s need for constant adoration and spectacle. It’s a year of potential conflict. Professionally, you may find yourself at odds with a powerful and charismatic leader. Don’t be afraid to speak your mind, but do so with tact and diplomacy. Financially, the Dragon’s extravagance will make you nervous. Stick to your own budget and don’t be tempted by risky schemes. In your love life, the Dragon’s passion can be exciting, but its self-centeredness can be hurtful. This is a year for standing your ground and for staying true to your own values, even in the face of overwhelming pressure."}}},u={introduction:`Noble Pig,
You are a pattern of honesty, goodness, patience, and respect.
You wish to do all things well.
You’ve got a good eye for beauty and a knack for truth.
We ask your plain sense tips and like your friendly presence.
You love the rural life.
Simple pleasures and rude jests make you giggle hard.
Fine meals are well-known to your taste too.
Admit it, Piglet, you’re a true lover of life’s joys.
Yet, you are much too helpful.
Folks exploit your soft ways.
Then, when you’ve tired yourself by doing too much, you burst into storms, outbursts, wild anger.
We all dash away when you’re mad, returning only when you are settled in your best plush chair, your eyes fixed on a costly art book, chewing noisily while eating a grand box of foreign chocolates.
Whew!

You Pig folks often grow wealthy.
You can’t avoid it.
You’re wild about splendor.
Silks, handmade silver, and pure gold candlesticks suit your rich likes.
In love matters, you match well with fiery Dragons, artsy Goats, and stylish, rural Cats.
No matter what, don’t let a sleek Snake sneak into your soul.
Keep away from handy Roosters, too.
Calmness arrives once you have mastered saying NO, firm and bold.
Then, often after mid-years, your bursts of fury will lessen, and life will turn into a true treat.
Try, for your own good protection, to use your choice to turn down helping others.
Just say no.
And recall … practice brings skill.`,elements:{Wood:`Honest and kind, this Pig is the most warm-hearted and caring of all.
He is gentle-natured and helpful, keen to please and sharing of his time and work for anything he trusts.
He seldom argues with folks, as he is patient with their quirks and open to their flaws.

Friendship with a Wood Pig offers one constant comfort.
His most obvious trait is kindness.
Wood Pigs sense the hurt of others more than their own.
If you know a Wood Pig in your days, you will clearly see the flow of care: “Got a cold?” “How I wish I could take it for you.” “You seem weary. Should I fetch you some soup?”, etc . . .
And he acts on your wants.
Run out of firewood? He’ll deliver a load of his own logs to ensure you stay warm.
Pressed for time? He’ll offer to press your clothes so you can focus on what else you must do.
Feeling low? He’ll share laughs and make you a big hearty stew to lift your spirits.
The Wood Pig is a timeless good soul, faithful and loving too.

Wood Pigs are imaginative and tied to culture.
They long for art and tunes, love reading tales and staying current with news.
Still, these polished folks have a country edge and nearly always opt to dwell far from the noisy throng (and if they don’t, they ought to).
Wood Pigs are tender of heart, and don’t do well when circled by crowds of loud people, machines, or bustle, or if they must face busy daily town life.
Without a peaceful country setting, the Wood Pig turns moody and hard to manage, grumbling and snapping at others, taking calm pills or drinking just to keep steady.
Kids, critters, and fields match the fussy Wood Pig perfectly well.

There is gloom in the Wood Pig’s makeup, too.
He often feels down.
But his sadness is not deep or lasting.
When he is upset by the actions of someone he cares for, the Wood Pig may show a glum look for a few days.
His thought is: “I figured you were greater than most of the world, but now I’m unsure.”
But it doesn’t stay long.
He is not one to cling to spite or hunt payback.

The Wood Pig is often held back by his shyness.
He has a terribly tough time letting others know him and is often stalled in his love life, because he dares show no hint of romantic interest or welcome.
This Pig may build courage, but he will need support and plenty of tries.
Don’t feel let down if he never transforms into a chatty star.
He is born timid, quiet, and guarded.
He would never shun others nor is he mean to them, but the Wood Pig will not step up to a stranger and begin an easy chat.
As he is privately caught up with what others think of him, he aims to stay unnoticed.
He is known for knowing how to mind his own affairs and steer clear of others’.
The Wood Pig may live beside a crook’s lair but he will never report him.
He can see a bank heist and act both to himself and all that he didn’t.
This way might nearly be seen to aid wrong, but it is only that the Wood Pig feels driven to be patient and gentle.
Besides, he’s so caring as to think that those poor thieves likely needed the cash.

The Wood Pig is first, last, and ever a home keeper and builder.
If you’re seeking your Wood Pig friend, you will almost always spot him at home, tinkering around, digging, weeding, and sowing in his yard.
Or he might be sharing tales with his kids or aiding them with school tasks.
Sometimes he’s fixing old treasures or is just busy bettering his space.
For someone who loves to roam and seeks a steady partner by the hearth, this soul is the top choice.
A note of caution to the Wood Pig - no matter how charming you find them, don’t wed a Snake.
Snakes love to curl around the Wood Pig’s mild nature and slowly squash him flat.`,Fire:`This Pig is the lively sort.
He’s a mix of home lover and changer, always putting himself at the head of efforts for the good of people.
He’ll do anything: hold signs, sign papers, gather funds, or even use some of his own wealth for what he trusts in.
Fairness for all is his aim.
The Fire Pig boldly waves his thoughts and dreams in a push to move forward against wrongs that he cannot stand.

In the same way, the Fire Pig often acts as helper to artistic folks, handing out cash for an artist’s living, urging him to craft free from the ups and downs of making a wage.
He doesn’t try to win anything himself but gives gladly for the good of art.
As he is a bit trusting and a very agreeable Pig, he is often tricked by dishonest “arty” types who grab his money and dash off to far seas to start a tavern.
When these sad events happen, the Fire Pig’s dismay is deep and mournful.
He cannot fathom anyone could be so selfish and sneaky, but such troubles do not teach the Fire Pig much about caution.
No matter how often he is fooled, he firmly keeps searching for somebody fresh to whom he might lend a hand.

The Fire Pig is strongly set in his views.
If he knows that the lady offering herself as hopeful for head of the group once said she didn’t like outsiders, he feels that this rules her out for the role.
Little we say can shift him from his beliefs.
No facts against it are enough.
The Fire Pig trusts what he trusts.
I think his firmness comes from a great need for safety.
He feels easy in his solid faith.
So he sticks with it.
It feels surer that way.

Clever Fire Pigs feel that they are stubbornly fixed, and unwilling to let much shift in their habits.
Some even outright reject bending.
They must, though, recall that while holding stiff ideas as pure truth feels nice to them and gives them a firm grip on something right, the picture that this mental block casts outward is silly.
Everyone knows that the truly safe thinker is he who can take new ideas, mix them up, blend and pair them until they form a fresh outcome.
Learning how to join the new with the old is true smarts indeed.
If Fire Pigs do not learn to grow their stiff views into bendy thoughts, they stall and cannot hope to dream up any brand new ideas.

To fix their stubbornness, Fire Pigs are urged to read more broadly, study papers whose outlooks differ from their own, and journey to strange lands where ways are done unlike what they have always known.
They should aim to befriend folks of varied political and cultural views and truly try to grasp—and even connect with—them.

With all of his backward thinking, the Fire Pig is still a keen dreamer.
He trusts deeply in a brighter future and truly wishes to work toward political and good progress, to help build friendship among folks.
He dreams hopefully of the fall of harsh rulers, the end of borders, the stop of hate.
In some ways, he is a perfect-world thinker.

As an outcome, the Fire Pig throws himself into grand (and often misled) plans and tasks that he trusts will push out the bad and bring in the good.
In true life, there are no such clear lines, and our Fire Pig is often a let-down Pig.
If he doesn’t step back and check, get a hold on his overblown dreams and calm his hopes of a better place, he will grow moody and even dislike people in old age.

Fire Pigs are hugely imaginative.
But they don’t usually just want success for themselves.
They don’t mind being the strength behind the seat or aiding their chosen star in his or her rise to power and riches.
The Fire Pig is a natural aid, supporter, and carer.
He will go to any stretch to see his mate or close pal win.
He yearns to glow in the shared shine of his own picked champ.
The Fire Pig loves the thrill of having smoothed his wife’s shirt the day she went in and nabbed that big rise.
Fire Pigs are givers of love, born carers.
They make top-notch parents and steady spouses.

But can they ever grumble!
Fire Pigs are often cranky and touchy.
Sometimes, they truly feel wronged because they chose to devote themselves to the goal of someone they love who fails them.
When they see just how much of their time and work it took to lift the other person, they may moan.
Their grumbles can be about all from “Nobody picks up stuff around here anymore” to “When I recall how great I was as a cloth maker, what I left when I came to stay with you…”
They huff and mutter, sulk and chuckle, and warn to leave for good.
At times, Fire Pigs do go.
But they never go for good.
Why? Because they are such truly good-hearted, sweet, giving souls.
Bottom line? Fire Pigs so badly want to trust that they rarely quit on anybody.`,Earth:`Strength, Grit, and Range are the three words I like to use to picture Earth Pigs.
This Pig is set on living the country life and will try to keep clear of towns.
He is a pure rural soul whose bold remarks can be more than sharp.
In an effort to cheer his guests.
It is not rare for an “earthy” Earth Pig to show fairly rough ways, tell a bold joke, and point to some of the lower sides of life.
I wouldn’t go so far as to call the Earth Pig a full country bumpkin, as he is both rural and at once drawn to the top forms of class.
But, oh well.
I’ll chance it and say that this certain Pig is a bit of a simpleton.

The Earth Pig is active, greatly imaginative, and bears the load of his creations on his own back, taking full charge for their use.
He’s fearless of judgment and will go the whole way to finish a task.
Often, he is linked to art.
He may be a painter or teller, a keeper or a gatherer of fine art.
His aims are rarely more daring than the feel and fullness of creative sharing.
He finds joy out of the act of crafting lovely things from his mind.
Money comes easy to The Earth Pig.
He is always gaining windfalls - wedding wealth, getting a sudden gift, or landing the best-paying deals.
He is lucky and doesn’t have to do much clever moves to secure his living.

This soul is slow to give up his born purity.
If he had his pick, the Earth Pig would live in a state of pure grace where good things never fail, where man is always kind to his peers, and where the whiff of wrong is unknown.
As he thinks better in clear settings, he has a habit to hide away for work aims in far-off retreats where the air is fresh.
Not only does the Earth Pig not want his life spoiled by the ills of a stained or packed life, but he knows how open he is to being tricked by less honest folks.
Rather than taking big risks, the wise Earth Pig dodges the fast crowd, the rich, and the spoiled, staying near to the earth and its healing ways.

The Earth part adds an even stronger pull for custom and closeness to the past than with other Pigs.
Earth Pigs are often tied to jobs dealing with old times, human studies, digging, history, or even people’s past.
Or they may choose to start antique shops or halls where aged treasures are seen or sold.
But whatever they pick to do, it is often tightly linked both to custom and beauty.

Wavering is the Earth Pig’s worst fault.
He is easily pulled and often muddled about which path he should take.
He has trouble settling his mind.
His great readiness to be bendy, open, and willing forms a risk to his look among his mates.
Folks always wonder what on earth the mixed-up Earth Pig is mulling, and very often, the last one to know is the Earth Pig himself.
It is no good nudging him, trying to aid him settle his mind, as he is firm about taking tips and hates meddling from others.
If you nudge too much, he’ll burst into one of his giant rages— and you’ll be floored.`,Metal:`Metal gifts the Pig with a big dose of toughness and staying power.
Here is a soul born with huge personal truth, who always aims to better his own past efforts.
If, at first, he does not win, the Metal Pig will always try once more.
He is honest and direct and real.

The worst wrong you could do against a Metal Pig would be to blame him of a sly deed, suspect him of trickery, or doubt his reasons.
Blame, to the Metal Pig, is nearly as bad as being found guilty.
Keeping his reliable, good-folk image among his fans keeps the Metal Pig steady.

He is fair too, the most steady of Pigs, flexible and easy to bargain with.
But, oddly, when pushed to the end of his calm, the Metal Pig can grow very firm and halt further deals.
Yet, he never lets himself too much freedom and rarely, if ever, chases any odd wish to stray outside the rules in the coloring book of life.

Metal Pigs do not like the clash of debate.
They favor quiet over fight.
Polite talk fits their nature, as does thoughtful chat and/or pure culture sharing.
If they find themselves facing a likely spat, rather than being drawn to voice a bold view and maybe stirring their listeners, Metal Pigs usually opt to step back and shift the topic.

They are always telling cheeky jokes or doing funny acts for their pals.
Whatever it takes, the Metal Pig keeps foes few by purposely keeping his crowd pleased with his tricks or simply chatting lightly or talking about the sun.

Deep ideas barely catch the Metal Pig at all.
He is not drawn to vague thinking.
Faith tires him, and soul matters push him off.
He’s even a bit leery of big thoughts.
He’d usually rather fade than see an odd healer.
And, no need to say, Metal Pigs hate the very being of star signs and its kin studies.

This soul is not wildly driven—not in the world-topping sense.
He’s even a tad timid.
He can be urged and poked into the spotlight, but if and when he reaches fame or praise, it is usually the outcome of someone pushing him until he slowly lets his quiet charms join the public view.`,Water:`Water brings soothing calm and warmth to this Pig.
He is a steady kind who doesn’t get swept away by his own quick whims.
In a tight spot, he keeps his calm and never fails to repay the love of those who claim to care for him and stay true to his values.
This Pig is a darling, a firm but peaceful soul who spends good time offstage but does not always want to leave the back room to join the newest talk show.
He’s fairly shy and low-key, a thinker with fine ways and a vast stock of self-control.

The Water Pig doesn’t seek power or rule over others.
He would rather be seen as a peacemaker than a ruler or top boss.
Again, as with other Pigs, his gifts lie in his heartfelt closeness to art and its cultural forms.
He loves to craft and even to flaunt the outcomes.
But the Water Pig rarely reaches for anything more greedy than perfection in his work.
Using his gifts for selfish gain feels nearly wrong to the goodness-aware Water Pig.

The Water Pig must be circled by folks.
Though at work he can act alone and churn out grand amounts of tough tasks, at the day’s end, this Pig wants friends—someone to chat with, laugh with, share supper, and swap thoughts with.
He’s not overly friendly in the bigger sense, choosing to stay unknown or, at least, out of the glow.
Yet he deeply craves warmth, a kin-like feel, a glad, bright setting in which to feel a bond of friendship.

The Water Pig is a born maker.
He often takes on building tasks where he plans and remolds.
He thrives on tearing down walls, crafting big open areas where his gathers of art pieces and old master works can best be enjoyed.

He is not loud in his shows of love or care.
The Water Pig is deep, simple, and dreamy.
He rarely pours out or yells.
Feelings, he thinks, are meant to be held, managed gently, and shown nicely.
His great loves are usually body joys.
The Water Pig cherishes fun moments and places closeness high on the list of joys to seek.
Good food comes next.
Water Pigs are quite frail and often face huge tummy woes from overdoing tasty treats.
Something about the sight of a full table, packed with good eats and drinks, breaks the Water Pig’s will to steer clear of heavy feasts.
He should watch out for health risks.

Lastly, this Pig is thrifty.
Unlike other Pigs who tend to splash and hoard by turns, this Pig saves his cash.
He likes safety and knows how to live well - even richly - on a tight plan.
The Chinese often say that because the Water Pig year rolls around at the end of the sixty-year loop, folks of that year have like traits to the first sign of the new loop, which is the Rat, who is a true pro at saving and guarding his stash.
Perhaps a bit of his thrift rubs off on his star-sign neighbor, the sweet, kind, pure-hearted Water Pig.`},compatibilities:{Rat:"Indeed, these two make marvelous mates. In China, the Pig symbolizes affluence, which alone keeps a disquiet Rat from tooth-grinding. The practical Pig mellows the fretful Rat, and is lucky with money. Money alone paints a full time grin on the face of the satisfied Rat. But the Pig’s gentle nature counts for a lot too. They share a common love for food, take holidays in France and Italy to taste the glories of old-world cuisine. The restive Rat, now safe in the peaceable Pig’s presence, finally lets go, surrendering worry beads and tranquilizers for a glamorous wallow in luxury. Despite this affluent couple’s bent for squandering, they are both potential hoarders. Having a robust savings to depend on will make the jolly Rat jollier. Overly kind and sensitive, the Pig is not always as clever as the Rat in business dealings. The circumspect Rat’s counsel is welcome here. This gregarious and delightful couple is on every host’s A-list. Genuine love marks this union. You can expect piglets to abound. This pair delights in lovemaking. The sensual Pig not only tickles the lusty Rat’s erogenous zones, but emotional and financial security allow the Rat to surrender fully in bed – where it counts!",Ox:"Indeed, these two get along famously. The good-natured Pig is so malleable that the Ox will end up thinking he really is boss. Let’s say that at the summit of a beautiful hill in the mountains of some exquisite location, the Ox and the Pig own a home. This home is so well cared-for that it sparkles. Pig loves to cook, and doesn’t mind cleaning up after dinner. Before bedtime, the careful Ox turns off all the lights and puts out the garbage and the cat. Then this cuddly combo springs into bed. It’s ideal. They are well matched. Early morning, they wake to the sound of the birds, who set a harmonious tone for the day. Of course, the birds are fed daily by the regimented Ox, who keeps this ship running on the tightest of schedules. But it’s the Pig who buys the birdseed. Piggies love animals, adore country life and are lavishly generous. Sex between these two country folk is lusty and satisfying. The Ox is a bit square and rude at first, but the Pig’s rich sensuality soon takes over, and they enjoy making a lovely, languorous lifetime of love.",Tiger:"The basic characters here are vastly different. Pigs are scrupulous and peace-loving. Tigers strategize every move and carry banners for their own noisy causes. Yet with the proper amount of gentle understanding from Piggy and the sort of generous reasonableness for which Tigers are famous, the pair can make a real go of marriage. The Pig admires the Tiger’s punchy gall and the Tiger respects the Pig’s guilelessness and purity of spirit. Pigs are mostly even-tempered and good-natured, while Tigers are pathologically changeable. Pigs find Tigers too mobile but they don’t mind staying at home and holding the fort while Tiger rushes about being self-important. Instead of clashing, these two complement one another. Their physical relationship is full of tenderness and mutual understanding. The Pig is sensual, adores pleasure and is lavishly generous. Tigers need a lot of affection and cherish the sort of warmth and homeliness the Pig offers their restless nature. Steamy cuddling sessions abound in the Pig/Tiger household.",Rabbit:"Here’s a pair tailor-made for successfully carving out a bucolic country life together. Both creatures love nature and thrive in rural, bourgeois opulence. They both covet ownership of the finer things in life. With time, the Cat/Pig couple can expect to lead a civilized, charming life together in peace and tenderness, without suffering want or lack of mutual respect. The Cat, of course, has an artistic side, and will be the one to maintain decorum, keep neat flowerbeds and establish house rules. The Pig, an earthier character given to rustic manners and relaxed—even sloppy—habits, will appreciate the Cat’s attempt at forging a pristine existence for them. These people are both malleable enough to accept the other’s shortcomings and honor their partner’s needs. Piggy is lavishly sexual. Kitty is not. Piggy is rampantly erotic. Kitty is borderline prudish. At first, there may be some misunderstanding in this area, but in the long run, the Pig’s sensuality and open-mindedness about sex will break down the Cat’s hesitancy, and a good old sexual entente can be established for life.",Dragon:"Most Dragon/Pig marriages last forever. The two have just enough in common and just enough differences to keep them both interested. The Pig is compliant and easygoing, always gives the benefit of the doubt to the other fellow and admires gutsiness and audacity in a mate. The Dragon needs an ally, a helpmate, a shoulder to cry on and someone nice to boss around—preferably someone who forgives easily. The Pig amply fills the bill. Both characters adore opulence—the more gilt sconces they can stick on the walls of their châteaux, the happier they will be. The Pig applauds Dragon’s successes and turns a blind eye to all chicanery. In turn, Dragon protects and admires the Pig’s scrupulousness. In short, Pig helps Dragon maintain the shine on an overactive ego. Dragon adores being put on a permanent pedestal and makes it clear that Pig’s homemaking talents are all he or she has ever dreamed. The sex is good. The Pig cleaves to sensuality and the Dragon just plain loves sex—lots of it. Piggy wants romance so Dragon must temper crudity and learn a thing or two about the value of hearts and flowers.",Snake:"The Pig’s nemesis. Chinese sages always advise against this relationship. They say that the rapacious Snake will eventually strangle the unsuspecting Pig. It’s interesting because Pigs are earthy, warm-hearted pushovers for beauty and cultural savoir-faire. So inevitably, the first gorgeous, sex-loving Snake to come along knocks the Pig for a loop. He cannot resist. Superficially, the luxury-loving Pig has much to recommend to a Snake lover. Pigs are scrupulous and mostly honest. They usually know how to make lots of money, which the Snake loves to lavish on their joint lifestyle. They both adore things traditional like antiques and vintage wines and castles in Spain. The problem here revolves around the weakness these share. Neither the Snake nor the Pig is a world-record decision maker: Pig changes his or her mind as readily as Snake changes his or her outfit. Snake procrastinates. Pig wallows and wonders. They are sexually compatible to a fault, but little is accomplished in life by lying about twisted up in each other’s limbs. Pigs don’t much care about appearances, making rude noises and smacking their lips when they eat. Eventually, a fastidious Snake grows critical of a Pig’s sloppy habits. Snake’s jibes bring out the worst in Piggy, who whimpers, which only makes the Snake more impatient and even cruel. The gracious Pig can never please the demanding Snake enough. He finally just withers sadly away and leaves all his money to the voracious beauty he couldn’t resist marrying.",Horse:"Poor Piggy! Horses are notoriously headstrong and willful. The Pig simply cannot say “no” to the Horse’s winning ways. And even though a right-thinking Horsey knows better than to walk all over an acquiescent mate, he cannot help himself. Because they are often very striking, Horses attract Pigs in droves. In their turn, Pigs win the hearts of Horses because they are so willing, generous and tantalizingly compliant. Sexually, these two are well matched. The Horse finds the Pig’s overt sensuality liberating. Pigs like the forceful side of Horse’s sexual nature and are turned on by his handsome appearance. Pigs attract money. Horses work hard and know how to make money, but often gamble it away. The Pig is a natural homebuilder and nurturer. The Horse is an outside person. They complement each other. Providing the Pig can endure the Horse’s frequent absences and accept the outgoing side of his personality, this couple can create a sound basis for a felicitous and prosperous family.",Goat:"In this pairing we find one of the happiest possible combinations. The atmosphere between Goat and Pig is mellow and smooth. They may have minor differences of opinion over small things, like taste in furniture or which sort of friends to frequent most, but the Goat likes the security he finds with Piggy and Piggy, in turn, enjoys the creative nuttiness of the charming Goat. Pig is lucky in money matters so he can support the gentle Goat, allow him free rein to dream, aimlessly inventing and reinventing his daily life. Pigs have endless patience and seem to be composed of goodwill and indulgence for the capricious Goat mate. Goat could not be better matched where emotional stability is concerned. The Pig usually stays in the country, away from madding city life, where the Goat can safely cavort, unhindered, in fertile fields. The sexual side of this affair is also enviably harmonious. The parties have similar sensitivities. Noble Piggy will undoubtedly be jealous of the Goat’s incessant dalliances and disapprove of his unfortunate tendency to try to take up with almost every attractive person who comes to call (the flirtatious Goat lacks tact). But, never mind. Once Piggy’s pain has passed, the darling Goat will be forgiven and both will return to their familiar devil-may-care, bucolic existence.",Monkey:"Piggy! The Pig must treat this relationship with less blind indulgence for the opposite party. Monkeys can be ruthless when necessary. The Pig’s naïveté is no help when it comes to dealing with a beloved, yet sometimes unscrupulous, Monkey. Unlike the Snake, whose intentions in the Pig’s regard are plainly lethal, the Monkey means no harm. Pigs’ and Monkeys’ tender hearts are mightily compatible—but their thinking processes are worlds apart. The Pig must adapt to the Monkey’s ways or the couple is doomed. As Pigs are very malleable, adaptation is not an unreasonable demand. But Piggy must be careful not to lose his or her purest ideals in Monkey’s constantly expanding bag of tricks. Pigs live by intuition. Monkeys cleave to logic. If they can teach their mutual talents to cooperate, it will assist their union’s progress. If not, there will be major rows. An angry Monkey is a hopping mad mini-volcano who forgets about it two minutes after the eruption. A mad Pig is fearsome, relentless, dangerous and vengeful. Monkey should accept and enjoy Pig’s smothering and homely charms. And Pig should try to see how innocently the Monkey needs room to wander and squander. If these concessions are made, they can have a lovely, long-lasting life复工",Rooster:"This partnership can succeed brilliantly. Roosters who find themselves in bed with willing, sensual Pigs are truly in luck. My advice to this lucky Rooster is to hang on tight: you will not find such amiability, charm and easygoing service anywhere else in the zodiac. Pigs are willing to adapt and change, modify their personalities and lifestyles to suit the one they love. With all of your ups and downs, resounding successes and failures, you will definitely benefit from the presence of a kindly, nurturing, understanding Pig. As for the Pig in this relationship, you will gain much from the pure rigor and frank style of a Rooster partner. Roosters like things as they are. They are not revolutionaries. Pigs, too, enjoy tradition and respect the basic tenets of a good society. Your common interests will flourish and after the first few years will take you very far towards achieving dreams and goals you only dreamed of before meeting. Sex, too, is favored in this couple. The Rooster can take charge in lovemaking. Pigs appreciate being moved to exotic heights in bed, adore almost anything sensual and make excellent cuddlers for roughshod Rooster to learn to snuggle with. If I were a Rooster, I think I might seek a Pig mate. Your lifetime happiness and financial security (Pigs attract money) would be assured.",Dog:"Intimacy between Dog and Pig people promises great enduring love, respect and passion. The Dog and Pig are complementary in thought and feeling. They both believe in the basic good of humankind. They both love the countryside and adhere to sanity as a fine way to live. Mind you, there are some basic differences to contend with: Pigs love opulence while Dogs couldn’t care less about luxury. Pigs tend to be conservative; Dogs are liberal. Pigs are sensualists—there’s nothing they love better than a good dirty story—while Dogs are puritanically-inclined. But all these differences are worked out between the Dog and Pig because they are each willing to respect and even admire the other for their individual tastes and preferences. Dog loves the cozy security Pig provides and Pig sees Dog’s politically active friends as perfect guests. He feeds them to death. Pig may at first be flummoxed by the Dog’s seeming sexual indifference. But Pigs have clever (sometimes devious) ways of getting people’s attention, and will always find a way to their Doggie’s heart. Pigs are infinitely patient. They know how to bide their time and cajole until they get what they want and need out of their cranky, but basically sweet-tempered Dog partner. Providing they husband and promote their mutual talent for goodwill, this pair will be blissfully content for a very long time.",Pig:"An excellent match. Here we have two interesting, nature-loving, sensitive and sensual people whose mutual quest for culture and respect for creative imagination are guaranteed to fend off boredom for a lifetime. Money will never be a problem: Pigs attract piles of it. They are not only lucky, but they are hardworking and fair-dealing in all transactions. Two Pigs are better than one in the financial arena, as they will be able to advise each other as to spending: which art to buy and which to sell, what stocks and bonds to invest, and which houses or other property would protect their future. There is a streak of masochism in the Pig character, so one or the other might, following an unfortunate incident or business betrayal, slide into a depression and be beset by pessimistic notions. If luck is with them, the other Pig will know how to respond and help their mate out of the doldrums. When things are going well, both Pigs have real talent for pleasure. They mutually enjoy a dirty joke and have few inhibitions about things sensual. The sexual conjugality of this couple is sublime. They are likely to be very vocal in bed, just as they make lots of noise when they eat. Neither will ever correct the other’s manners, so the ambiance at table around the Pig house might resemble something akin to “Dining with Wolves”."},futures:{2025:{year:"Snake",element:"Wood",prediction:"This year, you may be the victim of some malicious gossip. The Snake year is famous for intrigue. As you are a forthright and honest person, you are not well-equipped to deal with underhanded tactics. Your best defense is to be aware of the possibility of deceit and to take precautions. Do not reveal any secrets, even to your closest friends. Be wary of new acquaintances who seem overly friendly. They may be trying to take advantage of your good nature. Professionally, this is a year for consolidation rather than expansion. Focus on strengthening your existing projects and relationships. Financially, it’s a stable period, but avoid making any risky investments. Your love life may be a bit complicated. The Snake’s sensuality can be tempting, but its possessiveness can be suffocating. If you’re in a relationship, be prepared for some jealousy. If you’re single, you may be drawn into a passionate but ultimately destructive affair. It’s a year to be cautious and to trust your instincts."},2026:{year:"Horse",element:"Fire",prediction:"The energetic pace of the Horse year will suit your industrious nature. It’s a time of action and achievement. You will feel motivated to pursue your goals with vigor. Professionally, this is an excellent year for career advancement. Your hard work will be recognized, and you may be offered a leadership position. Financially, it’s a prosperous time. You will have opportunities to increase your income, but be mindful of the Horse’s tendency to spend extravagantly. Your practical nature will help you maintain a healthy balance. Romantically, it’s a passionate and exciting year. The Horse’s adventurous spirit will bring a spark to your love life. If you’re single, you may meet someone who sweeps you off your feet. If you’re in a relationship, it’s a time for shared adventures and new experiences. This is a year of progress and excitement."},2027:{year:"Goat",element:"Fire",prediction:"This is a wonderful year for you. The Goat’s artistic and gentle nature is highly compatible with your own. You will find yourself in a harmonious and creative environment. It’s a time for indulging in your love of beauty and culture. Professionally, it’s a good year for any creative pursuits. Your imagination will be firing on all cylinders. Financially, it’s a prosperous time. The Goat’s luck and your hard work will bring abundance. It’s a good time for investing in art or property. Romantically, this is a blissful period. The Goat’s sensuality and your loving nature make for a perfect match. You will experience deep emotional connection and contentment. This is a year of peace, creativity, and love. Enjoy every moment."},2028:{year:"Monkey",element:"Earth",prediction:"This year, your good nature will be tested. The Monkey’s cleverness can sometimes border on deceit, and you may find yourself the victim of a prank or a scheme. It’s a year to be cautious and not to take things at face value. Professionally, you may find that your honest efforts are undermined by more cunning colleagues. Stick to your principles and don’t get drawn into office politics. Financially, be wary of get-rich-quick schemes. The Monkey’s influence can lead to risky investments. Trust your practical instincts and stick to what you know. In your love life, the Monkey’s playful nature can be fun, but its lack of sincerity can be hurtful. Don’t be fooled by charming words that aren’t backed up by actions. This is a year for discernment and for protecting your gentle heart."},2029:{year:"Rooster",element:"Earth",prediction:"This will be a productive year for you. The Rooster’s diligence and your own hardworking nature are a good match. You will find satisfaction in a job well done. Professionally, it’s a time for meticulous work and attention to detail. Your efforts will be rewarded. Financially, it’s a stable year. The Rooster’s conservatism will curb any extravagant tendencies, and you will see your savings grow. It’s a good time for long-term financial planning. Romantically, you will appreciate the Rooster’s loyalty and commitment. However, the Rooster’s critical nature can be a bit much for your sensitive soul. Try not to take its nitpicking to heart. This is a year for steady progress and building a secure foundation for the future."},2030:{year:"Dog",element:"Metal",prediction:"This is a year of deep emotional connection and shared ideals. The Dog’s loyalty and your own devotion create a powerful bond. You will find great comfort and security in your relationships. Professionally, it’s a good time for collaborative projects, especially those with a humanitarian focus. Your combined efforts can make a real difference in the world. Financially, it’s a stable period. The Dog’s practicality and your good luck with money will ensure that you have everything you need. It’s a good time for charitable giving. Romantically, this is a time of profound love and mutual respect. You will feel deeply understood and cherished. This is a year for nurturing your relationships and finding fulfillment in helping others."},2031:{year:"Pig",element:"Metal",prediction:"This is your year to luxuriate in comfort and pleasure. You will feel a strong sense of well-being and contentment. It’s a time for enjoying the fruits of your labor. Professionally, you may not be particularly ambitious, but you will find satisfaction in your work. It’s a good year for creative pursuits and for working at your own pace. Financially, this is a very prosperous year. Your natural luck with money will be amplified. It’s a time for indulging in life’s luxuries. Romantically, if you are with another Pig, you will experience a deep and harmonious connection. If you are single, you may meet someone who shares your love of comfort and sensuality. This is a year for enjoying life to the fullest. Don’t be afraid to spoil yourself."},2032:{year:"Rat",element:"Water",prediction:"This is a socially active and prosperous year for you. The Rat’s energy and your own sociable nature will make you the life of the party. You will be surrounded by friends and admirers. Professionally, it’s a good time for networking and making new connections. Your charm and the Rat’s cunning will lead to success. Financially, this is an excellent year. The Rat’s shrewdness and your good fortune will bring you wealth. It’s a good time for investing and for expanding your business. Romantically, it’s a passionate and exciting time. You will be in high demand. If you’re single, you’ll have your pick of suitors. If you’re in a relationship, your partner will be captivated by your charm. This is a year for enjoying success and popularity."},2033:{year:"Ox",element:"Water",prediction:"This year will feel a bit slow and restrictive for your tastes. The Ox’s deliberate pace and conservative nature will clash with your desire for pleasure and spontaneity. You may feel that your plans are being thwarted by bureaucracy and red tape. Patience is required. Professionally, it’s a time for steady, methodical work. Don’t expect any sudden breakthroughs. Financially, it’s a stable but unexciting year. The Ox’s influence is good for saving, but not for making money. It’s a time to be frugal. In your love life, you may find the Ox a bit dull. Your sensual nature may not be fully appreciated. It’s a year for finding contentment in simple pleasures and for building a solid foundation for the future."},2034:{year:"Tiger",element:"Wood",prediction:"This is a year of dynamic energy and change. The Tiger’s boldness and your own willingness to help can lead to exciting new ventures. However, you may find the Tiger’s impulsiveness a bit overwhelming. You prefer a more measured approach. Professionally, you may be drawn into ambitious projects that are outside your comfort zone. It’s a time for courage and for embracing new challenges. Financially, it’s a year of ups and downs. The Tiger’s risk-taking can lead to both great gains and great losses. Be cautious. Romantically, it’s a passionate but potentially volatile time. The Tiger’s intensity can be both thrilling and exhausting. This is a year for adventure and for pushing your boundaries."},2035:{year:"Rabbit",element:"Wood",prediction:"This is a peaceful and harmonious year for you. The Rabbit’s refined taste and your own love of beauty will create a lovely synergy. It’s a time for enjoying art, culture, and the comforts of home. Professionally, it’s a good year for any work that requires a gentle touch and an eye for detail. You will find satisfaction in creating a beautiful and orderly environment. Financially, it’s a prosperous year. The Rabbit’s good judgment and your own luck will lead to financial security. It’s a good time for investing in your home. Romantically, this is a very compatible match. You will find a deep and tender connection with your partner. It’s a time for nurturing your relationship and enjoying a peaceful and happy home life."},2036:{year:"Dragon",element:"Fire",prediction:"This is a year of excitement and social activity. The Dragon’s flamboyant nature and your own love of a good time will make for a lively combination. You will be invited to many parties and events. Professionally, you will be inspired by the Dragon’s ambition. It’s a good time to pursue your goals with renewed vigor. The Dragon’s power can help you to achieve great things. Financially, it’s a year of extravagance. The Dragon loves to spend money, and you will be tempted to indulge. Be careful not to go overboard. Romantically, it’s a passionate and dramatic time. The Dragon’s intensity is captivating, but its ego can be a bit much. This is a year for enjoying the spotlight and for pursuing your dreams with confidence."}}},c={Rat:e,Ox:t,Tiger:o,Rabbit:a,Dragon:i,Snake:n,Horse:s,Goat:r,Monkey:l,Rooster:h,Dog:d,Pig:u};export{c as z};
